1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Jane Baskerville ===
2 CONT * Death: 1566 1
2 CONT * Burial: Fonthill, Wilts 2
2 CONT * Father: Philip Baskerville b: 1466 
2 CONT * Mother: Sybilla Scudamore
2 CONT * Married: 1) William Peverell of Balderston 2) Sir John Mervyn of Fountel Gifford, whose first wife she became. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by her 1st husband  
2 CONT # Jane Peverell (only daughter & heir of her father William)
2 CONT
2 CONT By her 2nd husband Sir John, she had thirteen children, five sons and eight daughters.  The eldest was 
2 CONT #  James Mervyn b: 1529
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=w8U4AQAAMAAJ&lpg=PA88&ots=YP1_2GzXAP&dq=roger%20churchill%20jane%20peverell&pg=PA87#v=onepage&q=roger%20churchill%20jane%20peverell&f=true "The Peverell's of Dorset"] Notes & Queries for Som
2 CONC erset and Dorset, Volume 1 by C. J. Creed, 1890 - Dorset (England).  Page 87-88
2 CONT
2 CONT Concerning the rest of this branch of the family I can add nothing to Hutchins’s account until we come down to WILLIAM PEVERELL, of Burdolston, 8 Henry VIII, [1516-17] His wife was jane, daughter of Philip Baskerville, of Sherborn
2 CONC e, Dorset. She survived her first husband, and married Sir John Mervyn of Fountel Gifford, whose first wife she became. She was buried at Fountel. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William Peverell had an only daughter and heiress,JANE PEVERELL, who married, first, Nicholas Meggs of Downham. By him she had a son,Lawrence Meggs. Bradford Peverell was held by his descendants until 1770. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Although Hutchins says she died in 1578,and that Nicholas Meggs died ‘circa 1579,’ thus making her predecease her husband, he states in his acccount of the Churchills that Roger Churchill, of Catherstone, married Jane, daughter of
2 CONC  William Peverell, and widow of Nicholas Meggs. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=ancestorsearch&id=I18738
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=PZUNAAAAQAAJ&lpg=PA12&ots=985iiZEPj4&dq=John%20mervyn%20member%20of%20parliament&pg=PA12#v=onepage&q&f=true Fasciculus Mervinensis,] notes historical, genealogical, and heraldic of the family o
2 CONC f Mervyn William Richard Drake (sir.) . 1873.  Page 9-12.  "SIR JOHN MERVYN, of Fountel-Giffard, Knight, succeeded his grandfather Walter. He married twice; his first wife being JANE, daughter of Philip BASKERVILLE, of Sherborne, 
2 CONC in the county of Dorset (afterwards of Erdesley, in the county of Hereford), and widow of William Peverell, of Bradford Peverell, in the county of Somerset. By Jane Baskerville, who was buried at Fountel, Sir John had thirteen chi
2 CONC ldren, five sons and eight daughters, viz.:— ... "
2 CONT * [http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1509-1558/member/marvyn-sir-john-1503-66 MARVYN, Sir John] (by 1503-66), of Fonthill Gifford, Wilts. Published in The History of Parliament: the House of Commons 1509-1558, ed. S.
2 CONC T. Bindoff, 1982.  "b. by 1503, 1st s. of John Marvyn of Fonthill Gifford by Elizabeth, da. and coh. of John Green of Stotfold, Beds. m. (1) by 1529, Jane, da. of Philip Baskerville of Sherborne, Dorset, wid. of William Peverell o
2 CONC f Bradford Peverell, Som., 5s. inc. James† 8da.; ..."
