2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/visitationofcound00stge#page/36/mode/1up
2 CONT *William Meggs of Canterbury. = Eliz. sister and h. of Tho. West. ; ch: Alice (m. Ralph Tonke.), Kath. (m. Peter Bruin), Thomas (m. Anne Copleston) Meggs.
2 CONT **	Thomas Meggs of Downam in the Isle of Ely. = Anne d. and h. of John Copleston of Exeter. ; ch: Robert 2., Henry 3., '''Nicholas (m. Jane Peverell)''' Meggs
2 CONT ***'''		Nicholas Meggs of Bradford Peverell co. Dors. = Jane d. and h. of Wm Peverell of Bradford Peverell. ; ch:''' Lawrence Meggs. _________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT From  [http://books.google.com/books?id=IkhAAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA191&ots=ul23pCmAxi&dq=Bartholomew%20Cherchile&pg=PA192#v=onepage&q=Bartholomew%20Cherchile&f=false Collin's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT The said Roger marrying Jane, Relict of Nichoki Megg, and Daughter to William Peverell of Bradford, by her had Matthew Churchill of Bradford, whose Wife was Alice, Daughter to James Gould of Dorchester ...
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________________________
2 CONT *'''The dormant and extinct baronage of England: or, An historical and ... Vol. I.   By Thomas Christopher Banks
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=v0cvAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA162&lpg=PA162&dq=a+survey+of+the+manor+of+bradford+peverell&source=bl&ots=TAAiaz_L6o&sig=IGcJr7eh6GbkQ85XUrdhHAAs23Q&hl=en&sa=X&ei=rsdxVaHRCMzIogTm4YH4DA&ved=0CFcQ6AEwCQ#v=onepa
2 CONC ge&q=meggs&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.162
2 CONT *PEVERELL
2 CONT * ....
2 CONT *   The was alfo another WILLIAM, called Peverel of London; and in the time of Edward I. there was a John Peverel, of Bradford Peverel, in the county of Dorfet ; but whether a branch of thofe of Nottingham, Dovor, or Brunne, is un
2 CONC certain; they bore their ames differently; viz. "Girony of Eight A. and G"d	 '''Jane the fole daughter and heir of this ancient family, who died in 1576, married Nicholas Meggs, efquire, of Downham, in the Ifle of Ely, whofe fon''
2 CONC ', Lawrence Meggs, fucceeded to the eftate at Bradford Peverel, where, for feveral ages, his pofterity continued to the the fame manor. __________________________________
