2 CONT *Description:	
2 CONT *Short title: Grosse v Megges.
2 CONT *Plaintiffs: Robert Grosse of Muckleford, Dorset.
2 CONT *Defendants: '''Nicholas Megges and his wife Jane.
2 CONT *Subject of decree: Several messuages with land and common of pasture for 4 plough beasts, 6 cattle and 240 sheep in Muckleford, Dorset.
2 CONT *Date of decree: 1 May 5 Eliz.
2 CONT *Date:	1563 May 1
2 CONT *Held by:	The National Archives, Kew
2 CONT *http://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/details/r/C14515627
2 CONT *
2 CONT *not digitised
2 CONT *Reference:	C 3/120/3
2 CONT *Description:	Short title: Megges v Grosse.
2 CONT *Plaintiffs: '''Nicholas Megges and Jane Megges his wife.
2 CONT *Defendants: Robert Grosse and others.
2 CONT *Subject: copyhold of manor of Bradford Peverell, Dorset.
2 CONT *Document type: [pleadings].
2 CONT *Date:	1558-1579
2 CONT *Held by:	The National Archives, Kew
2 CONT *http://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/details/r/C3781925
2 CONT *
2 CONT *cost £3.30
2 CONT *Reference:	PROB 11/61/518
2 CONT *Description:	'''Will of Nicholas Megges, Gentleman of Bradford, Dorset
2 CONT *Date:	10 November 1579
2 CONT *Held by:	The National Archives, Kew
2 CONT *http://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/details/r/D964058 __________________________
2 CONT *'''Index of Wills Proved in the Prerogative Court of Canterbury ..., Volume 18  By Church of England. Province of Canterbury. Prerogative Court https://books.google.com/books?id=JT8EAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA211&lpg=PA211&dq=nicholas+megges+
2 CONC 1579&source=bl&ots=4BaHWfMxM3&sig=maZWDKYURyYT2yI-Refj0J1oFkg&hl=en&sa=X&ei=0dlxVcSYEpO1oQSIjINw&ved=0CB0Q6AEwADgK#v=onepage&q=nicholas%20megges%201579&f=false https://archive.org/details/indexofwillsprov18chur https://archive.org
2 CONC /stream/indexofwillsprov18chur#page/211/mode/1up
2 CONT *Prerogative Court of Canterbury.
2 CONT *'''1579 Megges, Nicholas, gent., Bradforde, Dorset	46 Bakon _______________________________
2 CONT *DORSET ANCESTORS
2 CONT *Bradford Peverell
2 CONT *During the reign of Henry I (1100-1135) and Stephen (1135-1154) the manors of Bradford and Muckleford came into the possession of the De Port family as tenants of the Duchy of Lancaster. Adam de Port was outlawed and his land for
2 CONC feited to King Richard I who, as we tell above, granted the manors to Robert Peverel but during the reign of Elizabeth I the male Peveril line became extinct: William Peverel leaving an '''only daughter, Jane.
2 CONT *'''Jane married Nicholas Meggs of Cambridgeshire'''. The Meggs’ suffered heavy losses during the Civil War and in 1683 Thomas Meggs sold the manor of Muckleford, a small hamlet within the parish, to make good the family finances.
2 CONC  The rest of the parish remained in the hands of the Meggs family until 1770, when Harry Meggs sold it to John Purling. (See our story ‘The Muckleford Treasure’ in the Bradford Peverell category).
2 CONT * ....
2 CONT *Thomas Gerard in his book Coker’s Survey of Dorestshire (1732) '''wrote: “Bradford Peverll. The Seate for a longe time of the antient Familie of Peverells whose estate about Henry the Eighth’s time fell by a Female Heire to Nicho
2 CONC las Meggs and his Posteritie enjoy it.''' Neare Bradford the River dividing itself, making an Island of manie faire and fruitful Maedowes, and there joineth againe a little belowe Dorchester, the more northern branch, being the le
2 CONC sser, amongst these Maedoes runneth by Wolton, more trulie Wolvehampton, a fine and rich Seate which (by the daughter and Heire of John Jordan the antient owner of it) came to John Mohune. His only daughter and Heire Alice brought
2 CONC  a faire Estate unto her husband Henry Trinchard of Hampshire whose Grandchilde Sir Thomas Trinchard, gracious with King Henry the Eighth was called chief Builder of the Habitation of Sir George Trinchard, a Man of Great Courage.”
2 CONC  (See our article: ‘Thomas Gerard of Trent’ Published 17th July 2011, in the Trent category.)
2 CONT *From: http://dorset-ancestors.com/?p=2236 ____________________________
2 CONT *'''Notes and Queries for Somerset and Dorset ..., Volume 27
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=v_LgAAAAMAAJ&q=John+Peverell&dq=John+Peverell&hl=en&sa=X&ei=Yq9mU7vOAqLE7Aaw7YGACw&ved=0CCIQ6AEwAA
2 CONT *NO PAGE PREVIEWS Pg.185 "Certainly the Duke's great, great, great grandfather, '''Roger Churchill, married the widow of Nicholas Meggs of Bradford Peverell''' as even Sir Winston2 the old cavalier admits .... etc. _______________
2 CONC __________
