1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Devereux_(1411%E2%80%931459%29 Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia: '''Walter Devereux (1411–1459)''']
2 CONT
2 CONT *''''''Sir Walter Devereux, Sheriff of Herefordshire & Gloucestershire, Constable of Wigmore, Keeper of Leominster1,2,3,4,5,6
2 CONT *''''''M, b. circa 1412, d. 22 April 1459
2 CONT *Father Walter Devereux, Esq.7,3 b. c 1387, d. 1420 
2 CONT *Mother Maud Bromwich7,3 b. c 1391 
2 CONT *''''''     Sir Walter Devereux, Sheriff of Herefordshire & Gloucestershire, Constable of Wigmore, Keeper of Leominster was born circa 1412 at of Woebley & Bodenham, Herefordshire, England; Age 24 in 1436; age 26 in 1438.2,3 He ma
2 CONC rried Elizabeth Merbury, daughter of John Merbury, Esq., Justice of South Wales, Sheriff & Escheater of Herefordshire, Steward of Brecon and Alice Pembrugge, circa 1432; They had 2 sons (Sir Walter, Lord Ferrers of Chartley; & Sir
2 CONC  John) and at least 1 daughter (Anne, wife of Sir William Herbert, 1st Earl of Pembroke, 1st Lord Herbert). Sir Walter Devereux, Sheriff of Herefordshire & Gloucestershire, Constable of Wigmore, Keeper of Leominster died on 22 Apr
2 CONC il 1459.
2 CONT *''''''Family Elizabeth Merbury b. c 1412, d. b 1459 
2 CONT *Children 
2 CONT **◦Sir John Devereux, Sheriff of Herefordshire d. a 1489
2 CONT **◦Sir Walter Devereux, Lord Ferrers+8,3,4 b. c 1432, d. 22 Aug 1485
2 CONT **◦Anne Devereux+9,3,5,10,6 b. c 1433, d. a 25 Jun 1486
2 CONT **◦Isabel Devereux b. c 1437
2 CONT **◦Sybil Devereux+ b. c 1440, d. b 1499
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S5978] Unknown author, Lineage and Ancestry of HRH Prince Charles by Paget, Vol. II, p. 440; Plantagenet Anestry of 17th Century Colonists, by David Faris, p. 103; Wallop Family, p. 57.
2 CONT *2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 250.
2 CONT *3.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 3.
2 CONT *4.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 163-164.
2 CONT *5.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 280-281.
2 CONT *6.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 346-347.
2 CONT *7.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 249-250.
2 CONT *8.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 310.
2 CONT *9.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 395.
2 CONT *10.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 388.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p644.htm#i19348
2 CONT *_________________
2 CONT *''''''Sir Walter Devereux1
2 CONT *''''''M, #437999, b. 1411, d. from 22 April 1459 to 23 April 1459
2 CONT *Last Edited=17 Jul 2010
2 CONT *''''''     Sir Walter Devereux was born in 1411. He was the son of Sir Walter Devereux and Maud Bromwich. He married Elizabeth Merbury, daughter of Sir John Merbury. He died from 22 April 1459 to 23 April 1459.
2 CONT *''''''     He held the office of Chancellor of Ireland in 1449.1 He fought in the Wars of the Roses, as a Yorkist. He lived at Newbold Verdon, Leicestershire, England.1 He lived at Bodenham, Herefordshire, England.1 He lived at W
2 CONC eobley, Herefordshire, England. In 1459 he was granted land in Drogheda.
2 CONT *''''''Child of Sir Walter Devereux and Elizabeth Merbury
2 CONT ** 1.Sir Walter Devereux, 1st Lord Ferrers (of Chartley)+2 b. c 1432, d. 22 Aug 1485
