2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Merbury Heiress Of Weobley 1 2 3 4
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: Abt 1412, Lyonshall, , Herefordshire, England 3 Marriage: Sir Walter Devereux Knight about 1432 in Herefordshire, England, United Kingdom
2 CONT
2 CONT _________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth married Sir Walter Devereux Knight, son of Walter Devereaux Of Bodenham, Sir and Elizabeth (Maude) Bromwitch, about 1432 in Herefordshire, England, United Kingdom. (Sir Walter Devereux Knight was born about 1387 in Boden
2 CONC ham, , Herefordshire, England 2 3 and died on 22 Apr 1459 in Weobley, , Herefordshire, England 2 3 5.)
2 CONT
2 CONT _________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Merbury (c. 1412) was an English noblewoman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth was the daughter of Sir John Merbury, by his first wife, Alice Pembridge. She was married to Walter Devereux (1411–1459) about 1432 in Herefordshire, England. Together, they had several children:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT     Anne Devereux
2 CONT     Richard Devereux (c. 1426, Chartley, Herefordshire, England)
2 CONT     Thomas Devereux (c. 1428, Chartley, Herefordshire, England)
2 CONT     Walter Devereux, 7th Baron Ferrers of Chartley
2 CONT     John Devereux (c. 1434, Weobley, England)
2 CONT     Katherine (Sibyl) Devereux (c. 1438). Married firstly James Baskerville about 1464
2 CONT     Isabel Devereux (c. 1440, Weobley, England)
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT
2 CONT Yap, Brian. "Elizabeth Merbury Heiress Of Weobley". Retrieved 15 September 2013.
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	John Merbury, Esq., Justice of South Wales, Sheriff & Escheater of Herefordshire, Steward of Brecon b. c 1387, d. 29 Jan 1438
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother	Alice Pembrugge b. 1372, d. 1415
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Merbury[1] was born circa 1412 at of Lyonshall & Weobley, Herefordshire, England; Age 26 in 1438.[2] She married Sir Walter Devereux, Sheriff of Herefordshire & Gloucestershire, Constable of Wigmore, Keeper of Leominster
2 CONC , son of Walter Devereux, Esq. and Elizabeth Bromwich, circa 1432; They had 2 sons (Sir Walter, Lord Ferrers of Chartley; & Sir John) and 1 daughter (Anne, wife of Sir William Herbert, 1st Earl of Pembroke, 1st Lord Herbert).[3] E
2 CONC lizabeth Merbury died before 1459.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT     Sir Walter Devereux, Sheriff of Herefordshire & Gloucestershire, Constable of Wigmore, Keeper of Leominster b. c 1412, d. 22 Apr 1459 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	
2 CONT
2 CONT     Sir John Devereux, Sheriff of Herefordshire d. a 1489
2 CONT     Sir Walter Devereux, Lord Ferrers b. c 1432, d. 22 Aug 1485
2 CONT     Anne Devereux b. c 1433, d. a 25 Jun 1486
2 CONT     Isabel Devereux b. c 1437
2 CONT     Sybil Devereux b. c 1440, d. b 1499 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT     ↑ Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 250.
2 CONT     ↑ Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 3, 163-164.
2 CONT     ↑ Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. V, p. 249.
2 CONT     ↑ Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. II, p. 575-576.
2 CONT
