2 CONT *''''''A genealogical and heraldic history of the commoners of Great Britain and ... By John Burke
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=uo9AAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA90&lpg=PA90&dq=John+Baskerville+1408&source=bl&ots=3tCQwhIQHs&sig=sp2CQXVUFaG1P0MuqGFhNvDIEYA&hl=en&sa=X&ei=NxtoT5afOMPRiALMuLWVBw&ved=0CDYQ6AEwBDge#v=onepage&q=John%20Baskervill
2 CONC e%201408&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 90
2 CONT *   SIR RICHARD BASKERVILLE, knt. who sued out his livery in the 17th RICHARD II. He m. Joan, daughter of Adam de Everingham, of Laxton, and dying 16th September, 1395, was s. by his son,
2 CONT *   SIR JOHN BASKERVILLE, knt. living in the reign of HENRY IV. This gentleman m. Elizabeth, daughter and heiress of John Brugge, of Letton and Slanton, and had issue,
2 CONT **''''''	JOHN (Sir), his successor.
2 CONT **	Ralph, b. 21 October, 1410, who m. Anee, daughter and co-heiress of Sir John Blackett, knt. and left an only daughter and heiress,  ....
2 CONT *SIR JOHN BASKERVILLE was s. by his eldest son,
2 CONT *''''''   SIR JOHN BASKERVILLE, knt. of Combe, b. 12 February, 1408. He espoused Elizabeth, daughter of John Touchet, Lord Audley, and had issue,
2 CONT **	I. JAMES (Sir), his successor.
2 CONT **	II. John, who wedded Eleanor, daughter and heiress of Thomas Holcot, of Wotton, and became possessed of that estate in right of his wife. He was father of   ....
2 CONT **	III. Henry.
2 CONT **	IV. Humphrey.
2 CONT **	V. Sibill, m. to Richard Rowden, of Rowden.
2 CONT *''''''Sir John d. 23rd December, 1455, and was s. by his eldest son,
2 CONT *   SIR JAMES BASKERVILLE, knt. of Erdisley, sheriff of Hereford, 38th HENRY VI. 4th EDWARD IV. and 14th HENRY VII. which office had been frequently filled by his ancestors. This gentleman espoused Sibill, daughter of Walter Dever
2 CONC eux, Lord Ferrers, of Chartley,* and had issue,  ....
2 CONT *____________________________
2 CONT *''''''Elizabeth TOUCHET
2 CONT *''''''Born: ABT 1401
2 CONT *Father: John TOUCHET (1º B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT *Mother: Isabel ?
2 CONT *''''''Married: John BASKERVILLE
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. James BASKERVILLE (m. Catherine Devereux)
2 CONT **2. Jane BASKERVILLE (m. John Monington)
2 CONT *http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/TOUCHET.htm#Elizabeth TOUCHET1
2 CONT *_____________
2 CONT *''''''Magna Carta ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=wHZcIRMhSEMC&pg=PA832&lpg=PA832&dq=John+Baskerville+1408&source=bl&ots=2Ez8wp2z7Q&sig=35ePv6l94lpzveoD8KnOocGq4gs&hl=en&sa=X&ei=NiRoT9bkGKShiQLm85jqBg&ved=0CFMQ6AEwCTg8#v=onepage&q=John%20Baskervi
2 CONC lle%201408&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 832
2 CONT *   11. JOHN TUCHET, Knt., of Ashwell, Rutland, Markeaton, Derbyshire, Leegomery (in Wellington), Shropshire, etc., and Buglawton and Newhall, Cheshire, Keeper of Llandover Castle, Keeper of Brecknock Castle, son and heir, born 23
2 CONC  April 1371. He was co-heir in 1391 to his great-uncle, Nicholas Audley, Knt., 3rd Lord Audley, by which he inherited a on-third share in the Audley barony, including the Castle and lordship of Heleigh, Staffordshire, and the Cast
2 CONC le and lordship of Newport (in Camois), Pembrokeshire. He married before 1398 ELIZABETH STAFFORD, daughter of Humphrey Stafford, Knt., of Amblecote, Bramshall, and Perton, Staffordshire, by his 1st wife, Alice, daughter and heires
2 CONC s of John Grenville, Knt.  They had one son, James [5th Lord Audley], and two daughters, Margaret and ''''''Elizabeth (wife of John Baskerville, Knt.)''''''. He was in the Welsh wars against Owen Glendower. He was summoned to Parl
2 CONC iament on 20 Oct. 1403, by writ directed Johanni Tochet, and from 25 August 1404 to 26 August 1407, by writs directed Johanni Tuchet. He was frequently styled Lord Audley in offical documents, although never summoned to Parliament
2 CONC  as such. in 1404 he was at Coventry with 30 squires and 60 archers. In 1405 they received a papal indult for a portable altar. He was present at the surrender of Aberystwith in 1407. SIR JOHN TUCHET, 4th Lord Audley, died 19 Dec.
2 CONC  1408. in 1409 the king requested that his widow's brother, Humphrey Stafford the younger, deliver her son and heir to his custody. In 1436 Thomas Stawell, Knt. sued Elizabeth, late the wife of John Tuchet, Knt., her son, James Tu
2 CONC chet, Knt., her brother, John Stafford, Bishop of Bath and Wells, and William Lee for the manors of Nether Stowey, Honeybare, etc., Somerset. A verdict was delivered in favor of the defendants. She died 1446-7 (date of her IPM).
2 CONT *_______________________
