2 CONT
2 CONT SYBIL VAUGHAN (d.1559) http://www.kateemersonhistoricals.com/TudorWomenU-V.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Sybil Vaughan was the daughter of Watkin Vaughan of Hergest, Herefordshire and Elizabeth Baskerville. In 1511, she married John Scudamore of Holme Lacy, Herefordshire (d. September 25, 1571). They were the parents of William (1514
2 CONC -1560), Katherine, Joan, Sybil, Richard (d.1586), Elizabeth, Philip (d.1602), Jane, and John (d. January 29, 1599/1600). 
2 CONT
2 CONT For more pictures of her tomb, see http://www.britainexpress.com/counties/hereford/churches/Holme-Lacy/index.htm?page=2
2 CONT
2 CONT =<nowiki>---------------------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sybil Vaughn'''
2 CONT *'''F, #86804, b. circa 1496
2 CONT *Father      Watkin Vaughn, Esq.1 b. c 1460
2 CONT *Mother     Elizabeth Baskerville1 b. c 1464
2 CONT *'''     Sybil Vaughn was born circa 1496 at of Hergest, Herefordshire, England.1 She married John Scudamore, Esq., son of William Scudamore and Alice Mynors, circa 1519.1
2 CONT *'''Family      John Scudamore, Esq. b. c 1490, d. 25 Sep 1571
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Sybil Scudamore+2 b. c 1520
2 CONT **Jane Scudamore+1 b. c 1525
2 CONT **John Scudamore+ b. c 1537, d. 29 Jan 1600
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S61] Unknown author, Family Group Sheets, Family History Archives, SLC.
2 CONT * 2.[S11588] Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 107.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2889.htm#i86804
2 CONT =_____________________=
2 CONT '''SCUDAMORE, (SKYDMORE), John (by 1503-71), of Holm Lacy, Herefs.
2 CONT *b. by 1503, s. of William Scudamore of Holm Lacy by Alice, da of Richard Mynors of Treago. '''m. (1) Sybil, da. of Walter Vaughan of Hergest, 4s. 5da.'''; (2) Joan, da. of William Rudhale of Rudhall, wid. of Richard Rede (d. 18 J
2 CONC uly 1544) of Boddington, Glos., s.p.2
2 CONT *The Scudamores of Holm Lacy were a cadet branch of the family settled at Kentchurch: they had acquired Holm Lacy by marriage in the mid 14th century and John Scudamore was himself to augment it. He also built a house there on a s
2 CONC ite which, according to tradition, had been the dwelling-place of Walter de Lacy and his heirs. Further additions were to be made to the estate by the marriage of Scudamore’s son William with the heiress of (Sir) John Pakington of
2 CONC  Hampton Lovett, Worcestershire.4 .... etc.
2 CONT *Scudamore’s will, made on 20 July and proved on 17 Nov. 1571, was nevertheless as firmly Catholic as that of the more intransigent Thomas Havard, who had refused to subscribe. He bequeathed his soul to God, the Virgin Mary and th
2 CONC e company of heaven and gave £20 to the poor to pray for his soul; a further £100 was to be bestowed on his funeral if he died at or near Holm Lacy but otherwise was to be ‘distributed amongst poor people to pray for my soul and a
2 CONC ll Christian souls and in amending of highways’. His eldest son William had died before 1560 but he still had a large family to provide for, including several grandchildren. Of his daughters, Jane was then married to (Sir) William
2 CONC  Devereux of Merevale, Warwickshire. The residuary legatee was Scudamore’s grandson and heir, John, who was to serve in six Elizabethan Parliaments as junior knight for Herefordshire: he was named executor together with Edward Coo
2 CONC per, archdeacon of Hereford, with Richard Seborne as overseer. Scudamore died on 25 Sept. 1571 and was '''buried beside his first wife at Holm Lacy, the inscription on their altar-tomb praying passers-by ‘of their charity to say f
2 CONC or their souls a paternoster and an ave’.9'''
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1509-1558/member/scudamore-%28skydmore%29-john-1503-71
2 CONT =____________________________=
2 CONT *William DEVEREUX (Sir)
2 CONT *Born: ABT 1525, Chartley, Staffordshire, England
2 CONT *Acceded: Mirevale Abbey, Warwickshire
2 CONT *Died: BEF 2 Nov 1579
2 CONT *Notes: Burke's Peerage, sub Huntingdon.
2 CONT *Father: Walter DEVEREUX (1º V. Hereford)
2 CONT *Mother: Mary GREY
2 CONT *Married: Jane SCUDAMORE (dau. of '''John Scudamore and Sibyl Vaughn''') ABT 1578, Chartley, Staffordshire, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Barbara DEVEREUX
2 CONT **2. Margaret DEVEREUX
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/DEVEREUX.htm#William DEVEREUX1 ______________________
