2 CONT *'''Anne verch Morgan1
2 CONT *'''F, b. 1456, d. circa 1494
2 CONT *Father Morgan ap Jenkyn d. c 1472 
2 CONT *Mother Margred Mathew 
2 CONT *'''     Anne verch Morgan Other children of her husband from his second wife. She was born in 1456 at of Pencoyd, Wales. She married Sir Walter Baskerville, son of James Baskerville and Sybil Devereux, circa 1485.2 Anne verch Mor
2 CONC gan died circa 1494.
2 CONT *'''Family Sir Walter Baskerville b. 1462, d. 4 Sep 1508 
2 CONT *Children 
2 CONT **Sir James Baskerville+ b. c 1486, d. 13 Nov 1546
2 CONT **John Baskerville2 b. c 1488
2 CONT **Philip Baskerville2 b. c 1490
2 CONT **Elizabeth Baskerville2 b. c 1492
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S9400] Unknown author, Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 17; Wallop Family, p. 57.
2 CONT *2.[S11588] Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 17.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1013.htm#i30433 ________________
2 CONT *'''A genealogical and heraldic history of the commoners of Great Britain and ... By John Burke
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=uo9AAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA90&lpg=PA90&dq=John+Baskerville+1408&source=bl&ots=3tCQwhIQHs&sig=sp2CQXVUFaG1P0MuqGFhNvDIEYA&hl=en&sa=X&ei=NxtoT5afOMPRiALMuLWVBw&ved=0CDYQ6AEwBDge#v=onepage&q=John%20Baskervill
2 CONC e%201408&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 90
2 CONT *   SIR JAMES BASKERVILLE, knt. of Erdisley, sheriff of Hereford, 28th HENRY VI. 4th EDWARD IV. and 14th HENRY VII. which office had been frequently filled by his ancestors. This gentleman espoused Sibill, daughter of Walter Dever
2 CONC eux, Lord Ferrers, of Chartley,* and had issue,
2 CONT **'''	I. WALTER (sir) his heir.
2 CONT **	II. John, who espoused Alice, daughter and heiress of John Bridges, of Hereford, and had a son,   ....
2 CONT **Pg. 91
2 CONT **	III. Philip, who left issue,   ....
2 CONT *Sir James Baskerville was s. by his son,
2 CONT *'''   SIR WALTER BASKERVILLE, knt. of Erdisley, sheriff of Hereford, 9th of EDWARD IV. who was created a knight of the bath, on the marriage of Prince ARTHUR, in 1501. He m. first, Anne, daughter of Morgan ap Jenkin ap Philip, of
2 CONC  Pencoyd, and had issue,
2 CONT **	I. SIR JAMES BASKERVILLE, knt. of Erdisley, who m. Elizabeth, daughter and co-heir of John Breynton, of the county of Herford, and had, with several daughters, five sons, viz.  .....
2 CONT **Pg. 92
2 CONT **	II. John, (second son of Sir Walter Baskerville, by the daughter of Ap Philip) who left a son Henry.
2 CONT **	III. Thomas, of Pontrilas. *
2 CONT **	IV. Elizabeth, wife of Kynard Delabere, or according to some, of Sanacre Delabere, of Kynardsley.
2 CONT *Sir Walter m. secondly, Elizabeth, daughter of Henry ap Melo ap Harry, of Poston, by whom he had further issue,
2 CONT **	V. Philip.
2 CONT **	VI. Edward.
2 CONT **	VII. William.
2 CONT **	VIII. James, from whom some assume the Netherwood branch to be descended.
2 CONT **	IX. Simon, of whom are just about to treat. _________________________
2 CONT *'''Families Directly Descended from All the Royal Families in Europe (495 to ... By Elizabeth M. Leach Rixford
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=8giaoVUufYkC&pg=PA190&lpg=PA190&dq=Families+Directly+Descended+from+all+the+Royal+Families+in+Europe&source=bl&ots=n3GWcF25l0&sig=Cq8ij3Z511NCTuCwWOcVtbTQTHQ&hl=en&ei=C5awTaXaAYicsQOXmanuCw&sa=X&o
2 CONC i=book_result&ct=result&resnum=6&ved=0CEQQ6AEwBQ#v=onepage&q=Morgan&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.11
