1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Fasciculus Mervinensis, notes historical, genealogical, and heraldic of the ...   By William Richard Drake (sir.)
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=PZUNAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA9&lpg=PA9&dq=jane+baskerville+1565&source=bl&ots=985ii3CRh0&sig=yi8UDInrG8FVRdygRV6tfP-tHvI&hl=en&sa=X&ei=zGNvVfa9IMvWoAT6xYDwBQ&ved=0CCsQ6AEwAw#v=onepage&q=jane%20baskerville%2
2 CONC 01565&f=false
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/fasciculusmervi00sirgoog
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/fasciculusmervi00sirgoog#page/n18/mode/1up
2 CONT **	Mervyn Family
2 CONT *Walter Mervyn of Fountel, ob. 1512 = Mary Mompesson. ; ch: John (m. Elizabeth Green), Sir Edmund (m. Elizabeth Pakenham) Mervyn.
2 CONT **	Sir Edmund Mervyn, ob. 1553, of Durford. = Elizabeth Pakenham. ; ch: Henry (m. Edith Windsor) Mervyn
2 CONT ***		Henry Mervyn, of Durford. = Edith Windsor. ; ch: Edmund (m. Anna Jephson) Mervyn.
2 CONT ****			Edmund Mervyn, of Durford, ob. 1604. = Anna Jephson. ; ch: Sir Henry (m. Christian Audley) Mervyn.
2 CONT *****				Sir Henry Mervyn, ob. 1646. = Christian Audley, 4th daughter. ; ch: Sir Audley Mervyn, Speaker of the House of Commons, Ireland. ob. 1676.
2 CONT **	John Mervyn, of Fountel, ob. v.p. = Elizabeth Green. ; ch: Sir John (m. Jane Baskerville) Mervyn.
2 CONT ***		Sir John Mervyn, of Fountel, ob. 1556. = Jane Baskerville. ; ch: Sir James (m. Amy Clarke) Mervyn.
2 CONT ****			Sir James Mervyn, of Fountel, ob. 1611. = Amy Clark. ; ch: Lucy (m. George, Baron Audley) Mervyn.
2 CONT *****				Lucy Mervyn, only child and heiress. ob. v.p. = George, Baron Audley, ob. 1617. ; ch: Christian (m. Sir Henry Mervyn) Audley.
2 CONT ******					Christian Augley, 4th daughter. = Sir Henry Mervyn, ob. 1646. ; ch: Sir Audley Mervyn, Speaker of the House of Commons, Ieland. ob. 1676.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/fasciculusmervi00sirgoog#page/n24/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.4
2 CONT * .... JOHN MERVYN, who became the owner of the Manor and Estate of Fountel-Giffard, and (as is sstated*) married JOAN, daughter of the Lord HUNGERFORD, of Hytesbury, a statement which cannot I think, for the reasons after set for
2 CONC th, be implicitly relied on.
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT * .... Vincent's Pedigree give him two sons:-- WALTER, and Hugh ; but he must have had a third son, if the words "Nepos Walteri Maruin de Fountaine in Com. Wilts Ar." .... etc.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/fasciculusmervi00sirgoog#page/n28/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.8
2 CONT *   HUGH MERVYN, the second son, married; but Vincent's pedigree does not name his wife. It, however, shows a match between his "daughter and do-heir" (whose Christian name is not stated) with . . . . . .  "Bughton, of Cawsham" (C
2 CONC orsham).
2 CONT *   WALTER MERVYN, of Fountel-Giffard, the eldest son, married twice; his first wife JOAN, died without issue.* His second wife was MARY, daughter of John MOMPESSON, † or Mountpenson, of Bathampton, in the county of Wilts (by Isab
2 CONC el dau. and coh. of Thomas Drewe), who by his will .... etc.
2 CONT *   Walter Mervyn was possessed of the Manors of Fountel-Giffard and Farnehyll in fee, and died in possession of those estates on 12th July, 1512.* His will is dated 20th November, 2 Hen. VIII. (1510). By Mary Mompesson, he had tw
2 CONC o sons and three daughters.
2 CONT **'''	I. JOHN MERVYN of Fountel-Giffard, the eldest son, of whom hereafter.
2 CONT **	II. SIR EDMUND MERVYN, of Durford Abbey, in the county of Sussex (See "Durford Abbey Branch.")
2 CONT **	1. ALIANORA MERVYN, who was the wife of Ambrose DAUNTESEY, of West Lavington, in the co. of Wilts, by whom she had issue, represented, in the male line in 1623, by Ambrose Dauntesey, then aged 13 years.§
2 CONT **	2. A DAUGHTER (whose Christian name does not appear) married . . . . .  FITZ-JAMES, of Redlinch, in Somersetshire. II
2 CONT **	* .... etc.
2 CONT **https://archive.org/stream/fasciculusmervi00sirgoog#page/n29/mode/1up
2 CONT **Pg.9
2 CONT **	3. JANE MERVYN married Edward BURLEY, of Writtle, in the parish of Potterne co. Wilts, eldest son of Thomas Burley, of Esterton, in the same county.*
2 CONT *'''   JOHN MERVYN, the elder son''' of WALTER MERVYN and MARY MOMPESSON, '''married ELIZABETH, daughter and co-heiress''' of John GREEN, of Stotfold, co. Beds, by Edith LATIMER, † '''by whom he appears to have had three sons and 
2 CONC one daughter, and to have died during the lifetime of his father, who, 9th April, 1 Henry VIII. (1509), settled the Manor of Fountel-Giffard and Farnehyll, in trust for ELIZABETH, relict of his son JOHN MERVYN deceased, if she con
2 CONC tinued sole; with remainder to John Mervyn their son, remainder to settlor's right heir. Elizabeth Mervyn is mentioned in Inq. p. m. 4 Henry VIII. (1512), and was living at the date of her mother's will (1517).
2 CONT *'''The issue of the marriage of John Mervyn and Elizabeth Green were: --
2 CONT **	I. WILLIAM MERVYN, } ob. s.p.
2 CONT **	II. GEORGE MERVYN, } ob. s.p.
2 CONT **	III. SIR JOHN MERVYN, of Fountel-Giffard, Knt., of whom hereafter.
2 CONT **	I. ELIZABETH MERVYN, married Thomas HALL, ‡ of Bradford, in the county of Wilts, by whom she had issue (See Visit. Wilts, 1565) represented at the Visitation of Wilts 1623 by Thomas Hall, æt. 22. (Harl. Ms., No. IIII; Ms. Coll.
2 CONC  Arm "I.C, 22").
2 CONT *   SIR JOHN MERVYN, of Fountel-Giffard, Knight, succeeded his grandfather WALTER. He married twice ; his first wife being JANE, daugher of Philip BASKERVILLE, of Sherborne, in the county of Dorset (afterwards of Erdesley, in the 
2 CONC county of Hereford), and widow of William Peverell, of Bradford Peverell, in the county of Somerset.
2 CONT *  By Jane Baskerville, who was buried at Fountel, Sir John had thirteen children, five sons and eight daughters, viz. :--
2 CONT **	I. SIR JAMES MERVYN, Knt., of whom hereafter.
2 CONT **	* .... etc. ________________________________
