1 NOTE {geni:about_me} One of the most illustrious scholars of his day. Began his education at Winchester College in 1574. Then he entered Oxford University where he matriculated at New College in 1578 at the age of 19. He went on to rec
2 CONC eive his BA (1582), his MA (1586), his BD (1594), his DD (1599). He became the Warden of his college (1599-1613), Vice Chancellor (1601), Chaplain to Bishop of Winchester and Canon (1598), liscensd to preach (1604), Rector of seve
2 CONC ral parishes in Dorset and Oxford.
2 CONT
2 CONT One of the translators of the King James Authorized Version of the Bible. Specifically, he oversaw the translation of the New Testament.
