2 CONT *Pg.xiii
2 CONT *   13. WILLIAM CHURCHILL, who married MARY, eldest daughter of Richard Creuse of Wicroft Castle in Devonshire. They had three sons : Roger, who settled in Catherston, William in Corton, both in the County of Dorsetshire, and John
2 CONC , who settled in Muston in the same county. 
2 CONT *   14. ROGER CHURCHILL, married '''JANE, widow of Nicholas Meggs''', and daughter of Sir William Peverell, of Bradford, County of Yorkshire, by whom he had issue. 
2 CONT *   15. MATTHEW CHURCHILL, who married ALICE GOULD, daughter of James Gould of Dorchester, County of Dorsetshire, by whom he had issue. 
2 CONT *   .... etc. ______________________________
2 CONT *'''Notes and Queries for Somerset and Dorset ..., Volume 27
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=v_LgAAAAMAAJ&q=John+Peverell&dq=John+Peverell&hl=en&sa=X&ei=Yq9mU7vOAqLE7Aaw7YGACw&ved=0CCIQ6AEwAA
2 CONT *NO PAGE PREVIEWS Pg.185 "Certainly the Duke's great, great, great grandfather, Roger Churchill, married the widow of '''Nicholas Meggs of Bradford Peverell''' as even Sir Winston2 the old cavalier admits .... etc. _______________
