2 CONT [Elice's Tree-dad.FTW]     Birth Certificate: FC350487 no: 259     Anne Baskerville was born at All Saints, Hereford England on 11/7/1840 her parents lived in Bewell Street. She was the first child of Joseph and Eleanor Baskervill
2 CONC e.     Anne left England with her parents on the ship, Moffat, in January 1841, Anne would have been 5-1/2 months old. Her mother Ellen (Eleanor) was 3 months pregnant with her second child at the start of the voyage.     The book
2 CONC  "Log of Logs.. Volume 2...Ref. 10 AONSW reel, 1334 (held at the State Librery of NSW in Macquarie Street, Sydney) contains the Moffat's Surgeon Superintendent N. Ronald's report and it states that 4 passengers died during the tri
2 CONC p to Australia, all females: 1 adult 1 under the age of 1 year, 2 under the age of 7 years.     Our little Anne was the little baby.     The report also states the diseases on board apoplexy ( stroke) and Marasmus, which is a dise
2 CONC ase that strikes children mostly under the age of 1 year due to being undernourished.     Sadly, little Anne's exact death date and location is not known the ships report in the Log of Logs did not have that information more resea
2 CONC rch is needed.
