1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT The title Baron Ferrers of Chartley was created on 6 February 1299 for John de Ferrers, son of Robert de Ferrers, 6th Earl of Derby. The daughter of the 6th Baron Ferrers of Chartley, '''Anne''', married Walter Devereux who was su
2 CONC mmoned to parliament as Lord Ferrers in her right. Their descendants became Earls of Essex and so the peerage was also forfeited from 1601 to 1604.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anne_Ferrers,_7th_Baroness_Ferrers_of_Chartley Wikipedia]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter DEVEREUX Birth: Abt 1415 Chartley, Stafford, England Father: Walter DEVEREUX Mother: Elizabeth MERBURY User Submitted Individual Information Anne DE FERRERS Birth: 1416 Chartley, Stafford, England Death: 1472 Father: W. DE 
2 CONC FERRERS Mother: E. BELKNAP
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Anne Ferrers[3] was born in November 1438 at of Chartley, Staffordshire, England; Age 11 year, 8 months in July 1450.[4] She married Sir Walter Devereux, Lord Ferrers, son of Sir Walter Devereux, Sheriff of Herefordshire & Glouces
2 CONC tershire, Constable of Wigmore, Keeper of Leominster and Elizabeth Merbury, before 26 November 1446; They had 3 sons (Sir John, Lord Ferrers; Sir Richard; & Sir Thomas) and 2 daughters (Elizabeth, wife of Sir Richard Corbet; & Isa
2 CONC bel/Sibyl, wife of Sir James Baskerville).[5] Anne Ferrers died on 9 January 1469 at age 30.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7th Baroness Ferrer of Chartley[
