2 NOTE There were two William Herbert, 1st Earl of Pembroke. This portrait is the one of the 10th creation of the Earldom but the profile is referring to the one of the 8th creation. When a Dukedom or Earldom has no male heir to be passe
3 CONC d down to, all properties and titles revert back to the crown until such time as the head of the monarchy of the time reissues the said Dukedom or Earldom to someone.
3 CONT
3 CONT Typically when this occurs, the numbering restarts with a new creation. It is just a coincidence that the first Earl of Pembroke of both the 8th and 10th creations happened to bear the same name of William Herbert.
