1 NAME George /Herbert/ of St. Julian's
2 GIVN George
2 SURN Herbert
2 NSFX of St. Julian's
2 _MARNM Herbert
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1442
2 PLAC Of St. Julian's, Llebenydd, Monmouthshire, England
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1504
1 OCCU
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Peter Bartrum, https://cadair.aber.ac.uk/dspace/bitstream/handle/2160/5005/GODWIN%208%28A1%29_780.png?sequence=12&isAllowed=y (February 1, 2018; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''George HERBERT (Sir Knight)
2 CONT *'''Born: ABT 1442, Llebenydd, Monmouthshire, Wales
2 CONT *'''Notes: The Herbert family of St. Julian's, near Newport, was established by Sir George Herbert. George is called 'the 3rd son of William Herbert who was created Earl of Pembroke by Edward IV", in History of Parliament, however
2 CONC  it does not say by which of his 3 wives.
2 CONT *Father: William HERBERT (1º E. Pembroke)
2 CONT *Mother: Frond Verch HOESGYN
2 CONT *'''Married: Sibyl CROFT (dau. of Richard Croft of Croft Castle, Herefordshire) ABT 1475, Croft, Herefordshire, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Walter HERBERT of St. Julian (Sir)
2 CONT **2. William HERBERT
2 CONT **3. Leticce HERBERT
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/HERBERT2.htm#George HERBERT (Sir Knight)1
2 CONT *_______________________
2 CONT *MORGAN, William I (d.1569), of Tredegar, Mon.
2 CONT *1st s. of John Morgan of Tredegar by Lettice, da. of '''George Herbert of St. Julian’s'''. m. Catherine, da. of Sir Thomas Bodenham of Rotherwas, Herefs., s.p.; at least 1s. illegit.1
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/morgan-william-i-1569
2 CONT *____________________
2 CONT *'''Sir George Herbert1 
2 CONT *'''M, #52396, b. circa 1457
2 CONT *Father      Sir William Herbert, 1st Earl Pembroke, 1st Lord Herbert, Sheriff of Glamorgan & Morgannock, Chief Justice of North & South Wales b. c 1423, d. 27 Jul 1469
2 CONT *Mother     Anne Devereux1 b. c 1433, d. a 25 Jun 1486
2 CONT *'''     Sir George Herbert was born circa 1457 at of Llebenydd, Monmouthshire, England.2 He married Sibyl Croft, daughter of Sir Richard Croft, Sheriff of Herefordshire, Treasurer to Henry VII and Eleanor Cornwall, circa 1488.1
2 CONT *'''Family      Sibyl Croft b. c 1464
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S61] Unknown author, Family Group Sheets, Family History Archives, SLC.
2 CONT * 2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 391-392.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1743.htm#i52396
2 CONT *________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT *http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/HERBERT2.htm#George HERBERT (Sir Knight)1
2 CONT *''''''George HERBERT (Sir Knight)
2 CONT *''''''Born: ABT 1442, Llebenydd, Monmouthshire, Wales
2 CONT *''''''Notes: The Herbert family of St. Julian's, near Newport, was established by Sir George Herbert. George is called 'the 3rd son of William Herbert who was created Earl of Pembroke by Edward IV", in History of Parliament, howe
2 CONC ver it does not say by which of his 3 wives.
2 CONT *Father: William HERBERT (1º E. Pembroke)
2 CONT *Mother: Frond Verch HOESGYN
2 CONT *''''''Married: Sibyl CROFT (dau. of Richard Croft of Croft Castle, Herefordshire) ABT 1475, Croft, Herefordshire, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Walter HERBERT of St. Julian (Sir)
2 CONT **2. William HERBERT
2 CONT **3. Leticce HERBERT
2 CONT *______________
2 CONT *http://newsgroups.derkeiler.com/Archive/Soc/soc.genealogy.medieval/2005-08/msg00683.html
2 CONT *2B) ELEANOR CORNEWALL, born 1430/5, married 1st, Sir Hugh Mortimer, of Kyre Wyard and Martley, Worcestershire, and Tedstone Wafer, Herefordshire, heir of the Tedstone Wafer Mortimers. He was killed at Wakefield in December 1460, 
2 CONC and was buried in the Church of St. Peter, Martley. By him she had a son and a daughter. She married 2nd, Sir Richard Croft (d. 29 July 1509), of Croft Castle, Herefordshire, sheriff of Herefordshire 1471-72, 1477, 1486, MP Herefo
2 CONC rdshire 1477, and had three more sons and five more daughters. The Crofts had occupied Croft Castle since before the Conquest. Eleanor was the governess of Edward IV's sons at Ludlow Castle. She died 23 Dec. 1519, at an advanced a
2 CONC ge, and was buried with her second husband in the chapel of Croft Castle (tomb now in St. Michael church, Croft). Issue: 
2 CONT **2B1) Sir JOHN MORTIMER, of Kyre Wyard, etc., born 1450/5, sheriff of Herefordshire 1477-8, 1481-2, steward of Abberley, Worcestershire during Warwick's minority 15 Aug. 1480, Squire of the Body 1481-5, knighted 1485, Knight of t
2 CONC he Body 1485-1504, sheriff of Worcestershire 1485-6, banneret at Stoke 16 June 1487, sheriff of Herefordshire 1493-4, 1501-2, MP Worcestershire 1495. He married, after 1485, Margaret Nevill (c.1466-31 Jan. 1528), third daughter an
2 CONC d co-heiress of John Nevill, Marquess of Montagu (d. 1471) by his wife Isabel Ingaldesthorpe. They had no issue, and Margaret went on to marry Charles Brandon, have it annulled the same year (1507), and then marry in 1522, one Rob
2 CONC ert Downes, in addition to having had an illegitimate daughter. Sir John Mortimer died without issue in October 1504 (writ of d.c.e. 1 Nov. 1504). 
2 CONT **2B2) ELIZABETH MORTIMER, LADY DE LA WARR, born 1455/60, married about 1480, Sir Thomas West, 8th Lord De La Warr (c.1457- 11 Oct. 1525), and died 29 June 1502, having had issue at least one son and four daughters. 
2 CONT **2B3) Sir EDWARD CROFT, of Croft Castle, born about 1465, sheriff of Herefordshire 1505, married Joyce Scull, said to be daughter of Sir Walter Scull, of Holt Castle, Worcestershire (d. about 1472; buried at Holt Castle church), 
2 CONC by his first wife Margaret Beauchamp of Holt (d. 1456; buried at Holt Castle church), but this seems unlikely due to chronology, and she was probably his daughter by his second wife Frances Mulle (d. 1483). Sir Edward died 23 Marc
2 CONC h 1541, having had four sons and seven daughters, and was ancestor of the Crofts of Croft Castle, descendants of whom still occupy the castle today. 
2 CONT **2B4) JOHN CROFT, of Holt, Worcestershire, born 1465/70, married Elizabeth Seymour, daughter of John Seymour of Wolf Hall, Wiltshire (d. 1491), by his wife Elizabeth Darrell, and was ancestor of the Crofts of Holt. 
2 CONT **2B5) ROBERT CROFT, of Kyre Wyard, Worcestershire, married and had a sole daughter and heiress. 
2 CONT **2B6) ANN CROFT, married Sir Thomas Blount (1455- 4 June 1524), of Kinlet, Shropshire, and died 27 Sep. 1549, having had at least five sons and six daughters. 
2 CONT **2B7) ELIZABETH CROFT, married John Whittingham, of Pauntley, Gloucestershire. 
2 CONT **2B8) JOYCE CROFT, married Thomas Mill, of Avenbury, Herefordshire. 
2 CONT **2B9) JANE CROFT, married Sir Edward Darrell (1465/6- 9 Mar. 1530), of Littlecote, Witshire, and died by 1492, having had issue, two sons and two daughters. 
2 CONT **''''''2B10) SYBIL CROFT, married Sir George Herbert (c.1463/5- died after 1504), of St Julians, Monmouthshire, third son of William Herbert, Earl of Pembroke. He was knighted in 1487 at the battle of Stoke. Dame Sybil had two so
2 CONC ns and one daughter. 
2 CONT *____________________
2 CONT *http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1743.htm#i52396
2 CONT *''''''Sir George Herbert1
2 CONT *''''''M, b. circa 1457
2 CONT *Father Sir William Herbert, 1st Earl Pembroke, 1st Lord Herbert, Sheriff of Glamorgan & Morgannock, Chief Justice of North & South Wales b. c 1423, d. 27 Jul 1469 
2 CONT *Mother Anne Devereux1 b. c 1433, d. a 25 Jun 1486 
2 CONT *''''''     Sir George Herbert was born circa 1457 at of Llebenydd, Monmouthshire, England.2 He married Sibyl Croft, daughter of Sir Richard Croft, Treasurer to Henry VII and (Miss) Blount, circa 1475.1
2 CONT *''''''Family Sibyl Croft b. c 1446 
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S61] Unknown author, Family Group Sheets, SLC Archives.
2 CONT *2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 391-392.
2 CONT *____________________
2 CONT
