1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Peter Bartrum, http://cadair.aber.ac.uk/dspace/bitstream/handle/2160/5005/GODWIN%208%28A1%29_780.png?sequence=12&isAllowed=y (February 1, 2018; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Katherine Herbert1,2,3,4,5,6
2 CONT *'''F, #52399, b. circa 1459
2 CONT *Father      Sir William Herbert, 1st Earl Pembroke, 1st Lord Herbert, Sheriff of Glamorgan & Morgannock, Chief Justice of North & South Wales2,7,4,5,8 b. c 1423, d. 27 Jul 1469
2 CONT *Mother     Anne Devereux1,2,7,4,5,8 b. c 1433, d. a 25 Jun 1486
2 CONT *'''     Katherine Herbert was born circa 1459 at of Raglan, Monmouthshire, Wales.9 She married Sir George Grey, 2nd Earl of Kent, 5th Lord Grey of Ruthin, Constable of Northampton Castle, son of Sir Edmund Grey, 1st Earl of Kent,
2 CONC  4th Baron Grey of Ruthin, Lord High Treasurer and Katherine Percy, circa 1 October 1490; They had 3 sons (Sir Henry; George; & Anthony) & 1 daughter (Anne, wife of Sir John, Lord Hussey).1,2,3,4,5,6 Katherine Herbert left a will 
2 CONC on 1 December 1500; Requested burial in the church of Warden Abbey, Bedfordshire.2,4,5 Her estate was probated on 8 May 1504.2,4,5
2 CONT *'''Family      Sir George Grey, 2nd Earl of Kent, 5th Lord Grey of Ruthin, Constable of Northampton Castle d. 21 Dec 1503
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Anne Grey+10 d. bt 1 Mar 1545 - 11 Feb 1546
2 CONT **Sir Henry Grey, 14th Earl of Kent+11 b. c 1491, d. 24 Sep 1562
2 CONT **Anthony Grey+ b. c 1500
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. VII, p. 167.
2 CONT * 2.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 280-281.
2 CONT * 3.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 389.
2 CONT * 4.[S6] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry: 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 109.
2 CONT * 5.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. III, p. 132-133.
2 CONT * 6.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. III, p. 279.
2 CONT * 7.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 388-389.
2 CONT * 8.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. III, p. 278.
2 CONT * 9.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 395.
2 CONT * 10.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. VII, p. 17.
2 CONT * 11.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. VII, p. 167-169.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1744.htm#i52399
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *'''Lady Catherine Herbert1
2 CONT *'''F, #176731, d. before 8 May 1504
2 CONT *Last Edited=29 Dec 2008
2 CONT *'''     Lady Catherine Herbert was the daughter of William Herbert, 1st Earl of Pembroke and Anne Devereux.1 She married George Grey, 2nd Earl of Kent, son of Edmund Grey, 1st Earl of Kent and Lady Catherine Percy, before 1 Octob
2 CONC er 1490.1 She died before 8 May 1504.2
2 CONT *'''      From before 1 October 1490, her married name became Grey.1
2 CONT *'''Children of Lady Catherine Herbert and George Grey, 2nd Earl of Kent
2 CONT ** 1.Lady Anne Grey+2 d. fr 1 Mar 1544/45 - 11 Feb 1545/46
2 CONT ** 2.George Grey2
2 CONT ** 3.Anthony Grey+2
2 CONT ** 4.Tacy Grey+3
2 CONT ** 5.Henry Grey, 4th Earl of Kent+1 b. a 1482, d. 24 Sep 1562
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume VII, page 167. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT * 2.[S21] L. G. Pine, The New Extinct Peerage 1884-1971: Containing Extinct, Abeyant, Dormant and Suspended Peerages With Genealogies and Arms (London, U.K.: Heraldry Today, 1972), page 137. Hereinafter cited as The New Extinct Pe
2 CONC erage.
2 CONT * 3.[S37] BP2003 volume 2, page 1666. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://thepeerage.com/p17674.htm#i176731
2 CONT *_______________________
2 CONT *'''Catherine HERBERT (C. Kent)
2 CONT *'''Born: ABT 1464, Raglan, Monmouthshire, England
2 CONT *'''Died: AFT 1 Dec 1500
2 CONT *Father: William HERBERT (1º E. Pembroke)
2 CONT *Mother: Anne DEVEREUX (C. Pembroke)
2 CONT *'''Married: George GREY (2º E. Kent) 1 Oct 1490
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Henry GREY (4º E. Kent)
2 CONT **2. Anthony GREY of Brancepeth (Hon.)
2 CONT **3. Anne GREY (B. Hussey of Old Sleaford)
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/HERBERT1.htm#Catherine HERBERT (C. Kent)
2 CONT *_________________________
2 CONT *'''George Grey, 2nd Earl of Kent (1454 – 25 December 1505) was the son of Edmund Grey, 1st Earl of Kent and Lady Katherine Percy. He was the Second Earl of Kent from 1490 to 1505.
2 CONT *George Grey, 2nd Earl of Kent and 5th Baron Grey de Ruthyn, was the second son of the 1st Earl, his elder brother having died in 1480. He was made a Knight of the Bath by King Richard III in July 1483. He was a Justice of the Pea
2 CONC ce for Huntingdonshire from 1480, for Northamptonshire from 1480 and for Bedfordshire from 1483, for Buckinghamshire from 1494 and for Kent from 1496.
2 CONT *He fought for Henry VII against the Yorkist pretender Perkin Warbeck at the Battle of Stoke Field on 16 June 1487. In 1491 he was a commissioner to raise money in Bedfordshire for a war against France. On 17 June 1497, eleven yea
2 CONC rs and one day after Stoke Field he again fought in a royal army when it defeated Cornish rebels at Deptford Bridge, also known as the Battle of Blackheath.
2 CONT *He married Anne, daughter of Richard Woodville, Earl Rivers, the widow of Henry, Viscount Bourchier, sister of Elizabeth Woodville, queen to Edward IV and had one son by her, his heir Richard. She died on 30 July 1489 and was bur
2 CONC ied at Old Warden.
2 CONT *'''The following year he married Catherine, second daughter of William Herbert, Earl of Pembroke. She bore him four sons, including the future 4th Earl of Kent, and one daughter, who was to become grandmother to the 1st Earl of B
2 CONC edford. Catherine died in November 1506.
2 CONT *George died at Ampthill in December 1505. Earlier that year he had attended court on the visit of King Philip I of Castile (1504-1506) A letter from William Makefyr to Robert D'arcy and Giles Alington of 17 January 1506 reads [CR
2 CONC T190/45]: "The Earl of Kent was mounted on a sorrelled horse, harness of Venice gold with a deep fringe half a yard in length. My Lord of Kent's Coat was one bar of Gold Cloth and another crimson Velvet with a demi-mache cut off b
2 CONC y the elbow…a true soldier too, and a favourite of Henry but survived this pageant a very short time, dying within the year".
2 CONT *He married first Anne Woodville. She was a daughter of Richard Woodville, 1st Earl Rivers and Jacquetta of Luxembourg. They had a single son:
2 CONT ** Richard Grey, 3rd Earl of Kent (1481–1524).
2 CONT *Anne died in 1489. '''George secondly married Catherine Herbert, daughter of William Herbert, 1st Earl of Pembroke and Anne Devereux. They had four children:
2 CONT ** Anne Grey (1490–1545). Married John Hussey, 1st Baron Hussey of Sleaford.
2 CONT ** Henry Grey, 4th Earl of Kent (c. 1495-1562).
2 CONT ** George Grey.
2 CONT ** Anthony Grey. Paternal grandfather of Anthony Grey, 9th Earl of Kent
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Grey,_2nd_Earl_of_Kent
2 CONT *_____________________________
2 CONT *Links
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Herbert,_1st_Earl_of_Pembroke_(1468_creation)
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Grey,_4th_Earl_of_Kent
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Hussey,_1st_Baron_Hussey_of_Sleaford
2 CONT * http://www.cyberancestors.com/cummins/ps15/ps15_038.htm
2 CONT * http://histfam.familysearch.org/getperson.php?personID=I26813&tree=Nixon
2 CONT * http://www.ourfamilyhistories.org/getperson.php?personID=I28473&tree=00
2 CONT * http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/m/c/l/Donald-Mclaughlin/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-1944.html
2 CONT
2 CONT *_______________________
