1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Peter Bartrum, http://cadair.aber.ac.uk/dspace/bitstream/handle/2160/5005/GODWIN%208%28A1%29_780.png?sequence=12&isAllowed=y (February 1, 2018; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Maud Herbert''', ''Countess of Northumberland'' was born in 1448 at Pembroke, Pembrokeshire, Wales and died circa 27 July 1485. She was buried in Beverley Minster, Beverley, East Riding of Yorkshire, England, UK  [1] [2].
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: William Herbert, 1st Earl of Pembroke1 b. 1423 and Anne Devereaux1 b. between 1436 and 1442, d. 1486
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Henry Percy (1446-14899), 4th Earl of Northumberland, son of Henry Percy, 3rd Earl of Northumberland and Alianore, Lady Poynings.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Eleanor Percy, Duchess of Buckingham b. 1470, d. 13 Feb 1530.
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations:
2 CONT # [S1388] Tudor Place, online http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/index.htm, Herbert1.
2 CONT # [S1388] Tudor Place, online http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/index.htm, Herbert1, 27 Jul 1485/1495.
2 CONT #Find A Grave Memorial # 101559676.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Percy,_4th_Earl_of_Northumberland
2 CONT
2 CONT At some time between 1473 and 1476 Percy married Maud Herbert (1448 – 27 July 1485/1495), a daughter of William Herbert, 1st Earl of Pembroke (1423-1469) by his wife Anne Devereaux. They had eight children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Henry Percy, 5th Earl of Northumberland (14 January 1478 – 19 May 1527), who married Catherine Spencer.
2 CONT     Alianore Percy, Duchess of Buckingham[4] (d. 1530), wife of Edward Stafford, 3rd Duke of Buckingham.
2 CONT     Sir William Percy (d. 15 September 1540), who married firstly Agnes Constable and secondly Margaret Soothill, widow of Sir John Normanville.
2 CONT     Alan Percy (born 1479), Master of St John's College, Cambridge
2 CONT     Josceline Percy (1480–1532), who married Margaret Frost.
2 CONT     Arundel Percy (1483–1544).
2 CONT     Anne Percy, Countess of Arundel (27 July 1485 – 1552), second wife of William FitzAlan, 18th Earl of Arundel.
2 CONT     Elizabeth Percy.
