1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *''''''Magna Carta ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=wHZcIRMhSEMC&pg=PA832&lpg=PA832&dq=John+Baskerville+1408&source=bl&ots=2Ez8wp2z7Q&sig=35ePv6l94lpzveoD8KnOocGq4gs&hl=en&sa=X&ei=NiRoT9bkGKShiQLm85jqBg&ved=0CFMQ6AEwCTg8#v=onepage&q=John%20Baskervi
2 CONC lle%201408&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 832
2 CONT *   11. JOHN TUCHET, Knt., of Ashwell, Rutland, Markeaton, Derbyshire, Leegomery (in Wellington), Shropshire, etc., and Buglawton and Newhall, Cheshire, Keeper of Llandover Castle, Keeper of Brecknock Castle, son and heir, born 23
2 CONC  April 1371. He was co-heir in 1391 to his great-uncle, Nicholas Audley, Knt., 3rd Lord Audley, by which he inherited a on-third share in the Audley barony, including the Castle and lordship of Heleigh, Staffordshire, and the Cast
2 CONC le and lordship of Newport (in Camois), Pembrokeshire. He married before 1398 ELIZABETH STAFFORD, daughter of Humphrey Stafford, Knt., of Amblecote, Bramshall, and Perton, Staffordshire, by his 1st wife, Alice, daughter and heires
2 CONC s of John Grenville, Knt.  They had one son, James [5th Lord Audley], and two daughters, ''''''Margaret'''''' and Elizabeth (wife of John Baskerville, Knt.). He was in the Welsh wars against Owen Glendower. He was summoned to Parl
2 CONC iament on 20 Oct. 1403, by writ directed Johanni Tochet, and from 25 August 1404 to 26 August 1407, by writs directed Johanni Tuchet. He was frequently styled Lord Audley in offical documents, although never summoned to Parliament
2 CONC  as such. in 1404 he was at Coventry with 30 squires and 60 archers. In 1405 they received a papal indult for a portable altar. He was present at the surrender of Aberystwith in 1407. SIR JOHN TUCHET, 4th Lord Audley, died 19 Dec.
2 CONC  1408. in 1409 the king requested that his widow's brother, Humphrey Stafford the younger, deliver her son and heir to his custody. In 1436 Thomas Stawell, Knt. sued Elizabeth, late the wife of John Tuchet, Knt., her son, James Tu
2 CONC chet, Knt., her brother, John Stafford, Bishop of Bath and Wells, and William Lee for the manors of Nether Stowey, Honeybare, etc., Somerset. A verdict was delivered in favor of the defendants. She died 1446-7 (date of her IPM).
2 CONT *_______________________
2 CONT *John [Touchet], 4th Baron Audley of Heleigh
2 CONT *born
2 CONT **	23 Apr 1371
2 CONT *mar.
2 CONT **	Isabel (d. after Jun 1405)
2 CONT *children
2 CONT **	1. James Touchet, later 5th Baron Audley of Heleigh
2 CONT **''''''	1. Margaret Touchet (b. c. 1399; d. 1 Jun 1438), mar. (1) Sir John Mainwaring, and (2) Sir John Luttrell, of Dunster, co. Somerset, and had issue by both husbands
2 CONT **	2. Elizabeth Touchet (b. c. 1401 ; d. 14...), mar. John Baskerville, and had issue
2 CONT *died
2 CONT **	19 Dec 1408
2 CONT *suc. by
2 CONT **	son
2 CONT *note
2 CONT **	took part in the Welsh wars against Owen Glendower
2 CONT *http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/Audley1313.htm
2 CONT *_________________________________
2 CONT *''''''Margaret TOUCHET
2 CONT *''''''Born: ABT 1399, Nether Stowery, Somerset, England
2 CONT *''''''Died: 1 Jun 1438
