2 CONC kci.shtml
2 CONT *   (X) Adam Beckwith, son of Thomas Beckwith, married (second) Elizabeth Malebisse, widow of John Heringe. His children were all by his first wife. 
2 CONT *   (XI) Sir William Beckwith, son of Adam Beckwith, married a daughter of Sir John Baskerville, a descendant of English and French ancestry, who traced his lineage to the Emperor Charlemagne. 
2 CONT *''''''   (XII) Thomas (2) Beckwith, son of Sir William Beckwith. was of Clint, and married a daughter of William Heslerton. He died in 1495. 
2 CONT *   (XIII) John Beckwith, son of Thomas (2) Beckwith, married a daughter of John Radclift, of Mulgrave. 
2 CONT *______________________
2 CONT *''''''John Bailey Beckwith, M.D., of Smithfield, NC: A Biographical Sketch with Genealogy of the ... (1893)
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/details/johnbaileybeckw00beckgoog
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/johnbaileybeckw00beckgoog#page/n25/mode/
2 CONT *12. ADAM BECKWITH, 
2 CONT **   Of Clint, eldest son of Thomas (11) ; married Elizabeth de Malebisse, fourth year of Richard II., and thus united the two branches of the De Malebisse family, after a separation of over three hundred years. She was granddaugh
2 CONC ter of Francis Palms, Esq. (See page 47). 
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/johnbaileybeckw00beckgoog#page/n26/mode/1up
2 CONT *13. SIR WILLIAM BECKWITH, 
2 CONT **   Of Clint, Knight, eldest son of Adam (12) ; married a daughter of Sir John Baskerville. (See page 49). 
2 CONT *''''''14. SIR THOMAS BECKWITH, 
2 CONT **''''''   Of Clint, and by marriage Lord of one-third part of the manors of Filey-maston and Thorpe ; married a daughter and co-heiress of Sir William Heslerton, co-heiress to the said manors of Fileymaston and Thorpe, derived fr
2 CONC om Havisia, daughter and co-heiress of Ralph de Neville, one of the great and powerful Norman barons (see page 49). Sir Thomas died tenth year of Henry VII. ; issue, five sons, surviving. Thomas, the eldest son, and Adam, the four
2 CONC th son, died without issue. The second son, Sir William, succeeded to the title, and had issue, but his line became extinct in the next generation. Robert, the fifth son, married the daughter of Lawenthorp and was the ancestor of 
2 CONC the greater portion of the English branch of the Beckwith family. Many of his descendants have filled high and important public offices, and their names figure prominently in the military, judicial and civil annals of England. (Se
2 CONC e pages 28 to 31). 
2 CONT *15. JOHN BECKWITH, 
2 CONT **   Third son of ''''''Thomas, of Clint (14)'''''', married a daughter of Thomas Ratcliff, Esq., of Mulgrave, and had issue — two sons. Thomas, the elder, was heir to his uncle, Sir Wil- 
2 CONT **http://www.archive.org/stream/johnbaileybeckw00beckgoog#page/n27/mode/1up 
2 CONT **liam Beckwith, of Clint ; Robert, of Broxholm, the second son, succeeded his father. 
