1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Little is known about John Combe, except that he was from Astly in Worcester and settled in Stratford-upon-Avon. Chambers denies that there is any ground for connecting the Astley family with the family that held l
2 CONC and of the manor of Swanscombe, Kent until the time of Edward IV. C. C. Stopes, Shakespeare's Warwickshire Contemporaries (1907) 219. There was a Combes family at the Priory manor of Wroxall near Stratford by the middle of the 14t
2 CONC h century. J. P. Yeatman, The Gentle Shakespeare (1896) 235. The John Combe and his wife who joined the Gild of Knowle in 1460 might have been members of this family. There appears to be some connection, now untraceable, with the 
2 CONC Combes family at Stoke Newington (Middlesex) and afterwards at Hemel Hempstead (Hertfordshire), which used the same arms as those granted to the Stratford family in 1584. [VCH Stratford, p. 46; VCH Hertfordshire 2:219.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Arms of Combe: Ermine three lions passant in pale Gules.
