2 CONT --------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Plantagenet Ancestry: A Study In Colonial And Medieval Families, 2nd Edition ...  By Douglas Richardson
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=kjme027UeagC&printsec=frontcover&dq=Plantagenet+ancestry&hl=en&sa=X&ei=U8VLUYTME-boiALhroHwBw&ved=0CEcQ6AEwBA#v=onepage&q=puleston&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 265
2 CONT *11. JOAN TRUSSELL, married (as his 1st wife) EUSTACE WHITNEY, esq., of Whitney and Colepychard, Herfordshire, Knight of the Shire for Herefordshire, 1468, son and heir of Robert Whitney, Knt., of Whitney, Herefordshire, Sheriff o
2 CONC f Herefordshire, 1427-8, 1432-3, 1436-7, by Angharad, daughter of Madop ap Leuan Goch. He was born about 1411 (aged 30 in 1441) They had one son, Robert, Esq. He married (2nd) JANE CLIFFORD, daughter of Robert Clifford, Knt. They 
2 CONC allegedly had one daughter, Penelope (wife of William Abrahal). In 1457 he was sued in a plea of debt by William Forster, Citizen and tailor of London. The same year he sued John Cheyne and his wife, Perin, in a plea of land. EUST
2 CONC ACE WHITNEY, Esq., died 1481/1. ....
2 CONT *'''12. ROBERT WHITNEY, Esq., of Whitney, Herefordshire, Sheriff of Herefordshire, 1474-5, son and heir.''' He married (1st) CONSTANCE AUDLEY (or TUCHET), daughter of James Tuchet (or Audley), Knt., 5th Lord Audley (descendant of 
2 CONC King John), by his 2nd wife, Eleanor, illegitimate daughter of Edmund Holand, K.G., 4th Earl of Kent [see TUCHET 12 for her ancestry]. They had two daughters, Joan and Eleanor (wife of Thomas Vaughan, Knt., of Bredwardine). '''He 
2 CONC married (2nd) ELIZABETH VAUGHAN''', daughter of Thomas Vaughan, of Hergest, Herefordshire, by Ellen Gethin, daughter of Dafydd ap Cadwgan ap Phylip Dorddu. '''They had four sons''', James, Esq., John, Hugh, and Robert, '''and thre
2 CONC e daughters''', Eleanor (wife of John Puleston), Sibyl (wife of Roger ap Richard), and Elizabeth (wife of John Pye). He was attainted as a Yorkist by the Lancastrian Parliament in 1459. ROBERT WHITNEY, Esq., died shortly before 6 
2 CONC Oct. 1494. '''His widow Elizabeth, was living 4 May 1525'''. .... ____________________
2 CONT *'''Magna Carta Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, 2nd Edition ...  By Douglas Richardson
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=8JcbV309c5UC&printsec=frontcover&dq=Magna+Carta+ancestry:+a+study+in+colonial&hl=en&sa=X&ei=kshLUY2yHM_SigKTqYHwAg&ved=0CDwQ6AEwAQ#v=onepage&q=puleston&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 190
2 CONT *13. CONSTANCE AUDLEY (or Tuchet), married as his 1st wife) '''ROBERT WHITNEY, Esq., of Whitney, Herefordshire, Sheriff of Herefordshire, 1474-5''', son and heir of Eustace Whitney, Esq., of Whitney and Colepychard, Herefordshire 
2 CONC by his 1st wife Joan, daughter of William Trussell, Knt. They has two daughters, Joan and Eleanor (wife of Thomas Vaughan of Bredwardine). '''He married (2nd) ELIZABETH VAUGHAN''', daughter of Thomas Vaughan, of Hergest, Herefords
2 CONC hire, by Ellen Gethn, daughter of Dafydd ap Cadwgan ap Phylip Dorddu. '''They had four sons''', James, Esq., John, Hugh, and Robert, '''and three daughters''', Ellen (wife of John Puleston) Sibyl (wife of Roger ap Richard Vaughan,
2 CONC  of Hergest), and Elizabeth (wife of John Pye). ROBERT WHITNEY, Esq., died shortly before 6 Oct. 1494. '''His widow, Elizabeth, was living 4 May 1525'''. .... ________________________________
2 CONT *'''(THERE ARE SOME ERRORS IN THIS REFERENCE, THE DAU.S JOANNE & ELEANOR ATTRIBUTED TO HER, ARE LISTED IN THE BODY OF TEXT ON HER HUSBANDS ENTRY AS DAU.S OF HIS 1ST WIFE CONSTANCE, THE ELEANOR OR ELLEN WHO WAS HER DAU. MARRIED JOH
2 CONC N PULESTON.)
2 CONT *'''Elsbeth Vaughan
2 CONT *'''F, b. circa 1428, d. after 4 May 1525
2 CONT *Father Thomas Vaughan1 b. c 1400, d. 1469 
2 CONT *Mother Ellen (Ellena) Gethin1 b. c 1402 
2 CONT *'''     Elsbeth Vaughan was born circa 1428 at of Hengest, Herefordshire, England. She married Sir Robert Whitney, Sheriff of Herefordshire, son of Eustace Whitney, Esq. and Joan Trussell, circa 1451; They had 4 sons (James, Esq.
2 CONC , John, Robert, & Hugh) and 3 daughters (Ellen, wife of John Puleston; Sibyl, wife of Roger ap Richard Vaughan; & Elizabeth, wife of John Pye).2,1 Elsbeth Vaughan died after 4 May 1525.1
2 CONT *'''Family Sir Robert Whitney, Sheriff of Herefordshire b. c 1418, d. c 6 Oct 1494 
2 CONT *Children 
2 CONT **Elizabeth Whitney+3 b. c 1452, d. b 1495
2 CONT **Eleanor Whitney3 b. c 1454
2 CONT **Joanne Whitney3,2 b. c 1456
2 CONT **James Whitney+2 b. c 1465, d. 1500
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 190.
2 CONT *2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 104.
2 CONT *3.[S11588] Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 145.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1949.htm#i58579 _______________
2 CONT *James Whitney ('''Robert''', Eustace, Robert, Robert, Robert, Eustace, Eustace, Robert, ...), son of '''Robert and Elizabeth/Alice (Vaughn) Whitney''',[1] born say 1466, Whitney, Herefordshire;[2] died 31 July 1500,[3] probably W
2 CONC hitney, Herefordshire. 
2 CONT *He married, say 1490, Blanche Milbourne,[4] daughter and coheiress of Simon and Jane (Baskerville) Milbourne.[5] She was born say 1468, Tillington, Herefordshire,[6] and died after 24 March 1547/48.[7] She married secondly, as hi
2 CONC s second wife, Sir William Herbert,[8] of Troy, Monmouthshire, Wales, illegitimate son of William Herbert, 1st Earl of Pembroke (1423-1469) (Eighth Creation) and mistress Frond verch Hoesgyn,[9] born about 1448-1452[10]; died 1524
2 CONC .[11] Lady Blanche Herbert of Troy was eulogized by the Welsh bard Lewys Morgannwg. Sir William Herbert had married firstly Jane Dunn.[12] 
2 CONT *For more information, see The Ancestry of James Whitney of Whitney. 
2 CONT *From: http://wiki.whitneygen.org/wrg/index.php/Family:Whitney,_James_(s1466-1500) ____________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT the following is taken from http://wiki.whitneygen.org/wrg/index.php/Alleged_Royal_Ancestry_of_John_Whitney
2 CONT
2 CONT "Line 1.  17. Henry I, King of England , by an unknown mistress  16. Robert de Caen, 1st Earl of Gloucester (2-17), m. Maud FitzHamon  15. Christian of Gloucester, m. William FitzAlan  14. Christian FitzAlan, m. Hugh Pantulf  13. 
2 CONC Ivo Pantulf, m. <nowiki>-----</nowiki> <nowiki>-----</nowiki>  12. William Pantulf, m. Alice de Verdun  11. Rose Pantulf, m. Sir William Trussell  10. William Trussell, m. Maud Mainwaring (2-10)  9. Sir Warin Trussell, m. Maud de 
2 CONC St. Philibert (3-9)  8. Lawrence Trussell, m. Maud Charnells  7. William Trussell, m. Margery Ludlow  6. Jennet Trussell, m. Sir Eustace de Whitney  5. Sir Robert Whitney, m. (2) Elizabeth Vaughn  4. Robert Whitney, m. <nowiki>---
2 CONC --</nowiki> <nowiki>-----</nowiki>  3. Robert Whitney, m. Elizabeth verch Morgan ap William  Connection here is doubtful.  2. Thomas Whitney, m. Mary Bray  1. John1 Whitney, m.(1) Elinor <nowiki>-----</nowiki>
