2 CONT Residence: Holme Lacy, Herefordshire
2 CONT Occupation: Gentleman usher and esquire for the body to Henry VIII
2 CONT Memorial: Holme Lacy, Herefordshire: alabaster effigies of him and wife
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT On 10 May 1511 licence was granted for the marriage at St. Weonards ofJohn Scudamore, gentleman usher to Henry VIII and son of WilliamScudamore of Holm Lacy, and Sybil dau of Watkin Vaughan and stepdau ofRichard Mynors.[Richard My
2 CONC nors was John's grandfather.]
2 CONT ---
2 CONT John Scudamore, gentleman usher and esquire for the body to Henry VIII,had become rich by speculating with the property gained as receiver forthe Dissolution of the Monasteries. For example, the site and demesnelands of Abbey Dore
2 CONC  were granted to John Scudamore in 1536 under the Actof Suppression of King Henry VIII. He rebuilt Holme Lacy.
2 CONT ---
2 CONT GG grandfather of the 1st (and penultimate) Viscount Scudamore (d 1671).
2 CONT ---
2 CONT The finest tombs in St Cuthbert's, Holme Lacy are those belonging to theScudamore family including that of John Scudamore and his wife, whichdates from around 1570, depicting two alabaster effigies on a tomb-chestcarved with shiel
2 CONC ds and angels
