2 CONT *'''Sir John Scudamore1
2 CONT *M, #430302
2 CONT *Last Edited=11 Sep 2011
2 CONT *'''     Sir John Scudamore married Ursula Pakington, daughter of Sir John Pakington and Anne Rolle.1
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S37] Volume 2, page 1756. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p43031.htm#i430302 ___________________________
2 CONT *'''The House of Commons: 1660 - 1690 ; 1, Introductory survey ..., Volume 8 By Stanley T. Bindoff, John S. Roskell, Lewis Namier, Romney 
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=u_eIrJpc_T0C&pg=RA1-PA420&lpg=RA1-PA420&dq=John+Pakington+1506&source=bl&ots=DnGniuIHW2&sig=C6wRQSbrZ7pwfCBqvxcvz-279zo&hl=en&ei=4MCzTJT9AoessAOEsqiCCA&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=10&ved=
2 CONC 0CC4Q6AEwCQ#v=onepage&q=John%20Pakington%201506&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.48
2 CONT * .... By marriage Pakington was well connected: his wife's brothers-in-law included Robert Cheseman*, George Rolle* and Robert Dacres, The Privy Councillor, while his brother's father-in-law was (Sir) John Baldwin*. .... Pakingto
2 CONC n died at Hampton Lovett on 21 Aug. 1551, five days after making his will, and was buried in the chapel of St. Anne in the parish church despite his own wish to be interred in the chancel. He had made provision for his wife and hi
2 CONC s daughters, Bridget, wife of John Lyttleton*, and '''Ursula, wife of William Scudamore''', and left numerous small bequests to kinsmen, friends and charities. Pakington's sons had pre-deceased him without issue so that he was suc
2 CONC ceeded by his nephew Thomas Pakington. ________________________
2 CONT *'''Burke's genealogical and heraldic history of the peerage, baronetage and ...
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=RVggAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA1113&lpg=PA1113&dq=John+Pakington+1506&source=bl&ots=2AfD2wqeyH&sig=6Efpjzw00rvuCuXHgpkgvP_0gS0&hl=en&ei=pb6zTLHfHIOesQPA-8WOCA&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=1&ved=0CBIQ6A
2 CONC EwAA#v=onepage&q=John%20Pakington&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.942
2 CONT *.... Sir John Pakington's wife was Anne, widow of Tychbourne, and of the family of Rolle. She d. 22 Aug. 1563. His fortune was divided between his newphew, Sir Thomas Pakington, his brother, Humphrey Pakington, and his daughters,
2 CONT **'''URSULA, m. Sir John Scudamore, Knt. (OTHER SOURCE LISTS WILLIAM SCUDAMORE)
2 CONT **BRIDGET, m. Sir John Lyttleton, Knt. of Frankley ______________________________
2 CONT *Sir John Pakington (c.1477 – 21 August 1551), was Chirographer of the Court of Common Pleas, a Member of Parliament for Gloucester, and Sheriff of Herefordshire and Worcestershire. In 1529 he received an extraordinary grant from 
2 CONC Henry VIII permitting him to wear his hat ....
2 CONT *By his wife Anne, Pakington is said to have had two daughters, '''Ursula (d.1558),[24] who married William Scudamore (d.1560),[24] by whom she was the mother of Sir John Scudamore (1542–1623)''',[24][25] and Bridget, who married 
2 CONC Sir John Littleton of Frankley, Worcestershire,[3] and after his death three other husbands.[8] ....
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Pakington_(died_1551) ______________________________
2 CONT *Sir John Scudamore, (1 February 1542 – 14 April 1623) was the eldest son of '''William Scudamore (d.1560) and Ursula Pakington (d.1558), the daughter of Sir John Pakington''',[1][2] but due to his father's early death was a ward 
2 CONC of Sir James Croft ....
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Scudamore_(courtier) ______________________________
