1 OCCU Merchant
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GScid=2244840&GRid=77079482& Roger Hill Find a Grave]  The Toose family is revealed in The Visitation of Somerset (visSom, page 111), which shows Alexander Toose an
2 CONC d his unnamed first wife (uxor prima) as parents of Johannes (John) Toose. Alexander later married the widow of John Combes (relicta Johannis Combes), who was the mother by her prior husband (John Combes) of Johanna (Joan) Combes.
2 CONC  John Toose of Taunton subsequently married Joan Combes, his stepsister, and they were the parents of Margeria (Margery) Toose, who married Roger Hill. (Why this pedigree is in latin is not explained.)
2 CONT
2 CONT This Visitation actually displays the wife of Roger Hill of Taunton as Alicia, elder sister of Margeria. The Hill page (50) shows Roger's wife as "Margery d. and h. of . . . ."
2 CONT *______________
2 CONT *'''Abstracts of Somersetshire wills, etc: copied from the manuscript ..., Volume 1 By Frederick Arthur Crisp, Frederick Brown
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=PElFAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA55&lpg=PA55&dq=John+Symes+1572&source=bl&ots=b3jTjiqeRr&sig=9ws6f1BrfxWuZTkhKfR79Snq3OI&hl=en&ei=PyaJTf66HZKmsQPAzu2RDA&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=1&ved=0CBYQ6AEwADge#v
2 CONC =onepage&q=John%20Symes%201572&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 34
2 CONT *'''   ROGER HILL, of Taunton, Somerset, Merchant. Will dated Jan. 6, 1544, proved Apr. 8 1546, by Margery the relict. [7 Alen.] To the High Awter in Mawdelyn Church, 20/. Bequest for divers religious services. To an honest priest
2 CONC  to sing for my soul for 20 years, for every year L5. In alms, L100. To Alice my daughter, L100 at 21 or marriage. My sons William & Robert. My daughter Margaret. My daughter Jone, that was at Buckland, 40/. My eldest son, John Hi
2 CONC ll. Alexander Togwell, my son in law, a pack of wre cloths. Residue to Margery my wife. William Portman, Exq'r, & Alexander Togwell, Overseers, L4 each. My wife to be Extrix, & if she refuse, then William, Robert, Marg't, & Alexan
2 CONC der, my four children, to be Exors, & my wife then to have L500.
2 CONT *'''   MARGARET HILL, of Taunton, Somerset, widow. Will dated June 1, 1548, proved Feb. 14, 1550, by the Exors. [5 Bucke.] To be buried in S't Mary Magdalen, Taunton, near my husband. My son William Hill's three children. The thre
2 CONC e children of Alex. Togwell. My god-daughter Mary Portman, & to Henry Portman, L3. 6. 8 each. To my son in law, John Whyt, L3. 6. 8. To Sir John Hill & his sister Joan Hill, 10/ each. My apparell between my four daughters. My late
2 CONC  husband, Roger Hill, "whose soul Jesu pardon," by his last will constituted me his Extrix. Residue to my son Robert Hill, Exor. Sir William Portman, kn't, my son William Hill, & Alexander Togwell, my son in law, Overseers. To Joh
2 CONC n Cuffe & Will. Halley, 20/ each.
2 CONT *   A. 33. B. 50. WILLIAM HILL, of Poundsford, Somerset, Esq'r. Will dated June 6, 1592, proved Apr. 20, 1594, by Roger Hill. [31 Dixy.] My daughter Ellinor Hill, 200 marks. My daughter Luce Lawrence, L100. My son Gabriel Hill, 10
2 CONC 0 marks. My son John Hill, L100. Tho's Hill, L20. Benjamin Hill, L40. My son Alexander2. Residue to my son Roger Hill, Exor. M'r John Colles, & my son Alexander, Overseers.
2 CONT *   A. 33. JOHN HILL, of West Martyn, Wilts, esq. Will dated Apr. 27, 1602, proved Feb.2 1602-3, by Hugh Hill. [19 Bolein.] All my goods, &c., to my brother Hugh Hill, of Splat, by Taunton, esq.
2 CONT *   ROGER HILL, of Poundsford, Somerset, gent. Will dated Dec. 22, 1606, proved May 24, 1609, by W'm Hill. [42 Dorset.] To be buried at Pitminster. My father, William Hill, dec'd. My wife Mary3, an annuity of L30, & to have rooms 
2 CONC in my dwelling house at Poundsford. My son Roger Hill. My son John Hill, under 21. My daughters, Ann Shute, Frances Shaplin [Chaplin], & Elizabeth Sampson, three angells each, for three rings. My son William Hill, Exor. My friend 
2 CONC John Pyne, esq'r, & my brother Alexander Hill, gent., Overseers.
2 CONT *   ALEXANDER HILL, of Taunton, Somerset, Gent. Will dated Dec. 12, 1613, proved Jan. 28, 1613-14, by Robert Hill. [3 Lawe.] My wife Alice4. My daughter Elizabeth Hill. My daughter Godsall. My son Robert, Exor. Overseers, John Sym
2 CONC es, esq., & Thomas Strowde, gent, both of Pitminster.
2 CONT **	2. Alexander and Roger were sons by 1st wife.
2 CONT **	3. Daughter of John Hassard of Lyme.
2 CONT **	4. Daughter of John Hassard of Lyme.
2 CONT *   JOHN YOUNGE, of Coliton, Devon. Will dated Aug. 13, 1610, proved Oct. 1, 1613. [63 Fenner.] My son Walter. My wife Alice. My brother in law, John Starre, of Beare. My brother in law, Hercules Pyne. My daughter Mary Fry, & her 
2 CONC husband William Fry. My daughters, Joan Mallacke, Alice Cockeram, Ann Hill, & Jane Hill. My son in law Richard Mallacke. Roger, William, Mary, Ann, & Jane Hill, children of my son in law, William Hill, of Poundsford. Lusse & Mary 
2 CONC Hill. My sister Ellen S . . . .  My sons in law, Will. Hill & Rob't Hill.1
2 CONT *Pg. 36
2 CONT **	1 ? Roger. No son Robert is named in Visitation of Somerset.
2 CONT *________________
2 CONT *'''The Antiquary, Volume 32 edited by Edward Walford, John Charles Cox, George Latimer Apperson
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/antiquary32slsniala
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/antiquary32slsniala#page/222/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg. 222 Short Notes and Correspondence.
2 CONT *HILL OF SPAXTON.
2 CONT *  Since the notes on this family were published in the Antiquary of June last, they have been found to need correction in various ways, and the annexted tabular pedigree may be of interest as being more exact, it is believed, tha
2 CONC n previous attempts. It is founded mainly an that printed in Nichols' Collectanea (i. 409) from one compiled about 1530, and on those in Sir J. Maclean's Trigg Minor (i. 42), and Lieutenant Colonel Vivian's Visitations of Cornwall
2 CONC  (p. 227).* The chief blemish of the two latter is the identification of Robert Hill, of Spaxton (not Spraxton) with his contemporary namesake Sir Robert Hill, of Shilston, as Judge of the Common Pleas, and last husband of Joan, t
2 CONC he daughter and heir of Sir Otto de Bodrugan. This mistake was made by Foss in his Lives of the Judges, and has thus crept into the Dictionary of National Biography; so that it is well to point out (1) that Robert Hill, of Spaxton
2 CONC , died "on Sunday, on the feast of St. Mark the Evangelist," in the first year of Henry VI., i.e., on April 25, 1423, while his namesake, the judge, was acting in 1425; and (2) that Isabell Hill (Fychet) was married to Robert Hill
2 CONC  in 1396, and was still living in 1416, being mentioned in Dame Latymer's will, while Joan de Bodrugan had married the other Robert Hill before 1408, and died about 1428.
2 CONT *  The property of John Hill, of Spaxton, was, according to Sir J. Maclean, divided among the four heirs in 1529. The Waldegraves seem to have received the bulk of the Somerset property, and the Cloptons that in Devonshire and Cor
2 CONC nwall. William Clopton, however, sold his share, and thus (about 1562) the Rouses, of Devonshire, had possession of Halton and Dittesham; the last of the Clopton family at Liston seems to have been Dr. Poley Clopton, who died in 1
2 CONC 730. Robert Hussey, of Sleaford, was the second (or third) son of Sir William Hussey, Chief Justice of the King's Bench; Thomas Hussey left a daughter and heir, Elizabeth, who married Thomas Stidolph, of Mickleham in Surrey, and t
2 CONC heir son, Sir Francis, was a man of some note in the first half of the seventeenth century (Manning's Surrey, ii., 651). George Babington, who married Helen Ellis, seems to have been the second son of Sir Anthony Babington, of Det
2 CONC hick, by his second wife (Katharine Ferrers); if this be so, he must afterwards have married Anne Constable, who on his death, became the second wife of Sir Anthony Thorold. George Babington left no children.    . . . . . 
2 CONT *   Hill, of Poundisford. This family having been mentioned, an outline of their pedigree is annexed, based on the Somerset Visitation of 1623, and Le Neve's Pedigrees of the Knights (Harleian Society), the confused account in Tou
2 CONC lmin's History of Taunton (1822), and the monumental inscriptions in Lipscombe's History of Buckinghamshire (iv., 445). 
2 CONT *   (1) William Hill  'c. 1450-1510), probably a grand-son of Robert Hill, of Spaxton, settled at Taunton. He married Eleanor __ , and was succeeded by his son, 
2 CONT *'''   (2) Roger Hill, of Taunton, who married Margery , by whom he had three sons and two daughters. One son, Robert, resided at Yard, or Yard House, near Taunton ; a name suggestive of the manor of Yarde, in Combe Flory, held by
2 CONC  Robert Hill, of Spaxton, one of the few properties in the long list of his possessions {Cal. Inq. Post Alortem, iv., 70), which may have been patrimonial. This Robert Hill, of Taunton, was twice married ; one son, Hugh, is descri
2 CONC bed as " of Splot," and had a son James. Another of Roger's sons, apparently the younger, was
2 CONT *   (3) William Hill, of Poundisford, in Pitminster, a village to the south of Taunton. He also was twice married, and had fourteen children. One of these, Alexander, lived at Taunton, and his monument stated that he died December
2 CONC  14, 1613. The heir, however, was .... etc.
2 CONT *____________________________
2 CONT *  'Hill06'
2 CONT *William Hill m. Eleanor
2 CONT **''' 1. Roger Hill of Taunton Visitation (Weaver, Somerset, 1551+1575+1595, Hill) identifies Roger's wife and mother of her children as Alice Towse, Visitation (1623) shows the mother of Roger's children as a Margery so we prsume
2 CONC  that Alice Towse was Roger's 2nd wife. m1. Margery
2 CONT ***    A. William Hill of Poundsford, Somerset m1. Ann Trowbridge (dau of John Trowbridge of Clyton)
2 CONT ***     m2. Lucy Ryves (dau of John Ryves of Dorset)
2 CONT ***    B. Robert Hill of Yard near Taunton m1. Alice Clark
2 CONT ***      m2. Eleanor Martyn (dau of Sir James Martyn)
2 CONT ***    C. John Hill (dsp)
2 CONT ***    D. Margaret Hill m. Alexander Togwell
2 CONT **'''  m2. Alice Towse (dau of John Towse of Somerset (by Joan Combes), m2. Sir Thomas Grenville of Cornwall)
2 CONT *From: http://www.stirnet.com
