2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT ==Biography==Roger Hill of "Taunton" was born on January 10, 1495, at Poundisford, Taunton, Somerset, England.  His father, William Hill, had establishedthe family seat at Poundisford, just south of Taunton, in what was a deer par
2 CONC k, owned by the Bishop of Winchester, who had hunted there since early Medieval times.  The Hill family began as tenants, although they were of the gentry, landowning, social class.  Eventually, as their fortunes rose in the 15-16
2 CONC th Centuries, they came to own the entire estate, divided in two parcels for two family branches.  
2 CONT Roger Hill is said to have had two wives.  In about 1515 he first married Alice (Alicia), the older daughter of John Toose of Taunton and Johanna Combes, his wife.  They had two children:
2 CONT # Joan Hill, b. ca. 1516
2 CONT # John Hill, b. ca. 1518Both were named in their father's 1544 Will but apparently neither hadan heir as the family estate at Poundisford was inherited by Robert Hill, Roger's first-born by his 2nd wife, Margery Toose, younger sis
2 CONC terof Alice (Toose) Hill, who must have died between 1518 and 1522.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1523, Roger Hill married Margery Toose.  They had 5 children:
2 CONT # Robert Hill b: 1525 in Somerset, England
2 CONT # William Hill, b: 1527 in Poundisford, Somerset, England
2 CONT # Edward Hill b: 1528 in England
2 CONT # Margaret Hill b: 1530 in Shepton Mallet, Somerset, England
2 CONT # Alice Hill b: 1531 in Poundisford, Somerset, England Roger Hill became a wealthy wool merchant in the early 15th Century.  He was knighted in about 1540.  He wrote his Will in January 1544 and it was proven shortly after his dea
2 CONC th, on April 8, 1546.  He named hiswife, Margery, as his Executor.  --------Roger Hill and the Hill Family Wills:<ref> [http://books.google.com/books?id=PElFAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA34& Abstracts of Somersetshire wills, etc: copied from the 
2 CONC manuscript ..., Volume 1, By Frederick Arthur Crisp, Frederick Brown, 1827.  Pg. 34] </ref> : ROGER HILL, of Taunton, Somerset, Merchant. Will dated Jan. 6, 1544,proved Apr. 8 1546, by Margery the relict. [7 Alen.] To the High Awt
2 CONC er in Mawdelyn Church, 20/. Bequest for divers religious services. To an honest priest to sing for my soul for 20 years, for every year L5. In alms, L100. To Alice my daughter, L100 at 21 or marriage. My sons William & Robert. My 
2 CONC daughter Margaret. My daughter Jone, that was at Buckland, 40/. My eldest son, John Hill. Alexander Togwell, my son in law, a pack of wre cloths. Residue to Margery my wife. William Portman, Exq'r, & Alexander Togwell, Overseers, 
2 CONC L4 each. My wife to be Extrix, & if she refuse, then William, Robert, Marg't, & Alexander, my four children, to be Exors, & my wife then to have L500. : MARGARET HILL, of Taunton, Somerset, widow. Will dated June 1, 1548,proved Fe
2 CONC b. 14, 1550, by the Exors. [5 Bucke.] To be buried in S't Mary Magdalen, Taunton, near my husband. My son William Hill's three children. The three children of Alex. Togwell. My god-daughter Mary Portman, & to Henry Portman, L3. 6.
2 CONC  8 each. To my son in law, John Whyt, L3. 6. 8. To Sir John Hill & his sister Joan Hill, 10/ each. My apparellbetween my four daughters. My late husband, Roger Hill, "whose soul Jesu pardon," by his last will constituted me his Ex
2 CONC trix. Residue to myson Robert Hill, Exor. Sir William Portman, kn't, my son William Hill, & Alexander Togwell, my son in law, Overseers. To John Cuffe & Will.Halley, 20/ each. : WILLIAM HILL, of Poundsford, Somerset, Esq'r. Will d
2 CONC ated June 6, 1592, proved Apr. 20, 1594, by Roger Hill. [31 Dixy.] My daughter EllinorHill, 200 marks. My daughter Luce Lawrence, L100. My son Gabriel Hill, 100 marks. My son John Hill, L100. Tho's Hill, L20. Benjamin Hill, L40. M
2 CONC y son Alexander.<ref>2. Alexander and Roger were sons by 1st wife.</ref>  Residue to my son Roger Hill, Exor. M'r John Colles, & my sonAlexander, Overseers.  [A. 33. B. 50.]  :  JOHN HILL, of West Martyn, Wilts, esq. Will dated Ap
2 CONC r. 27, 1602, proved Feb.2 1602-3, by Hugh Hill. [19 Bolein.] All my goods, &c., to mybrother Hugh Hill, of Splat, by Taunton, esq. : ROGER HILL, of Poundsford, Somerset, gent. Will dated Dec. 22, 1606,proved May 24, 1609, by W'm H
2 CONC ill. [42 Dorset.] To be buried at Pitminster. My father, William Hill, dec'd. My wife Mary,<ref> 3. Daughter of John Hassard of Lyme. </ref> an annuity of L30, & to have rooms in my dwelling house at Poundsford. My son Roger Hill.
2 CONC  My son John Hill, under 21. My daughters, Ann Shute, Frances Shaplin [Chaplin], & Elizabeth Sampson, three angells each, for three rings. My son William Hill, Exor. My friend John Pyne, esq'r, & my brother Alexander Hill, gent., 
2 CONC Overseers. :  ALEXANDER HILL, of Taunton, Somerset, Gent. Will dated Dec. 12, 1613, proved Jan. 28, 1613-14, by Robert Hill. [3 Lawe.] My wife Alice.<ref> 4. Daughter of John Hassard of Lyme.</ref> My daughter Elizabeth Hill. My d
2 CONC aughter Godsall. My son Robert, Exor. Overseers, John Symes, esq., & Thomas Strowde, gent, both of Pitminster. :   JOHN YOUNGE, of Coliton, Devon. Will dated Aug. 13, 1610, proved Oct. 1, 1613. [63 Fenner.] My son Walter. My wife 
2 CONC Alice. My brother in law, John Starre, of Beare. My brother in law, Hercules Pyne. My daughter Mary Fry, & her husband William Fry. My daughters, Joan Mallacke, Alice Cockeram, Ann Hill, & Jane Hill. My son in law Richard Mallacke
2 CONC .Roger, William, Mary, Ann, & Jane Hill, children of my son in law, William Hill, of Poundsford. Lusse & Mary Hill. My sister Ellen S . . . . My sons in law, Will. Hill & Rob't Hill. <ref> 1 Roger.  (No son Robert is named in Visi
2 CONC tation of Somerset).</ref>
