2 TITL Orville and Wilbur Wright's relationship to Roger Hill of Taunton, b. 1-10-1495
1 NOTE  Per J. Gardner Bartlett's "John Hill of Dorchester, Mass., 1633, & 5 Generations of His Descendants" (c.1904), he was a merchant in Taunton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Birde
2 CONT Will of Roger Hill/Hyll
2 CONT January 6, 1544, Roger Hill, Marchant of Taunton. My body to rest in the church of St Magdalyn in Taunton. To the mother church of Wells 12pence. To the high altar in Mawdlyn church 20 shillings. To the high cross service and sepu
2 CONC lchre service there 6sh 8d to each. To our lady service of St James by Taunton 10 shillings and to St Katreyn's service there 10shillings. To our lady service in Lyme 3sh 4d. To the repair of the Cobbe there 3sh 4d.
2 CONT
2 CONT A priest to sing in Mawdlyn church for 20 years having 6£ a year. To Sir Robert rede my ghostly father 20 shillings (godfather). To every priest in Mawdlyn church 20d. To poor at my burial and at the month ende, 100£. To my daught
2 CONC er Alice 100£ if she be married and ruled by the advice of my executors, or else her bequests to be dividied between my sons William and Robert and my daughter Margaret. To my daughter Jone late at Buckland, 40sh. No implements of
2 CONC  my house to be removed by my wife, viz, table bourdes, cubbourds, great cheste and hangings in every chamber, hall and parlour. To John Hill his children 4£. To each godchildren 12 pence. To John Toose's children 4£. To John Hill
2 CONC  my eldest son a packe of warecloth. To Alexander Togwell my son in law the same.
2 CONT
2 CONT Residue - Margery my wife, my executrix
2 CONT Overseers William Portman Esq. sergeant at law and Alexander Togwell my son in law.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Hill Family of Poundsford in Pitminster, Somersetshire, England, ed. & compiled by J. Gardner Bartlett, Boston, 1904
2 CONT ROGER HILL of Taunton, born about 1470-1475, who beame a merchant of that place and died in 1546. His will, dated Jan. 6, 1544-5, mentions wife Margery, eldest son John; sons William and Robert; daughters Margaret and Jeane; daugh
2 CONC ter Alice not of age; and son-in-law Alexander Togwell. He married first about 1500, Alice, daughter of John Toose of Taunton; he married second about 1510 Margery _________, who died in 1550. In her will, dated June 1, 1548, she 
2 CONC mentions "the three children of my son William Hill"; children of Alexander Togwell; son-in-law John Whyte; Sir John Hill and his sister Joane; son Robert Hill; late husband Roger Hill.
