1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT * https://archive.org/stream/johnhillofdorche01bart#page/4/mode/2up
2 CONT * https://archive.org/stream/visitationofcoun00byustge#page/n64/mode/1up
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Mary probably died before Jan. 6, 1544-5 in England, as she was not mentioned in her father's will, while an otherwise unaccounted for son-in-law of his, John Whyte, (probably her husband) was. It may be they had children underage
2 CONC  who weren't mentioned. He received inheritance from his mother-in-law also, when she died 5 years later.
2 CONT ----
