2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on George Tuchet:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p4752.htm#i47519
2 CONT
2 CONT George Tuchet, 1st Earl of Castlehaven [1]
2 CONT *M, #47519, 
2 CONT *b. circa 1551, 
2 CONT *d. 20 February 1616/17
2 CONT *Last Edited=30 Dec 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT George Tuchet, 1st Earl of Castlehaven was born circa 1551.[2] He was the son of Henry Tuchet, 10th Lord Audley (of Heleigh) and Elizabeth Sneyd.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, firstly, Lucy Mervyn, daughter of Sir James Mervyn and Amy Clark, before 28 August 1584.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, Elizabeth Noel, daughter of Sir Andrew Noel and Mabel Harington, on 29 April 1611 at St. Mary le Strand, London, England.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 20 February 1616/17.2
2 CONT *He succeeded to the title of 11th Lord Audley, of Heleigh [E., 1313] on 30 December 1563, by writ.[1] 
2 CONT *He was educated in 1570 at Magdalen College, Oxford University, Oxford, Oxfordshire, England.[2] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Governor of Utrecht, in the Netherlands.[2] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Governor of Kells, County Meath in 1599.[2] 
2 CONT *He was commander of the eight companies against the Irish rebels in 1599.[2] He fought in the Battle of Kingsale on 24 December 1601, where he was wounded.[2] 
2 CONT *He was created 1st Earl of Castlehaven, co. Cork [Ireland] on 6 September 1616.[2] 
2 CONT *He was created 1st Baron Audley of Orier, co. Armagh [Ireland] on 6 September 1616.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of George Tuchet, 1st Earl of Castlehaven and Lucy Mervyn
