1 NAME Elizabeth /Ryves/
2 GIVN Elizabeth
2 SURN Ryves
2 _MARNM Berkeley
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE AFT 1641
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 1724
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * I propose that she is not the daughter of William, but either the granddaughter (dad might be https://www.geni.com/people/John-Ryves/299829558870004455??) or a cousin, thus also was not married to Arthur LEIGH
2 CONT
2 CONT ****
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Ryves-176
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT Little is known of Elizabeth Ryves, wife of Edward Berkeley of Pylle Somerset, except that she is said by Burke in Volume 1 of Commoners, in the entry for "Portman", [1] to be the daughter of John Ryves of Ranston. The identity of
2 CONC  this John Ryves is not clear, and unfortunately no marriage record of Edward and Elizabeth Berkeley has been discovered. However, in Volume 3 [2] Burke states that John Ryves of Ranston, "whose estate was sequestered in 1645", ma
2 CONC rried Mary, relict of Henry Seymer and daughter of Henry Welsted. This John Ryves is identified by Hutchins [3] as the eldest son of George Ryves and his first wife Mary Hussey, whose wife was Mary, daughter of Henry Welsted, and 
2 CONC relict of Henry Seymer of Hanford, who died in 1688. This John Ryves was said by Hutchins to have had two daughters: Elizabeth and Mary.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is an apparent difficulty in Hutchins, who lists Elizabeth Ryves daughter of John as buried at Ewerne Courtney on 23 August 1672. Edward Berkeley named his wife Elizabeth as a legatee in his Will dated 1701, [4] so that she 
2 CONC must have been alive at that date. However, it can be seen in Hutchins' pedigree that another Elizabeth Ryves, a cousin, daughter of George Ryves and his wife Mary Chaffin, is also listed as buried there on that exact date. This i
2 CONC s confirmed by the memorial stone commemorating the deaths of twins Mary and Elizabeth Ryves, daughters of George Ryves and Mary Chaffin on that date. [5] It thus seems that the burial of Elizabeth Berkeley, daughter of John Ryves
2 CONC , was erroneously conflated in the pedigree with that of her cousin Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT While the date of 1724 is plausible, no record of her burial has yet been discovered. She was named in the 1712 Will of her son Maurice Berkeley, [6] dated 19 May 1712 and proved 8 May 1717.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth married Edward Berkeley at about the time her cousin was buried, on 28 January1672/3. [7] Known children of the marriage were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (1) - bp. 20 October 1674; bur. 8 September 1677
2 CONT Edward - b. 12 and bp. 27 February 1677 ; bur. 14 October 1680
2 CONT Maurice - b. 25 September and bp. 21 October 1679
2 CONT William - b. 28 October and bp. 10 November 1681
2 CONT Mary (2) - bp. 4 September 1688 ?
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT Mary Seymer
2 CONT While there is no record for the marriage of Elizabeth and Edward Berkeley, the marriage of her mother with Henry Seymer was recorded in 1623. [8] As he died about 1641, [9] this dates her subsequent marriage with John Ryves and t
2 CONC hus the births of her daughters as after that date.
2 CONT
2 CONT In her Will, dated 1686, she left £500 to her daughter Elizabeth Berkeley, who was named an executor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Berkeley, in his 1701 Will [10] named Henry Seymer - probably Mary Seymer's great-grandson - as one of the overseers. In the 1641 Will of Henry Seymer, [9] he named as an administrator his "cousin" George Ryves of Ranston, 
2 CONC probably the father of John. Unfortunately he did not name his wife, but it is clear that the families were already connected.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1666 Will of John Ryves [11] named as trustees George Hussey (kin of his mother Mary Hussey) and Robert Seymer of Hanford (kin of his wife's first husband, Henry Seymer). Unfortunately, the Will does not mention his wife or na
2 CONC me his daughters, but it does serve as additional confirmation of their identity.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Ryves
2 CONT A number of sources, including Burke in Vol. 3 of Commoners, p. 51. [12] in the entry for "Hawker", claims her as one of the four daughters of Sir William Ryves.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Pedigree of Ryves in Hutchins [13] also claims her as a daughter of Sir William Ryves, Attorney-General for Ireland, son of John Ryves of Damory Court, and dying in 1724.
2 CONT
2 CONT The WikiTree profile for Sir William Ryves shows his daughter Elizabeth as married to Sir Arthur Leigh in 1633. She may have married twice after him. [14] These dates, given that Elizabeth Berkeley was bearing children between 167
2 CONC 4 and 1688, strongly suggest that another generation should have intervened between her and Sir William, if, in fact, she is included in his lineage. Certainly, an Elizabeth who married Sir Arthur Leigh in 1633 could not have live
2 CONC d until 1724.
2 CONT
2 CONT Childs [15] states that, in his Will, Sir William Ryves names "my wellbeloved daughter Dame Elizabeth Leigh". Childs also lists another daughter of Sir William, unnamed, as the wife of "Arthur Lee." Obviously, conflation has taken
2 CONC  place.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is fortunate that John Ryves is the more likely candidate for Elizabeth's father, as the difficulties with Sir William Ryves in that role would be hard to overcome.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT ↑ Burke, John. A genealogical and heraldic history of the commoners of Great Britain and Ireland ..., Vol. 1, p. 64. London, H. Colburn, 1835-8. p. 64
2 CONT ↑ Burke, John. A genealogical and heraldic history of the commoners of Great Britain and Ireland ..., Vol. 3, p. 496. "Ker-Seymer of Hanford" p. 496
2 CONT ↑ Hutchins, John. "The history and antiquities of the county of Dorset," Vol. 4, p. 97. FamilySearch
2 CONT ↑ Will of Edward Berkeley of Pylle, Somerset, dated 20 January 1700/1 and proved 2 July 1707. PROB 11/495/307
2 CONT ↑ Hutchin, p. 100. p. 100
2 CONT ↑ Will of Maurice Berkeley of Pill, Somerset PROB 11/558/50
2 CONT ↑ Dorset Marriages: Hanford. FindMyPast
2 CONT ↑ Ancestry Marriage Index Ancestry UK
2 CONT ↑ 9.0 9.1 Will of Henry Seymer or Seamer of Hanford, Dorset PROB 11/186/300
2 CONT ↑ Will of Edward Berkeley of Pylle, Somerset. PROB 11/495/307
2 CONT ↑ Will of John Ryves of Ranston, Dorset PROB 11/325/187
2 CONT ↑ p. 51
2 CONT ↑ Hutchins, John. "The history and antiquities of the county of Dorset," Vol. 4, p. 97. FamilySearch
2 CONT ↑ Notes and Queries. 7 (7). Oxford University Press: 144. 23 February 1889. Notes
2 CONT ↑ Childs, James Rives. Reliques of the Rives (Ryves), p. 22. Lynchburg, Va., J. P. Bell company, inc., 1929. p. 22
