1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The oldest son of 01.001 Robert Harbin I, he inherited his father's estates, becoming the second owner of Newton Surmaville  House.  He married 02.008 Bridget Drewry, the oldest daughter of his father's second wife
2 CONC .  In 1623 he was the High Sheriff of  Dorset.  He was also a student at Middle Temple in London.  In  1631 he was fined for refusing to accept the honor of    Knighthood.  He died in 1638 and is buried in the family vault in  the
2 CONC  Church of St. John the Baptist, Yeovil, Somerset.  His will,  listed in the index at Somerset House has been lost.
2 CONT
