1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT === Biography: Agnes alias Ann Coplestone (c. 1485 – 1547)
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes (Ann) Coplestone was a Devonshire heiress of high standing. The 1565 Visitation of Dorset explicitly identifies her as the daughter and heir of "John Copleston of Exeter."
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ann/Agnes Identity
2 CONT
2 CONT Historical analysis confirms that Ann and Agnes are the same individual. The different names appear to be regional or scribal variations (often recorded as Annis in Devonshire). Her identity is consistently defined by her father (
2 CONC John, 2nd son of Coplestone/Hawley) and her husband (Thomas Megges).[^3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and Migration
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Thomas Megges (Maggs), Gent., of Downham in the Isle of Ely, Cambridgeshire. This union moved the wealth and prestige of the Hawley and Tresilian lineages from the West Country to the East of England, and eventually to
2 CONC  Bradford Peverell, Dorset, through their son Nicholas.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===NGS Style Register Report
2 CONT
2 CONT First Generation
2 CONT
2 CONT John Coplestone of Exeter was born circa 1422, the son of John Coplestone and Elizabeth Hawley. He died after 1458. He married Joan [Coppleton] circa 1445.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John and Joan (Coppleton) Coplestone:
2 CONT
2 CONT i. Agnes [Ann] Coplestone. She married Thomas Megges [Maggs] of Downham.
2 CONT
2 CONT Second Generation
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes [Ann] Coplestone (John¹) was born circa 1485 and died on 25 September 1547. She married Thomas Megges, Gent., son of William Megges.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Thomas and Agnes (Coplestone) Megges:
2 CONT
2 CONT # i. Nicholas Megges, Esq., of Bradford Peverell.
2 CONT # ii. Robert Megges.
2 CONT # iii. Henry Megges.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Footnotes
