2 CONC r and heir of Thomas West, bishop of Ely. She was born in 1477, and died in 1562.
2 CONT *'''   "Their fifth child, Thomas Meggs, was born in 1507 ; he resided in Devon, Eng., Isle of Ely; he married Anne Coppleston of Exeter, daughter and heir''' of John Coppleston, gentleman. 
2 CONT *'''   "Their first child''', Nicholas Meggs, was born in 1527, and at the time of his death lived in Dunham, in the Isle of Ely ; he died Nov. 20. 1579. He married Jane Peverell, daughter and heir of William Peverell of the count
2 CONC y of Dorset, Eng.  She died in 1578. The manor of Bradford Peverell in Dorset County, Eng., was held by Nicholas Meggs, and afterwards by nine of the Meggs family. The manor house was occupied, 1896, by the Middleton family. This 
2 CONC house was in the Peverell and Meggs families from 1410 to 1610. In the great banquet hall is to be found a large illuminated window, representing the coat of arms granted to William Meggs by a patent dated June 4, 1479, in the rei
2 CONC gn of Edward the Fourth.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/recordofdescenda00meig#page/166/mode/1up
2 CONT *   "Their third child, Lawrence Meggs, born in 1551 at Bradford Peverell, county of Corset, Eng., died in 1595. He married Anne Wood of Ashridge, daughter of Richard Wood of the county of Devon, Eng.
2 CONT *   "Their fourth child, Vincent Meggs, was born in 1583, in Bradford Peverell, died Thursday, Dec. 1, 1658, at Hammonassett, Conn. His grave is marked on the maps of New Haven County, Conn. He came to America, and the first recor
2 CONC d that can be found of him is at Plymouth, Mass., in the early part of 1637.
2 CONT *   "His wife died in England. Her maiden name is unknown. He and his two sons are the progenitor of the whole Meigs family in the United States of America.
2 CONT *   "He had three sons; Vincent, born in England in 1609, and died there without issue; John, born in England, Wednesday, February 29, 1612, who came to America with his father Vincent and brother; Mark, born in England in 1614 ; 
2 CONC he died in Connecticut and had no issue.
2 CONT *   "John Meigs, 1st, spelled his name Meigs ; he died Friday, January 4, 1672, at Killingworth, Conn., and his grave is to be found in the old Hammonassett (Conn.) Cemetery. He married Thimersine Frye, daughter of William Frye, o
2 CONC f Weymouth, Eng. They were married in England in 1632, and had one child, Mary, born to them in England.
2 CONT *   " Their second child, John Meigs, 2nd, was born at Weymouth, Mass., Sunday, Feb. 29, 1640."
2 CONT *From William M. Meigs, April 10, 1900.
