2 CONC fe da. and heir of Sir Robert Tresylyan in co. Cornwall and of Emelyn his wife da. and heir of Richard Hewishe, Kt., which John was son and heir to John Copleston and of Katherine his wife da and heir to John Graase of co. Devon, 
2 CONC Gent., which John Copleston was son and heir to Adam ; and the said Thomas Megges and Ann his wife had issue, NICHOLAS, his eldest son ; Robert, second son ; Henry, third son. 
2 CONT *   NICHOLAS MEGGES of Bradford Peverell co. Dorset, Esq., eldest son and heir to Thomas, mar. Jane, da. and sole heir to William Peverell of Bradford Peverell, Gent., and by her had issue, '''LAWRENCE, his eldest son and heir. 
2 CONT *'''   LAWRENCE MEGGES of Bradford Peverell, Gent.''', eldest son and heir to Nicholas, mar. '''Ann, da. to Richard Wood of Asheridge, co. Devon, Gent., and by her hath issue,''' Percival, eldest son ; Peverell, second son ; Andre
2 CONC w, third son ; Jone and Jane.  ___________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT 11257. Anne Woods-220 was born in 1555 in Weymouth, Dorset, Eng.. She died in , Eng. She married Lawrence Meigs in 1582 in Weymouth, Dorset, Eng. He was born in 1553 in Weymouth, Dorset, Eng.. He died in 1595 in Bradford Peverel, 
2 CONC Dorset, Eng.
2 CONT
2 CONT     3/11/91, FHC, Ancestral File, WILCOXS1;
2 CONT
2 CONT     LDS Computer, Ancestral File, A:Hubbell1;
2 CONT
2 CONT Child:
2 CONT
2 CONT Vincent Meigs-214 was born about 1583 in Bradford Peverel, Dorset, Eng.. He died on 1 Dec 1658 in Madison, Middlesex, Ct. He was buried in East Guilford, Middlesex, Ct. He married Em Churchill-216 in 1606/1608 in Bradford Peverel,
2 CONC  Dorset, Eng.. [Parents]
2 CONT
2 CONT     Source:History of the Hubbell Family, Emigrated to America and settled in Weymouth,Mass. Was living in New Haven,Conn., in 1647. He afterwards removed to Guilford, and finally to what is now Killingworth,Conn.m where he died i
2 CONC n 1658.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Source:The Compedium of American Genealogy,Vol. 5 pg.774, Meigs,Vincent (ca 1583--1658) from England with his sons John and Mark, to Weymouth,Mass., ca 1639; was at New Haven,Ct. 1646, later at Milford, Guilford and what is no
2 CONC w Killingworth; m. 1606 ________ Churchill.
2 CONT
2 CONT     5/15/90-Colonial Families of USA, Vol. II, pg.511;
2 CONT
2 CONT     7/26/1990, Record of the Descendants of Vincent Meigs by Henry B. Meigs,
2 CONT
2 CONT     Mary & John, Vol. 16, p. 137;
2 CONT
2 CONT 5597. Em Churchill-216 was born in 1587 in Bradford Peverel, Dorset, Eng.. She died before 1634 in , Eng.. [Parents]
2 CONT
2 CONT     7/26/1990, Record of the Descendants of Vincent Meigs by Henry B. Meigs,
2 CONT
2 CONT     4/20/91, Note from Doug Richardson for given name;
2 CONT
2 CONT _________________________
2 CONT *'''The Family Of Brice and Cathy Alvord      By Brice Alvord
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=etmSAwAAQBAJ&pg=PA197&lpg=PA197&dq=lawrence+meigs+1553&source=bl&ots=1Hr0KPtmf5&sig=qR82oE6mg6ChWL9v5ZWtA6H5rRY&hl=en&sa=X&ei=XapcVZnkDdfioAS5woCABw&ved=0CDwQ6AEwCA#v=onepage&q=lawrence%20meigs%2
2 CONC 01553&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.197
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *50200. Nicholas Meggs was born in Bradford, Peverell, Dorset, England. He died on 12 Aug 1579 in Bradford, Peverell, Dorset, England. He married Jane Peverell.
2 CONT *50201. Jane Peverell was born in 1523 in Bradford, Dorset, England. She died on 07 Aug 1579 in Bradford, Peverell, Dorset, England.
2 CONT *Jane Peverell and Nicholas Meggs had the following child:
2 CONT **	25100.  i. '''Lawrence Meigs''', son of Nicholas Meggs and Jane Peverell was born in 1553 in Bradford, Dorset, England, He died in 1595 in Bradford, Dorset, England. '''He married Anne Woods. She was born in 1553 in Weymouth, D
2 CONC orset England. She died in 1612 in Bradford, Dorset, England.
2 CONT *50202. Richard Woods was born in 1532 in Weymouth Dorset, England. He died in 1554 in Weymouth, Dorset England. He married Izote Copplestone.
2 CONT *50203. Izote Coppletone was born in 1530 in Tamirton, Devon, England. She died in 1554 in Weymouth, Dorset, England.
2 CONT *Izote Copplestone and Richard Woods had the following child:
2 CONT **	25101. i. '''Anne Woods''', daughter of Richards Woods and Izote Copplestone '''was born in 1553 in Weymouth, Dorset, England, She died in 1612 in Bradford, Dorset, England. She married Lawrence Meigs.''' He was born in 1553 in
2 CONC  Bradford, Dorset, England. He died in 1595 in Bradford, Dorset, England.
2 CONT * .... etc. _____________________________
2 CONT *'''Record of the Descendants of Vincent Meigs: Who Came from Dorsetshire ... By Henry Benjamin Meigs
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=m640AAAAMAAJ&pg=PA7&lpg=PA7&dq=Vincent+Meigs+1658&source=bl&ots=CIqDcRXOH0&sig=7_vo_Lx2SvlWU1lfA2c4F4UXqaM&hl=en&sa=X&ei=XbpcVZ_DL9bioATb8oEw&ved=0CDcQ6AEwBA#v=onepage&q=Vincent%20Meigs%201658&f=
2 CONC false
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/recordofdescenda00meig
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/recordofdescenda00meig#page/164/mode/1up
2 CONT *      The following account with reference to the Coat of Arms of the Meigs family, was dictated by (890) M. Fayette Meigs, to a stenographer in the office of the author, Baltimore, Md., March 12, 1900. 
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *   "Their first child, Nicholas Meggs, was born in 1527, and at the time of his death lived in Dunham, in the Isle of Ely ; he died Nov. 20. 1579. He married Jane Peverell, daughter and heir of William Peverell of the county of D
2 CONC orset, Eng.  She died in 1578. The manor of Bradford Peverell in Dorset County, Eng., was held by Nicholas Meggs, and afterwards by nine of the Meggs family. The manor house was occupied, 1896, by the Middleton family. This house 
2 CONC was in the Peverell and Meggs families from 1410 to 1610. In the great banquet hall is to be found a large illuminated window, representing the coat of arms granted to William Meggs by a patent dated June 4, 1479, in the reign of 
2 CONC Edward the Fourth.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/recordofdescenda00meig#page/166/mode/1up
2 CONT *   "Their third child, '''Lawrence Meggs''', born in 1551 at Bradford Peverell, county of Corset, Eng., died in 1595. '''He married Anne Wood of Ashridge''', daughter of Richard Wood of the county of Devon, Eng.
2 CONT *   "Their fourth child, Vincent Meggs, was born in 1583, in Bradford Peverell, died Thursday, Dec. 1, 1658, at Hammonassett, Conn. His grave is marked on the maps of New Haven County, Conn. He came to America, and the first recor
2 CONC d that can be found of him is at Plymouth, Mass., in the early part of 1637.
2 CONT *   "His wife died in England. Her maiden name is unknown. He and his two sons are the progenitor of the whole Meigs family in the United States of America.
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *From William M. Meigs, April 10, 1900.
2 CONT *'''   "Bradford Peverell is situated in Dorsetshire, near the County town of Dorchester, and a family of Meggs lived there for many years, but I am abliged to say that I do not think there is a scratch of evidence known to me tha
2 CONC t the family in this country is a branch of them. .... etc. __________________________
2 CONT
