1 NAME John /Churchill/
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Churchill
2 _MARNM Churchill
1 NAME John Churchill, of Munston
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1512
2 ADDR
3 CITY Dorchester
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 15 APR 1557 AND 25 AUG 1557
2 ADDR
3 CITY Dorchester
3 STAE England
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The name is of MUSTON, not Munston and it's very easily checked anywhere. There is no such a thing as Churchill of Munston.
2 CONT Here one:
2 CONT https://freepages.rootsweb.com/~fordingtondorset/genealogy/Files2/ChurchillFamily.html
2 CONT Here another:
2 CONT http://www.piddlevalley.info/history/piddlehinton/sop/piddlehinton_chap2.php
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.John CHURCHILL of Dorchester was born about 1512 in Dorchester, Dorsetshire, England.He owned Lands in Dorset in 1549 in Dorchester, Dorsetshire, England.He died between 15 Apr 1557 and 25 Aug 1557.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of William CHURCHILL of Dorset & Mary CREUSE
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Edith BOND (daughter of William BOND of Herringston and Lutton and Elizabeth PROWZ of Bridy) about 1540 in Dorchester, Dorsetshire, England.Edith BOND was born in 1519 in Lutton, Isle of Purbeck, Dorset, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT John CHURCHILL of Dorchester and Edith BOND had three children.The eldest was:
2 CONT
2 CONT        +8       i.       William CHURCHILL of Dorchester (born in 1541).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT John Churchill, the eldest son of William, was born about 1512. John married Edith Bond. He died between 15 April 1557 and 25 August 1557. He had three children, William, Elizabeth, and John
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/churchill/1168/ Re: Josiah (Josias) Churchill (ca. 1613 - 1686) 2012 (msg from Malcolm Churchill)]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://books.google.com/books?id=IkhAAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA191&ots=ul23pCmAxi&dq=Bartholomew%20Cherchile&pg=PA192#v=onepage&q=Bartholomew%20Cherchile&f=false Collin's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT William Churchill, his Heir and Successor, who married Mary, eldest Daughter to Richard Creuse of Wicroft-Castle in the County of Devon, Esq; and by her he had three Sons, Roger of Catherston, William of Corton, and '''John''' who
2 CONC  was seated at Muston, all in the County of Dorset.
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/churchill/3023/ Re: Churchill-Bogart Connection 2005]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Churchill, the eldest son of William, was born about 1512.Note that your birth date of 1561 would have him born when his mother, Mary Creuse, was about 71, as she was born about 1490.John married Edith Bond.He died between 15
2 CONC  April 1557 and 25 August 1557.He had three children, William, Elizabeth, and John.  Younger son John had two daughters, Anne and Elizabeth.  William, born in 1541, married Missy Swayne and had six children, the first two of whom 
2 CONC were sons, William and John.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===ancestry===
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas and Grace (Tylle) Churchill had sons Thomas and William. Thomas was the eldest. He married Ibote [true spelling Iseult] Provedher and in accordance with the custom of the day assumed the whole of the Rockbeare holding upon 
2 CONC the death of his father (i.e. through Primogeniture).
2 CONT
2 CONT William was married off to Mary Creuse the eldest daughter of Richard of Wicroft (Wycroft) Castle in Devonshire. He initially removed to Colyton, Devon (pronounced like “Colliton.”) where he apparently became a minor Copyholder (a
2 CONC  renter). He then removed to Catherston Leweston in Dorset where he acquired free tenure (possibly through Richard Creuse or possibly in his own right since he was a Yeoman of Devon). He is the earliest confirmed ancestor of the D
2 CONC orset Churchills and was the progenitor of the later very prominent Churchills of Colliton and Alderholt Park.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son '''John''' acquired an interest in a manor farm called Muston in Piddlehinton Parish, Dorsetshire initially by copyhold. Muston Manor survives to this day.
