2 CONT      Sir Walter Devereux, Sheriff of Herefordshire, Constable of Builth Castle was born circa 1359 at of Bodenham, Herefordshire, England; He may be the son of Sir Walter Devereux of Bodenham instead.6 He married Agnes Crophull, d
2 CONC aughter of Sir Thomas de Crophull and Sibilla de la Bere, before 1 November 1382 at of Braunston, Cotesbach, Hemington in Lockington, & Newbold Verdun, Leicestershire, England; They had 4 son (Sir Walter, John, Richard, & Thomas) 
2 CONC and 2 daughters (Elizabeth, wife of John Milborne, Esq; & Margaret).2,7,3,4,5,6 Sir Walter Devereux, Sheriff of Herefordshire, Constable of Builth Castle died on 20 June 1401 at Battle of Pilleth, Knighton, Powys, Wales; He died 3
2 CONC  days after the battle (which occurred on the 17th of June).2,3,4,5,6 Family 	Agnes Crophull b. c 1372, d. 3 Feb 1436 Children	
