2 CONT Sir Walter Devereux, Sheriff of Herefordshire, Constable of Builth Castle was born circa 1359 at of Bodenham, Herefordshire, England."[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He may be the son of Sir Walter Devereux of Bodenham instead.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Agnes Crophull, daughter of Sir Thomas de Crophull and Sibilla de la Bere, before 1 November 1382 at of Braunston, Cotesbach, Hemington in Lockington, & Newbold Verdun, Leicestershire, England; They had 4 son (Sir Walte
2 CONC r, John, Richard, & Thomas) and 2 daughters (Elizabeth, wife of John Milborne, Esq; & Margaret).[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Walter Devereux, Sheriff of Herefordshire, Constable of Builth Castle died on 20 June 1401 at Battle of Pilleth, Knighton, Powys, Wales; He died 3 days after the battle (which occurred on the 17th of June).[4] 
