1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William de Ferrers, 6th Baron Ferrers of Chartley (1412–1450)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William de Ferrers - was born in 1412 and died in 1450 . He was the son of Sir Edmund de Ferrers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William married Elizabeth Bealknap.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: (Quick Family Chart)
2 CONT
2 CONT i. 	Agnes Ferrers was born in 1438 and died on 9 Jan 1468/1469 . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes married Sir Walter Devereux before 1446. Sir Walter was born in 1432. He died on 22 Aug 1485 in Bosworth Field .
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes - married by 1446 (thus Anne was at most 7 years of age at her marriage - Sir Walter was six years older). 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The name Ferrers means in French 'to bind with iron' or 'to shoe a horse'. Ferrières in Normandy was known for its iron-working industry. The Ferrers coat of arms was black horseshoes on a silver background.
2 CONT
2 CONT i.  Henry de Ferrers was born about 1036, lived in Ferriers, Normandy, France and died in 1088 while living in Castle Tutbury, Staffordshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Henry de Ferrers - was born about 1036, lived in Ferriers, Normandy, France and died in 1088 while living in Castle Tutbury, Staffordshire, England . He was the son of Wachelinde de Ferrers.  Henry married Bertha Roberts about 
2 CONC 1061 while living in Normandy, France. Bertha was born about 1040, lived in Gostenois, Normandy, France. She died in Darley, Derbyshire, England . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry - is widely believed to have fought at the Battle of Hastings, 1066, as his name appears on various versions of the Battle Abbey Roll, though it is impossible to be certain. He was a Domesday Commissioner, 1086, and held som
2 CONC e 210 lordships and manors at the time of the Survey, mostly in co. Derby, but also in 14 other counties, by gift of William the Conqueror. Founded a priory of Benedictine monks near Tutbury, Staffs. He married Bertha. He was buri
2 CONC ed at Tutbury  
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:  i.  Robert de Ferrers was born about 1062, lived in Derbyshire, England and died in 1139 . See #3. below.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----- Third Generation <nowiki>-----</nowiki>  3. Robert de Ferrers - was born about 1062, lived in Derbyshire, England and died in 1139 . He was the son of Henry de Ferrers and Bertha Roberts.  Robert married Hawise de Vitre abou
2 CONC t 1087 while living in Brittany, France. Hawise was born about 1069, lived in Vitre, Brittany, France. She is the daughter of Seigneur Andre de Vitre and Agnes de Mortaigne. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert - succeeded to the greater part of his father's possessions in England. For his services to King Stephen at the battle of the Standard in 1138, he was created Earl of Derby during that year, but died the following year, 113
2 CONC 9. Children:   i.  Robert de Ferrers was born about 1090, lived in Derbyshire, England and died in 1141 in Merevale, Warwickshire, England . See #4. below.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----- Fourth Generation <nowiki>-----</nowiki>  4. Robert de Ferrers - also known as: Ferrieres - was born about 1090, lived in Derbyshire, England and died in 1141 in Merevale, Warwickshire, England . He was the son of Robert de 
2 CONC Ferrers and Hawise de Vitre.  Robert married Margaret Peverel about 1135 while living in Nottinghamshire, England. Margaret was born about 1114, lived in Nottingham, Nottinghamshire, England. She is the daughter of William "the Yo
2 CONC unger" Peverel and Avice de Lancaster. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert - founded the Abbeys of Merevale, co. Warwick, and Darley, near Derby. Married Margaret, daughter and heiress of William Peverel of Nottingham, the younger. William de Peverel's father, of the same name, is said to have bee
2 CONC n an illegitimate son of William the Conqueror. Robert de Ferrieres died before 1160 and was buried at Merevale Abbey. His father: Children:   i.  William de Ferrers was born about 1140, lived in Oakham Rutlandshire, England and d
2 CONC ied in 1190 in Acre, Palestine .
2 CONT
2 CONT Fifth Generation <nowiki>-----</nowiki>  5. William de Ferrers - also known as: William - was born about 1140, lived in Oakham Rutlandshire, England and died in 1190 in Acre, Palestine . He was the son of Robert de Ferrers and Mar
2 CONC garet Peverel.  William married Sibilla de Braose about 1173/1174 while living in Sussex, England. Sibilla was born in 1150, lived in Bramber, Sussex, England. She was the daughter of William de Braose II and Bertha de Gloucester.
2 CONC  She died in 1227 in England . 
2 CONT   Then William married Goda de Toni in 1162. Goda was born about 1140 in Eggington, Derbyshire, England. She is the daughter of Robert Toni. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William - 3rd Earl of Derby, or Earl of Ferrieres. Rebelled against King Henry II in 1173 and was imprisoned at Caen. He married Sibyl, daughter of William de Braose, Lord of Bramber. He died on Crusade at the siege of Acre, in Pa
2 CONC lestine, in 1190. Children with Sibilla de Braose i.  William de Ferrers was born in 1168 and died in 1247 . See #6. below.   ii.  Milisent de Ferrers was born about 1165.  Milisent married Roger de Mortimer. Roger was born about 
2 CONC 1155, lived in Wigmore, Herefordshire, England. He was the son of Hugh de Mortimer and Maud de Meschines. He died on 24 Jun 1214 in Wigmore, Herefordshire, England . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with Goda de Toni   iii.  Isabel de Ferrers was born in 1172, lived in Oakham, Rutlandshire, England and died before 31 May 1252 .  Isabel married Roger de Mortimer about 1190 while living in Rutlandshire, England. Roger 
2 CONC was born about 1155, lived in Wigmore, Herefordshire, England. He was the son of Hugh de Mortimer and Maud de Meschines. He died on 24 Jun 1214 in Wigmore, Herefordshire, England . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel - Heiress of Lechlade and Oakham. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Also married Piers Fitzherbert about 1215. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----- Sixth Generation <nowiki>-----</nowiki>  6. William de Ferrers - was born in 1168 and died in 1247 . He was the son of William de Ferrers and Sibilla de Braose.  William married Lady Agnes of Chester in 1192. Lady Agnes was 
2 CONC born in 1174. She was the daughter of Earl of Chester Hugh of Kevelioc de Meschines and Bertrade de Montfort. She died in 1247 . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Agnes - - Lady of Chartley. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William - - 4th Earl of Derby, or Earl of Ferrieres. Children: (Quick Family Chart)  i.  William de Ferrers was born about 1200 and died in 1254 in Evington and was buried in Merevale Abbey . 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----- Seventh Generation <nowiki>-----</nowiki>  7. William de Ferrers - was born about 1200 and died in 1254 in Evington and was buried in Merevale Abbey . He was the son of William de Ferrers and Lady Agnes of Chester. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William - 5th Earl of Derby. Accompanied the King to France in 1230. Married c. 1219 Sibyl, 3rd daughter of William (the Marshal), Earl of Pembroke, by whom he had seven daughters, but no son. Married secondly c. 1238 Margaret, fi
2 CONC rst daughter and coheir of Roger de Quincy, Earl of Winchester. Invested with the Earldom at Westmoreland, 1247. Children:  i.  Robert de Ferrers was born about 1239 and died in 1279 . See #8. below.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----- Eighth Generation <nowiki>-----</nowiki>  8. Robert de Ferrers - was born about 1239 and died in 1279 . He was the son of William de Ferrers.  Robert married Eleanor de Bohun on 26 Jun 1269. Eleanor was born about 1225. She 
2 CONC was the daughter of Humphrey de Bohun and Maud de Lusignan. She died on 20 Feb 1312/1313 . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert - 6th and last Earl of Derby. Succeeded his father as Earl of Derby, 1254. He rebelled against King Henry III and seized three of Prince Edward's castles in 1263. He was imprisoned at the Tower of London and at Windsor Cast
2 CONC le. In 1266 his lands were forfeited to the King's son, Edmund, and his Earldom effectively forfeited. He could have recovered his lands and, presumably, the Earldom by payment of £50,000, but was unable to raise the money. His so
2 CONC n, John, in 1298 tried to borrow the money, but was prohibited by the King. Robert married c. 1249 Mary, the King's niece and daughter of Hugue XI, Count of La Marche and Angoulême, but had no male issue. He married secondly in 12
2 CONC 69 Alianore, daughter of Sir Humphrey de Bohun of Kimbolton, son and heir apparent of Humphrey, Earl of Hereford and Essex Children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i.  Sir John de Ferrers was born in 1271 in Cardiff and died about 1312 in Gascony . See #9. below.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----- Ninth Generation <nowiki>-----</nowiki>  9. Sir John de Ferrers - was born in 1271 in Cardiff and died about 1312 in Gascony . He was the son of Robert de Ferrers and Eleanor de Bohun.  Sir John married Hawise de Muscegros. 
2 CONC Hawise was born on 21 Dec 1276. She was the daughter of Robert de Muscegros. She died about Jun 1340 . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John - of Chartley, Southoe and Keyston (Hunts), and Bugbrooke (Northants) (apparently died of poison). He was created Lord Ferrers sometime between 1297 and 1311. Children: i.  Robert de Ferrers was born on 25 Mar 1309 in Cha
2 CONC rtley, Straffordshire, England and died on 28 Aug 1350 . See #10. below.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----- Tenth Generation <nowiki>-----</nowiki>  10. Robert de Ferrers - was born on 25 Mar 1309 in Chartley, Straffordshire, England and died on 28 Aug 1350 . He was the son of Sir John de Ferrers and Hawise de Muscegros.  Robert m
2 CONC arried Aeneas de Bohun. Aeneas was born about 1314 in Caldecot, Northampton, England. She was the daughter of Humphrey de Bohun VIII and Princess Elizabeth of England. She died about 1343 . Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT i.  Baron Robert de Ferrers died on 31 Dec 1380 . See #11. below.   ii.  Baron John de Ferrers was born about 1331 in Southhoe, Huntingtonshire, England and died on 3 Apr 1367 in Battle of Najera . See #12. below.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----- Eleventh Generation <nowiki>-----</nowiki>  11. Baron Robert de Ferrers - died on 31 Dec 1380 . He was the son of Robert de Ferrers and Aeneas de Bohun.  Baron Robert married Elizabeth le Boteler. Elizabeth was born about 13
2 CONC 45. She was the daughter of Baron William le Boteler IV and Joan de Sudeley. She died on 19 Jun 1410 . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Baron Robert - 8th Earl of Hereford. Children: (Quick Family Chart)  i.  Lord Robert Ferrers was born about 1370, lived in Chartley,Stafford,England and died before 29 Nov 1396 .   ii.  William Ferrers 
2 CONT
2 CONT William - - Earl of Northampton. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Elizabeth /de Bedlesmere/  
2 CONT
2 CONT 12. Baron John de Ferrers - was born about 1331 in Southhoe, Huntingtonshire, England and died on 3 Apr 1367 in Battle of Najera . He was the son of Robert de Ferrers and Aeneas de Bohun.  Baron John married Elizabeth de Stafford.
2 CONC  Elizabeth was born before 1342. She was the daughter of Sir Ralph de Stafford and Margaret de Audley. She died on 7 Aug 1375 . Children:  i.  Sir Robert de Ferrers was born in 1357/1359 and died in 1412/1413 and was buried in Mer
2 CONC evale Abbey .  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----- Twelth Generation <nowiki>-----</nowiki>  13. Lord Robert Ferrers - was born about 1370, lived in Chartley,Stafford,England and died before 29 Nov 1396 . He was the son of Baron Robert de Ferrers and Elizabeth le Boteler.  L
2 CONC ord Robert married Countess Joan de Beaufort about 1392. Countess Joan was born on 29 Jan 1374/1375 in Beaufort Castle, France. She was the daughter of Duke John of Gaunt and Catherine de Roet. She died on 13 Nov 1440 in Howden, Y
2 CONC orkshire, England . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Countess Joan - - Countess of Wes 
2 CONT
2 CONT The name Beaufort refers to a castle in Champagne, France (now Montmorency-Beaufort). 
2 CONT
2 CONT email from William Skyvington 
2 CONT
2 CONT In your website, you indicate that Joan de Beaufort 1375-1440 was born in a castle in the French province of Anjou. You are referring, no doubt, to the place that is now named Beaufort-en-Vallée, but your information is incorrect.
2 CONC  The Beaufort Castle that was the birthplace of the children of John of Gaunt was located in the province of Champagne, in the vicinity of Troyes, at a place that is now named Montmorency-Beaufort.   Children: (Quick Family Chart)
2 CONC   i.  Elizabeth Ferrers was born about 1393, lived in Chartley, Staffordshire, England and died about 1434 in York, Yorkshire, England .  Elizabeth married John Greystoke on 28 Oct 1407. John was born in 1389 in Owesley, Yorkshire
2 CONC , England. He died on 8 Aug 1436 in Northamptonshire, England and was buried in Greystoke, Northumberland, England . 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii.  Mary de Ferrers was born about 1394, lived in Obersley, Warwickshire, England and died on 25 Jan 1457/1458 .  
2 CONT
2 CONT 14. Sir Robert de Ferrers - was born in 1357/1359 and died in 1412/1413 and was buried in Merevale Abbey . He was the son of Baron John de Ferrers and Elizabeth de Stafford.  Sir Robert married Margaret le Depenser. Margaret was b
2 CONC orn about 1360. Children: i.  Sir Edmund de Ferrers was born before 1387 and died in 1435 . 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----- Thirteenth Generation <nowiki>-----</nowiki>  15. Sir Edmund de Ferrers - was born before 1387 and died in 1435 . He was the son of Sir Robert de Ferrers and Margaret le Depenser. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:   i.  Sir William de Ferrers was born in 1412 and died in 1450 . 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----- Fourteenth Generation <nowiki>-----</nowiki>  16. Sir William de Ferrers - was born in 1412 and died in 1450 . He was the son of Sir Edmund de Ferrers.  Sir William married Elizabeth Bealknap. Children:  i.  Agnes Ferrers wa
2 CONC s born in 1438 and died on 9 Jan 1468/1469 .  Agnes married Sir Walter Devereux before 1446. Sir Walter was born in 1432. He died on 22 Aug 1485 in Bosworth Field . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes - married by 1446 (thus Anne was at most 7 years of age at her marriage - Sir Walter was six years older).  
2 CONT
