2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p49694.htm#i496932 _________________________________
2 CONT *Sir Thomas Leighton (c.1530–1610) was an English soldier and politician. He served as the Governor of Guernsey and Jersey from 1570 to 1609. Although the ancestral link still awaits confirmation,[1][2] there is evidence that Sir 
2 CONC Thomas and his wife are common ancestors of the current Duke and Duchess of Cambridge; being 12th great-grandparents of William, and 11th great-grandparents of Catherine, which would make them 12th cousins, once removed.[3][4][5]
2 CONT *Sir Thomas was knighted in 1579 during the reigns of Elizabeth I and James I. He was from Feckenham, Worcestershire, England, born to '''John Leighton of Wattlesborough and Joyce Sutton''', daughter of Edward Sutton, 2nd Baron Du
2 CONC dley.[6]
2 CONT *Leighton was unpopular as governor. He developed the defensive capabilities of Castle Cornet, but to do so he imposed heavy taxes on the islanders.[4] In 1588 he was sent as a diplomat to Henry III of France, and then served at t
2 CONC he camp at Tilbury in the defensive moves against the Spanish Armada. For some years from 1595 he employed Thomas Cartwright as chaplain.[6]
2 CONT *Leighton served as Member of Parliament for Worcestershire in 1601. He died in Guernsey.[6]
2 CONT *Leighton married Elizabeth Knollys (cousin once removed of Elizabeth I) in 1578. They had two daughters, Elizabeth and Anne Leighton, and one son, the father's namesake Thomas Leighton (born 1584), who married Mary, daughter of E
2 CONC dward la Zouche, 11th Baron Zouche.[6]
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Leighton_(Governor) ____________________
2 CONT *LEIGHTON, Sir Thomas (c.1535-c.1611), of Feckenham, Worcs. and Guernsey.
2 CONT *b. c.1555, 2nd s. '''of John Leighton of Wattlesborough''', and bro. of Edward. m. 1578, Elizabeth, da. of Sir Francis Knollys, 1s, 1da. Kntd. 1579.1
2 CONT *http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/leighton-sir-thomas-1535-1611 ___________________
2 CONT *Sir Edward Leighton (by 1525-1593) was an English politician.
2 CONT *He was the eldest son of '''John Leighton of Wattlesborough Castle, Shropshire''', and admitted in 1541 to Gray's Inn to study law. He succeeded his father in 1532.
2 CONT *He was appointed High Sheriff of Montgomeryshire for 1549 and 1591 and High Sheriff of Shropshire for 1567 and 1587. He was elected a Member (MP) of the Parliament of England for Shropshire in October 1553 and 1563. He was knight
2 CONC ed in 1591.
2 CONT *He married twice: firstly Elizabeth née Edwards, the widow of a Mr. Meverell and secondly Anne, the daughter of Paul Darrell of Lillingstone Dayrell, Buckinghamshire, with whom he had 4 sons and 3 daughters.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edward_Leighton_(died_1593) _________________________
2 CONT *LEIGHTON, Edward (by 1525-93), of Wattlesborough, Salop.
2 CONT *b. by 1525, 1st s. of '''John Leighton of Wattlesborough by Joyce''', da. of Edward Sutton, 2nd Lord Dudley; bro. of Sir Thomas†. educ. G. Inn, adm. 1541. m. (1) Elizabeth, da. of one Edwards, wid. of one Meverell; (2) by 1553, A
2 CONC nne, da. of Paul Darrell of Lillingstone Dayrell, Bucks., 4s. inc. Thomas† 3da. suc. fa. 28 Feb. 1532. Kntd. 1591.1
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1509-1558/member/leighton-edward-1525-93 ________________________
2 CONT *LEIGHTON, Edward (by 1525-93), of Wattlesborough, Salop.
2 CONT *b. by 1525, 1st s. of '''John Leighton of Wattlesborough by Joyce''', da. of Edward Sutton, 2nd Lord Dudley; bro. of Sir Thomas. educ. G. Inn 1541. m. (1) Elizabeth, da. of one Edwardes, wid. of one Meverell; (2) by 1553 Anne, da
2 CONC . of Paul Darrell of Lillingstone Dayrell, Bucks., 4s. inc. Thomas 3da. suc. fa. 28 Feb. 1532. Kntd. 1591.1
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/leighton-edward-1525-93 _____________________
2 CONT *Sir Edward Sutton, 2nd Baron Dudley,[1] and the 6th Baron Sutton, (c. 1460 – 31 January 1531) was a Member of Parliament (MP) of the Parliament of England from 12 August 1492 to 3 November 1529. He was one of the English noblemen
2 CONC  elected as Knight of the Garter (KG) in the beginning of King Henry VIII's reign.[2] He was chamberlain to Princess Mary (later Queen Mary I) from 1525 to 1528.[3]
2 CONT *Edward Sutton was the son of Sir Edmund Sutton and Joyce de Tiptoft,[1] daughter of Sir John Tiptoft, 1st Baron Tiptoft. In right of his wife Joyce, Edmund Sutton became Baron Tibetot and Baron Cherleton, and thus co-heir to the 
2 CONC Powis inheritance.
2 CONT *Edward married Cecily Willoughby,[1] granddaughter of Katherine Neville, Duchess of Norfolk, by whom he had:[2]
2 CONT **1. John Sutton, 3rd Baron Dudley, his successor.
2 CONT **2. Geoffrey Sutton, who married Eleanor Talbot, by whom he was father of Thomas Sutton of Russels.
2 CONT **3. Thomas Sutton.
2 CONT **4. Arthur Dudley, prebendary in Lichfield Cathedral (see Chad of Mercia#Cult and Relics).
2 CONT **5. Elizabeth Sutton, who married Thomas Butler, son of Piers Butler, 8th Earl of Ormond.
2 CONT **6. Alice Sutton.
2 CONT **7. Eleanor Sutton, who married firstly Charles Somerset, 1st Earl of Worcester, and secondly Leonard Grey, 1st Viscount Grane.
2 CONT **8. '''Joyce Sutton, who married Sir John Leighton of Wattlesborough. Their son''', Sir Thomas Leighton, was Governor of Jersey and married Elizabeth Knollys, daughter of Catherine, Lady Knollys and sister of Lettice Knollys.
2 CONT **9. Jane (Joan, Johanna) Sutton, who married Sir Thomas Fiennes, son of Thomas, Baron Dacre. Their son Thomas Fiennes, 9th Baron Dacre was executed for murder in 1541.
2 CONT **10. Margaret Sutton, who married John Grey, 2nd Baron Grey of Powis. Their son was Edward Grey, 3rd Baron Grey of Powis, to whom his uncle John, Lord Dudley, sold the Tiptoft-Dudley portion of Powis Castle.
2 CONT **11. Catherine Sutton, who married Sir George Gresley of Drakelow.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edward_Sutton,_2nd_Baron_Dudley __________________________
2 CONT *'''Joyce SUTTON
2 CONT *Born: 1492
2 CONT *Died: AFT 1586
2 CONT *Father: Edward SUTTON (2º B. Sutton of Dudley)
2 CONT *Mother: Cecily WILLOUGHBY (B. Sutton of Dudley)
2 CONT *'''Married 1: John LEIGHTON of Watlesburgh 1508, Feckenham, Worsestershire, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Thomas LEIGHTON (Sir Gov. of Jersey) (d. ABT 1611, S.P.) (m. Elizabeth Knollys)
2 CONT *Married 2: Richard LEE AFT 28 Feb 1531/1532
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/SUTTON.htm#Joyce SUTTON2 _________________
2 CONT *Sir Edward Sutton, 2nd Lord Dudley & Lord Powys1,2,3,4,5,6 
2 CONT *M, #46807, b. circa 1460, d. 31 January 1532
2 CONT *Father      Sir Edmund Sutton7,8,9 b. c 1435, d. bt 6 Jul 1483 - 1486
2 CONT *Mother     Joyce Tiptoft10,7,8,9 d. b 1472
2 CONT *     Sir Edward Sutton, 2nd Lord Dudley & Lord Powys was born circa 1460; Age 26 in March 1486, but age 28 or 30 in 1487.10,2,5,6 He married Cecily Willoughby, daughter of Sir William Willoughby and Joan Strangeways, circa 1480; 
2 CONC They had 7 sons (Sir John, 3rd Lord Dudley; Edward; Thomas; Arthur, a cleric; George; Geoffrey; & William) & 8 daughters (Margaret, wife of John, Lord Grey of Powis, & of Robert Sutton; Eleanor, wife of Sir Charles Somerset, 1st E
2 CONC arl of Worcester, Lord Herbert; Jane, wife of Thomas Fiennes; Katherine, wife of Sir George Gresley; Elizabeth, wife of Sir John Huddleston, & of Thomas Boteler; '''Joyce, wife of John Leighton'''; Dorothy; & Constance).11,12,2,3,
2 CONC 4,5,6 Sir Edward Sutton, 2nd Lord Dudley & Lord Powys died on 31 January 1532; About age 72.11,2,5,6
2 CONT *Family      Cecily Willoughby d. a 14 Nov 1541
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Margaret Sutton+13,14 b. c 1486, d. b 11 May 1525
2 CONT **Eleanor Sutton15,2,4,5,6 b. c 1490, d. b 24 May 1532
2 CONT **Sir John Dudley, 3rd Lord Dudley+11,2,5 b. c 1496
2 CONT **Elizabeth Sutton+16,3,5,6 b. c 1498, d. a 1532
2 CONT **Katherine Dudley16,2 b. c 1505
