1 OCCU Married before Dec 15, 1503 in Chartley Lodge, Stafford, England
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Yorkist
2 CONT
2 CONT In May 1501, his father died and Walter succeeded him as the 9th Baron Ferrers of Chartley. On 7 December 1509 he had special livery, although still under age, without proof of age or payment of relief for his father’s lands.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was created High Steward of Tamworth on 20 November 1510, and joint Constable of Warwick Castle on 15 Feb 1511 with Sir Edward Belknapp. He was also joint Steward of the manor, town, or borough of Warwick. On 27 January 1513, h
2 CONC e was appointed Keeper of Netherwood Park; Councillor and Royal Commissioner of Wales and the Marches on 1 August 1513; and High Steward of Hereford in 1514.
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter Devereux served with distinction in the War of the League of Cambrai (1508–1516) and the Italian War of 1521-1526. He was Captain in the English Army in France 24 August 1523. For his gallantry in the sea fight off Conquet 
2 CONC (Brittany) he was honored on 13 July 1523 with his creation as a Knight of the Garter  by Henry VIII of England alongside diplomat Thomas Boleyn, later Earl of Wiltshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was appointed Bailiff of Sutton Coldfield (11 February 1525); Steward of the Household and Councillor to Mary, Princess of Wales (1525); Chief Justice of South Wales (22 Aug. 1525); High Steward of Builth (22 Aug. 1525); and Ch
2 CONC amberlain of South Wales, Carmarthen and Cardigan (25 May 1526).
2 CONT
2 CONT In the late 1520s, Devereux came into increasing conflict with Welsh magnate Rhys ap Gruffydd following King Henry's grants of major power to him in Wales as described above. This reached a head when Rhys, with a gang of armed sup
2 CONC porters, threatened Ferrers with a knife in 1529. The two men were allowed to air their grievances, but Rhys's family continued to stir up trouble. Eventually Rhys was charged with treason, convicted and executed. The consolidatio
2 CONC n of Devereux's position in Wales helped prepare the way for the reformation.
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter served as Custos Rotulorum of Cardiganshire from 1543 to his death. He was with King Henry VIII when Boulogne was taken on 18 September 1544.
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter Devereux was created Viscount Hereford on 2 February 1550. He was appointed Privy Councillor (1550); joint Lord Justice and Lieutenant of Stafford (4 May 1551); and Justice of the Peace for Stafford, Worcester and Salop (18
2 CONC  February 1554).[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter Devereux died on 17 September 1558] and was buried at Stowe-by-Chartley, Staffordshire. _______________________________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Sir Walter Devereux, 1st Viscount Hereford1
2 CONT *'''M, #67730, b. 1491, d. 17 September 1558
2 CONT *Father      John Devereux, 3rd Lord Ferrers b. c 1464, d. 3 May 1501 or 7 May 1501
2 CONT *Mother     Cicely Bourchier b. c 1468
2 CONT *'''     Sir Walter Devereux, 1st Viscount Hereford was born in 1491 at of Castle Bromwich, Warwickshire, England. He married Mary Grey, daughter of Sir Thomas Grey, 1st Marquess of Dorset, Lord Ferrers, Constable of the Tower of 
2 CONC London & Ruthland Castle and Cecily Bonville, before 3 May 1501.2 Sir Walter Devereux, 1st Viscount Hereford married Margaret Garneys, daughter of Robert Garneys and Ann Bacon, after 22 February 1538; His 2nd wife.3 Sir Walter Dev
2 CONC ereux, 1st Viscount Hereford died on 17 September 1558.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family 1      Mary Grey b. c 1494, d. 22 Feb 1538
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Sir Richard Devereux+4 b. c 1516, d. 13 Oct 1547
2 CONT **Sir William Devereux+5 b. c 1525, d. b 2 Nov 1579
2 CONT *'''Family 2      Margaret Garneys b. c 1520, d. a 12 Feb 1594
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Sir Edward Devereux+ b. 3 Aug 1558, d. 22 Sep 1622
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. VI, p. 478-9.
2 CONT * 2.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. V, p. 326-327.
2 CONT * 3.[S74] Brent Ruesch's Research Notes.
2 CONT * 4.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. V, p. 326-329.
2 CONT * 5.[S11588] Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 65.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2254.htm#i67730 _________________
2 CONT *'''Walter Devereux, 1st Viscount Hereford1 
2 CONT *'''M, #139900, b. circa 1491, d. 27 September 1558
2 CONT *Last Edited=16 Aug 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.0% 
2 CONT *'''Walter Devereux, 1st Viscount Hereford was born circa 1491.2 He was the son of John Devereux, 2nd Lord Ferrers (of Chartley) and Cicely Bourchier.1 He married, secondly, Margaret Garneys, daughter of John Garneys.3 He married,
2 CONC  firstly, Lady Mary Grey, daughter of Thomas Grey, 1st Marquess of Dorset and Cecilia Bonville, Baroness Bonville and Harington, before 15 December 1530.2 He died on 27 September 1558.3
2 CONT *'''     Walter Devereux, 1st Viscount Hereford succeeded to the title of 3rd Lord Ferrers, of Chartley [E., 1461] in May 1501.2 He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Garter (K.G.) in 1523.2 He was invested as a Privy Counsell
2 CONC or (P.C.) in January 1549/50.2 He was created 1st Viscount Hereford [England] on 2 February 1549/50.1
2 CONT *'''Children of Walter Devereux, 1st Viscount Hereford and Margaret Garneys
2 CONT **1.Sir Edward Devereux, 1st Bt.+4 d. 22 Sep 1622
2 CONT **2.Katherine Devereux4
2 CONT *'''Children of Walter Devereux, 1st Viscount Hereford and Lady Mary Grey
2 CONT **1.Sir Richard Devereux+1 d. 13 Oct 1547
2 CONT **2.Sir William Devereux+5
2 CONT **3.Henry Devereux4
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extin
2 CONC ct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 250. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 1875. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *3.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 2, page 1876.
2 CONT *4.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *5.[S3470] Marian Hastings, "re: Hastings Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 31 Deember 2008. Hereinafter cited as "re: Hastings Family."
2 CONT *From: http://thepeerage.com/p13990.htm#i139900 ________________________
2 CONT *'''Walter Devereux, 1st Viscount Hereford (1488 – 17 September 1558) was an English Peer.
2 CONT *Family
2 CONT *'''He was born in either Chartley Castle or the Chartley Manor which replaced it as the residence of the Barons Ferrers of Chartley following the Wars of the Roses. He was a son of John Devereux, 8th Baron Ferrers of Chartley and
2 CONC  Cecily Bourchier.
2 CONT *His paternal grandparents were Anne Ferrers, 7th Baroness Ferrers of Chartley and her husband Walter Devereux, Lord Ferrers of Chartley. His maternal grandparents were William Bourchier, Viscount Bourchier and Anne Woodville.
2 CONT *William Bourchier was a son of Henry Bourchier, 1st Earl of Essex and Isabel Plantagenet. Anne Woodville was a daughter of Richard Woodville, 1st Earl Rivers and Jacquetta of Luxembourg.
2 CONT *Baron Ferrers
2 CONT *'''On 5 March 1501, his father died and Walter succeeded him as the 9th Baron Ferrers of Chartley. He served with distinction in the War of the League of Cambrai (1508-1516) and the Italian War of 1521-1526.
2 CONT *'''In 1523, the Baron was created a Knight of the Garter by Henry VIII of England alongside diplomat Thomas Boleyn, later Earl of Wiltshire. He served as Custos Rotulorum of Cardiganshire from 1543 to his death.
2 CONT *'''He was created Viscount Hereford in 1550.
2 CONT *Marriages and children
2 CONT *'''He was first married to Mary Grey (1491- 22 February 1538) on 15 December 1503. She was a daughter of Thomas Grey, 1st Marquess of Dorset and his second wife Cecily Bonville, Baroness Harington and Bonville.
2 CONT *Cecily Bonville was the daughter and heiress of William Bonville, 6th Baron Harington by his wife Katherine Neville. Her maternal grandparents were Alice Montagu, 5th Countess of Salisbury and her consort Richard Neville, 5th Ear
2 CONC l of Salisbury (jure uxoris).
2 CONT *'''He was secondly married in 1539 to Margaret Garneys. She was a daughter of John Garneys of Kenton.
2 CONT *'''By his first wife, Mary Grey he had three children:
2 CONT **Sir Richard Devereux (d. 13 October 1547). Married Dorothea Hastings. She was a daughter of George Hastings, 1st Earl of Huntingdon and Anne Stafford. They were parents to Walter Devereux, 1st Earl of Essex.
2 CONT **Sir William Devereux of Mirevale Abbey. Married Jane Scudamore, daughter of John Scudamore. The marriage produced two daughters, Barbara Devereux and Margaret Devereux.
2 CONT **Henry Devereux, died unmarried.
2 CONT *'''By his second wife, Margaret Garneys he had two children:
2 CONT **Sir Edward Devereux, 1st Baronet of Castle Bromwich. Married Catherine Arden. They were parents of Walter Devereux, 5th Viscount Hereford, fourth-generation ancestors of Price Devereux, 9th Viscount Hereford and fifth-generation
2 CONC  ancestors of Edward Devereux, 11th Viscount Hereford.
2 CONT **Katherine Devereux. Married Sir James Baskerville.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Devereux,_1st_Viscount_Hereford ______________________
2 CONT *'''Walter DEVEREUX (1° V. Hereford)
2 CONT *'''Born: 1488, Chartley, Staffordshire, England
2 CONT *'''Acceded: 1550
2 CONT *'''Died: 17 Sep 1558, Chartley
2 CONT *'''Buried: Stowe Church, Chartley, Staffordshire, England
2 CONT *'''Notes: Knight of the Garter. B. Ferrers of Chartley. The Complete Peerage vol.V, pp.326-328. Present at the capture of Boulogne.
2 CONT *Father: John DEVEREUX (2º B. Ferrers of Chartley)
2 CONT *Mother: Cecille BOURCHIER (B. Ferrers of Chartley)
2 CONT *'''Married 1: Mary GREY BEF 15 Dec 1503
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Richard DEVEREUX (Sir Knight)
2 CONT **2. Edward DEVEREUX
2 CONT **3. William DEVEREUX (Sir)
2 CONT **4. Catherine DEVEREUX
2 CONT **5. Henry DEVEREUX
2 CONT *'''Married 2: Margaret GARNEYS (V. Hereford) (m.2 William Willoughby, Lord Parham) ABT 1557, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **6. Edward DEVEREUX
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/DEVEREUX.htm#Walter DEVEREUX (1° V. Hereford) _____________________
2 CONT *The National Library of Wales :: Dictionary of Welsh Biography
2 CONT *http://yba.llgc.org.uk/en/s-DEVE-REU-1100.html
2 CONT *DEVEREUX of Lamphey, Pembs. , Ystrad Ffin, Carms. , Vaynor and Nantariba, Mont. , Pencoyd , Brecknock , etc. A Norman family, one branch of which settled in Herefordshire soon after the Conquest , and eventually acquired importan
2 CONC t interests in south and central Wales 
2 CONT *'''WALTER DEVEREUX ( c. 1491 - 1559 ), 1st viscount Hereford , was the eldest son of John , lord Ferrers , to whose title he succeeded in 1501 , adding to it in 1550 that of viscount Hereford . He became a member of the Council o
2 CONC f Wales in 1513 ; in 1525 steward of the household of Mary , Princess of Wales , and C. J. of South Wales ; in 1526 chamberlain of South Wales and of the counties of Cardigan and Carmarthen . He was also high steward of Builth and
2 CONC  steward of Old Carmarthen . In 1531 a large share of the confiscated estates of Sir Rhys ap Gruffydd (see under Rice of Dynevor ) fell to Devereux , who thus ‘assumed the leadership of West Wales ’ ( Laws , Little England , 272),
2 CONC  and his position there was safeguarded in the Act of Union ( 27 Henry VIII, c. 26 § 39 ). He was involved in disputes with William Barlow (q.v.) , bishop of S. Davids , in 1538 , with Henry Somerset (see Somerset family ), 2nd ea
2 CONC rl of Worcester over the stewardship of Arwystli and Cyfeiliog in the same year, with the boroughs of Haverfordwest ( 1536 ) and of New Carmarthen ( 1540 ), one result of this last quarrel being the amalgamation of the two Carmart
2 CONC hen s. He was also a commissioner for the coastal defence in South Wales in 1539 . He is credited with the foundation of the grammar school at Carmarthen which from 1576 bore the title of Queen Elizabeth's Grammar School . 
2 CONT *His son Sir RICHARD (d. 1547 ) deputized for him in many of his Welsh offices, became mayor of Carmarthen ( 1536 ), and M.P. for Carmarthenshire ( 1545 ), and in 1547 received from the Crown the episcopal manor of Lamphey , recen
2 CONC tly alienated to Henry VIII by bishop Barlow , and the principal Welsh seat of the Devereux for the next century.  ________________________
2 CONT *DEVEREUX, Sir William (c.1525-79), of Merevale, Warws.
2 CONT *b. c.1525, 2nd s. of '''Walter, 1st Visct. Hereford by his 1st w. Mary, da. of Thomas Grey''', 1st Mq. of Dorset; bro. of Sir Richard† and half-bro. of Edward. m. Jane, da. of John Scudamore of Holme Lacy, Herefs., wid. of John W
2 CONC arnecombe† of Lugwardine and Hereford, Herefs., 2da. Kntd. 21 Aug. 1565.
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/devereux-sir-william-1525-79 ______________________
2 CONT *DEVEREUX, William (by 1525-79), of Merevale, Warws.
2 CONT *b. by 1525, 2nd s. of '''Walter Devereux, 3rd Lord Ferrers of Chartley, 1st Viscount Hereford, by 1st w.'''; bro. of Richard and half-bro. of Edward Devereux. m. settlement 12 Nov. 1554, Jane, da. of John Scudamore of Holme Lacy,
2 CONC  Herefs., wid. of John Warnecombe of Lugwardine and Hereford, Herefs., 2da. Kntd. 21 Aug. 1565.2
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1509-1558/member/devereux-william-1525-79 ____________________
2 CONT *DEVEREUX, Richard (by 1513-47), of Carmarthen, Carm. and Lamphey, Pemb.
2 CONT *b. by 1513, 1st s. and h. app. of '''Walter Devereux, 3rd LordFerrers of Chartley, 1st Viscount Hereford, by 1st w. Mary, da. of Thomas Grey''', 1st Marquess of Dorset; bro. of William and half-bro. of Edward Devereux. m. settlem
2 CONC ent 1 July 1536, Dorothy, da. of George† Hastings, 1st Earl of Huntingdon, 2s. inc. George 3da. KB 20 Feb. 1547.2
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1509-1558/member/devereux-richard-1513-47 ______________________
