2 CONT *7.^ Shaw, W (1906). The knights of England; a complete record from the earliest time to the present day of the knights of all the orders of chivalry in England, Scotland, and Ireland, and of knights bachelors; Incorporating a com
2 CONC plete list of knights bachelors dubbed in Ireland, compiled by G. D. Burtchaell.. London: Printed and published for the Central chancery of the orders of knighthood, Sherratt and Hughes. 
2 CONT *8.^ Sylvanus Urban, ed. (1845). "The Family of Herbert". The Gentleman's Magazine (London: John Moyer Nichols & Sons) 178: 596. 
2 CONT *9.^ a b Spurgeon, C (2000). An inventory of the Ancient Monuments in Glamorgan. 3. Royal Commission on Ancient and Historical Monuments in Wales. p. 409. http://books.google.com/books?id=oXRnAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA409. 
2 CONT *10.^ Malcolmson, C (1999). Heart-work: George Herbert and the Protestant ethic. Standford, CA USA: Stanford University Press. p. 16. http://books.google.com/books?id=a2DbDJ2DiHMC&pg=PA16. 
2 CONT *11.^ Nichols, J, ed. (1863). The Herald and Genealogist. 1. London: John Boyer Nichols and Sons. p. 34. 
2 CONT *12.^ Jeremy Bolwell (2008). "The tomb of Sir Richard Herbert of Ewyas". http://www.geograph.org.uk/photo/710352. Retrieved 2011-02-09.
2 CONT *http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sir_Richard_Herbert
2 CONT *____________________
