2 CONT See Peter Bartrum, https://cadair.aber.ac.uk/dspace/bitstream/handle/2160/5218/Bleddyn%20ap%20Maenyrch%2020.png?sequence=1&isAllowed=y (December 7, 2017; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William ap Thomas''' (died 1445) was a member of the Welsh gentry family that came to be known as the Herbert family through his son William Herbert, 1st Earl of Pembroke and is an ancestor of the current Earls of Pembroke.
2 CONT
2 CONT Raglan manor, attained through marriage through heiress Elizabeth Bluet, was greatly expanded by William and his son, William Herbert, into the well-fortified Raglan Castle, one of the finest late medieval Welsh castles.
2 CONT
2 CONT William served King Henry V of England during his first French campaign and in numerous subsequent capacities and was knighted in 1426. He fought in the Battle of Agincourt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Remarks
2 CONT
2 CONT >In 1410, he and Thomas, lord Berkeley (brother of Sir James Berkely, whose widow he married) feloniously seized a Genoese ship laden with wine, for which they had to make restitution. (Bradney, History of Monmouthshire, vol. 1 p.
2 CONC  5, 6)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_ap_Thomas
2 CONT * http://www.castlewales.com/wmaptho.html
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://histfam.familysearch.org/getperson.php?personID=I5162&tree=Welsh
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.celtic-casimir.com/webtree/17/36757.htm Family Links Spouses/Children: 1. Elizabeth BLUET Heiress of Raglan 2. Gwladus FERCH DAFYDD Margaret HERBERT+ William HERBERT K.G., 1st Earl of Pembroke+ 3. Cari DDU John HERBERT 
2 CONC of Itton Sir William AP THOMAS of Raglan
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: Abt 1377, Plas yn-y-berth-hir (Perth-hir), Monmouthshire, Wales Married (1): After 1405, 3rd husband 1st wife 411,2223,10607 Married (2): After 1415, 2nd husband 2nd wife 2223,10491 Married (3): Before 1418, No Marriage 411 
2 CONC Died: 1446, Raglan Castle, Usk, Monmouthshire, Wales 2223,10491 Buried: Priory Church, Abergavenny, Monmouthshire, Wales
2 CONT
2 CONT    Another name for William was Sir William ap Thomas HERBERT of Raglan. 411,2223,10491,10607
2 CONT
2 CONT    General Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Thomas, called "Y Marchog Glas o Went" ("The Blue Knight of Gwent"), of Raglan, Mon, the (feudal) Lordship of which he bought from 1st Lord (Baron) Berkeley; knighted 1415; married 1st his former employer Elizabeth (to
2 CONC  whom he had been steward), daughter and heiress of Sir John Bluet, of Raglan, and widow of Sir James Berkeley (by whom she was mother of the 1st Lord (Baron) Berkeley; married 2nd, as her 2nd husband, Gwladus (died 1454), daughte
2 CONC r of Dafydd Gam (killed at Agincourt) and widow of Sir Roger Vaughan, of Tretower (also killed at Agincourt), and died 1446. [Burke's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Built the "Great Tower" of Raglan Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Copied from Herbert, George biography, 88.1911 encyclopedia.org/H/HERBERT_GEORGE.htm:
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas’s fifth son, William or Gwilim ap Thomas, who died abt 1446, was the first man of the family to make any figure in history. This Gwilim ap Thomas was steward of the lordships of Usk and Caerleon under Richard, duke of York.
2 CONC  Legend makes him a knight on the field of Agincourt, but his knighthood belongs to the year 1426. He appears to have married twice, his first wife being Elizabeth Bluet of Raglan, widow of Sir James Berkeley, and his second a dau
2 CONC ghter of David Gam, a valiant Welsh squire slain at Agincourt. Royal favour enriched Sir William, and he was able to buy Raglan Castle from the Lord Berkeley, his first wife’s son, the deed, which remains among the Beaufort munime
2 CONC nts, refuting the pedigree-maker’s statement that he inherited the castle as heir of his mother Maude daughter of Sir John Morley.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The following material was copied from Jane Williams Flank, World Connect db=jwflank, rootsweb.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT Other sources:
2 CONT
