2 CONT # William Harris, b. 1505, Southminster, England, d. 1556, Southminster, England.
2 CONT # Alice HARRIS
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Discussion==
2 CONT +Despite some difficulties with dates, strong evidence supports the Percy-Harris connection as given. [1]
2 CONT * Joanne (Johanna) Percy, supposedly (but maybe doubtfully) the wife of Arthur Harris of Prittlewell (or his son, Arthur). It is suggested that Joanne was the daughter of Sir Thomas Percy, the second son of Henry Algernon Percy, 5
2 CONC th Earl of Northumberland and his wife Catherine Spencer. Joanne's mother is supposedly Eleanor Harbottle. However, a glance at pg 417 of A General and Heraldic Dictionary of the Peerages of England, Ireland and Scotland (etc, etc
2 CONC ) by John Burke(pub. 1831), shown no such daughter descended from Sir Thomas Percy (left only two sons).  A website [http://www.theharrislegacy.com/ the Harris Legacy] shown nothing of any relationship between Arthur Harris and Jo
2 CONC anne Percy (click on the Harris Family of Essex, England, scroll down for Arthur Harris, who had a different wife). [2]
2 CONT
