1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''John Touchet, 1st Lord Audley1,2,3
2 CONT *'''M, #30455, b. circa 1350, d. 23 June 1372
2 CONT *Father      Sir John Touchet2,4 b. 25 Jul 1327, d. c 10 Jan 1362
2 CONT *Mother     Joan de Audley2,4 b. c 1332
2 CONT *'''     John Touchet, 1st Lord Audley was born circa 1350 at of Markeaton & Ashwell, Derbyshire, England; A minor in 1362 and 1365.5,2,3 He married Margery de Grey, daughter of Sir Reginald de Grey, 4th Baron Grey and Maud Boteto
2 CONC urt, before 1371; They had 1 son (Sir John, 4th Lord Audley).2,6,3 John Touchet, 1st Lord Audley died on 23 June 1372 at Battle of La Rochell, Bay of Biscay; Died at Sea.5,2,3
2 CONT *'''Family      Margery de Grey b. c 1352, d. b 3 Nov 1405
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Sir John Touchet, 4th Lord Audley, Keeper of Llandovery & Brecknock Castles+3 b. 23 Apr 1371, d. 19 Dec 1408
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S9416] Unknown author, The Complete Peerage, by Cokayne, Vol. I, p. 340; Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 111; The Ancestry of Dorothea Poyntz, by Ronny O. Bodine, p. 43.
2 CONT * 2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 721.
2 CONT * 3.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. IV, p. 215-216.
2 CONT * 4.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. IV, p. 215.
2 CONT * 5.[S11588] Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 111.
2 CONT * 6.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 765-766.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1014.htm#i30455
2 CONT *___________
2 CONT *'''John Tuchet1
2 CONT *M, #47279
2 CONT *Last Edited=22 May 2004
2 CONT *'''     John Tuchet is the son of Sir John Tuchet and Joan Audley.1
2 CONT *'''Child of John Tuchet
2 CONT ** 1.John Tuchet, 4th Lord Audley (of Heleigh)+1 b. 23 Apr 1371, d. 19 Dec 1408
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 340. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p4728.htm#i47279
2 CONT *___________________
2 CONT *'''John TOUCHET
2 CONT *'''Born: ABT 1350, Markeston, Derbyshire, England
2 CONT *'''Died: 23 Jun 1372 
2 CONT *Father: John TOUCHET of Markeaton (Sir)
2 CONT *Mother: Joan De AUDLEY
2 CONT *'''Married: Maud De MORTIMER (b. ABT 1352 - d. 1405) BEF 1371
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. John TOUCHET (1º B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/TOUCHET.htm#John TOUCHET1
2 CONT *_____________
2 CONT *John Tuchet, 4th Baron Audley, 1st Baron Tuchet (23 April 1371 — 19 December 1408) was an English peer.
2 CONT *John Tuchet, 4th Baron Audley was the son of '''Sir John Tuchet, called "Baron Audley", and his wife Maud''', widow of Sir Richard de Willoughby.[1] His paternal grandparents were Sir John Tuchet (1327—1371) and his wife Joan Aud
2 CONC ley (1331–1393, daughter of James Audley, 2nd Baron Audley and first wife Lady Joan Mortimer).[1]
2 CONT *In 1391, when his childless great-uncle Nicholas Audley, 3rd Baron Audley died, the Audley Barony was abeyant. Meanwhile he was created 1st Baron Tuchet in 1403 and received one-third of the share of the barony of Audley.
2 CONT *In 1408 the Barony was revived, and John Tuchet became 4th Baron Audley.
2 CONT *Before 1398, he married Elizabeth Stafford, daughter of Sir Humphrey Stafford and his first wife, Alice Grenville. They had one son, James, and two daughters, Margaret and Elizabeth. John was succeeded by his only son, James Tuch
2 CONC et.[1]
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Tuchet,_4th_Baron_Audley
2 CONT *________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT From    http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL.htm#_Toc186716635
2 CONT
2 CONT NICHOLAS Audley (11 Nov 1289-1316 before 6 Dec).  He was summoned to parliament 8 Jan 1313, whereby he is held to have become Lord Audley.  m (1312) as her second husband, JOAN Martin, widow of HENRY de Lacy Earl of Lincoln, daugh
2 CONC ter of WILLIAM Martin Lord Martin & his wife Eleanor de Mohun née FitzPiers (-[Feb 1320/1 Aug 1322]).  Lord Nicholas & his wife had one child:  
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          JAMES Audley (Knesale, Nottinghamshire 8 Jan 1313-Heleigh 1 Apr 1386, bur Hulton Abbey).  He succeeded his father in 1316 as Lord Audley.  m firstly (before 13 Jun 1330) JOAN Mortimer, daughter of ROGER Mortimer Earl o
2 CONC f March & his wife Joan de Joinville (-[1337/51]).  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Wigmore Abbey names “Edmundum primogenitum…Rogerum militem, Galfridum…Johannem…Katherinam…Johannam…Agnetam…Margaretam…Matildam… Blanchiam
2 CONC … et Beatricem” as children of “Roger comes et Johanna uxor eius”, adding that Joan married “domino Jacobo de Audeley”[1319].  m secondly (before Dec 1351) ISABEL, daughter of [ROGER Le Strange Lord Strange of Knokyn] (-after 1366
2 CONC ).  Lord James & his first wife had four children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)       NICHOLAS Audley ([1328]-22 Jul 1391).  He succeeded his father in 1386 as Lord Audley.  m (settlement [1330/31]) ELIZABETH Beaumont, daughter of HENRY Beaumont Lord Beaumont & his wife Alice Ctss of Buchan (-27 Oct 1400,
2 CONC  bur [Hulton Abbey]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT (b)       ROGER (-after 1352).  
2 CONT
2 CONT                         **************************
2 CONT
2 CONT (c)       JOAN Audley .  m Sir JOHN Tuchet of Markeaton, Derbyshire (-killed in battle Rochelle 1371).  Their grandson John Tuchet was summoned to parliament in 1405 as Lord Audley.  
2 CONT
2 CONT                       *****************************
2 CONT
2 CONT (d)       MARGERY Audley ([1345]-1411).  m (1353 or before) Sir ROGER Hillary .  
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord James & his second wife had five children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT (e)       MARGERY Audley .  m FULK FitzWarin .  
2 CONT
2 CONT (f)        THOMAS Audley (-before 1391).  
2 CONT
2 CONT (g)       ROWLAND Audley (-before 1391).  
2 CONT
2 CONT (h)       JAMES Audley (-before 1391).  
2 CONT
2 CONT (i)         KATHERINE Audley .  m THOMAS Spigurnel .  
