1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/K4P6-ZVD
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/146377337/alianore-de-holand
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Primary Sources
2 CONT 1430. 16 Kal. March. SS. Apostoli, Rome. (f. 303.)<br>
2 CONT To the bishop of Lichfield. Mandate to dispense '''James Touchet, lord of Audeley, knight, and  Eleanor Holond, damsel''', of the dioceses of Lichfield and London, after absolution from excommunication, penance and temporary separ
2 CONC ation, to contract renew and remain in the marriage which they contracted per verba legitime de presenti, but did not consummate, not in ignorance that they were related in the third and third degrees of affinity. Oblate etc. (Pe.
2 CONC  xxx. de Casatiis.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: 'Lateran Regesta 295: 1429-1430', in Calendar of Papal Registers Relating To Great Britain and Ireland: Volume 8, 1427-1447, ed. J A Twemlow (London, 1909), pp. 157-175. British History Online http://www.british-history.ac
2 CONC .uk/cal-papal-registers/brit-ie/vol8/pp157-175 [accessed 22 September 2017].
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor (de Holland) Tuchet is a direct decendent and bloodline of the kings of England, Scotland, France, and Norse Kings from Denmark/Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor's identified family bloodline runs to the Plantagenet kings through both her father's and mother's lines, starting with English King Edward III (her Great Grandfather on her mother's side), and traveling through the Englis
2 CONC h manarchy to Kings Edward II (Plantagenet) and Edward I (Plantagenet) "Longshanks" of England (reign 1272-1307ad) her 3rd great grandfather. Her Father's Plantagenet bloodline comes from King Edward I.  Through both bloodlines, E
2 CONC leanor is a direct decendent and blood line of the House of Mercia, House of Wessex, House of Normandy, and the House of Plantagenet (Angevin). Mother's side: (King Edward I of England; King Edward II; King Edward III; Edmund Plan
2 CONC tagenet, KG, of Langley, 1st Duke of York; Constance Plantagenet, Duchess of Gloucester; Eleanor (de Holland) Tuchet, Baroness of Audley.
2 CONT
2 CONT Data:
2 CONT
2 CONT From the English Wikipedia page on Eleanor de Holland:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleanor_de_Holland
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor de Holland (b. c. 1406) was the illegitimate daughter of Constance of York and Edmund Holland, 4th Earl of Kent.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married James Tuchet, 5th Baron Audley (son of John Tuchet, 4th Baron Audley and his wife Isabel). Children of Eleanor de Holland & James Tuchet, 5th Baron Audley: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *1. Sir Humphrey Audley, 5th Baron Audley, born After 1430, died May 6 1471
2 CONT *2. Edmund Touchett, Bishop of Salisbury, born c. 1432 - died Aug. 23 1524
2 CONT *3. Thomas Touchett, born c. 1435, died June 1507
2 CONT *4. Henry Touchett, born c. 1437, died unknown
2 CONT *5. Margaret Touchett, born c. 1438, died before Feb. 2 1481
2 CONT *6. Anne Touchett, born c. 1440, died unknown
2 CONT *7. Constance Touchett, born 1443, died unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Eleanor de Holland: (http://www.thepeerage.com/p10274.htm#i102736)
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor de Holland [1]
2 CONT *F, #102736, *b. circa 1406 *Last Edited=11 Nov 2011 *Consanguinity Index=0.82%
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor de Holland was born illegitimately circa 1406 [1] She was the daughter of Edmund de Holand, 4th Earl of Kent and Constance Langley.[1]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A contract for the marriage of Eleanor de Holland and James Tuchet, 5th Lord Audley (of Heleigh) was signed in March 1429/30 [2]. As a result of her marriage, Eleanor de Holland was styled as Baroness Audley in March 1430 and her 
2 CONC married name became Tuchet [1], [2].
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Eleanor de Holland and James Tuchet, 5th Lord Audley (of Heleigh):
2 CONT
2 CONT *1. Elizabeth Tuchet [3]
2 CONT *2. Sir Humphrey Audley [2] b. a 1430, d. 4 May 1471
2 CONT *3. Edmund Audley [2] b. a 1430, d. 23 Aug 1524
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 111. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
2 CONT *2. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 341. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *3. [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume III, page 346.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Note: Eleanor Tuchet (born Holland) and Eleanor Tuchet (born Holand) and Eleanor de HOLAND might be the same person. Unknown if true but I have a feeling we have a glitch. Because of it Iam only adding Eleanor Tuchet (born Holand)
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor de HOLAND Gender:	Female Birth:	Circa 1405 	 Kenilworth, WAR, England Marriage:	Feb 14 1428 	 Disp Father:	Edmund Holland Mother:	Constance Plantagenet (born York) Husband:	James Touchet Children:	Thomas Touchet Margaret T
2 CONC ouchet Ann Touchet Constance Touchet Edmund Touchet Elizabeth Touchet Humphrey Touchet Sibling:	Eleanor Tuchet (born Holland) Source:	View full record on WikiTree website (wikitree.com)
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------
2 CONT Eleanor Tuchet (born Holand) Gender:	Female Birth:	1405 	 Woodstock, Kent, England Death:	1452 Father:	Edmund Holand Mother:	Constance Plantagenet (born York) Husband:	Baron James Tuchet Children:	Constance Tuchet Sir Knight Humph
2 CONC rey Tuchet Source:	View full record on WikiTree website (wikitree.com)
