1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-20792
1 NOTE The parentage of Eleanor has been variously given however, by her own statement she was the daughter of the parentage recorded in this file.  In making the claim she stated Edmund and Constance were married, which was disproved by
2 CONC  parliamentary action, and she was acclaimed illegitmate, but no implication was made that the parentage was otherwise.  There is a statement in Mills' "Catalogue of Honour" (see Eng.V,v.1,p.341), that she was the dau. of Edmund d
2 CONC e Holland by Elizabeth Burghersh widow of Edward le Despenser.  This is not only corrected by a statement in "Notes and Queries", 4s, v.3, p.608, but it is observed that Elizabeth was 27 or more in 1369, so she would have been too
2 CONC  old to have been the mother of Eleanor, who could hardly have been born much earlier than the year 1400 and still be young enough to be mother to the childrem accredited to her.  The claim that Eleanor was the daughter of Thomas 
2 CONC de Holand by the listed Constance does not appear likely, since Constance was the wife of Thomas le Despenser from as early as 1379 until he was beheaded 13 Jan 1399/1400 one week after Thomas de Holand was beheaded.  The claim th
2 CONC at Thomas de Holand was associated with Constance as the widow of Thomas le Despenser is therefore impossible.  It is believed that Constance was in liason with Edmund de Holand, brother of Thomas, during the period from 17 Feb 14
2 CONC 04/1405 until possibly as late as 18 Jun 1406.  Inasmuch as Edmund was not married to his wife Lucy until 24 Jan 1406/1407, there is every indication that he could be the father of Eleanor, which is, of course, justified by Eleano
2 CONC r's own statement and by the statement in Sandford's "Genealogical History" 1707, p. 379, which reads, "Constance of York was the paramour of Edmond Holand, Earl of Kent, by whom she had been so long courted that at last she broug
2 CONC ht him a da. named Eleanor, m. to James Touchet, Lord Audley..."
2 CONT
2 CONT Sealed to Thomas le Despenser, Earl of Gloucester and Constance, Countess of Gloucester 2 Jan 1957 in the Salt Lake Temple
2 CONT
2 CONT Information taken from the Archive Record filed in the Family History Library.
2 CONT Sources of information:
2 CONT The Complete Peerage, G.E.C., Eng. V.v.1, p.341, v.3, p.346, v.4, p.274-581, v.7, p.156-163; Notes and Queries, Eng. Pub. P, 4s, v.3, p.608; The Royal Dau. of Eng., Eng. 120, v.1, p.219, 221, 240, 242, 265-268;
1 NOTE "OR ELEANOR"; PARENTAGE UNCERTAIN (UNSUCCESSFULLY CLAIMED LEGITIMACY)
