2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Magna Carta Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, 2nd Edition ... By Douglas Richardson
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=8JcbV309c5UC&printsec=frontcover&dq=Magna+Carta+ancestry:+a+study+in+colonial&hl=en&sa=X&ei=kshLUY2yHM_SigKTqYHwAg&ved=0CDwQ6AEwAQ#v=onepage&q=puleston&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 190
2 CONT *JAMES TUCHET, Knt., 5th Lord Audley, married ELEANOR HOLAND [see TUCHET 12].
2 CONT *'''13. CONSTANCE AUDLEY (or Tuchet), married as his 1st wife) ROBERT WHITNEY, Esq., of Whitney, Herefordshire, Sheriff of Herefordshire, 1474-5, son and heir''' of Eustace Whitney, Esq., of Whitney and Colepychard, Herefordshire 
2 CONC by his 1st wife Joan, daughter of William Trussell, Knt. '''They had two daughters''', Joan and Eleanor (wife of Thomas Vaughan of Bredwardine). He married (2nd ELIZABETH VAUGHAN, daughter of Thomas Vaughan, of Hergest, Herefordsh
2 CONC ire, by Ellen Gethn, daughter of Dafydd ap Cadwgan ap Phylip Dorddu. They had four sons, James, Esq., John, Hugh, and Robert, and three daughters, Ellen (wife of John Puleston) Sibyl (wife of Roger ap Richard Vaughan, of Hergest),
2 CONC  and Elizabeth (wife of John Pye). ROBERT WHITNEY, Esq., died shortly before 6 Oct. 1494. His widow, Elizabeth, was living 4 May 1525. ....
2 CONT *14. JOAN WHITNEY, '''daughter by her father's 1st marriage'''. She married ROGER VAUGHAN, Knt., of Porthaml (in Talgarth), Breconshire, Wales, Steward and Receiver of the Lordship of Dinas, 1509, 2nd son of Roger Vaughan, Knt., o
2 CONC f Tretower, Breconshire, by his 1st wife, Denise, daughter of Thomas ap Philip Vaughan of Tyle-Glas. They had four sons, Watkin, Esq., John, Harry, Esq., and Thomas, Esq., and four daughters, Elinor (wife of Thomas Gwyn, Hywel ap 
2 CONC Gwilym, and William Dometh), Elizabeth, __ (wife of Jenkin ap Thomas), and Margaret (wife of John Parker). by a mistress or mistresses, he also had three illegitimate sons, Thomas, Roger, and Robert. SIR ROGER VAUGHAN died before 
2 CONC 25 Sept. 1514. .... _______________________________
2 CONT *'''Plantagenet Ancestry: A Study In Colonial And Medieval Families, 2nd Edition ...  By Douglas Richardson
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=kjme027UeagC&printsec=frontcover&dq=Plantagenet+ancestry&hl=en&sa=X&ei=U8VLUYTME-boiALhroHwBw&ved=0CEcQ6AEwBA#v=onepage&q=puleston&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 265
2 CONT *11. JOAN TRUSSELL, married (as his 1st wife) EUSTACE WHITNEY, esq., of Whitney and Colepychard, Herfordshire, Knight of the Shire for Herefordshire, 1468, son and heir of Robert Whitney, Knt., of Whitney, Herefordshire, Sheriff o
2 CONC f Herefordshire, 1427-8, 1432-3, 1436-7, by Angharad, daughter of Madop ap Leuan Goch. He was born about 1411 (aged 30 in 1441) They had one son, '''Robert, Esq.'''. He married (2nd) JANE CLIFFORD, daughter of Robert Clifford, Knt
2 CONC . They allegedly had one daughter, Penelope (wife of William Abrahal). In 1457 he was sued in a plea of debt by William Forster, Citizen and tailor of London. The same year he sued John Cheyne and his wife, Perin, in a plea of lan
2 CONC d. EUSTACE WHITNEY, Esq., died 1481/1. ....
2 CONT *'''12. ROBERT WHITNEY, Esq., of Whitney, Herefordshire, Sheriff of Herefordshire, 1474-5, son and heir. He married (1st) CONSTANCE AUDLEY (or TUCHET)''', daughter of James Tuchet (or Audley), Knt., 5th Lord Audley (descendant of 
2 CONC King John), by his 2nd wife, Eleanor, illegitimate daughter of Edmund Holand, K.G., 4th Earl of Kent [see TUCHET 12 for her ancestry]. '''They had two daughters''', Joan and Eleanor (wife of Thomas Vaughan, Knt., of Bredwardine). 
2 CONC He married (2nd) ELIZABETH VAUGHAN, daughter of Thomas Vaughan, of Hergest, Herefordshire, by Ellen Gethin, daughter of Dafydd ap Cadwgan ap Phylip Dorddu. They had four sons, James, Esq., John, Hugh, and Robert, and three daughte
2 CONC rs, Eleanor (wife of John Puleston), Sibyl (wife of Roger ap Richard), and Elizabeth (wife of John Pye). He was attainted as a Yorkist by the Lancastrian Parliament in 1459. '''ROBERT WHITNEY, Esq., died''' shortly before 6 Oct. 1
2 CONC 494. His widow Elizabeth, was living 4 May 1525. ....
2 CONT *13. JOAN WHITNEY, '''daughter by her father's 1st marriage'''. She married ROGER VAUGHAN, Knt., of Porthaml (in Talgarth), Breconshhire, Wales, Steward and Receiver of the Lordship of Dinas, 1509, 2nd son of Robert Vaughan, Knt.,
2 CONC  of Tretower, Breconshire, by his 1st wife Denise, daughter of Thomas ap Philip Vaughan of Tyle-Glas. They had four sons, Watkin, Esq., John, Harry, Esq., and Thomas, Esq., and four daughters, Elinor (wife of Thomas Gwyn, Hywel ap
2 CONC  Gwilym, and William Dometh), Elizabeth, __ (wife of Jenkin ap Thomas), and Margaret (wife of John Parker). By a ....
2 CONT *Pg. 266 - NOT VIEWABLE ______________________________________
2 CONT *'''Constance Touchet1,2,3,4,5 
2 CONT *'''F, #30437, b. circa 1432, d. circa 1451
2 CONT *Father       Sir James Touchet, 5th Lord Audley, Chief Justice & Chamberlain of South Wales2,3,4,6 b. c 1398, d. 23 Sep 1458
2 CONT *Mother      Eleanor Holand2,3,4,6 b. c 1404, d. a 1455 
2 CONT *'''     Constance Touchet was born circa 1432 at of Heleigh, Staffordshire, England.7,8 She married Sir Robert Whitney, Sheriff of Herefordshire''', son of Eustace Whitney, Esq. and Joan Trussell, '''circa 1449; They had 2 daught
2 CONC ers''' (Joan (Jane), wife of Sir Roger Vaughan; & Eleanor, wife of Sir Thomas Vaughn.2,3,4,5 '''Constance Touchet died circa 1451.
2 CONT *'''Family      Sir Robert Whitney, Sheriff of Herefordshire b. c 1418, d. c 6 Oct 1494
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Jane Whitney+9,4 b. c 1450
