1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The dates for Adam Beckwith's Ancestors need more sources, The fourth (iiij) year of Richard's reign was 1381 this date is stated as his year of marriage. Adam's father, Thomas is listed with a birth date of August
2 CONC  29, 1375 which would not be correct if Adam was married 1381.
2 CONT
2 CONT *''''''The Beckwiths" (1891)
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/details/thebeckwiths00beck
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/thebeckwiths00beck#page/23/mode/1up
2 CONT *  William Beckwith was succeeded by his son Thomas of Clint, in the fourth year of the reign of Richard the Second ; he held the Manors of Magna Otringer and Huxley near Thursk, and married the daughter of John Sawley of Saxton. 
2 CONC Thomas Beckwith was succeeded by his son ''''''Adam Beckwith of Clint, who married Elizabeth de Malebisse'''''', and thus reunited the two branches of the Malebisse family, after a separation of over three hundred years. Sir Willi
2 CONC am, the eldest son of ''''''Adam Beckwith'''''', married a daughter of Sir John Baskerville, and was succeeded by his son ...
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/thebeckwiths00beck#page/35/mode/1up
2 CONT *   John, Lord de Malebisse, 16, de Miles, Vice-comes, Co. York. High Sherilf 1314, 8th year Edward 2d. 
2 CONT **	17. William de Malebisse, de Miles, living time Edward 3d, married daughter of John Lampson of Miles. 
2 CONT **	18. Margarette de Malebisse married Thomas Viscount Fairfax. 
2 CONT **	19. Walter de Malebisse, on going to the Holy Land, mortgaged Scalton Castle to William Fairfax, making Richard, his son, his heir, if he did not return. He probably died in Palestine. 
2 CONT **	20. Thomas de Malebisse. 
2 CONT *   Thomas de Malebisse de Miles, 20, de Ancaster-Malebisse, 38th year of Edward the 3d. married Mary, daughter of Francis Palmer, Esq, of Naburn. 
2 CONT **	21. Margaret de Malebisse, co-heiress, married Richard Fairfax. 
2 CONT **''''''	22. Elizabeth de Malebisse, co-heiress ; married, first, John Herringe, 38th year Edward 2d ; for her second husband she married Adam Beckwith of Clint, in the 4th year of Richard 2d. 
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/thebeckwiths00beck#page/36/mode/1up
2 CONT *   William Beckwith, 27, seized of the Manor of Beckwithshaw, 38th year of Edward 3d. 1364, married a daughter of Sir Girard Urtleet. 
2 CONT **	34. Thomas. 
2 CONT **	35. Hercules; married daughter of William Walgrave. 
2 CONT **http://www.archive.org/stream/thebeckwiths00beck#page/39/mode/1up 
2 CONT **	36. John ; married daughter of Sir John Ratcliff, Knt. of Cressell. 
2 CONT *   Thomas Beckwith, 34, of Clint and Manors of Magna Otrigen and Housley, near Thursby, 4, Richard 2d, which lands were holden of John Lord Mowbray, as his Manor of Thursk. He married the daughter of John Sawly of Saxton. 
2 CONT **''''''	37. Adam. 
2 CONT *''''''   Adam Beckwith de Clint, 37, married Elizabeth de Malebisse, 4, Richard 2d. 
2 CONT **	38. Sir William. 
2 CONT **	39. John. 
2 CONT **	40. Margaret ; married Richard Hulse, Esq. 
2 CONT **	41. Anne ; married John Chesney, Esq. 
2 CONT **	42. Amye ; married John Lawton, Esq. 
2 CONT *   Sir William Beckwith. 38, de Clint, Knight, married the daughter of Sir John Baskerville. 
2 CONT *___________________________
2 CONT *''''''The history of the state of Rhode Island and Providence Plantations (Volume 8). 
2 CONT *http://www.ebooksread.com/authors-eng/thomas-williams-bicknell/the-history-of-the-state-of-rhode-island-and-providence-plantations-volume-8-kci/page-63-the-history-of-the-state-of-rhode-island-and-providence-plantations-volume-8-
2 CONC kci.shtml
2 CONT *   (VIII) William Beckwith, son of Hamon Beckwith, married a daughter of Sir Gerard Usfleet. 
2 CONT *   (IX) Thomas Beckwith, son of William Beckwith. was of Clint. He married a daughter of John Sawley, of Saxton. 
2 CONT *''''''   (X) Adam Beckwith, son of Thomas Beckwith, married (second) Elizabeth Malebisse, widow of John Heringe. His children were all by his first wife. 
2 CONT *   (XI) Sir William Beckwith, son of Adam Beckwith, married a daughter of Sir John Baskerville, a descendant of English and French ancestry, who traced his lineage to the Emperor Charlemagne. 
2 CONT *______________________
2 CONT *''''''Beatty-Asfordby; the ancestry of John Beatty and Susanna Asfordby, with some of their descendants ([c1909])
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/details/beattyasfordbyan00turk2
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/beattyasfordbyan00turk2#page/71/mode/1up
2 CONT *   8. William Beckwith of Beckwith, Esquire, in
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/beattyasfordbyan00turk2#page/72/mode/1up 
2 CONT *1364 seized of the manors of Beckwith and Beckwithshaw, who married a daughter of Sir Gerard Usfleet of Wighill, County York, and had issue: 
2 CONT *   9. Thomas Beckwith, who, in the fourth year of Richard II., was seized of Clint, the manor of Magna Otrington, Hornby near Thurske, which land he held of John, Lord Mowbray, as of the latter's manor of Thurske. He married a da
2 CONC ughter of John Sawley of Saxton, by whom he had issue: 
2 CONT *''''''   10. Adam Beckwith of Clint, who married, in the fourth year of Richard II., Elizabeth, the widow of John Heringe and the daughter and co-heiress of Sir Thomas de Malebisse, by whom he had issue : 
2 CONT *   11 and 13. Sir William Beckwith, de Clint, Knight, who married a daughter of Sir John Baskervile, and had issue : 
2 CONT *_________________________
2 CONT *''''''John Bailey Beckwith, M.D., of Smithfield, NC: A Biographical Sketch with Genealogy of the ... (1893)
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/details/johnbaileybeckw00beckgoog
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/johnbaileybeckw00beckgoog#page/n25/mode/1up
2 CONT *10. WILLIAM BECKWITH, 
2 CONT *   Eldest son and heir of the above, was seized of the manors of Beckwith and Beckwithshaw, thirty-eighth year of Edward III., 1364 ; married a daughter of Sir Girard Urfleet, Knight, of Wighill, County York ; commanded a Knight'
2 CONC s retinue at the battle of Agincourt. 
2 CONT *11. THOMAS BECKWITH, 
2 CONT *   Of Clint, eldest son of the above, married the daughter of John Sawley, of Saxton ; held the manors of Magna-Otringer and Huxley, near Thursk, of John, Lord Mowbray. 
2 CONT *''''''12. ADAM BECKWITH, 
2 CONT *''''''   Of Clint, eldest son of Thomas (11) ; married Elizabeth de Malebisse, fourth year of Richard II., and thus united the two branches of the De Malebisse family, after a separation of over three hundred years. She was grand
2 CONC daughter of Francis Palms, Esq. (See page 47). 
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/johnbaileybeckw00beckgoog#page/n26/mode/1up
2 CONT *13. SIR WILLIAM BECKWITH, 
2 CONT *   Of Clint, Knight, eldest son of Adam (12) ; married a daughter of Sir John Baskerville. (See page 49). 
2 CONT *___________________________
2 CONT *''''''Adam Beckwith (1405 - 1480)
2 CONT *''''''Born in England on 1405 to Thomas Beckwith and Sawley. Adam married Elizabeth De Malebisse and had 5 children. He passed away on 1480 in England.
2 CONT *http://records.ancestry.com/Adam_Beckwith_records.ashx?pid=16850850
2 CONT *____________________
2 CONT *THIS REFERENCE SEEMS TO HAVE ADDED ANOTHER ADAM BECKWITH AS THE FATHER OF ADAM BECKWITH WHO MARRIED ELIZABETH DE MALEBISSE and LISTS A CONTROVERSY OVER THE WIFE WHETHER SHE WAS ELIZABETH FAIRFAX OR ELIZABETH DE MALEBISSE
2 CONT *''''''Maltby-Maltbie family history By Mrs. Dorothy Lord (Maltby) Verrill, Birdsey Lucius Maltbie
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=qd41AAAAMAAJ&pg=PA77&lpg=PA77&dq=Elizabeth+d'Malebisse+Adam+Beckwith&source=bl&ots=uMR48aYqCw&sig=gzGqEpxUV5wBdT58lElPmimOAsU&hl=en&sa=X&ei=1dpkT8PGA8OgiQLEy7GiDw&ved=0CDkQ6AEwBA#v=onepage&q=Eliza
2 CONC beth%20d'Malebisse%20Adam%20Beckwith&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 77
2 CONT *   IX. WILLIAM (9) de Malebisse, Miles, 1339 (d. about 1365, 12 Edward III.); m. a dau. of John Sampson, Miles. His sister Margaret (9) m. Thomas Fairfax of Walton. They had Clarissa (10) Fairfax, who m. first, William Palmes (q.
2 CONC v.) and second, Sir William Milbis. William (9) Maltby had Sir Thomas (10).
2 CONT *   X. WALTER (10), the latter, on going to the Holy Lands mortgaged Scalton to William Fairfax, making latter's son, Richard, his heir if he did not return. His brother, Sir Thomas (10) de Malebisse, had a daughter, Margaret (11)
2 CONC  who m. Richard Fairfax (son of William to whom Walter (10) Maltby mortgaged Scalton), who was heir of her uncle Walter (10). Sir Thomas (10) also had a daughter, Elizabeth (11) Maltby, co-heiress with Margaret Maltby Fairfax.
2 CONT *   XI. MARGARET Malebisse Fairfax had a dau. Elizabeth (12) Fairfax, who m. first, John Herringe, and second ''''''Adam Beckwith of Clynt, according to one authority; another claims it was Elizabeth (11) Malebisse, co-heiress wit
2 CONC h Margaret (11), who m. first John Herringe and second Adam Beckwith of Clint. It must be remembered that Adam Beckwith was a Maltby by blood, the Beckwith being a maternal ancestry. See Pedigree of Beckwith''''''.
2 CONT *   This family apparently died out, as it ends in female lines only, but is must be remembered that only the line of one son was carried down, and there must have been many branches from this tree. For proof that this was the cas
2 CONC e we find: "4 Oct., 1426, the will of Dame Sibilla, relic. of Sir William Malbys, K., of Acaster Malbys. Adm. Vol. II., folio 497.  ....
2 CONT *Pg. 80
2 CONT *   VII. Harmon Beckwith m. a dau. of Sir Philip Tylney. He took upon him a coat-of-arms of Hugh Maltby in 1339, incident to John Lord Malebisse. (q. v.)
2 CONT *   VIII. William Beckwith m. ____ Usfleet.
2 CONT *   IX. Thomas Beckwith, 4 Richard III., m. ____ Sawley.
2 CONT *   X. Adam Beckwith.
2 CONT *''''''   XI. Adam Beckwith of Clint. m. Elizabeth Malebisse, co-heiress of Thomas Malebisse, wid. of John Herringe. (Vide Vist. of Yorkshire, edit C. B. Northcliffe: Harl. Soc. Pub., Vol. XVI., p. 117.)
2 CONT *__________________
