2 CONT *''''''   Thomas Beckwith of Clint, 43, Lord of a one-third part of Fily, Muston and Thorp; he died 10th year of Henry 7th; he married the daughter and heiress of William Heslerton, heiress of a one-third part of the manors of Fil
2 CONC ey, Muston and Thorp, inherited from Havisia, daughter and heiress of Ralph Neville, above mentioned.
2 CONT **	44. Thomas of Clint; married Elizabeth, daughter of Thomas Ingleby, of Ripley; died without issue.
2 CONT **	45. Sir William.
2 CONT **	46. John.
2 CONT **http://archive.org/stream/thebeckwiths00beck#page/41/mode/1up
2 CONT **	47. Adam; married Amye, daughter of William Redman of Harewood Castle.
2 CONT **	48. Robert.
2 CONT **	49. Ellen; married J. Vavasour of Weston, Co. York.
2 CONT **	50. Joan; married Falkner, Esq.
2 CONT *   Sir William Beckwith, 45, of Clint; Knight in 1481; married twice; his second wife was the daughter of Sir John Rattcliff, K. G.; by his first wife, Elizabeth, daughter of Sir William Plumpton, he had the following children:  
2 CONC  ....
2 CONT *   John Beckwith, 46, married the daughter of Thomas Radcliff of Mulgrave.  ....
2 CONT *___________________________
2 CONT *THIS REFERENCE SEEMS TO HAVE LEFT OUT ADAM BECKWITH WHO IS LISTED IN OTHER REFERENCES AS THE SON OF THOMAS & ? SAWLEY AND FATHER OF WILLIAM WHO MARRIED THE DAU. OF JOHN BASKERVILLE
2 CONT *''''''A genealogical and heraldic History of the Commoners of Great ..., Volume 2 By John Burke
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=0I9AAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA115&lpg=PA115&dq=Thomas+Beckwith+1495&source=bl&ots=d96eEYmx4Y&sig=IuJQlSqr8EVVhBjDoSCqR1GvMKA&hl=en&sa=X&ei=ux9kT_KPIOiQiAL21MiiDw&ved=0CCkQ6AEwATgo#v=onepage&q=Beckwith&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 636
2 CONT *   THOMAS BECKWITH, esq. living 4th Richard II. who espoused a daughter of John Sawley, of Saxton, and had issue,   ....
2 CONT *   The elder son,
2 CONT *   SIR WILLIAM BECKWITH, knt. of Clint, m. a daughter of Sir John Baskerville, knt. and was s. by his son,
2 CONT *''''''   THOMAS BECKWITH, who wedded a daughter of Sir William Haslerton, knt. and in her right was lord of the third part of the manors of Filey Maston, and Thorp. He had issue,
2 CONT **	I. THOMAS, who m. Elizabeth, daughter of Sir William Ingilby, knt. of Ripley, but d. s. p. in 1478.
2 CONT **	II. WILLIAM (Sir), who m. first Elizabeth, daughter of Sir William Plompton, knt. of Plompton, and by her had one son, William, who married Janetta, daughter of William Beckwith, of Clint, but d. s. p. in 1476. Sir William espo
2 CONC used, secondly, a daughter of Sir William Radcliffe, K. G. but had no other issue.
2 CONT **	III. JOHN, of whom presently.
2 CONT **Pg. 637
2 CONT **	IV. Adam, who m. Ayme, daughter of William Redman, of Harewood Castle, but d. without issue.
2 CONT **	V. Robert, who m. Barbara, daughter of John Leventhorp, and had, with a daughter Mary, a son,  ....
2 CONT **	I. Ellen, m. to John Vavasor, of Weston (see vol. i. p. 53). This lady made her will 2nd HENRY VII.
2 CONT **	II. Joan, m. to Thomas Althere.
2 CONT *The third son,
2 CONT *   JOHN BECKWITH, esq. espoused a daughter of Thomas Radcliffe, esq. of Mulgrave, and had two sons, viz.   ..... 	I. THOMAS, heir to his uncle Sir William Beckwith, m. Maud, *_____________________
2 CONT *''''''The history of the state of Rhode Island and Providence Plantations (Volume 8). 
2 CONT *http://www.ebooksread.com/authors-eng/thomas-williams-bicknell/the-history-of-the-state-of-rhode-island-and-providence-plantations-volume-8-kci/page-63-the-history-of-the-state-of-rhode-island-and-providence-plantations-volume-8-
2 CONC kci.shtml
2 CONT *   (X) Adam Beckwith, son of Thomas Beckwith, married (second) Elizabeth Malebisse, widow of John Heringe. His children were all by his first wife. 
2 CONT *   (XI) Sir William Beckwith, son of Adam Beckwith, married a daughter of Sir John Baskerville, a descendant of English and French ancestry, who traced his lineage to the Emperor Charlemagne. 
2 CONT *''''''   (XII) Thomas (2) Beckwith, son of Sir William Beckwith. was of Clint, and married a daughter of William Heslerton. He died in 1495. 
2 CONT *   (XIII) John Beckwith, son of Thomas (2) Beckwith, married a daughter of John Radclift, of Mulgrave. 
2 CONT *______________________
2 CONT *''''''John Bailey Beckwith, M.D., of Smithfield, NC: A Biographical Sketch with Genealogy of the ... (1893)
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/details/johnbaileybeckw00beckgoog
