1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In 1534 John Combe (or possibly his father) was chosen an alderman of the Stratford gild and later the same year he and Elmor Hickmons leased a house on Eport Street in Worcester from Worcester Priory. In 1537 John
2 CONC  Combe leased the manor place of Ruin Clifford from John Greville for 60 years at a reserved rent of £9 10s. In 1534/35 John Combe made payment to gild at Stratford for the soul of daughter Dorothy. It is not entirely clear, howev
2 CONC er, which John Combe. License granted by the Bishop of Worcester for a marriage between "Joahennem Combe Juniorem de Astley Wigorniensis dioc. et Katherinam Quynye de Stratford." Katherine can no longer have been young and there i
2 CONC s some doubt about whether she was the mother of his children. Chambers shows her only as mother of William and leaves the other children in doubt.
