2 CONT ==brief biography and family==
2 CONT From an unidentified source:
2 CONT
2 CONT >Watkin (Walter) Vaughan (d. 1456) of Bredwardine, Esquire,[8] married Elinor, daughter of Sir Henry Wogan,[2][7] On Easter 1456, Watkin was murdered at home, Bredwardine Castle for which half-brother William Herbert and Walter De
2 CONC vereux forcibly ensured prosecution of execution of the culprits at Hereford.[1]
