2 CONT *'''13. CONSTANCE AUDLEY (or Tuchet), married as his 1st wife) ROBERT WHITNEY, Esq., of Whitney, Herefordshire, Sheriff of Herefordshire, 1474-5, son and heir''' of Eustace Whitney, Esq., of Whitney and Colepychard, Herefordshire 
2 CONC by his 1st wife Joan, daughter of William Trussell, Knt. '''They has two daughters''', Joan and Eleanor (wife of Thomas Vaughan of Bredwardine). '''He married (2nd ELIZABETH VAUGHAN''', daughter of Thomas Vaughan, of Hergest, Here
2 CONC fordshire, by Ellen Gethn, daughter of Dafydd ap Cadwgan ap Phylip Dorddu. '''They had four sons''', James, Esq., John, Hugh, and Robert, '''and three daughters''', Ellen (wife of John Puleston) Sibyl (wife of Roger ap Richard Vau
2 CONC ghan, of Hergest), and Elizabeth (wife of John Pye). '''ROBERT WHITNEY, Esq., died shortly before 6 Oct. 1494. His widow, Elizabeth, was living 4 May 1525. ....
2 CONT *14. JOAN WHITNEY, '''daughter by her father's 1st marriage'''. She married ROGER VAUGHAN, Knt., of Porthaml (in Talgarth), Breconshire, Wales, Steward and Receiver of the Lordship of Dinas, 1509, 2nd son of Roger Vaughan, Knt., o
2 CONC f Tretower, Breconshire, by his 1st wife, Denise, daughter of Thomas ap Philip Vaughan of Tyle-Glas. They had four sons, Watkin, Esq., John, Harry, Esq., and Thomas, Esq., and four daughters, Elinor (wife of Thomas Gwyn, Hywel ap 
2 CONC Gwilym, and William Dometh), Elizabeth, __ (wife of Jenkin ap Thomas), and Margaret (wife of John Parker). by a mistress or mistresses, he also had three illegitimate sons, Thomas, Roger, and Robert. SIR ROGER VAUGHAN died before 
2 CONC 25 Sept. 1514. .... __________________________________
