2 CONT *5.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 722-723.
2 CONT *6.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 709.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1013.htm#i30436 _____________
2 CONT *'''Genealogical and personal memoirs relating to the families of Boston and eastern Massachusetts, Volume 3 edited by William Richard Cutter
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=qaK9Vz1UdDcC&pg=PA1398&lpg=PA1398&dq=Robert+Whitney+1379&source=bl&ots=kTyc24a62q&sig=6WVzO7BwbUU9aIEAULHNsFK0m6Q&hl=en&ei=oU7sS-qONYbOsQOMyK20Dw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=2&ved=0CBkQ6A
2 CONC EwATgK#v=onepage&q=Robert%20Whitney%201379&f=false
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/genealogicaland00cuttgoog
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/genealogicaland00cuttgoog#page/n344/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.1398
2 CONT *   (VIII) Sir Robert Whitney, son of Sir Robert (7), was granted the castle of Clifford and lordships of Clifford and Glasbury by Henry IV in 1404, on account of the services of his father. He was sheriff of Herefordshire in 1413
2 CONC -28-33-37; member of parliament, 1416-22. He fought in the French war under Henry V, and was captain of the castle and town of Vire in 1420. He was named as one of the five knights in Herefordshire in 1433, and died March 12, 1441
2 CONC .
2 CONT *   (IX) Sir Eustace de Whitney, son of Sir Robert (8), was born in 1411. He was head of a commission sent to Wales by Henry VI in 1455 and was member of parliament for Herefordshire in 1468. He married Jenett Russell; second, Jan
2 CONC e Clifford.
2 CONT *'''   (X) Robert Whitney, son''' of Sir Eustace (9), '''was probably a knight and was an active participant in the War of the Roses, and was attainted as a Yorkist in 1459. He was probably at the battle of Mortimer's Cross in 146
2 CONC 1. He was the subject of a poem of Lewis Glyn Cothi, on the occasion of his marriage to Alice''', the great-granddaughter of Sir David Gam. '''He married first, Alice, daughter''' of Thomas Vaughan; '''second, Constance Touchett, 
2 CONC who was the mother of his sons'''. She was descended from William the Conqueror, through the second wife of Edward I, King of England.
2 CONT *   (XI) James Whitney, son of '''Robert (10)''', was appointed receiver of Newport, part of the estate of the Duke of Buckingham, confiscated by Henry VII in 1522. He married Blanche, daughter and an heir of Simon Milbourne. ____
2 CONC _____________________
2 CONT *'''Constance TOUCHET
2 CONT *Born: 1443, Heleigh, Staffordshire
2 CONT *Died: AFT 1467
2 CONT *Father: James TOUCHET (2º B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT *Mother: Eleanor HOLLAND (B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT *'''Married: Robert WHITNEY of Whitney''' (son of Eustace Whitney and Jennet Russell) '''ABT 1464
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. James WHITNEY (Sir) (m. Blanche Milbourne)
2 CONT **2. Joan WHITNEY (m. Roger Vaughan)
2 CONT **3. Eleanor WHITNEY (m. John Pulleston)
2 CONT **4. John WHITNEY
2 CONT **5. Robert WHITNEY
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/TOUCHET.htm#Constance TOUCHET1 _________________
2 CONT *James Whitney ('''Robert''', Eustace, Robert, Robert, Robert, Eustace, Eustace, Robert, ...), son of '''Robert and Elizabeth/Alice (Vaughn) Whitney''',[1] born say 1466, Whitney, Herefordshire;[2] died 31 July 1500,[3] probably W
2 CONC hitney, Herefordshire. 
2 CONT *He married, say 1490, Blanche Milbourne,[4] daughter and coheiress of Simon and Jane (Baskerville) Milbourne.[5] She was born say 1468, Tillington, Herefordshire,[6] and died after 24 March 1547/48.[7] She married secondly, as hi
2 CONC s second wife, Sir William Herbert,[8] of Troy, Monmouthshire, Wales, illegitimate son of William Herbert, 1st Earl of Pembroke (1423-1469) (Eighth Creation) and mistress Frond verch Hoesgyn,[9] born about 1448-1452[10]; died 1524
2 CONC .[11] Lady Blanche Herbert of Troy was eulogized by the Welsh bard Lewys Morgannwg. Sir William Herbert had married firstly Jane Dunn.[12] 
2 CONT *For more information, see The Ancestry of James Whitney of Whitney. 
2 CONT *From: http://wiki.whitneygen.org/wrg/index.php/Family:Whitney,_James_(s1466-1500) ____________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°
