2 CONT *http://www.thepeerage.com/p32488.htm#i324874
2 CONT *''''''Joyce Skull1
2 CONT *F, #324874
2 CONT *Last Edited=20 Dec 2008
2 CONT *''''''     Joyce Skull is the daughter of Sir Walter Skull.1 She married Sir Edward Croft, son of Sir Richard Croft and Eleanor Cornwall.1
2 CONT *''''''     Her married name became Croft.
2 CONT *''''''Children of Joyce Skull and Sir Edward Croft
2 CONT **1.Richard Croft+2 d. 1 Jan 1562
2 CONT **2.George Croft1 d. 1540
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 966. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Pe
2 CONC erage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *2.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *______________________
2 CONT *''''''Plantagenet ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=p_yzpuWi4sgC&pg=PA388&lpg=PA388&dq=Elizabeth+Beauchamp+Thomas+Croft&source=bl&ots=RQBQ9KV579&sig=h_nX2IsjT251Ez0RpKrNuLFgX48&hl=en&ei=2Ah4TfDaM83vrAHW9_XICQ&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=2&
2 CONC ved=0CB4Q6AEwAQ#v=onepage&q=Elizabeth%20Beauchamp%20Thomas%20Croft&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 388
2 CONT *13 MARGARET BEAUCHAMP, daughter and heiress, born about 1400. She married (1st) JOHN PAUNCEFOOT (died before 1420). She married (2nd) before 1422 JOHN WYSHAM ( or WISHAM), Knt., of Churchill, Shelsley Beauchamp, Woodmanton (in Cl
2 CONC ifton upon Teme), and Wolverton (in Stoulton), Worcestershire, and, in right of his wife, of Holt, Worcestershire, Ardley, South Weston, and Wigginton, Oxfordshire, and Bubbenhall, Warwickshire, son and heir of William Wysham, Knt
2 CONC ., of Churchill, Shelsley Beauchamp, etc., Worcestershire (descendant of King Henry II) [see WYSHAM 9 for his ancestry]. They had three daughters, Alice, Joan (wife of __ Westcote and John Croft), and Elizabeth (wife of Thomas Cro
2 CONC ft and Nicholas Crowmer). He was living in 1434. She married (3rd) before 1437 (as his 1st wife) WALTER SKULLE, Knt., of Hereford and London, attorney, Keeper of the King's Wardrobe, Treasurer of the Household, Knight of the Shire
2 CONC  for Worcestershire, Sheriff of Herefordshire, of Oxfordshire and Berkshire, and of Worcestershire. They had one son, Thomas. Sir Walter married (2nd) before 1464 Frances Winchcombe, widow of William Mulle (or Mille), of Harescomb
2 CONC e, Gloucestershire, and Allensmore and Avenbury, Herefordshire, and daughter and heiress of Edmond Winchcombe. They had one daughter, ''''''Joyce (wife of Edward Croft)''''''. He died in 1482. His widow, Frances, left a will prove
2 CONC d in 1483 (P.C.C. 7 Logge).
2 CONT *__________________________
