2 CONT *Pg.153
2 CONT **THOMAS MORGAN of Maughan, Efq.
2 CONT *Kydivor Vawr, Lord of Blain Cych, paternally defcended from Bely the great, King of Britain, married Elen, daughter and heri to Llewellin Vawr.
2 CONT *Bledry ap Kydivor Vawr, Lord of Kylfant = Clidwen, daughter and heirefs to Griffith Cedreth, Lord of Gwnfay.
2 CONT *Ivor ap Bledry, Lord of Kylfant, Efq. = Tangluft, daughter and heirefs to Howel Sais, Lord of St. Clere-y-mvch, Efq.
2 CONT *Llewellin ap Ivor, Lord of St. Clere, Efq. = Lleykye, daughter to Griffith ap Eli, Lord of Gilfield in Powis.
2 CONT *Ivor ap Llewellin, Lord of St. Clere, Efq. = Neft, daughter to Cadwgan, and great grandchild to Eliftan, Prince of Ferlix.
2 CONT *Llewellin ap Ivor, Lord of St. Clere = Angharand, daughter and heirefs to Sir Morgan Meredith, Knight, Lord of Tredegar.
2 CONT *Morgan ap Llewellin, Lord of Tredegar, Efq. = Maud, daughter to Rhun ap Grono ap Llwarch, Lord of Kybor, Efq.
2 CONT *Llewellin Morgan of Tredegar, Efq. = Jonet, daughter to Dd Yehan of Rydoclyn, Efq.
2 CONT *Evan Morgan of Tredegar, Efq. = Denis, daughter to Thomas ap Howell Yehan, Efq.
2 CONT *Sir John Morgan of Tredegar, Knight = Jonet, daughter and heirefs of John Matthewes of Llandaff, Efq.
2 CONT *Thomas Morgan of Machen, Efq. his brother, Sir John, Dying fans iffue.
2 CONT *Rowland Morgan of Maughan and Tredegar, Efq. = Elizabeth, fifter to Sir Roger Bodingham of Potheras, Com. Hereford.
2 CONT *Pg.154
2 CONT *Sir William Morgan of Tredegar, Knight = Daughter to Wintour, Knight, Com. Glocefter.
2 CONT *Thomas Morgan Maughan and Tredegar, Efq. now living, 1661.
2 CONT **		William Morgan, Efq. heir-apparent.
2 CONT * .....
2 CONT *The eldeft fon of Llewelyn ab Ifor, was Morgan ab Llewelyn of Tredegyr, in the parifh of Maefaleg; and his fecond fon was Ifor Hael, or the Generous Lord of Maefaleg, the Wenallt and Gwern-y-Cleppa. Their other was Angharad the d
2 CONC aughter of Sir Morgan ab Meredydd, ab Greffydd, av Meredydd Gethin, the fon of Rhys ab Tewdwr, Prince of South-Wales. Ifor Hael died without heirs, and his eftate came to his nephew Llewelyn, the fon of Morgan ab Llewelyn, and fro
2 CONC m him, in a direct line, are defcended the worthy family of Morgans of Tredegyr; the the ancient inheritance is ftill entire in their poffeffion; and if any merit, .... __________________
2 CONT *'''A genealogical and heraldic history of the extinct and dormant baronetcies ...  By John Burke, John Bernard Burke (sir.)
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=K1kBAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA370&lpg=PA370&dq=baronetLlantarnam&source=bl&ots=E8TtZ2olal&sig=sPTN7EzpqKq_KY8tYZSOL-hCsOA&hl=en&sa=X&ei=HYjNUuW9M-ir2gWbjoEo&ved=0CEEQ6AEwBAv=onepage&q=baronet%20llantarnam&f=f
2 CONC alse#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.369
2 CONT *   LLEWELLIN AP IVOR, lord of St. Clere, lineally descended from Kidivor Vawr, lord of Kilsaint, married Angharad, daughter and heir of Sir Morgan Meredith, knt. lord of Tredegar, and was father of
2 CONT *   MORGAN AP LLEWELLIN, lord of St. Clere and Tredegar, who m. Maud, daughter of Rhys ap Gronwy, lord of Kybor, and had two sons, viz.
2 CONT **	CLEWELLYN, of Tredegar, ancestor of the MORGANS of Tredegar.
2 CONT **	PHILIP.
2 CONT *Pg.370
2 CONT *The second son,
2 CONT *   PHILIP MORGAN, esq. of Langston, acquired that estate in marriage with the daughter and heir of Sir John Norris, knt. of Penlline Castle. He was direct ancestor* of
2 CONT *   WILLIAM MORGAN, esq. sheriff for Monmouthshire in 1567, and M.P. in 1571, who was the first proprietor of Llantarnam. He m. Elizabeth, daughter of Sir Rees Mansel, knt. of Margam, and was s. by his son,
2 CONT *   EDWARD MORGAN, esq. of Llantarnam and Penrice, M. P. for Monmouthshire in 1586, who m. Elizabeth, daughter and heir of Hugh Smith, esq. of Long Ashton, in Somersetshire, and had a son and successor,
2 CONT *   WILLIAM MORGAN, esq. of Llantarnam, who m. the Lady Frances Somerset, daughter of Edward, Earl of Worcester, and was father of
2 CONT *   I. SIR EDWARD MORGAN, of Llantarnam, who was created a BARONET in 1642. He m. Mary, daughter of Sir Francis Englefield, bart, of Wotton Basset, in Whiltshire and was s. at his decease, 24th June 1653, by his son,
2 CONT **	*The intervening descent was as follows:
2 CONT *	Philip Morgan, esq. of Langston = Gwenllian, daughter and heir of Sir John Norris, of Penlline Castle, Glamorganshire.
2 CONT *	Jenkin ap Phillip, of Langston = Cicely, daughter of Sir John Welsh, knt.
2 CONT *	Morgan ap Jenkin, (t) of Langston = Elizabeth, daughter of Sir Roger Vaughan.
2 CONT *'''	Sir Thomas Morgan, knt. of Pencoed = Joan, daughter and heir of John Gwilliam Herbert, of Itton.
2 CONT *	John Morgan, esq. of Caerleon, second son = Ely, daughter of Lewes ap Richard Gwynn, esq. of the Van.
2 CONT *	William Morgan, first of Llantarnam.
2 CONT **	(t) By his third wife, Morgan ap Jenkin had a son, John Morgan, esq. of Tredunnock, in Monmouthshire, ancestor of the MORGANS of TREDUNNOCK, now represented by Mrs. JANE HAWKINS. _______________________
2 CONT
