2 CONT _____________________________
2 CONT ===John Talbot, 10th Earl of Shrewsbury===
2 CONT John Talbot, 10th Earl of Shrewsbury, 10th Earl of Waterford (1601 – 8 February 1654), was an English nobleman.
2 CONT Life
2 CONT He was the '''child and son of John Talbot of Longford, Newport, Shropshire''' (died London, 1607 or c. 1607), '''and his wife Eleanor Baskerville''', daughter of Sir Thomas Baskerville of Wolvershill, Herefordshire, and of Brinso
2 CONC p, Herefordshire, and paternal grandson of Sir John Talbot of Grafton and Catherine or Katharine Petre.
2 CONT He remained in his family's Roman Catholic faith and took part on the side of King Charles I in the English Civil War. He was First Commissioner of Advice for the counties of Worcestershire, Shropshire and Staffordshire in 1644/45
2 CONC , and he served on the Royalist garrison at Worcester when it surrendered to Parliament in July 1646. In 1647 his estates were sequestered and compounded by Parliament on grounds of his being a "Papist and delinquent" (i.e. Cathol
2 CONC ic and royalist).[1]
2 CONT In September 1651 he accompanied Charles II when he fled after defeat at the battle of Worcester, escorting him to White Ladies Priory in Shropshire, where the king was hidden for a time.[1] The Earl died in 1653/54 at Tasmore, Ox
2 CONC fordshire,[1] (Tusmore?) and was succeeded by his second son.
2 CONT Family
2 CONT Talbot married Mary Fortescue, by whom he had seven children:
2 CONT *Lady Frances Talbot (d. 17 July 1641), who married George Winter, 1st Baronet (1622-1658), and had one child, Thomas Winter.
2 CONT *George Talbot, Baron Talbot (circa 1620 - 7 March 1644[1]), who married Mary, daughter of Percy Herbert, 2nd Baron Powis. He had one daughter, Mary, who was living in 1649 but died young and unmarried.[1]
2 CONT *Francis Talbot, 11th Earl of Shrewsbury (1623-1667), who succeeded
2 CONT *Edward Talbot, who died at the Battle of Marston Moor, 1644
2 CONT *Hon. Gilbert Talbot (bef. 1654-1711), who married Jane Flatsbury and had children, including Gilbert Talbot, 13th Earl of Shrewsbury
2 CONT *Lady Catherine, who married Thomas Whetenhall of East Peckham[2]
2 CONT *Lady Mary Talbot (bef. 1654 - c. March 1711), who married first Charles Arundell and second Mervyn Tuchet, 4th Earl of Castlehaven; she had children from both marriages.
2 CONT He later married Hon. Frances Arundell, 4th daughter of Thomas Arundell, 1st Baron Arundell of Wardour and had three sons and a daughter by her:
2 CONT *Hon. John Talbot, who died young
2 CONT *Hon. Bruno Talbot, abt 1650- aft 1690 Chancellor of the Exchequer of Ireland, 1686-1690
2 CONT *Hon. Thomas Talbot, who married Anne Tate daughter of Sir John Tate. Thomas and Anne's son Matthew Talbot (I) immigrated to Maryland and then moved to Virginia. Matthew (I) is the proginator of the Talbot Family of Virginia and G
2 CONC eorgia.
2 CONT *Lady Anne, who became a nun in France
2 CONT References
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Talbot,_10th_Earl_of_Shrewsbury
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________________
2 CONT ===John Talbot of Grafton===
2 CONT Sir John Talbot of Grafton, Worcestershire (1545 – 28 January 1611[1]) was a prominent recusant English Catholic layman of the reigns of Elizabeth I of England and James I of England. etc.
2 CONT Family
2 CONT He was the only son and heir of Sir John Talbot, of Grafton Manor, Worcestershire, and of Albrighton, Shropshire (died 6 June 1555), and wife Frances Giffard, daughter of Sir John Giffard, and grandson of Sir John Talbot of Albrig
2 CONC hton (died 10 September 1549) by his second wife Margaret Troutbeck.[5]
2 CONT He was the father, by Katherine Petre, daughter of Sir William Petre and his second wife, Anne Browne, daughter of Sir William Browne, Lord Mayor of London, of three sons and three daughters,[1] who included:
2 CONT *Anne Talbot, married 18 November 1585 Thomas Hanmer (died 18 April 1619), and had issue, including Sir John Hanmer, 1st Baronet
2 CONT *George Talbot, 9th Earl of Shrewsbury, a Catholic priest
2 CONT *Gertrude Talbot, married Robert Wintour of Huddington, Worcestershire (executed 30 January 1606)
2 CONT *'''John Talbot of Longford, Market Drayton, Shropshire''' (died London, in or around 1607), '''married Eleanor Baskerville''', daughter of Sir Thomas Baskerville of Wolvershill, Herefordshire, and of Brinsop, Herefordshire, and '
2 CONC ''had one son''', John Talbot, 10th Earl of Shrewsbury
2 CONT References
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Talbot_of_Grafton
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________________
2 CONT ===The peerage of England; containing a genealogical and historical account of all the peers of England, ... By Arthur Collins, ...  1741: Vol 2===
2 CONT by Collins, Arthur
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/bim_eighteenth-century_the-peerage-of-england-_collins-arthur_1741_2/mode/1up
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/bim_eighteenth-century_the-peerage-of-england-_collins-arthur_1741_2/page/63/mode/1up
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT Which Sir John Talbot, in his laft Teftament, writes himfelf of Grafton, and died in 4 E. VI. as fhould feem by the Probate thereof, which bears date 11 Oct. 1549. And by Margaret his firft Wife, Daughter and Heir of Adam Troutbec
2 CONC k, of the County Palatine of Chefter, Efq; left Iffue, befides other Children, John Talbot of Grafton. And by his fecond Wife, Elizabeth, Daughter of ___ Wrotefley of Wrotefley, in Com' Staff. Efq; left Iffue John Talbot of Salwar
2 CONC p, in Com' Wigorn. Efq; from whom defcended a numerous Pofterity, as the Talbots of Salwarp, the Talbots of Badgworth, in Com' Glouc. and Okely, in Com' Wigorn, and the Talbots of Worril, Com' Salop, Sherington Talbot of Salwarp, 
2 CONC The eldeft Son, was Grandfather to William Talbot, late Lord Bifhop of Durham, who was Grandfather to the prefent Lord Talbot. But I return to John Talbot of Grafton, who died Anno 2 & 3 Phil. and Mary, and by Frances, his Wife, D
2 CONC aughter of Sir John Giffard of Chillington, in Com' Staff. Knt. had Iffue John Talbot of Grafton, and a Daughter, Joan, married to Sir John Bowes.
2 CONT Which John Talbot of Grafton, Efq; married Catherine, Daughter to Sir William Petre, Knt. Principal Secretary of State to Queen Mary, and left Iffue two Sons, George, who became Earl of Shrewbury, and '''John Talbot of Longford, i
2 CONC n Com' Salop, Efq''';
2 CONT Which George, in the 15th Year of King James I. fucceeded Edwared, Earl of Shrewbury, before-mention's, but died unmarried the 2d of April 1630, and was buried in the Church of Albrighton, in Com' Salop. To whom fucceeded John his
2 CONC  Nephew, viz. Son to '''John his brother, by Eleanor his Wife, Daughter and Coheir''' of Sir Thomas Baskerville, of Wolverfhil,
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/bim_eighteenth-century_the-peerage-of-england-_collins-arthur_1741_2/page/64/mode/1up
2 CONT in Com' Wigorn, Knt. who had Iffue by him likewife a Daughter, Catharine, Wife of James Pool of Pool, in Com' Cefter. Efq;
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________________
2 CONT ===Shrewsbury, Earl of (E, 1442)===
2 CONT 5. Sir Gilbert Talbot KG, of Grafton, co. Worcester, fought on the Lancastrian side at the Battle of Bosworth 1485, Commander at the Battle of Stoke 1487, Deputy Captain of Calais (d. 19 Sep 1518), mar. (1) after 1475 Elizabeth le
2 CONC  Scrope (widow of Thomas [le Scrope], 5th Baron Scrope of Masham), 5th dau. by his first wife of Ralph [de Greystock], 5th Baron Greystock, and had issue:
2 CONT *1a. Sir Gilbert Talbot, of Grafton, co. Worcester, Sheriff of Worcestershire c. 1540 (dspms. 22 Oct 1542), mar. (1) Anne Paston, dau. and cohrss. of Sir William Paston, by his wife Lady Anne Beaufort, sister and cohrss. of Henry 
2 CONC [Beaufort], 2nd Duke of Somerset, and 5th dau. of Edmund [Beaufort], 1st Duke of Somerset, and (2) Elizabeth Wynter, and had issue by his first wife:
2 CONT **1b. Humphrey Talbot  (dsp.)
2 CONT **2b. Walter Talbot (dsp.)
2 CONT **1b. Margaret Talbot, mar. Sir Robert Newport
2 CONT **2b. Elizabeth Talbot, mar. Sir John Lyttelton, of Frankley in the County of Worcester (d. 17 May 1532), and had issue
2 CONT **3b. Mary Talbot, mar. Sir Thomas Astley, of Patshull, co. Stafford, and had issue
2 CONT *2a. Sir Humphrey Talbot (dsp. in the Holy Land)
2 CONT Sir Gilbert Talbot KG mar. (2) Etheldreda Gardiner (widow of (1) Thomas Barton and (2) Richard Gardiner, Lord Mayor of London), dau. of William Landwade, of Landwade, co. Cambridge, and had further issue:
2 CONT *3a. Sir John Talbot, of Albrighton, co. Shropshire, and later of Grafton, co. Worcester, High Sheriff of Shropshire 1528, 1538 and 1542 (d. 10 Sep 1549), mar. (1) Margaret Troutbeck, dau. and hrss. of Adam Troutbeck, of Mobberley
2 CONC , co. Cheshire, and had issue:
2 CONT **1b. Sir John Talbot, of Grafton and Albrighton (d. 6 Jun 1555), mar. Frances Giffard, dau. of Sir John Giffard, and had issue:
2 CONT ***1c. Sir John Talbot, of Grafton, mar. (1) Catherine Petre, 1st dau. of Sir William Petre, Secretary of State 1543-66, by his second wife Anne Tyrell, widow of Thomas Tyrell and dau. of Sir William Browne, Lord Mayor of London 1
2 CONC 514, and (2) Hon Margaret Windsor, dau. of Henry [Windsor], 5th Baron Windsor, and had issue by his first wife:
2 CONT ****1d. George Talbot, later 9th Earl of Shrewsbury
2 CONT ****2d. '''John Talbot, of Longford, co. Shropshire''' (d. 1607), '''mar. Eleanor Baskerville''', dau. and cohrss. of Sir Thomas Baskerville, of Brinsop, co. Hereford, and '''had issue''':
2 CONT *****1e. John Talbot, later 10th Earl of Shrewsbury
2 CONT
2 CONT John [Talbot], 10th Earl of Shrewsbury
2 CONT '''1st son and heir of John Talbot, of Longford, co. Shropshire (by his wife Eleanor Baskerville''', dau. and cohrss. of Sir Thomas Baskerville, of Brinsop, co. Hereford), yr. bro. of George [Talbot], 9th Earl of Shrewsbury
2 CONT born	bef. 1601
2 CONT mar. (1)	bef. 1619 Mary Fortescue (bur. 6 Jan 1635/6; bur. at Albrighton, co. Shropshire), dau. of Sir Francis Fortescue, of Salden Hill, co. Buckingham, by his wife Grace Manners, dau. of Hon Sir John Manners, of Haddon Hall, co.
2 CONC  Derby (by his wife Dorothy Vernon, dau. and cohrss. of Sir George Vernon, of Nether Haddon, co. Derby), 2nd son by his second wife of Thomas [Manners], 1st Earl of Rutland
2 CONT children by first wife
2 CONT *1. Hon George Talbot, styled Lord Talbot (b. c. 1620; dvp. and spm. May 1644; bur. at Albrighton, co. Shropshire), mar. Jan 1639 Hon Mary Herbert (bapt. 10 Oct 1623; d. aft. 16 Jan 1662/3), only dau. of Percy [Herbert], 2nd Baron
2 CONC  Powis, by his wife Elizabeth Craven, sister and in her issue cohrss. of William [Craven], 1st Earl of Craven, and 1st surv. dau. of Sir William Craven, Lord Mayor of London 1610-11, and had issue:
2 CONT **1a. .... etc.
2 CONT *2. Hon Francis Talbot, later 11th Earl of Shrewsbury
2 CONT *3. Hon Gilbert Talbot (b. c. 1631; bur. 11 Apr 1702), mar. Jane Flatsbury, dau. of William Flatsbury, and had issue:
2 CONT **1a. .... etc.
2 CONT *1. Lady Mary Talbot (bur. 15 Mar 1710/1), mar. (1) Charles Arundell, 2nd but 1st surv. son and heir of Hon William Arundell, of Horningsham, co. Wiltshire (by his wife and second cousin Hon Mary Paulet, widow of Lord William Paul
2 CONC et, styled Earl of Wiltshire, 1st son and heir of William [Paulet], 4th Marquess of Winchester, and 1st dau. of Anthony Maria [Browne], 2nd Viscount Montagu), 2nd son by his first wife of Thomas [Arundell], 1st Baron Arundell of W
2 CONC ardour, and (2) Mervyn [Tuchet], 4th Earl of Castlehaven, and had issue by both husbands
2 CONT mar. (2)	bef. 15 Feb 1647/8 Hon Frances Arundell (dsp. 2 May 1652), 4th dau. of Thomas [Arundell], 1st Baron Arundell of Wardour, by his second wife Anne Philipson, dau. of Miles Philipson, of Crook, co. Westmorland
2 CONT died	8 Feb 1653/4
2 CONT suc. by	son by first wife
2 CONT From: http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/shrewsbury1442.htm?zoom_highlight=talbot
2 CONT '''''Cracrofts Peerage is no longer active'''''
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________________
2 CONT 'Talbot02'
2 CONT Sir John Talbot, 1st Earl of Shrewbury (b 1390, d Chastillon 20.07.1453)
2 CONT m1. (12.03.1406) Maud Nevill, Baroness Furnivall (b c1391, d before 1433, dau of Thomas Nevill, Lord Furnival)
2 CONT *	1. John Talbot, 2nd Earl of Shrewsbury, Lord Chancellor of Ireland (b 1413, d Northampton 10.07.1460, 2nd son)
2 CONT *	  m1. (before 08.06.1421, sp) Catherine Burnel (dau of Sir Edward Burnel) this marriage may not have taken place
2 CONT *	  m2. Elizabeth Butler (d 08.09.1473, dau of James Butler, 4th Earl of Ormonde, Lord Lieutenant of Ireland)
2 CONT **		A. .... etc.
2 CONT **		B. Sir Gilbert Talbot of Grafton, Sheriff of Shropshire (d 19.09.1518, 5th son)
2 CONT **		Brydges identifies Sir Gilber's 1st wife as Elizabeth, widow of Thomas, Lord Scrope of Masham, dau of Henry, Lord Scrope of Bolton by Alice Scrope. BP1934 identifies her as ...
2 CONT **		  m1. Elizabeth Greystock (dau of Ralph Greystock, 7th Lord of Greystoke, widow of Thomas, Lord Scrope)
2 CONT ***			i. .... etc.
2 CONT **		  m2. Etheldreda/Audrey Cotton (dau of William (not John) Cotton of Landwade)
2 CONT ***			iii. Sir John Talbot of Albrighton & Grafton, Sheriff of Shropshire (d 10.09.1549)
2 CONT ***			  m1. Margaret Troutbeck (dau of Adam Troutbeck of Mobberley)
2 CONT ****				a. Sir John Talbot of Grafton & Albrighton (d 06.06.1555)
2 CONT ****				  m. Frances Giffard (dau of Sir John Giffard of Chillington)
2 CONT *****					(1) Sir John Talbot of Grafton
2 CONT *****					  m1. Catherine Petre (dau of Sir William Petre, Secretary of State)
2 CONT ******						(A) George Talbot, 9th Earl of Shrewsbury (d unm 02.04.1630)
2 CONT ******						(B) '''John Talbot of Longford''' (d 1607)
2 CONT ******						  '''m. Elizabeth Baskerville''' (dau of Sir Thomas Baskerville of Wolvershill)
2 CONT *******							(i) .... etc.
2 CONT ******						(C) Gertrude Talbot (d young)
2 CONT ******						(D) Anne Talbot
2 CONT ******						Wife of Thomas Needham of Shenton, shown as of this generation by Brydges but of 2 generations earlier by BP1934.
2 CONT ******						(E) Gertrude Talbot mentioned by Brydges but not by BP1934
2 CONT ******						  m. Robert Wintour
2 CONT *****					  m2. Margaret (dau of Lord Windsor)
2 CONT *****					(2) Bridget Talbot (d 1619)
2 CONT *****					  m. Sir John Talbot of Castlering (d 07.11.1613)
2 CONT *****					(3) Jane (Joan) Talbot
2 CONT *****					  m. Sir George Bowes of Streatlam (Knight Marshall)
2 CONT ****				b. .... etc.
2 CONT Main source(s): BP1934 (Shrewsbury) with some support from Collins (Brydges, vol 3 (1812), 'Talbot, Earl of Shrewsbury', p11+) with some support/contradiction from Visitation (Worcestershire, 1569, Talbot) and input/support as rep
2 CONC orted above
2 CONT From: Stirnet.com
2 CONT http://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/tt/talbot02.php 
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________________
