1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Nicholas Latimer1 
2 CONT *'''M, b. circa 1427
2 CONT *Father      John Latimer1 b. c 1390, d. 11 Jan 1460
2 CONT *Mother     Catherine Pipard1 b. c 1405
2 CONT *'''     Nicholas Latimer was born circa 1427 at of Duntish, Dorsetshire, England.1 He married Johanna Hody, daughter of Sir John Hody, Chief Justice of the King's Bench and Margareta Cole, on 17 December 1450.1 Nicholas Latimer l
2 CONC eft a will on 17 April 1505.1
2 CONT *'''Family      Johanna Hody b. c 1432
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Edith Latimer+1 b. c 1460
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S61] Unknown author, Family Group Sheets, SLC Archives.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2944.htm#i88467
2 CONT *'''OTHER REFERENCE LIST ELIZABETH JEWE AS JOHN HODY'S WIFE AND MARGARET COLE AS HIS MOTHER, WIFE OF THOMAS HODY.
2 CONT *__________________
2 CONT *'''Nicholas Latimer1 
2 CONT *M, #178012
2 CONT *Last Edited=23 Dec 2005 
2 CONT *'''     Nicholas Latimer lived at Duntish, Dorset, England.1
2 CONT *'''Child of Nicholas Latimer
2 CONT ** 1.Edith Latimer+1
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S15] George Edward Cokayne, editor, The Complete Baronetage, 5 volumes (no date (c. 1900); reprint, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 1983), volume IX, page 193. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Baronetage.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p17802.htm#i178012
2 CONT *______________
2 CONT *HODY, John (d.1441), of Stowell, Som. and Pilsdon, Dorset.
2 CONT *s. of Thomas Hody, esquire (d.1442), of Kington Magna, Dorset; er. bro. of Alexander†. m. by 1430, Elizabeth (d. 3 Aug. 1473), da. and h. of John Jewe (d.1415/16), of Whitfield in Wiveliscombe, Som. and Pilsdon,2 5s. inc. Sir Wil
2 CONC liam†, 3da. Kntd. bef. June 1440.
2 CONT * .... Sir John Latimer of Duntish (Dorset) sought the hand of '''Hody’s daughter Joan for his heir, Nicholas'''.
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1386-1421/member/hody-john-1441
2 CONT *________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Sir Nicholas Latimer
2 CONT
2 CONT Will dated 8 Feb 1504/05, proved 17 Apr 1505. He was sheriff of Dorset and Somerset 1453-54 and 1471-72.62, p. 175
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Nicholas Latimer is mentioned in several histories of the Wars of the Roses. According to Rosemary Horrox,65, pp. 162 and 167 for example, Latimer fought for the Lancastrians at Towton and was included in Edward IV’s act of at
2 CONC tainder of 1461. Latimer reconciled with the Yorkists, but then joined the Duke of Clarence in his revolt of 1470 and was attainted a second time. Latimer returned to the fold with Clarence and was made knight banneret after the b
2 CONC attle of Tewkesbury in 1471. He joined the revolt of the Duke of Buckingham (whose chamberlain he was) in 1483 and was attainted a third time. Latimer went on to fight with the Lancastrians at Bosworth Field in 1485.66
2 CONT
2 CONT The victorious Henry VII reversed Latimer’s last attainder and installed him on the Dorset bench, where he served until his death in 1505. Yet Latimer and his colleague Hugh Luttrell apparently did not benefit greatly from their s
2 CONC ervice to the Lancastrians and Tudors. According to D. A. Luckett, “Neither Latimer nor Luttrell, having worked hard and suffered considerably in the furtherance of the Lancastrian/Tudor cause, can have felt any great sense of sat
2 CONC isfaction after the euphoria of Bosworth had subsided.”67, p. 584 Another disappointed partisan was James, Lord Audley. These “heads of three senior Somerset and Dorset families,”67, p. 586 along with the peasantry and at least 25
2 CONC  members of the local gentry, joined in the southwest insurrection of 1497, which was to cost Latimer a fine of 400 marks.
2 CONT
2 CONT See the Richard III Society’s Web site at http://www.richardiii.net for a wealth of information on this period of English history.
2 CONT *<nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>   
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://soc.genealogy.medieval.narkive.com/8smhT5Jx/halstead-s-genealogies-and-the-families-of-latimer-greene-mordaunt
