2 CONT *'''B.110. WILLIAM SYMES, of Poundsford, Somerset, Merchant. Will dated June 4, 1597, proved July 27, 1597, by Elizabeth Symes the relict'''. [66 Cobham.] Poor of Chard & Pitminster. The R't Hon. Sir Edward Seymour, Kn't. Lord Sey
2 CONC mour of Pomeroy, Devon by deed, Nov. 29, 31 Elizab: hath granted me an annuity of 100 marks out of the demesne of Bury Pomeroy, for 99 years, if '''Elisabeth my wife''', & Henry & James '''my sons shall live so long. To my son''' 
2 CONC John Symes, L2000, according to certain covenants between me & Sir John Popham, K't, Chief Justice, & Thomas Horner, Esq. To Henry '''my son''', 1000 marks. To '''my son''' Robert, L500. '''My son''' William, L500, at age of 21. '
2 CONC ''My daughter''' Elizabeth, 1000 marks. '''My daughter''' Margaret, 1000 marks at age of 21 or marriage. '''My daughter Margery''' Pyne, 100 marks. Jasper Pyne, '''my son in law''', living in Charde. '''My Manors of Barwick, Bowre
2 CONC , & Stoford, Somerset, & Frankham, Dorset. Mill in West Coker, & lands in Taunton. My manor house in Charde, to Elizabeth my wife, during her life, Extrix.''' Supervisors, John Pyne, esq., Roger Hill, gent., & '''my brother in law
2 CONC ''', Hugh Hill, gent.
2 CONT *Pg. 67
2 CONT *   A. 33. B. 50. ROBERT HILL, of Taunton, Somerset, Esq. Will dated Apr. 21, 1581, proved Jun 15, 1581, by Elianor(3) the relict. [26 Darcy.] Poor of Taunton, Hillbrishe & Pytminster. To my son James Hill, my estate in the Capita
2 CONC l Messuage called Pownsforde alias Lodge, in Pytminster, & lands which I hold in common with Sir Henry Portmant, K't, in Pytminster. Many pieces of plate. The spice plate of silver. One piece called the Nutt. To my wife Elynor, a 
2 CONC messuage in Taunton, wherein William Awdey dwelleth, & one in Fore Street, wherein Julian Greye dwelleth, &c. To my son John Hill, an annuity of L10 from my farm called Heydon, & also an annuity of L20 to my son Hugh, & after the 
2 CONC death of my wife Elynor, the farm of Haydon to Hugh Hill, & to James Hill if he pay L30 per ann. to Hugh Hill. To my daughter Jane, L200, & "a pott of silver called the Skynkinge pott," &c. To my daughter Margaret, L200, & my silv
2 CONC er beere jug. My goddaughter Rachel Portman, daughter of Sir Henry Portman, an old roiall of gold. To my other goddaughters 12d each. A marriage intended between my son James Hill and Ann Moryce, daughter of M'r Moryce, of Coxwell
2 CONC , Berks, esq., he to pay me L300, of which L200 to be paid to my wife, for the advancement of my daughters. '''My son in law, William Symes,(5)  one silver spoon gilt, & 6/8 to their children'''. My wife, Extrix. Sir James Marrven
2 CONC , K't, my brother in law, M'r Nicholas Wadham, my son, James Hill, M'r John Walker, of Stowey, & M'r Thomas Davidge, of Taunton, Supervisors. March 31 1593, Admon. was granted to William Wigsted, of Fontmell Gifford, Wilts, yeoman
2 CONC , on decease of Elianor, Relict of Robert Hill.
2 CONT **	(3) Daughter of Sir James Mervyn, and second wife of the testator.
