1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger Hill is said to have had two wives. In about 1515 he first married Alice (Alicia), the older daughter of John Toose of Taunton and Johanna Combes, his wife. They had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Joan Hill, b. ca. 1516
2 CONT * John Hill, b. ca. 1518
2 CONT
2 CONT Both were named in their father's 1544 Will but apparently neither had an heir as the family estate at Poundisford was inherited by Robert Hill, Roger's first-born by his 2nd wife, Margery Toose, younger sister of Alice (Toose) Hi
2 CONC ll, who must have died between 1518 and 1522.
2 CONT
2 CONT ——
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hill of Dorchester, Mass., 1633, and five generations of his ... edited by J. Gardner Bartlett  https://archive.org/details/johnhillofdorche00bart https://archive.org/stream/johnhillofdorche00bart#page/n106/mode/1up Pg.95
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hill was the son of Roger Hill of Taunton, known as Sir Roger of Taunton Hill - from the Southwest county of Somerset. He is said to have been a merchant in the wool trade. His forebears were men of law and government.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hill met and, in January 1558, married "Lady" Joane Hadley who was from the manor at Wolverley, a village in Worcestershire, over 100 miles northeast of Somerset. She must have inherited the property for John moved to Wolverl
2 CONC ey, the only of his immediate family to leave Somerset.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hill was the son of Roger Hill of Taunton, known as Sir Roger of Taunton Hill - from the Southwest county of Somerset. He is said to have been a merchant in the wool trade. His forebears were men of law and government.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hill met and, in January 1558, married "Lady" Joane Hadley who was from the manor at Wolverley, a village in Worcestershire, over 100 miles northeast of Somerset. She must have inherited the property for John moved to Wolverl
2 CONC ey, the only of his immediate family to leave Somerset.
