2 TITL John Hill of Dorchester, Mass., 1633, and five generations of his ... edited by J. Gardner Bartlett Pg.95
1 NOTE  Source: Hill Family of Poundsford in Pitminster, Somersetshire, England, ed. & compiled by J. Gardner Bartlett, Boston, 1904
2 CONT ARMS (granted in 1570). Gules, a chevron engrained ermine, between three garbs, or, within a bordure arg. CREST. A dove rising azure, legged gules, holding in beak and oak branch vert., fructed or.
2 CONT
2 CONT The following pedigree has been compiled from the Visitation of Somersetshire in 1623, together with wills of various members of the family. Of the places mentioned Taunton is a town in the south-western part of Somersetshire. Pou
2 CONC ndsford is a hamlet in Pitminster, a parish four miles south of Taunton. Chard is a town about seven miles southeast of Pitminster. Chaffcombe is a small parish about two miles northeast of Chard; and Lyme Regis is a seaport about
2 CONC  ten miles south of Chard. Dorchester is in Dorsetshire, about fifteen miles southeast of Chard. WILLIAM HILL of Taunton, born about 1440-1450, married Eleanor.
2 CONT
