1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Source:''' [http://www.british-history.ac.uk/no-series/london-aldermen/hen3-1912/pp168-195 BHO/British History Online - Notes on the aldermen, 1502-1700]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lord Mayor of London.'''
2 CONT * '''1552 Alderman Sir Thomas Leigh''' married the niece of Sir Rowland Hill (Lord Mayor 1549–50). From his eldest son the Lords Leigh of the present creation, and from his second those of the earlier creation were descended; his 
2 CONC third son was grandfather of Sir Francis Leigh, created Earl of Chichester, through whom he was ancestor of Chatham and the younger Pitt. '''His daughter Winifred married Sir George Bond (Lord Mayor 1587–8)''' and was ancestress o
2 CONC f the Dukes of Marlborough, Viscount Melbourne (the Premier) and the later Dukes of Leeds. First found in Somerset where they were seated from very early times and were granted lands by Duke William of Normandy, their liege Lord, 
2 CONC for their distinguished assistance at the Battle of Hastings in 1066 A.D.
2 CONT * '''1578.  Sir George Bonde.''' Son-in-law of Sir Thomas Leigh (Lord Mayor 1558–9). Through one daughter he was ancestor of Viscount Melbourne, the first Prime Minister of Queen Victoria, and through another of the Dukes of Marlb
2 CONC orough, Lord Randolph Churchill, Mr. Winston Churchill and the later Dukes of Leeds.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * Some of the first settlers of this family name or some of its variants were: Barnard Bond who settled in Virginia in 1654; Edward Bond settled in 1636 in Virginia; Francis Bond settled in the Barbados with his wife, son, and ser
2 CONC vants, in 1680.
2 CONT ** (Above is a small excerpt from our 1800 word history) 
2 CONT * Motto Translated: The world does not suffice.
2 CONT * Copyright © 2000 - 2008 Swyrich Corporation, all rights reserved
2 CONT * Sheriff of London (1578-1579) and later Lord Mayor of London (1587-1588). Knighted by Queen Elizabeth I.
2 CONT * '''Suggested Readings for the name Bond:''' "The Bonds: An American Family" by Roger M. Williams.
2 CONT * '''Some noteworthy people of the name Bond:'''
2 CONT ** William Cranch Bond, American astronomer * George Phillips Bond, American astronomer * Ward Bond (1903-1960), American actor * Julian Bond (b. 1940), American politician and civil rights leader * Carrie Jacobs Bond (1862-1946),
2 CONC  American composer * Frederick Bligh Bond (1864-1945), English Ecclesiastical architect, and archaeologist * Graham Bond (1937-1974), English Rock musician * Edward Bond (b. 1934), English playwright, theatre director, theorist an
2 CONC d screenwriter * Sir Robert Bond, Newfoundland political leader * Alan Bond (b. 1938), Australian businessman ___________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The PEDIGREE of George (Sir) BOND'''
2 CONT *  Lord Mayor of London (1587); (BONDE)
2 CONT *  Born: abt. 1534 
2 CONT *  Died: abt. 1592
2 CONT *  Poss. U.S. President's 9-Great Grandfather. 
2 CONT *  HRH Charles's 10-Great Grandfather. 
2 CONT *  PM Churchill's 10-Great Grandfather. 
2 CONT * Lady Diana's 11-Great Grandfather. 
2 CONT * P.M. Cameron's 13-Great Uncle. 
2 CONT * Poss. Gen. Pierpont Hamilton's 11-Great Grandfather. [6]
2 CONT * First found in Somerset where they were seated from very early times and were granted lands by Duke William of Normandy, their liege Lord, for their distinguished assistance at the Battle of Hastings in 1066 A.D.
2 CONT
