2 CONT =='''Will'''==
2 CONT
2 CONT  <br/>
2 CONT dated Mar. 2, 1591-2, proved 30 Apr. 1592
2 CONT
2 CONT A third of my goods to my '''wife Winifred Bonde''', & another third among my five '''children, George, Thomas, Marie, Rose and Joane''', ate ages of 21. My '''daughter Ann, to whom I gave 1,000 marks at marriage with her husband 
2 CONC Richard Martin'''. The other third part of my goods to my son in law Mr. Henry Winston, & to Agnes Winston, 100 Pounds. Bequests of cloth for black gowns to my mother in law Dame Alice Leigh, widow, & to my brothers and sisters in
2 CONC  law on my wife's side, viz.: --my brother Cobb & his wife, brother Rowland & his wife, my brothers Richard Leigh & Sir Thomas Leigh & his wife, & my brother William Leigh & his wife. Also black cloth to my cousin William Bond & h
2 CONC is wife, & his brother, my cousin Martin Bonde, & my cousin Mr. William Whitmore, Haberdasher. To cousin Simon Bourman, Haberdasher, & his wife, my neighbour Sir Thomas Goore, my cousin Christopher Bourman, yeoman, & to his sister
2 CONC  Alice Lighe, widow, & Cicelie Clarke, 40/ each for rings. To my brother & sister Palmer & his wife, of Trull, 3.6.8 pounds, & to their children 40/each. To Ann & Dionis Westcombe, daughters of my sister Anstice Westcombe, 40/ eac
2 CONC h. To Isabel Ulid (?) of Wilscombe, & Joan Hurston, of North Currie, daughters of my sister Agnes Cade, 40/ eachTo John Bowier, als Studier, of Filerr, 40/. To John, Dionis, & Katherine, children of my brother Edward Bonde, deceas
2 CONC ed, 40/ each. To William & Lawrence, sons of my sister, Ann Gifford, 40/ each.To the poor of Buckland, where I was born, 5 Pounds, poor of Wilscombe, 5 Pounds. To my cousins, Mr. Doctor Bisse, & his brothers Mr. James Bisse & Rich
2 CONC ard Bisse, of Coscombe, & to their mother, Marie Bisse, widow, 50/ each for rings. To Mr. Nicholas Streete, of Ash priors, Somerset, gent. 4 marks for rings. To Roger Howe, Mercer, cloth for a gown. To poor Scholars of Oxford & Ca
2 CONC mbridge, 5 Pounds. Bequests to poor of Walbrook Ward. Company of Haberdashers, Children of Christ's Hospital, Prisons, & c. My '''son in law Mr. Henry Winston & my daughter Dyonis''', his wife, 5 pounds for rings. Residue between 
2 CONC my wife, Lady Winifred Bonde (my Exix) & '''my daughter Martin'''. My '''son in law Mr. William Quarles & my son William Bonde,''' Oversees, & to each 6.13.4 pounds. George Quarles & his sister Alice Quarles, 40/ each. 
