2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Bond_(mayor) Wikipedia - George Bond (mayor)]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir George Bond''' (died 1592) was 
2 CONT * a 16th-century English politician who served as Lord Mayor of London in 1587/8.[1] 
2 CONT * A native of Somerset, 
2 CONT * he was the younger son of William Bond of Buckland and younger brother of William Bond, alderman and Sheriff of London.[2]      
2 CONT * He was a member of the Haberdasher's Company.[3] 
2 CONT * Prior to becoming mayor, he was elected as Sheriff of London in 1579 and alderman of Walbrook in 1584. 
2 CONT * At the time of his election in 1587, the usual Mayoral Feast was cancelled, on account of plague within the city of London.[4]
2 CONT * Sir George Bond married Winifred Leigh, the 
2 CONT ** daughter of another Lord Mayor, Sir Thomas Leigh.[5] 
2 CONT * Among his children were Thomas Bond, MP for Launceston and Southampton,[6] and William Bond, alderman, whose grandson Thomas was the first of the Bond Baronets of Peckham.  
2 CONT * He died in 1592[7] and was buried in the Mercers' Chapel. 
2 CONT * After his death, his widow married John Colles of Barton Grange, Corfe, MP for Minehead.[8]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References:'''
2 CONT * 1.  Stow, John [1] "A Survey of London, Written in the Year 1598" pg. 195
2 CONT * 2.  Burke, John [2] "A Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Commoners of Great Britain and Ireland, Vol. 1" pg. 241
2 CONT * 3.  Wright, W.H.K. [3] "The Western Antiquary; Or, Devon and Cornwall Notebook, Volume 7" pg. 284
2 CONT * 4.  White, James George [4] "History of the Ward of Walbrook in the City of London" pp. 210-211
2 CONT * 5. 	http://www.british-history.ac.uk/no-series/london-aldermen/hen3-1912/pp168-195
2 CONT * 6.  http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1604-1629/member/bond-thomas-1580-1652
2 CONT * 7. Waters, Henry FitzGilbert [5] "The New England Historical and Genealogical Register, Vol. 47" pg. 349
2 CONT * 8.  http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/colles-john-1541-1608
2 CONT
2 CONT
