2 CONT === Life Sketch ===
2 CONT Sir George Bond (born 1534 - died 1592) was a 16th-century English politician who served as Lord Mayor of London in 1587/8.[ A native of Somerset, he was the younger son of William Bond of Buckland and younger brother of William B
2 CONC ond, alderman and Sheriff of London. He was a member of the Haberdasher's Company. Prior to becoming mayor, he was elected as Sheriff of London in 1579 and alderman of Walbrook in 1584. At the time of his election in 1587, the usu
2 CONC al Mayoral Feast was cancelled, on account of plague within the city of London.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir George Bond married Winifred Leigh, the daughter of another Lord Mayor, Sir Thomas Leigh. Among his children were Thomas Bond, MP for Launceston and Southampton,[6] and William Bond, alderman, whose grandson Thomas was the fir
2 CONC st of the Bond Baronets of Peckham. He died in 1592 and was buried in the Mercers' Chapel. After his death, his widow married John Colles of Barton Grange, Corfe, MP for Minehead.
