1 NOTE {geni:about_me} King'sWalden,HertfordsireSt , the hamlet now has a population of 35 and dates from 1300's 
2 CONT
2 CONT Copied from About me of http://www.geni.com/people/William-Hale-Esq-High-Sheriff/6000000002665618784
2 CONT
2 CONT William Hale was the son of Richard Hale of King's Warden and his first wife Mary Lambert. He was born c. 1551 at Codicote, Hertfordshire, England. He married Rose Bond of Watton-at-Stone, Hertfordshire. Rose was born c. 1555, the
2 CONC  daughter of Sir George Bond, Knight. They were the parents of eight children. He died Aug. 1634.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Hale was named High Sheriff of Hertfordshire in 1621, during the reign of James I.
2 CONT
2 CONT William was the primary heir of his father, Richard Hale, however, King's Walden was bequeathed to William's brother Richard. Eventually, the property ended up coming into William's estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT I have seen sources stating a first wife name Martha but cannot find sources for her or for the children she bore. There are several Hale families in Hertfordshire, with similar names, so I am sure there is confusion among familie
2 CONC s. I have NOT included Martha or her children in this profile overview.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William Hale and wife Rose Bond:
2 CONT
2 CONT #Richard Hale, b. 1596, Herefordshire,England
2 CONT #William Hale, b. 1597, Hexton, Hertfordshire, England
2 CONT #Rowland Hale, b. Abt 1599, Of Herfordshire,England
2 CONT #George Hale, c. 13 Jul 1601, Herefordshire,England
2 CONT #Alicia Hale, b. 1603, Herefordshire,England
2 CONT #Winefreda Hale, b. 1604, Herefordshire,England
2 CONT #Anne Hale, c. 25 Jun 1609, Kings Warden,Hertfordshire,England , d. 2 Sep 1651
2 CONT #Dionisia Hale, c. 17 Mar 1611, Hertfordshire, England
2 CONT
