1 NOTE {geni:about_me} was born 1580 in Brentwood, Middlesex, England, and died 1638 in Maryland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT This may or may not be the same Jerome Hawley who was instrumental in the settlement of Maryland. However, the extensive family connections with Barbados and St. Croix lean in that direction.
2 CONT
2 CONT This one acquired the wardship of Philip Sture, probably by marrying his mother, Judith Hawkins, and made a, quite literally, Parliamentary case over it.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1621 a Jerome Hawley - believed, but not proven, to be the same as the Jerome Hawley who was active in the early development of Virginia and Maryland - published a broadside:
2 CONT
2 CONT "To the honourable, the knights, citizens, and burgesses of the Commons House of Parliament : The humble petition of Ierom Hawley Esquire, for and on the behalfe of Phillip Sture an infant, the sonne and heire of Tristram Sture;
2 CONT
2 CONT Concerning a dispute between Sture and Sir Miles Fleetwood over inheritance".
2 CONT
2 CONT Further developments in 1633:
2 CONT
2 CONT September 10th 1633 Articles between Sir Edmond Fowell, Jerome Hawley, Lewis Hele and Philip Sture, being a settlement made upon the marriage of Mary Fowell, one of the daughters of Sir Edmond Fowell with Philip Sture, ward of Jer
2 CONC ome Hawley. It affects lands in the parishes of Dipford, North Huish, and Ugborough, co Devon
