2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on William Button:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p19589.htm#i195882
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Button, 1st Bt.[1]
2 CONT *M, #195882, 
2 CONT *b. circa 1584, 
2 CONT *d. 16 January 1654/55
2 CONT *Last Edited=11 Jun 2006
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Button, 1st Bt. was born circa 1584.[1] He was the son of William Button and Jane Lamb.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Ruth Dunch, daughter of Walter Dunch and Deborah Pilkington.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 16 January 1654/55.[1] He was buried at Wraxall, Wiltshire, England.[1] His will (dated 29 December 1654) was probated on 10 March 1654/55.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Career:
2 CONT *He matriculated at Queen's College, Oxford University, Oxford, Oxfordshire, England, on 13 February 1600/1.[1] 
2 CONT *He was invested as a Knight on 15 July 1605 at Whitehall, London, England.[1] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Sheriff of Wiltshire from 1611 to 1612.[1] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Morpeth in 1614.[1] 
2 CONT *He was created 1st Baronet Button, of Alton, co. Wilts. [England] on 18 March 1621/22.[1] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Wiltshire from 1628 to 1629.[1] 
2 CONT *On 2 January 1647 he was fined £2,380, as a Royalist.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir William Button, 1st Bt. and Ruth Dunch
2 CONT *1. Sir William Button, 2nd Bt.[1] b. c 1614, d. 8 Mar 1659/60
2 CONT *2. Sir Robert Button, 3rd Bt.[1] b. 1622, d. c 1679
2 CONT *3. Sir John Button, 4th Bt.[1] b. a 1622, d. 29 Nov 1712
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S15] George Edward Cokayne, editor, The Complete Baronetage, 5 volumes (no date (c. 1900); reprint, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 1983), volume I, page 193. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Baronetage.
2 CONT
