2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sir William Kingsmill was Sheriff of Hampshire
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT About Kingsmill, William Will off William KINGSMILL:-
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Name of God Amen I Willm Kingesmill of Sidmontaine in the countie of Southt knight beinge of pfecte mind and memorie and also well and whole in bodie doe ordaine and make this my laste will and testament the xxxth day of Ja
2 CONC nuarie in the yeare of our Lord God one thousand five hundred eightie sixe in manner and forme followinge. Towchinge my soule hoolly and salvation of the same, I have in other tinste? now meanes but only in the bludd sheddinge of 
2 CONC Jesus Christ, whoo by the same hath and in full and pfecte satisfaction for all his elected and chosen.
2 CONT
2 CONT And my body I will to be buried in plane conveniater? accordinge to the discretion of my executor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I geve and bequeath to Bridget Kingesmell my wife all my corne and graine, and wole growinge and otherwise as also all my shepe oxen and kine and all other bothe bease or catle wheresoever performinge fedinge and goinge uppon
2 CONC  my mannor of Sidmountaine or any pte thereof (my horse mewes and geldinge used to the …….. onely excepted)
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I will and bequeath unto the same Bridget Kingesmell my wife all my carte and plough horse geldinge and maire their apptaince unto the carte or ……. at Sidmountaine with all the harness, carte and plough and with all the furni
2 CONC ture to the same.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I geve unto Bridget my wife three of my …….. geldings for the sadle, with my furniture and apparel as upp jointly unto them.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I will my howshoud stuffe in Sidmountaine or as so wherever to be equally divided betwixt Brigett Kingesmill my said wife and Willm Kingesmill my sonne and heir (except my bason and ewer of salver a gylt bowle and a cover to 
2 CONC the same gall? gylt, a turkey carpet for a longer boarde and also all my houshold stuffe at Lechfielde? the which I geve and bequeath unto Willim Kingesmill my sonne and heire). The residue of all my goods not bequeathed ( my lega
2 CONC sies and debts paid) I geve and bequeath unto the said Willim Kingesmill my sonne and heire and whom I make my sole executor.
2 CONT
2 CONT And I will that this shall stand as my laste will and testamete and all other wills herebefore to be f ……… and of none affecte.
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed Wm Kingesmill
2 CONT
2 CONT Witness hereunto Thomas Hillman ………..
2 CONT
2 CONT 42 · 1596B/42 · Will of William Kingsmill (Kingesmill) of S ydmonton, Hampshire, Knight · 1596
2 CONT
2 CONT From the nine sons and three daughters of Sir John (died 1556) and Constance Goring Kingsmill, the eldest son and heir, a Sir William who held significant offices under both Elizabeth and James I (sheriff, Justice of the Peace, &c
2 CONC  for Hampshire), and was written down as 'the wisest gentleman of his country.'
2 CONT
2 CONT The Hampshire Lay Subsidy Rolls1586
2 CONT
2 CONT THE HUNDRED OF KINGSCLERE (Kingsclere Division) The Lay Subsidy was a tax based on the value of lands and possessions and was used to raise money for the Crown to facilitate such things as payment of military forces and building o
2 CONC f ships.
2 CONT
2 CONT The spelling and format of monetary amounts has been left unaltered. For those unfamiliar with pre-decimal English money it will help to know that there were twelve pence (d) in a shilling (s) and twenty shillings in a pound (£).
2 CONT
