2 CONT Late 13th century-20th century Description Original deposit includes: Charters, deeds of title, leases and related papers, including lands at: Alton Eastbrook, 1368; Ashe manor, 1472; Basing, 1338; Basingstoke, 1450-16th century; 
2 CONC Burghclere, 1598-1810; Eastrop, 1506; Ecchinswell, 1598-1838; Hartley Wintney, 1415; Hawkley, 1418-66; Heckfield and Mattingly, 1483; Kimpton, 1561-1638; Kingsclere, 1533-1793; Litchfield, 1316-1817; Longparish, 1348; Newtown (Bur
2 CONC ghclere),
2 CONT
2 CONT 1393-1500; Church Oakley, 1343-1760; Overton, 1471; St Mary Bourne, 1437, 1546-1654; Sherborne St John, 1409-1539; Monk Sherborne, 1298-1706; Sydmonton, 1557-1818; Tangley manor, 1584, 1599; North Warnborough, 1492; Wherwell, 1538
2 CONC -40; Whitchurch and Freefolk, 1323-1565, Winchester, 1414; Woodcott, 1479-1790; East Woodhay, 16th-17th centuries; out-county lands, 13th-19th centuries.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family and estate papers, including: settlements, wills and general deeds, 1337-1836; official appointments and other papers, 1499-1727; personal papers, letters, etc. of members of Kingsmill family,
2 CONT
2 CONT 1453-18th century; family and estate account books, 17th-19th centuries; Sydmonton estate account books, 18th-19th centuries; Sydmonton and general estate rentals, accounts, surveys and valuations, 17th-19th centuries; maps, 18th-
2 CONC 19th centuries; family and estate vouchers, 16th-19th centuries; pedigree material, printed material and miscellanea, 16th-19th centuries; papers of Archbishop Howley and Mrs Howley, 18th-19th centuries.
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional material (acquired 1986 and 1995) includes: Manorial documents (cartulary and court rolls), 1319-1639.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deeds and leases (lands in Church Oakley, Kingsclere and Litchfield, and lands in Berkshire, Dorset, London, Somerset, Warwickshire, and many deeds re Irish lands, 13th-19th centuries.
2 CONT
2 CONT Estate papers (accounts, vouchers, rentals, valuations and surveys, papers re tithes and taxation, correspondence, ledgers and household accounts), 17th-19th centuries.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family and official papers, including papers re family history, 18th-20th centuries, legal papers, 18th-19th centuries; papers re Admiral Sir Robert Kingsmill (1st Baronet), late 18th-early 19th centuries, Major Sir Robert Brice K
2 CONC ingsmill (2nd Baronet), late 18th-early 19th centuries, and Colonel Sir John Kingsmill (commander of the Battle Axe Guards, Ireland), early-mid 19th century; papers re families connected to Kingsmill family, (Garrett, Willmott and
2 CONC  Marsland families), 19th-early 20th centuries. PersonName Kingsmill; family; Sydmonton AdminHistory Many documents in the 1986 purchase relate to Admiral Sir Robert Brice Kingsmill (1730-1805) and John Woodham (died 1859), who to
2 CONC ok the name of Kingsmill on his marriage to Sir Robert's great-niece, Elizabeth Katherine, in 1824. A substancial number of papers also survive from the time of William Kingsmill 'the Lunatic' (1685-1766), mainly relating to his e
2 CONC states which were managed apparently scrupulously by his 'Committee' from 1709.
2 CONT
2 CONT The second collection of papers contains few deeds of title, with most of these relating to the family's Irish estates. The Irish connection is illustrated by the records relating to Sir John Kingsmill's command of the Battle-Axe 
2 CONC Guards of Dublin Castle, 1828-1832. RelatedMaterial Detailed family trees, with helpful biographical details, can be ordered by quoting 19M61/4183
2 CONT
