2 CONC Knights of Eng. ii. 157. 7. N and Q (ser. 10), xii. 332. 8. CPR Ire. Chas. I, 47. 9. VCH Herts. iii. 464. 10. C181/3, ff. 91v, 128, 184v. 11. SP16/20/23. 12. PROB 11/147, f. 140v; CSP Dom. 1625-6, pp. 411, 572; G.E. Aylmer, King’s
2 CONC  Servants, 287. 13. C2/Jas.I/H7/16. 14. Chauncy, Herts. i. 535; VCH Herts. iii. 464. 15. HMC Hastings, iv. 203. 16. CSP Dom. 1619-23, p. 258. 17. C78/295/3. 18. E. de Villiers, ‘Parl. Bors. Restored by the House of Commons 1621-41
2 CONC ’, EHR, lxvii. 191; L. Stone, ‘Electoral Infl. of the 2nd earl of Salisbury’, EHR, lxxi. 391-3. 19. Villiers, 192. 20. Wilts. Arch. Mag. lxxviii. 72. 21. SP16/20/23; CJ, i. 818a. 22. PROB 11/151, f. 280v. 23. Chauncy, Herts. i. 53
2 CONC 6.
