1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Probably second generation immigrant from Normandy.  He and his father purchased lands in Dorset, England, called Damory Court in or near Blandford Forum.  He was a nobleman.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN RYVES (John or Sir John of Damory Court in Dorset)
2 CONT *c 1514 - c 1549
2 CONT *Born in England, probably
2 CONT *Occupation: Unknown
2 CONT *Spouse = Amy Harvey of Tarant Launceston
2 CONT *Biographical: Unknown
2 CONT *His issue:
2 CONT **i. John Ryves = Elizabeth Mervyn
2 CONT **ii. Mary Ryves, b c 1538 = William Aden
2 CONT **iii. Margaret Ryves, b c 1540; = 11Dec1559 to Richard Lawrence of Steepleton
2 CONT **iv. Jane Ryves; b c 1542 = Thomas Sydenham of Wynford Eagle
2 CONT **v. Robert Ryves, 1544-1576
2 CONT **vi. Richard Ryves, b c 1547 (see #12)                              
2 CONT **vii. Thomas Ryves, b c 1549, d after 1596 
2 CONT *Will Dated 1547, Will proved 11 Feb 1549
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT John Ryves lived at Damory Court (Dorset) and predeceased his father. He made his will in 1547 and died shortly thereafter. 
