1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Matriculated to Queen's College, Oxford in 1650. Student of the Middle Temple (1651). Appointed one of the Deputy Lord Lieutenants of the county of Dorset in 1672. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at bachelor and "last of the Damory line" might well be his epitaph for when he died childless as the head of the house of Ryves, the Damory Court was reunited with Ranston through the marriage of his heir-at-law, his fath
2 CONC er's sister, Elizabeth Ryves with 109. George Ryves of Ranston, her second cousin. This was the first time the two houses had been reunited in over five generations.
