1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/bb4ae/berkeley04.php#port3
2 CONT ((A))	Edward Berkeley of Pylle (d 1707) '''((ii)) Maurice Berkeley of Pylle (dsp 1717)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Berkeley-1011
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT Maurice Berkeley was the eldest surviving son and heir of Edward Berkeley of Pylle Somerset and his wife Elizabeth Ryves. He was born at Pylle on 25 September and baptised there on 2 October. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT At age 16, he matriculated at Wadham College Oxford on 15 June 1697. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was named as eldest son and executor in his father's 1701 Will. [3] Following his father's retirement from Parliament, he stood successfully for his seat of Wells in 1705, joining the Tory faction. He regained the seat in 1710.
2 CONT
2 CONT He did not live long enough to have a prominent career in Parliament, and died unmarried by 1717.
2 CONT
2 CONT In his Will [4] dated 19 May 1712 and proved 8 May 1717, he left his estate to his younger brother William, with legacies to his mother and to his cousins Mary and Margaret Bayley.
2 CONT
2 CONT His burial does not appear to be recorded in the Pylle parish register, which is corrupted for that period.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT ↑ Parish Register of Pylle Somerset 1591-1759, Img 17/27 Ancestry UK
2 CONT ↑ "Bennell-Bloye". Alumni Oxonienses 1500-1714. Ed. Joseph Foster(Oxford, 1891), British History Online. Web. 20 July 2024. Oxon
2 CONT ↑ Will of Edward Berkeley of Pylle, Somerset, dated 20 January 1700/1 and proved 2 July 1707. PROB 11/495/307
2 CONT ↑ Will of Maurice Berkeley of Pill, Somerset PROB 11/558/50
