1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT === Biography: John Coplestone III (c. 1436 – abt 1472)
2 CONT
2 CONT John Coplestone III was a 15th-century English gentleman belonging to the influential Coplestone family of Devon. As the second son of a high-ranking administrative family, his life reflects the mid-15th-century practice of distri
2 CONC buting family influence across various regional centers in the West Country.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lineage and Early Life
2 CONT
2 CONT John was the son of John Coplestone II (d. 1458), a lawyer and three-time Member of Parliament, and Elizabeth Hawley (d. 1457), the sole heiress of the prominent Dartmouth merchant John Hawley the Younger.[^1] He was the brother o
2 CONC f Philip Coplestone (the heir to the main family seat) and Walter Coplestone (the progenitor of the Bowden branch).
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT John III married Joan Coppleton.[^2] While the eldest branch of the family focused on the inherited lands in Colebrooke and the Hawley properties in Dartmouth, John and Joan’s line established its own localized presence in Devon.
2 CONT
2 CONT The union produced the following known children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Anne Copplestone: Mentioned in family records as a daughter of this branch.[^3]
2 CONT * Agnes Coplestone: Who married into the Maggs family and is frequently recorded as Agnes Maggs.[^4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Historical Position
2 CONT
2 CONT John III lived during a period of significant growth for the Coplestone family. His position as the "middle" brother meant he occupied a rank of local importance, supporting the family's broader political interests in Devon while 
2 CONC his siblings managed the larger manorial estates at Colebrooke and Bowden.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===NGS Style Register Report
2 CONT
2 CONT First Generation
2 CONT
2 CONT John Coplestone III was born circa 1422 in Devon, England, the son of John Coplestone and Elizabeth Hawley. He died after 1458. He married Joan Coppleton circa 1445.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John and Joan (Coppleton) Coplestone:
2 CONT
2 CONT # i. Anne Copplestone.
2 CONT # ii. Agnes Coplestone. She married [—] Maggs.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Footnotes
2 CONT
