1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT === Biography: Elizabeth West (c. 1475 – c. 1540)
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth West was a 15th-century heiress from Kent. Her significance to the Meggs family is paramount, as she provided the "West Inheritance" that fueled the family's transition into the higher landed gentry of the West Country.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lineage and Heritage
2 CONT
2 CONT The Geni profile identifies her as the daughter of Hugh West. While 15th-century records for minor gentry are often fragmented, the Visitation of Dorset (1565) provides the most reliable contemporary evidence of her status. She is
2 CONC  explicitly recorded as the sister and heir to Thomas West. This status as an "heir" indicates that her brother died without legitimate issue, passing the family's Kentish estates to Elizabeth and, by extension, her husband Willia
2 CONC m Meggs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: William Meggs of Canterbury
2 CONT
2 CONT She married William Meggs of Canterbury, Gent., circa 1475. This union joined two Kentish families of the "Gentleman" class. Through Elizabeth, the Meggs family acquired the social and financial leverage that allowed their son, Th
2 CONC omas, to eventually move to the Isle of Ely and marry into the prestigious Coplestone family of Devon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth was the mother of the three verified children who define the Canterbury/Dorset branch:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Thomas Megges (c. 1480 – 1559): Eldest son and heir; progenitor of the Meggs of Bradford Peverell.
2 CONT # Alice Meggs (c. 1485 – ?): Married Ralf Touke of the Kentish and Hertfordshire gentry.
2 CONT # Katherine Meggs (c. 1488 – ?): Married Peter Bruyne.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===NGS Style Register Report
2 CONT
2 CONT First Generation
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth West was born circa 1475 in England and died circa 1540. She married William Meggs of Canterbury, Gent., circa 1475.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William and Elizabeth (West) Meggs:
2 CONT
2 CONT # i. Thomas Megges, Gent. (c. 1480 – 1559).
2 CONT # ii. Alice Meggs (c. 1485 – ?). She married Ralf Touke.
2 CONT # iii. Katherine Meggs (c. 1488 – ?). She married Peter Bruyne.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Researcher’s Note: The "Judith" Conflation
2 CONT
2 CONT The Geni profile manager uses the name "Elizabeth or Judith West." This is a result of a 19th/20th-century genealogical "smash-up" that researchers must carefully untangle:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Elizabeth West (Historical): Documented in the Visitation of Dorset (1565) as the "sister and heir to Thomas West" and wife of William Meggs of Canterbury. Her identity is anchored in contemporary Tudor heraldic records.
2 CONT *Judith West (Theorized): Introduced in 20th-century works (notably by Fayette Mark Meigs in 1890) as the "sister of the Bishop of Ely" and wife of a London Alderman.
2 CONT *Verdict: The primary 16th-century records (The Visitations) only recognize Elizabeth. The name "Judith" and the connection to a "Bishop of Ely" are later additions or conflations with a different branch not supported by contempor
2 CONC ary Tudor evidence for this specific line.
2 CONT
2 CONT Footnotes
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Bibliography
2 CONT # Harvey, William. The Visitation of Dorsetshire, A.D. 1565. Edited by Walter C. Metcalfe. Exeter: William Pollard & Co., 1887. https://archive.org/details/visitationofdors00harvuoft
2 CONT # Meigs, Henry Benjamin. Record of the Descendants of Vincent Meigs. Baltimore: John S. Bridges & Co., 1901. https://archive.org/stream/recordofdescenda00meig
2 CONT # Metcalfe, Walter C., ed. The Visitation of the County of Dorset, 1623. London: Mitchell and Hughes, 1885. https://archive.org/details/visitationofcoun00stge
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
