1 NAME Alice /Meggs or Meigs/
2 GIVN Alice
2 SURN Meggs or Meigs
2 _MARNM Tooke
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1482
2 PLAC Canterbury, Kent, , England
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Based on the Visitation of Dorset (1565) and related records from the Visitation of Hertfordshire, Alice Meggs (also recorded as Meigs) was the daughter of William Meggs of Canterbury, Gent., and his wife Elizabeth West.
2 CONT +2
2 CONT
2 CONT Parentage and Origin
2 CONT
2 CONT Contrary to some digital profiles that place her origins solely in London, the primary heraldic record identifies her family as being established in Canterbury, Kent.
2 CONT +1
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: William Meggs of Canterbury, co. Kent, Gent..
2 CONT +1
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Elizabeth West, who was the sister and heir of Thomas West.
2 CONT +1
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband: Alice married Ralf Touke (also spelled Toke or Tooke).
2 CONT +1
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings: Her brother was Thomas Megges of Downham in the Isle of Ely (the ancestor of the Meggs of Bradford Peverell), and her sister was Katherine, who married Peter Bruyne.
2 CONT +1
2 CONT
2 CONT The Canterbury vs. London Distinction
2 CONT
2 CONT While a related branch of the family (the "Merchant" branch) was prominent as Citizens and Drapers of London, Alice's father is specifically styled "of Canterbury". The confusion in some online trees often stems from the fact that
2 CONC  her brother Thomas lived in the Isle of Ely and his descendants eventually settled in Dorset, leading to a wide geographical spread of records for this single gentry family.
2 CONT +1
2 CONT
2 CONT Disambiguation Note
2 CONT
2 CONT It is important to distinguish her father, William Meggs of Canterbury (husband of Elizabeth West), from the later William Meggs, Citizen and Draper of London (d. 1559), who was the husband of Katherine Haugh. Alice's lineage is r
2 CONC ooted in the gentry of Kent through the West inheritance.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
