1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 8. William CHURCHILL of Dorchester was born in 1541 in Dorchester, Dorsetshire, England. He signed a will on 12 Mar 1599. He died before 18 Nov 1602.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of John CHURCHILL of Dorchester & Edith BOND
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Miss (Missy) SWAYNE (daughter of John SWAYNE of Blandford and Agnes RYVES) in 1565 in Dorchester, Dorsetshire, England. Miss SWAYNE was born about 1545 in Blandford, Dorset, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William CHURCHILL of Dorchester and Miss SWAYNE had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT #        +15       i.       Eldest son CHURCHILL (born about 1565, Given name unknown.)
2 CONT #        +16       ii.       John CHURCHILL of Stinsford and Muston, Dorset (born about 1566).
2 CONT #        +17       iii.       Virtue CHURCHILL (born about 1568).
2 CONT #        +18       iv.       Grace CHURCHILL (born about 1570).
2 CONT #        +19       v.       Ann CHURCHILL (born in 1572).
2 CONT #        +20       vi.       Mary CHURCHILL (born about 1574).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~fordingtondorset/Files2/Dorchesterfreeschoolb.html The Free School] (1567-1680) [Also known as 'The Thomas Hardye' or 'Dorchester Grammar School'] -  The 10 Trustees for the endowment
2 CONC  made by Thomas Hardye of Melcombe Regis on 3rd August 1579.  By Michael Russell OPC for Dorchester © September 2009  (Revised July 2010)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7.  William Churchill'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >William Churchill was born in Dorchester c1541. He is shown as the head of the family in the 1623 visitation but this does not name his wife. He married in 1565 in Dorchester to the daughter of John Swayre of Blandford and his wi
2 CONC fe Agnes Ryves but she only appears to have been known as 'Missy'. They had 6 children one of which was John Churchill of Muston & Stinsford (born about 1566) who married Eleanor Miller of Came and their descendants are covered in
2 CONC  the visitation.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://genforum.genealogy.com/churchill/messages/1168.html
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=zCgEAAAAIAAJ&vq=Gould&pg=PA28#v=onepage&q&f=true The Visitation of the County of Dorset:] Taken in the Year 1623  By Sir Henry Saint-George, Henry St. George, Samson Lennard.  Page 28
