1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas Churchill of Arncot and Blackthorn = Joan. (Thomas: - 1615, buried at Ambrosden and the Arncots, The Deddington and Steeple Claydon branches of Churchills descend from he and Joan) (Joan: ?, had 10 children)
2 CONC  (source: http://www.deddingtonhistory.uk/__data/assets/pdf_file/0015/12912/ChurchillChroniclescilckablecontentsjan15.pdf and https://www.geni.com/people/Penelope-Churchill/6000000025795068892)
2 CONT
2 CONT Note on Thomas Churchill of Arncot: Thomas lived in Blackthorn but owned property in Nether Arncot, both of these places, being chapelries of Ambrosden almost obliterated by the buildings and sheds of the Central Ordnance Depot, b
2 CONC uilt here between 1941 and 1945. It covers 12 and a half square miles surrounding Ambrosden and the Arncots, extending as far as Piddington. Thomas died in 1615 and was buried at Ambrosden, leaving a will, which mentioned his ten 
2 CONC children, who were all aged under 21. After his death, it seems that his widow went to live in Steeple Claydon, where she married again. (from: The ‘Churchill Chronicles’) 
