1 NAME John /Churchill/
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Churchill
2 _MARNM Churchill
2 NICK Rev Churchill
1 NAME John Churchill, of Wootton Glanville
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1595
2 ADDR
3 CITY Mintern
3 STAE England
1 BURI
2 DATE 1652
2 PLAC Steeple, Wareham, Dorset, England
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 6 APR 1652
2 ADDR
3 CITY Glanvilles Wootton
3 STAE England
1 OCCU Lawyer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Churchill held the office of Deputy Registrar of Chancery before 1639.2 He lived at Minterne, Dorset, England.3 He was admitted to Middle Temple.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1660-1690/member/churchill-winston-1620-88
2 CONT
2 CONT Churchill constructed for himself an impressive pedigree, but he was in fact the grandson of a Dorset copyholder. His father '''John Churchill''' studied law at the Middle Temple, and became deputy registrar of Chancery, in which 
2 CONC capacity he acted as jackal, and later Judas, to Bacon. 
2 CONT
2 CONT During the Civil War John, who had resigned his Chancery post to his cousin (Sir) John Churchill, was active as commissioner of array, compounding for £440 in 1646 on property valued at £245 p.a. .4
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT * 4.N. and Q. for Som. and Dorset, xxvii. 190-2; Gen. Mag. xv. 110; Black Bk. L. Inn, ii. 458-63; SP23/186/410-16; Cal. Comm. Adv. Money, 1092.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From  [http://books.google.com/books?id=IkhAAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA191&ots=ul23pCmAxi&dq=Bartholomew%20Cherchile&pg=PA192#v=onepage&q=Bartholomew%20Cherchile&f=false Collin's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Churchill, eldest Son and Heir of Jasper, by Elizabeth Chaplet, was of the Society of the Middle-Temple, where, by his Proficiency in the Study of the Laws, he made an Addition to his Estate, and was seated at Mtntern in the 
2 CONC County of Dorset. He married Sarah, Daughter and Co-heir of Sir Henry Winston, of Standiston, in the County of Gloucester, by Dionifi his Wife, Daughter and Co-heir of Sir Thomas Bond, Kt. and by her was Father of Sir Winston Chur
2 CONC chill, born at Wotton-Glanville in the County of Dorset
2 CONT
2 CONT
