1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Family legend has it that Harriett Ann Moore (as related by her son Jack Green to his children) was born on a bullock wagon whilst on the way to Bathurst for her birth.  A destination they made after the birth.     Her grandson, M
2 CONC ax Green remembers seeing his father being coaxed onto his mother's lap and him being very embarrassed. To the young person that he was Max remembers her as an old lady dressed in black.  She was a kind and gentle woman with a goo
2 CONC d sense of fun.  Harriet enjoyed a bit of a bet occasionally but because she was living with her daughter Alma who was a strict Baptist, it was a little difficult for her to get her bets on.  When visiting her at Coraki, her grand
2 CONC children would sneak out to place her bets for her.  She always made an excuse not to go to church on Sundays so she could stay home and listen to the race results on her tiny little radio.     Harriett moved from Coraki to Lewish
2 CONC am to live with her son Carl and daughter in law Carra until her death.
