1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sybil de la Bere and her husband Thomas Crophull did not have any male issue & she predeceased her husband.  [established in the IPM of her husband Thomas. See below. ]
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Sibilla de la Bere1,2,3,4,5,6
2 CONT *'''F, #22390, b. 19 May 1338, d. before 18 November 1381
2 CONT *Father      Sir John de la Bere2,3,4,5,6 b. c 1308
2 CONT *Mother     Agnes Turberville
2 CONT *'''     Sibilla de la Bere was born on 19 May 1338. A settlement for the marriage Sibilla de la Bere and Sir Thomas de Crophull was made on 18 October 1371; They had 1 daughter (Agnes, wife of Sir Walter Devereux, of Sir John Par
2 CONC r, & of John Merbury, Esq.).3,4,5,6 Sibilla de la Bere died before 18 November 1381.2,3,6
2 CONT
2 CONT 19 May 1382, Westminster To the treasurer and the barons of the exchequer. Order not to suffer John de Crophulle knight hereafter to be troubled by reason of his homage for the manor of Neubold Verdoun co. Leycester, except the kn
2 CONC ights' fees and advowsons thereto pertaining and 80 acres of wood, one stewpond and 4l. of rent therein; as upon the finding of an inquisition, taken by George del Castell' then escheator, that the said John held that manor withou
2 CONC t exception in chief by knight service as parcel of the barony of Theobald Verdoun, that [by] the late king's licence he gave the same with the exceptions aforesaid to Thomas de Crophulle his son, Sibyl wife of the said Thomas and
2 CONC  the heirs male of their bodies with remainder to himself and his heirs, and that Sibyl died in the lifetime of her husband and the said Thomas died after without issue male between them begotten, wherefore by form of the gift the
2 CONC  premises ought to revert to the said John, on 7 March last for a fine by him paid in the hanaper the king respited the said John's homage until Midsummer, and commanded livery of the premises to be given him; and the king has tak
2 CONC en his homage for the premises.
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Family      Sir Thomas de Crophull b. c 1350, d. 18 Nov 1381
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Agnes Crophull+2,7,3,4,5,6 b. c 1372, d. 3 Feb 1436
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S6951] Unknown author, Wallop Family, p. 242, 261.
2 CONT * 2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 249.
2 CONT * 3.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 2.
2 CONT * 4.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 297-298.
2 CONT * 5.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. IV, p. 304.
2 CONT * 6.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. V, p. 248.
2 CONT * 7.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 565.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p745.htm#i22390 
2 CONT *'''Sibyl de la Bere1
2 CONT *'''F, #190807, d. before 1381
2 CONT *Last Edited=2 Apr 2009
2 CONT *'''     Sibyl de la Bere was the daughter of Sir John de la Bere.1 She married Thomas de Crophill, son of Sir John Crophill and Margery de Verdun, circa 18 October 1371.1 She died before 1381.1
2 CONT *'''      From circa 18 October 1371, her married name became de Crophill.1
2 CONT *'''Child of Sibyl de la Bere and Thomas de Crophill
2 CONT ** 1.Agnes Crophill+1 b. c 1371, d. 3 Feb 1436
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S79] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry (Baltimore, Maryland, U.S.A.: Genealogical Publishing Company, 2004), page 249. Hereinafter cited as Plantagenet Ancestry.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p19081.htm#i190807www.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Sibyl de “Crophull” La Bere Crophill
2 CONT BIRTH unknown
2 CONT DEATH unknown
2 CONT BURIAL
2 CONT Burial Details Unknown
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID 175449576 
2 CONT
2 CONT Magna Carta Ancestry pg 247 Crophill 8 names Sibyl de la Bere daugher of Sir John de la Bere as Thomas' wife. Sibyl predeceased Thomas. She had one daughter Agnes.
2 CONT
2 CONT I believe the daughter to be at the memorial titled Agnes Crophull #111729994 but the manager does not agree with the spelling variant.
