2 CONT *''''''Blanche MILBOURNE 
2 CONT *''''''Born: ABT 1474
2 CONT *''''''Died: 1557
2 CONT *''''''Notes: born in England but living in a Welsh environment, Blanche was heiress of Milbourne. She was married first in 1494 to James Whitney of Whitney and Pen-cwm. Her dowry was the manor of Ilcomb in Gloucestershire. When s
2 CONC he was widowed, remarried soon after, taking as her second husband William Herbert of Troy Parva. In Aug 1502 entertained King Henry VII and Elizabeth of York at Troy House near Monmouth. In 1516, William Herbert was knighted. Bla
2 CONC nche received part of the estate of Edward Stafford, 3rd Duke of Buckingham, when Henry VIII confiscated it. In the late 1520s and early 1530s, she was probably part of the Countess of Worcester’s household and may have acted as g
2 CONC overness to the Earl’s children. She may have been put in charge of Princess Mary’s household as early as 1531, when Mary was separated from her mother, Catalina of Aragon. Sometimes referred to as Lady Herbert and other times as 
2 CONC Lady Troy, Blanche was the one charged with giving their earliest lessons to both Princess Elizabeth and Prince Edward. In each household in turn she became Lady Mistress when Lady Bryan relinquished that post. She carried Elizabe
2 CONC th’s train at the christening of Prince Edward in 1537. She was still in the Lady Elizabeth’s household as late as 1545 but had left by the time King Henry died in 1547. Lady Troy retired to Troy House, living there into her late 
2 CONC seventies. Blanche Milborne’s niece and goddaughter, Blanche Parry, was Queen Elizabeth’s Confidante.
2 CONT *Father: Simon MILBOURNE (Sir)
2 CONT *Mother: Jane BASKERVILLE
2 CONT *''''''Married 1: James WHITNEY (Sir) (b. ABT 1472 - d. 30 Jun 1499/1500) (son of Robert Whitney and Constance Touchet) ABT 1490, Whitney, England 
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Robert WHITNEY (Sir Knight) (b. 1491 - d. AFT 1555) (m.1 Margaret Wye - m.2 Elizabeth Morgan) 
2 CONT **2. James WHITNEY (b. ABT 1493 - d. 1546) 
2 CONT **3. Watkin WHITNEY (m. Margaret Riece) 
2 CONT **4. Elizabeth WHITNEY (b. ABT 1496) (m. Thomas Morgan of Arkston) 
2 CONT **5. Anne WHITNEY (b. ABT 1497) (m. Henry Carey) 
2 CONT **6. Eustace WHITNEY (b. ABT 1498) (m. Anne Parry) 
2 CONT *''''''Married 2: William HERBERT of Troye (Sir) ABT 1499 
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **6. Charles HERBERT (Sir Knight)
2 CONT **7. Thomas HERBERT
2 CONT **8. Son HERBERT
