1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Family notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/soc.genealogy.medieval/3LapNz_UuRY
2 CONT
2 CONT Amice (Amy) Pembridge, dead by 1375, married Sir John Burley KG, had issue at least Sir Richard Burley KG, and William; (?) also Elizabeth who married Sir John Hopton, a quo Corbet of Moreton C.?). The Burleys inherited Fordingbri
2 CONC dge etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hawise's sister Amice married Sir John Burley KG (d.c.1383), the elder brother of Sir Simon Burley who was b.1336? (ODNB) and ex.1388. John and Amice had Sir Richard KG (d.1387 in Spain, sp ), William (dsp 1388), Roger (issue fail
2 CONC ed 1445) and Isabel who m. Sir John Hopton, with issue (descendant Thomas H. s. to Burley properties in 1445),
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Pembridge-4
2 CONT
2 CONT Amice was the daughter of Richard Pembrugge.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amice married Sir John, son of Sir Roger Burley and Lucy Gilford. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Amice de Burele was noted in the Inquisition Post Mortem of her nephew Henry Pembrugge, son of Richard, in 1375. Henry's heirs were Richard de Burele, knight, son of Amice de Burele, sister of Richard de Pembrugg, and Thomas Barre
2 CONC , knight, son of Hawise, second sister of the same Richard. The heirs were both of full age.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT 'Parishes: Fordingbridge', in A History of the County of Hampshire: Volume 4, ed. William Page (London, 1911), pp. 567-577. British History Online http://www.british-history.ac.uk/vch/hants/vol4/pp567-577 [accessed 26 May 2020].
2 CONT
2 CONT >... The former was living in 1361, (fn. 63) but had apparently died before 1364, when the manor was granted in custody to Richard de Pembridge, (fn. 64) and two years later to Richard and his heirs. (fn. 65) Richard, then a knigh
2 CONC t, died in July 1375, and on the death of his only child Henry a few months later (fn. 66) the manor was divided between Richard de Burley and Thomas atte Barre, sons respectively of the two sisters and heirs of Sir Richard, Amice
2 CONC  and Hawise. Thomas, reserving a yearly rent, gave up his share to Richard de Burley, (fn. 67) who in 1386 settled the whole manor on himself and his wife Beatrice with remainder in default of issue male to Sir Simon Burley, to wh
2 CONC om it passed on his death a few years later. (fn. 68) After the execution of Sir Simon, the favourite of Richard II, in 1388 the manor again fell to the Crown, ... 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT *↑ A. E. Stamp, J. B. W. Chapman, Cyril Flower, M. C. B. Dawes and L. C. Hector, 'Inquisitions Post Mortem, Edward III, File 251', in Calendar of Inquisitions Post Mortem: Volume 14, Edward III (London, 1952), pp. 193-214. British
2 CONC  History Online http://www.british-history.ac.uk/inquis-post-mortem/vol14/pp193-214 [accessed 22 May 2020]. Inquisition Post Mortem of Henry, son and heir of Richard de Pembrugg, knight. Item 192.
2 CONT *↑ Calendar of the Fine Rolls. Vol. VIII. Edward III. AD 1368-1377. HMSO, 1924, p310-311 [1].
2 CONT *See also: Lewis, M. (2014, February 1). "Sir Richard de Pembrugge, Governor of Bamborough & Dover Castles, Chamberlain of the Household." ORTNCA. Web.
2 CONT *Lewis, M. (2014, February 10). "Amice Pembrugge #24040," citing: Wallop family; various works by Douglas Richardson . ORTNCA. Web. citing: Wallop Family, p. 160; Magna Carta Ancestry, 2011, 2nd ed, III, p. 453; Royal Ancestry, IV
2 CONC , p. 493-4; Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 612-613.
2 CONT * https://www.genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00048330&tree=LEO
2 CONT * Magna Carta Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, 2nd Edition ... page 207.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=8JcbV309c5UC&lpg=PA207&ots=kwqCKYKP82&dq=John%20de%20Burley%2C%20K.G.&pg=PA207#v=onepage&q&f=false Go
2 CONC ogleBooks] page 453. [https://books.google.com/books?id=8JcbV309c5UC&lpg=PA207&ots=kwqCKYKP82&dq=John%20de%20Burley%2C%20K.G.&pg=RA2-PA453#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks]
2 CONT *http://archiver.rootsweb.ancestry.com/th/read/GEN-MEDIEVAL/2006-11/1162898903
2 CONT *http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=jweber&id=I37258
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Amicia (Anne) Pembrugge (Richard /Pembrugge/, of Clehonger & Monnington,Sir, Henry /Pembrugge/, of Newland & Clehonger, Sir, Henry /Pembrugge/, of Weston & Leigh, Sir, Henry /Pembrugge/, of Weston & Leigh) was born ABT 1325 in For
2 CONC dingbridge, Hampshire, England, and died BEF 1375. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married John de Burley, son of Simon de /Burley/& Culmington, Sir. He was born ABT 1325 in Birley, Weobley, Herefordshire, England, and died 1383. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Amicia (Anne) /Pembrugge/, Heir of Fordingbridge and John de /Burley/, KG, Sir include
2 CONT *Roger de Burley was born ABT 1352 in Birley, Weobley, Herefordshire, England, and died 1399 in Broncroft Castle, Tugford, Shropshire, England.
2 CONT *Isabel (Elizabeth) de Burley was born ABT 1357 in Birley, Weobley, Herefordshire, England.
