1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Margaret Ferrars=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Margaret Ferrars was the daughter of Sir Edmund Ferrars.
2 CONT *  As a result of her marriage, Margaret Ferrars was styled as Baroness Beauchamp of Powick on 2 May 1447. Her last will was dated 29 January 1487.1
2 CONT * Died after 29 January 1487
2 CONT * Margaret de Ferrers Beauchamp Find A Grave - https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/105783271/margaret-beauchamp
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: John Beauchamp, 1st Baron Beauchamp of Powick, KG,1, before 1434.1  John (died April 1475) was an English nobleman and administrator. He was the son and eventual heir of Sir William Beauchamp of Powick in Worcestershire
2 CONC  (ca. 1370–ca. 1421), Constable of Gloucester, and his wife, Katherine Usflete (d. after 1436).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Galfridus de Beauchamp''' 2 d. after 1487
2 CONT * '''Richard Beauchamp, 2nd Baron Beauchamp of Powick'''+1 b. c 1435, d. 19 Jan 1502/3
2 CONT
2 CONT =Short History=
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Sir Edmund Ferrers, Knight of Chartley, Staffordshire, descendant of King Edward I, by Ellen de la Roche, daughter and co-heiress to Sir Thomas. Granddaughter of Sir Robert Ferrers and Margaret le Despenser, Thomas de 
2 CONC la Roche and Elizabeth Bermingham.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Sir John Beauchamp of Powick and Acton Beauchamp, son of Sir William Beauchamp and Katherine Usflete. They married before 1434 and had two sons, Sir Richard, 2nd Lord Beauchamp and Thomas.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1448, Margaret received a papal indult allowing her to eat during Lent and on other fast days as she pleased due to weak health. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret's will was dated 29 Jan 1488. Both she and her husband were buried at Dominican Black Friars at Worcester.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Family=
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund de Ferrers, 5th Baron Ferrers of Chartley (1386–1435) was the son of Robert de Ferrers, 4th Baron Ferrers of Chartley and Margaret Le Despenser - a daughter of Edward le Despencer, 1st Baron le Despencer.
2 CONT He inherited the title of Baron Ferrers of Chartley upon his father's death in 1413 but was never summoned to parliament. Edmund fought in most of the great victories of King Henry V including the Battle of Agincourt and married H
2 CONC elen, daughter and co-heir of Thomas de la Roche, by whom he acquired large landed possessions, amongst which was that of Castle Bromwich in the county of Warwickshire. Edmund de Ferrers, 5th Baron Ferrers of Chartley died aged 49
2 CONC  in 1435.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The couple had two sons and one daughter'''
2 CONT
2 CONT *''' Edmund''' (to whom his estates were entailed) 
2 CONT * '''William''' who became William, 6th Baron Ferrers of Chartley 
2 CONT * '''Margaret de Ferrers''' who married John Beauchamp, 1st Baron Beauchamp of Powick becoming Lady Beaucamp of Powick.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT *  G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct or
2 CONC  Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 47. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT * Douglas Richardson; Magna Carta Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, 2nd Edition p.392 'Friaries: Worcester', in A History of the County of Worcester: Volume 2, ed. J W Willis-Bund and William Page (London, 1971)
2 CONC , pp. 167-173. 
2 CONT * British History Online http://www.british-history.ac.uk/vch/worcs/vol2/pp167-173 [accessed 13 May 2018].
2 CONT * Oxford Dictionary of National Biography, G.E. Cokayne.(1910–1959). 
2 CONT * The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct or Dormant.
2 CONT * Wikivisually - https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Edmund_de_Ferrers,_5th_Baron_Ferrers_of_Chartley
2 CONT * Ancestral Roots of Certain American Colonists Who Came to America Before 1700, 8th Edition; William R Beall; 
2 CONT * The Royal Descents of 600 Immigrants to the American Colonies or the United States, Final Edition; Gary Boyd Roberts; Genealogical Publishing Co, Baltimore, MD, 2008;personal copy,.
2 CONT * U.S. and International Marriage Records, 1560-1900; ; Yates Publishing.
2 CONT * The Peerage, web site: http://thepeerage.com/; Darryl Lundy.
