1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''John Leighton, Esq., Sheriff & Escheater of Shropshire, Steward of Bishop's Castle, Constable of Oswestry Castle1,2,3
2 CONT *'''M, #44635, b. 1430, d. circa 4 February 1496
2 CONT *Father      Edward Leighton1,4,5
2 CONT *Mother     Elizabeth Stapleton1,4,5 d. b 1444
2 CONT *'''     John Leighton, Esq., Sheriff & Escheater of Shropshire, Steward of Bishop's Castle, Constable of Oswestry Castle was born in 1430 at of Stretton-en-le-Dale, Shropshire, England.1,2,3 He married Ankaret Burgh, daughter of 
2 CONC Sir John Burgh, Sheriff of Shropshire and Jane Clopton, before 1453; They had 1 son (Sir Thomas).1,2,3 John Leighton, Esq., Sheriff & Escheater of Shropshire, Steward of Bishop's Castle, Constable of Oswestry Castle died circa 4 F
2 CONC ebruary 1496.1,2,3
2 CONT *'''Family      Ankaret Burgh d. c 1471
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Sir Thomas Leighton, Sheriff of Shropshire1 b. 1454
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S147] Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage, Baronetage, and Knightage, 1938 ed., by Sir Bernard Burke, p., 1523.
2 CONT * 2.[S6] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry: 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 94.
2 CONT * 3.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. II, p. 640-641.
2 CONT * 4.[S6] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry: 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 93.
2 CONT * 5.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. II, p. 640.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1485.htm#i44635 ______________________
2 CONT *'''John Leighton1
2 CONT *'''M, #496927, d. 1493
2 CONT *Last Edited=17 Nov 2013
2 CONT *'''     John Leighton was the son of Edward Leighton and Elizabeth Stapleton.2 He married Ankaret Burgh, daughter of Sir John Burgh and Jane Clopton.1 He died in 1493.1
2 CONT *'''      He acquired the Manors of Cardeston, Loton and Wattlesborough, Shropshire.1 William, married Margery, daughter and coheir of Sir Fulk Sprencheaux, of Plash, Salop, and was ancestor of the extinct LEIGHTONs of Plash) and 
2 CONC a daughter (Elizabeth, married William Lyster, of Rowton).1 He held the office of Constable of Oswestry Castle.1 He held the office of Steward of Montgomery Castle, for Richard, Duke of York, but he switched to King Henry VII befo
2 CONC re the Battle of Bosworth.1 He held the office of Sheriff of Shropshire.1 He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Shropshire in 1460.1 He lived at Stretton-in-le-Dale, Shropshire, England.1
2 CONT *'''Children of John Leighton and Ankaret Burgh
2 CONT ** 1.William Leighton1
2 CONT ** 2.Elizabeth Leighton1
2 CONT ** 3.Cuthbert Leighton1
2 CONT ** 4.Sir Thomas Leighton+2 b. 1454
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S37] Volume 2, page 2294. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT * 2.[S37] See. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p49693.htm#i496927 _______________
2 CONT *William de la Pole (of Mawddwy)
2 CONT *Sir William de la Pole (died before 1319) was the fourth son of Gruffydd ap Gwenwynwyn and would have inherited ....
2 CONT * .... Sir William was succeeded in this lordship by his son Gruffydd (who was of age in 1319), his son, another William, and his son John. John's son Fulk predeceased his father without issue in about 1414. Accordingly, Mawddwy t
2 CONC hen passed to Fulk's sister Elizabeth, who married Hugh Burgh. Hugh Burgh's son John (1414–1471) owned the lordship, but only left four daughters who were John's coheiresses.
2 CONT *One of Sir John Burgh's daughters, Elisabeth (Isabella) de Burgh (died 1522) married Sir John Lingen (died 1505), buried Aymestrey, Herefordshire and ancestor of the Sir Henry Lingen of Lingen, Sutton and Stoke Edith (died 1662),
2 CONC the family of Burton-Lingen of Longnor Hall and the 1st Baron Lingen (died 1905, buried Brompton cemetery, London).{Visitation of Shropshire in 1623, Robert Tresswell Somerset herald }
2 CONT *'''Another daughter Anchoretta de Burgh, married John Leighton of Streeton, later of Wattlesborough and Loton, Sheriff of Shropshire (d 1493)''' as can be seen on Stirnet.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_de_la_Pole_(of_Mawddwy) ________________________
