1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT MP, Constituency Dates: 1542 MONTGOMERYSHIRE
2 CONT
2 CONT Family and Education
2 CONT
2 CONT b. by 1518, s. of James Leche of Newtown by da. of Sir Robert Stonefield of Carden, Cheshire. m. Elizabeth (?illegit.) da. of Sir Thomas Leighton of Wattlesborough, Salop, 1s. 2da. suc. fa. by 1518.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of an esquire of the body to Henry VII, James Leche was described as ‘of the new town of Cydewain’ in one of the two chancery cases in which he was engaged in the period 1538-44. He was almost certainly the Shropshire just
2 CONC ice of the peace of his name, for he married into that shire, but is to be distinguished from a namesake of Llawhaden, Pembrokeshire, who was both an esquire of the body and had Shropshire connexions.  One of the original justices
2 CONC  for Montgomeryshire, the shire’s first Member and its fourth sheriff (an office he was discharging during the third session of the Parliament), Leche made little mark in the closing years of his life. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The request contained in his will of 30 Dec. 1553 that he should be buried with Catholic rites wherever he should chance to die suggests that he was about to undertake a journey, and it was in London that he died between then and 
2 CONC the following 21 Feb., when the will was proved. One of his daughters married successively Charles Price and Andrew Vavasour of Newtown.3
2 CONT
2 CONT [1] LECHE, James (by 1518-54), of Newtown, Mont.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in The History of Parliament: the House of Commons 1509-1558, ed. S.T. Bindoff, 1982 Available from Boydell and Brewer
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ==Leche, of Carden. (Harl. MS. 1535.) 
2 CONT I finde one Sr Robert Stanford knight Lorde of the fourthe parte of the manor of Cawaredon had yssue James Leiche of Carden esqr. of the body to H. 7 who had James Leiche who had anne his daughter & heire first maried to Andrew Wi
2 CONC llsonne & after to Richard Price in Shropshire.  http://cheshire-heraldry.org.uk/visitations1613/1613.pdf
