2 CONT  HOPTON CASTLE. 
2 CONT
2 CONT SIR HENRY RIPLEY, BART. 
2 CONT
2 CONT IN 1268 Walter de Hopton was SherifF of Shropshire. He was a Judge of the  Exchequer, and was the first of the name associated with Shropshire. Hopton  was held as a knight's fee in the Fitzalan's Barony of Clun. In 1337 and in 13
2 CONC 64  Hoptons were Knights of the Shire, and in 1430 Thomas Hopton was SherifF, His  daughter and heiress married Sir Roger Corbet, of Morton, and in the family of  Corbet the castle remained till Elizabeth, daughter and heiress of 
2 CONC Robert Corbet, of  Moreton, married Sir Henry Wallop, Sheriff in 1606. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://archive.org/stream/shropshirehouses00leiguoft/shropshirehouses00leiguoft_djvu.txt
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Her Capetian lineage:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT #Hugh "Magnus" of Paris, count of Paris, duke of the Franks [First Capet]
2 CONT #Hugues Capet, roi des Francs
2 CONT #Robert II Capet, "the Pious" king of the Franks
2 CONT #Henry I, king of France
2 CONT #Philip Capet; Philip I, king of France
2 CONT #Louis VI the Fat, king of France
2 CONT #Louis VII the Young, king of France
2 CONT #Philip II Augustus, king of France
2 CONT #Louis VIII le Lion, roi de France
2 CONT #Louis IX the Saint, King of France
2 CONT #Philip III, "the Bold" king of France
2 CONT #Margaret of France, Queen consort of England
2 CONT #Thomas of Brotherton, 1st Earl of Norfolk
2 CONT #Margaret of Brotherton, Duchess of Norfolk
2 CONT #Elizabeth de Segrave, Baroness de Mowbray
2 CONT #Lady Margaret de Lucy (de Mowbray)
2 CONT #Sir Walter de Lucy, Joint Warden of the Welsh Marches
2 CONT #Eleanor Hopton (Lucy)
2 CONT #Elizabeth Stanley (Hopton)
2 CONT ----
