1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * originally buried at Shawbury Church but tomb of Richard and wife moved to Church of St. Bartholomew at  Moreton-Corbett. Sources: The family of Corbet; its life and times Vol. II by Sir Roland James Corbet, Bart
2 CONC  Augusta Elizabeth Brickdale, 1836-
2 CONT
2 CONT Photos of church and burials of Sir Richard Corbett and wife '''Margaret'''
2 CONT Source: Craig Thornber  https://thornber.net/england/htmlfiles/moretoncorbet.html
2 CONT There is a highly coloured tomb of Sir Robert Corbet of 1513 and his wife, '''who outlived him by fifty years.''' His effigy bears armour of the Tudor period with his head on a helmet and his feet on a lion. In the panels '''aroun
2 CONC d the tomb are shown six children and ten angels. The second 16th century tomb is of Richard Corbet of 1567. On the side panels are elephants and owls.''' 
2 CONT     Sources
2 CONT     The Buildings of England, by Nikolaus Pevsner, Penguin Books, 1958.
2 CONT       The King's England, Shropshire, by Arthur Mee, revised by E.T. Long, Hodder and Stoughton, first edition, 1939, revised and reset 1968.
