1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Tyrrell (c. 1430-c.1471), son of Thomas Tyrrell (d. 1475) and Abbe Marney, married, firstly, '''Eleanora Darcy''', daughter of Sir Robert Darcy, Keeper of the Writs of Common Pleas, Burgess of Malden and Alice Filongle
2 CONC y, circa 1441.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Tyrrell married, secondly, Eleanor Hungerford, daughter of Sir Robert Hungerford, 2nd Lord Hungerford and Margaret Botreaux, circa 30 June 1470.[2][3][4][5][6][7][8][9]
2 CONT
2 CONT William was [NOT] killed at the Battle of Barnet on 14 April 1471.[10]
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 1 Eleanora Darcy b. c 1418, d. 1476
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT #     Sir Thomas Tirrell+1 b. c 1445. Married 1) Elizabeth Devereux 2) Beatrix Cokayn.  Heir to his grandfather, Sir Thomas Tyrrell, of Heron.
2 CONT #     Alice, ux Robart Rochester
2 CONT #     Humfrey tirrell, 2 sonne.
2 CONT #     Mawde, ux Richard White of Hampshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 2 Eleanor Hungerford b. c 1430, d. b 1489
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT THE NATIONAL ARCHIVES PROB 11/6/417 8 
2 CONT http://www.oxford-shakespeare.com/Probate/PROB_11-6-417.pdf 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the will below [of Thomas Tyrrell in 1475], Eleanor Darcy is mentioned as Sir William Tyrrell’s first wife:
2 CONT
2 CONT (Page 17)
2 CONT
2 CONT >''And also that a stone be ordained for Sir William Tyrrell, my son, with his image and the image of Dame Alianor [=Eleanor], his first wife, thereupon to be made with their arms and furniture about them, the which stone I will s
2 CONC hall be laid upon his burying-place in Friar Austins of London.''
2 CONT
2 CONT As the testator’s eldest son and heir had predeceased him the testator’s heir was his grandson, Sir William Tyrrell’s son, Sir Thomas Tyrrell (c.1453-1510?), as noted in the ODNB:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.oxford-shakespeare.com/Probate/PROB_11-6-417.pdf Page 10
2 CONT
2 CONT >''Sir Thomas [ii] Tyrell of Heron (c.1411–1476), followed his father into the king's service, and was a knight of the body by 1452. ... With his wife, Anne, the daughter of Sir William Marney of Layer Marney, Essex, Thomas had fo
2 CONC ur sons ...The eldest, William, predeceased him and was buried with his wife, Alianore Darcy, at the Church of the Austin Friars, London, where Thomas's father and stepmother were also buried. Sir Thomas's heir was thus William's 
2 CONC son Sir Thomas [iii] Tyrell (c.1453–1510?).'' ... 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
