2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''Lady Elizabeth Stafford [1] 
2 CONT *''''''F, #107557, d. 1532
2 CONT *Last Edited=9 Sep 2010
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.01%
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Elizabeth Stafford married Robert Radcliffe, 1st Earl of Sussex, son of John Radcliffe, 9th Lord FitzWalter and Margaret (?).[2] She married Robert Radcliffe, 1st Earl of Sussex, son of John Radcliffe, 9th Lord FitzWalter and
2 CONC  Margaret (?), after 23 July 1505.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died in 1532.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Henry Stafford, 2nd Duke of Buckingham and Katherine Woodville.[1] From after 23 July 1505, her married name became Radcliffe.[1] As a result of her marriage, Lady Elizabeth Stafford was styled as Countess 
2 CONC of Sussex on 8 December 1529. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She and Henry VIII Tudor, King of England were associated.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lady Elizabeth Stafford and Robert Radcliffe, 1st Earl of Sussex
2 CONT * 1.Sir Humphrey Radcliffe+3 d. 1566
2 CONT * 2.Henry Radcliffe, 2nd Earl of Sussex+4 b. c 1506, d. 17 Feb 1556/57
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 130. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
2 CONT * 2.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1442. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT * 3.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT * 4.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume XII/1, page 520. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p10756.htm#i107557
