2 CONT *'''Sir Richard Croft, Sheriff of Herefordshire, Treasurer to Henry VII1,2,3
2 CONT *'''M, #77311, b. circa 1427, d. 29 July 1509
2 CONT *Father	William Croft3 b. c 1393, d. a 1433
2 CONT *Mother	Margaret Walwyn3 b. c 1395
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''     Sir Richard Croft, Sheriff of Herefordshire, Treasurer to Henry VII was born circa 1427 at of Croft Castle, Herefordshire, England.2,1,4 He married (Miss) Blount circa 1444.5 Sir Richard Croft, Sheriff of Herefordshire, T
2 CONC reasurer to Henry VII married Eleanor Cornwall, daughter of Sir Edmund Cornwall and Elizabeth Barre, between 1460 and 1465; They had 3 sons (Sir Edward; John; & Robert) & 5 daughters (Anne, wife of Sir Thomas Blount; Elizabeth, wi
2 CONC fe of John Whittington, Esq; Joyce, wife of Thomas Mill, Esq; Jane (Alice), wife of Edward Darrell; & Sibyl, wife of Sir George Herbert). He also had an illegitimate son (Thomas).3 Sir Richard Croft, Sheriff of Herefordshire, Trea
2 CONC surer to Henry VII left a will on 11 July 1509.3 He died on 29 July 1509; Buried in the church of St. Michael, Croft Castle, Herefordshire.2,3 His estate was probated on 11 November 1509.3
2 CONT *'''Family 1	(Miss) Blount b. c 1428
2 CONT *'''Family 2	Eleanor Cornwall b. c 1435, d. 1520
2 CONT *Children	
2 CONT **Anne Croft+1 b. c 1463, d. 27 Sep 1549
2 CONT **Sibyl Croft5 b. c 1464
2 CONT **Sir Edward Croft, Sheriff of Herefordshire+6,3 b. c 1465, d. 23 Mar 1547
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S11571] A Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Commoners of Great Britain and Ireland, Vol. III, by John Burke, Esq., p. 199.
2 CONT *[S147] Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage, Baronetage, and Knightage, 1938 ed., by Sir Bernard Burke, p., 695.
2 CONT *[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. II, p. 311.
2 CONT *[S11588] Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 53.
2 CONT *[S61] Unknown author, Family Group Sheets, Family History Archives, SLC.
2 CONT *[S11588] Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 54.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2573.htm#i77311
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Sir Richard Croft1
2 CONT *'''M, #324871, d. 29 July 1509
2 CONT *Last Edited=11 Dec 2008
2 CONT *'''     Sir Richard Croft was the son of William de Croft and Margaret Walwyn.1 He married Eleanor Cornwall, daughter of Sir Edmund Cornwall.1 He died on 29 July 1509.1
2 CONT *'''     Sir Richard Croft held the office of High Sheriff of Herefordshire.1 He held the office of Treasurer of the Household, to King Henry VII.1 He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Herefordshire.1 He fought in
2 CONC  the Battle of Mortimer's Cross in 1461, with the Yorkists, the battle being fought on his own estate.1 He fought in the Battle of Tewkesbury in 1471, where he captured Prince Edward, son of King Henry VI, but was not responsible 
2 CONC for the Prince's murder.1 He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Bath (K.B.) in 1487.1 He fought in the Battle of Stoke in 1487.1 He lived at Croft Castle, Herefordshire, England, Croft Castle.1
2 CONT *'''Child of Sir Richard Croft and Eleanor Cornwall
2 CONT **1.Sir Edward Croft+2 d. 1547
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 966. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Pe
2 CONC erage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *2.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p32488.htm#i324871
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Sir Richard Croft
2 CONT *'''Birth: 	unknown
2 CONT *'''Death: 	Jul. 29, 1509
2 CONT *'''Sir Richard was a Yorkist partisan during the 'Wars of the Roses', and was governor at Ludlow and Wigmore of the household of Edward IV's sons, Edward and Richard of York. "A fierce and warlike marchman," his rough handling pr
2 CONC ompted the young princes to complain to their father "of the odious rule and governance of Richard Croft." He managed to navigate the murky time during the Tudor coup d'état which culminated at Bosworth Field [1485], and was made 
2 CONC Treasurer of the Royal Household and Privy Counsellor to Henry VII. 
2 CONT *Family links: 
2 CONT * Parents:
2 CONT *  William Croft
2 CONT *  Margaret Walwyn Croft
2 CONT * Spouse:
2 CONT *'''  Eleanor Cornewall Croft (____ - 1519)
2 CONT * Children:
2 CONT **  Edward Croft (____ - 1562)*
2 CONT **  Jane Croft Darrell*
2 CONT * Sibling:
2 CONT *  Richard Croft (____ - 1509)
2 CONT *  Richard Croft the younger (1440 - 1501)*
2 CONT *'''Note: His tomb with a recumbant effigy was relocated from the chapel at Croft Castle upon its demolition.
