2 CONT *   SIR JOHN DE CROFT,(*) Knt. of Croft Castle, co. Hereford, Capt. of Merk Castle, near Calais who was frequently employed in negotiations in Flanders, between 1402 and 1404. He m. Janet, dau. and presumed co-heir of Owen ap Grif
2 CONC fith Vychan, Lord of Wlyndowrdwy, in Merionethshire, the renowned OWEN GLENDOWER, representative of the Princess of Powys, (see HUGHES OF GWERCLAS,) and was father of WILLIAM DE CROFT, whose son was
2 CONT *'''   SIR RICHARD CROFT, Knt. of Croft Castle, high-sheriff of the co. of Hereford, the captor of Prince Edward, son of Henry VI., at the battle of Tewkesbury, in 1471. This gallant soldier was appointed treasurer of the househol
2 CONC d to HENRY VII., and had the high honour of knight-banneret conferred upon him at the battle of Stoke, in 1487. He m. Eleanor, dau. of Sir Edward Cornwall, of Burford, and widow of Sir Hugh Morimer, Knt., and d. 29 July 1 HENRY VI
2 CONC II., 1609, leaving (with other issue) and elder son and heir,
2 CONT *   SIR EDWARD CROFT, knt. of Croft Castle, sheriff of Hereford, 20 HENRY VII., and 3, 9, 21, and 25 HENRY VIII., and appointed one of the learned counsel to the Princess Mary, (afterwards Queen.) 17 HENRY VIII. He m. Joyce, dau. 
2 CONC and sole heir of Sir Walter Skull, of the Holt, co. Worcester, and was father (with other children) of
2 CONT *   RICHARD CROFT, Esq., who m. Katherine, dau. of Sir Richard Herbert, Knt. of Montgomery, and was father of
2 CONT *   SIR JAMES CROFT, Knt., M.P. for the co. of Herford, lord-deputy of Ireland in 1552, and subsequently privy-councillor and comptroller of the household to Queen ELIZABETH. He m. Alice, dau. of Richard Warncombe, and relict of W
2 CONC illiam Wygmore, and d. 4 Sept., 32 ELIZ., 1590, and was s. by his eldest son,
2 CONT *   EDWARD CROFT, Esq. of Croft, M. P. for Leominster in 1571 and 1586, who m. Anne, dau. and heir of Thomas Browne, of Aldborough, co. Norfolk, and d. 29 July, 1601, when he was s. by his elder son.
2 CONT *   SIR HERBERT CROFT, Knt., M.P. for the co. of Hereford, temp. ELIZABETH and JAMES I.
