2 CONT *'''William Morgan1
2 CONT *M, #471596, d. 1569
2 CONT *Last Edited=10 Jun 2011 
2 CONT *'''     William Morgan was the son of John Morgan.1 He died in 1569, without issue.1
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S21] L. G. Pine, The New Extinct Peerage 1884-1971: Containing Extinct, Abeyant, Dormant and Suspended Peerages With Genealogies and Arms (London, U.K.: Heraldry Today, 1972), page 271. Hereinafter cited as The New Extinct Pe
2 CONC erage.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p47160.htm#i471596 __________________
2 CONT *'''MORGAN, William I (d.1569), of Tredegar, Mon.
2 CONT *'''1st s. of John Morgan of Tredegar by Lettice, da. of George Herbert of St. Julian’s. m. Catherine, da. of Sir Thomas Bodenham of Rotherwas, Herefs., s.p.; at least 1s. illegit.1
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/morgan-william-i-1569 ____________________
2 CONT *'''A history of the family of Morgan, from the year 1089 to present times ([1902?])
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/historyoffamilyo00morg
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyoffamilyo00morg#page/13/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.13
2 CONT *   VIII. LLEWELYN ap IVOR of Tredegar, Lord of St Clear, married Angharad, daughter of Sir Morgan ap Meredith, from the Welsh Lords of Caerleon, ap Griffith ap Meredith ap Rhys, who bore "Argent a lion rampant sable." Sir Morgan 
2 CONC died 1332, when Angharad was aged 32. They had : 1. Morgan. 2. Ivor Hael, whence MORGAN OF GWERN-Y-CLEPPA. 3. Philip, whence LEWIS OF ST. PIERRE. 
2 CONT *   IX. MORGAN of Tredegar and St. Clear, married Maud, daugter of Rhun ap Grono ap Llwarch, Lord of Cibwr. He died before 1384. Issue: 1. Llewelyn. 2. Philip, whence MORGAN OF LANGSTONE. 3. John, father of Gwenllian, married Davi
2 CONC d Goch ap David, 4. Christian, married Jevan ap Jenkin Kemeys. 5. Ann, married David Gwilim David of Rhiwperra. 6. Margaret, married Traherne ap Meyric of Merthyr. 7. A daughter, married Thomas ap Gwillim of Carnllwyd. 8. Elenor, 
2 CONC married Grono ap Howel Bennet. 
2 CONT *   X. LLEWELYN ap MORGAN of Tredegar and St. Clear, living 1387, married Jenet daughter and heir of David-vychan ap David of Rhydodyn, 1384-87. Issue: 1. Jevan. 2. Christy, married Madoc ap Jevan of Gelligaer. 3. —— , married Rog
2 CONC er ap Adam of St. Mellon's. 4. —— , married Madoc of Bassalleg. 5. —— , married Thomas Llewelyn. 6. Ann, married John ap Jenkin. 7. ——  , married  —— of Raglan. 8. ——  , married  ——  of Builth. 
2 CONT *   XI. JEVAN MORGAN, 1415-48, married Denise, or Elizabeth, daughter of Thomas ap Llewelyn-vychan of Lllangattog-on-Usk. Issue: 1. John. 2. David, 1442-48. 3. Jenkyn, 1454. 
2 CONT *   XII. SIR JOHN MORGAN, Knight of the Sepulchre, 1448, steward of Gwentlloog ; married Jenet, daughter and co-heir of John ap David Mathew of Llandaff. Issue: 1. Morgan. 2. Thomas, whence MORGAN OF MACHEN AND TREDEGAR. 3. John, 
2 CONC whence a BRANCH. 4. Lewis, 1491. 5. William Morgan, coroner, 1501, father or John of Newport, died 1541, father of William, 1541-1559. 6. Philip, 1491. 7. Elizabeth, married John Fiennes, 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyoffamilyo00morg#page/14/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.14
2 CONT *Lord Clinton and Say. 8. Jane, married William David Powel. 9. Mary, married Thomas Llewelyn-vychan of Rhiwperra. 10. Isabella, married James Kemeys of Began, ob. 1591. 
2 CONT *  XIII. SIR MORGAN JOHN, knighted 22 June, 1497. after Blackheath ; died in 1504; married Margaret, daughter of Sir Thomas Morgan of Pencoyd. Issue : 1. John. 2. Margaret.
2 CONT * XIV. JOHN MORGAN ; will dated 4 April, 1513 ; died about 1513 ; married Lettice, daughter of Sir George Herbert of St. Julian's. Issue : 1. '''William, M. P. for county 1556-57, sheriff 1565 ; will dated 8 August, 1568 ; died 15
2 CONC 69, s. p.; married Catherine, daughter of Thomas Bodenham'''. 2. John. 3. Joan, married Miles Mathew of Llandaff. By Felice, daughter of Thomas Richards : 4. John. 5. Nest, married John Henry Kemeys of Newport. 
2 CONT *  XV. JOHN MORGAN of Newport, 1545. married Elizabeth, daughter of Sir Edward Stradling. Issue: 1. Miles. 2. Elenor, married William Morgan.  __________________________________
2 CONT *MORGAN, Thomas II (d.1603), of Machen and Tredegar, Mon.
2 CONT *1st s. of Rowland Morgan of Machen by Blanche, da. of John Thomas of Llanarth. educ. M. Temple 1567. m. Elizabeth, da. of Roger Bodenham, 4s. 4da. suc. fa. 1577, cos. 1578.1
2 CONT * ....  Morgan belonged to a junior branch of a leading Monmouthshire family. The death of his cousin '''William Morgan I in 1569 without legitimate children''' led eventually to his inheriting Tredegar, long the seat of the senio
2 CONC r line of the family. ....
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/morgan-thomas-ii-1603 ___________________
