2 CONC  round, 46 mm., armorial, quarterly and IV quarterly,1 and 4 Barry three chaplets (Fitz William)2 and 3, three cushions (Greystock) II and IIIa fess checky between six crosses crosslet (Botiler afterwards Ferrers of Wemme). The sh
2 CONC ield is couched and above it is a mantled helm with a bush of feathers as crest. Legend: “sigillum: radulphi: [dom]inis: de: greystok.”). ''C P.'' 6 (J92ó): 197–199 (sub Greystoke). Harvey et al. ''Vis. of the North'' 3 (Surtees S
2 CONC oc. 144) (1930) ! 23–32 (Neville ped.: “Radulphus dominus Graystok nupsit Elizabetham filiam domini Fitzhugh” [Ralph, lord of Graystok, married Elizabeth, daughter of lord Fitzhugh]), 132-133 (Fitzhugh ped.: “Elizabeth (Fitzhugh] 
2 CONC nupta Radulpho domino de Graystoke” [Elizabeth [Fitzhugh] married to Lord Ralph of Graystoke]), 139–141 (Greystoke ped.: ”Radulphus dominus de Graystok” [Ralph lord of Graystok] [1] = “Elizabeth filia domini Willelmi domini Fitzhu
