2 CONT *'''Elizabeth FITZHUGH (B. Greystoke of Greystoke)
2 CONT *'''Born: ABT 1419, Ravensworth, Yorkshire, England
2 CONT *'''Died: 20 Mar 1468, Greystoke Manor, Northumberland, England
2 CONT *Father: William FITZHUGH (4° B. Fitzhugh of Ravensworth)
2 CONT *Mother: Margery WILLOUGHBY (B. Fitzhugh of Ravensworth)
2 CONT *'''Married: Ralph GREYSTOKE (7º B. Greystoke of Greystoke) 1 Jul 1436, Worcester, Worcestershire, England DISPENSATION
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Joan GREYSTOKE
2 CONT **2. Anne GREYSTOKE
2 CONT **3. John GREYSTOKE
2 CONT **4. Richard GREYSTOKE (Rector of Wheldrak)
2 CONT **5. Elizabeth GREYSTOKE (B. Scrope of Masham)
2 CONT **6. Robert GREYSTOKE (Sir Knight)
2 CONT **7. Anne GREYSTOKE
2 CONT **8. Ralph GREYSTOKE
2 CONT **9. Margaret (Margery) GREYSTOKE
2 CONT **10. William GREYSTOKE
2 CONT **11. William GREYSTOKE
2 CONT **12. Mary GREYSTOKE
2 CONT **13. Thomas GREYSTOKE
2 CONT **14. Isabella GREYSTOKE
2 CONT **15. Ralph GREYSTOKE
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/FITZHUGH.htm#Elizabeth FITZHUGH2
2 CONT *________________________
2 CONT *William FitzHugh, 4th Baron FitzHugh (c. 1399 - 22 October 1452) was an English nobleman and Member of Parliament.
2 CONT *Born at Ravensworth, North Riding of Yorkshire, England. He was the son of Henry FitzHugh, 3rd Baron FitzHugh and Elizabeth Grey. He served as a Member of Parliament from 1429-1450.
2 CONT *FitzHugh married, before 18 November 1406, at Ravensworth, Margery Willoughby, daughter of William Willoughby, 5th Baron Willoughby de Eresby, and Lucy le Strange, by whom he had a son and seven daughters:[1]
2 CONT ** Henry FitzHugh, 5th Baron FitzHugh, who married Lady Alice Neville, daughter of Richard Neville, 5th Earl of Salisbury and Alice Montacute, 5th Countess of Salisbury, daughter and heiress of Thomas de Montacute, 4th Earl of Sal
2 CONC isbury and Lady Eleanor Holland.[2] They were great-grandparents to queen consort Catherine Parr.
2 CONT **''' Elizabeth FitzHugh, whom married Ralph Greystoke, 5th Baron Greystoke.[2]
2 CONT ** Eleanor FitzHugh, who married Ranulph Dacre, 1st Baron Dacre of Gilsland.[2]
2 CONT ** Maud FitzHugh, whom married Sir William Bowes (d. 28 July 1466) of Streatlam, Durham, by whom she was the grandmother of Sir Robert Bowes.[3][2]
2 CONT ** Lora FitzHugh, who married Sir John Constable of Halsham, Yorkshire.[2]
2 CONT ** Lucy, who became a nun.[2]
2 CONT ** Margery FitzHugh, who married John Melton.[2]
2 CONT ** Joan FitzHugh, who married John Scrope, 5th Baron Scrope of Bolton.[2]
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_FitzHugh,_4th_Baron_FitzHugh
2 CONT *______________________
