2 CONT *_______________________
2 CONT *'''Elizabeth GREYSTOKE (B. Scrope of Masham)
2 CONT *'''Born: ABT 1436, Greystoke, Cumberland, England
2 CONT *'''Died: ABT 1483 / AFT 20 Dec 1490, Masham, Yorkshire, Yorkshire, England
2 CONT *Father: Ralph GREYSTOKE (7º B. Greystoke of Greystoke)
2 CONT *Mother: Elizabeth FITZHUGH
2 CONT *'''Married: Thomas SCROPE (5° B. Scrope of Masham) 4 May 1453, in Sett.
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Thomas SCROPE (6° B. Scrope of Masham)
2 CONT **2. Elizabeth SCROPE
2 CONT **3. Alice SCROPE
2 CONT **4. Margaret SCROPE
2 CONT **5. Ralph SCROPE (7° B. Scrope of Masham)
2 CONT **6. Geoffrey SCROPE (8° B. Scrope of Masham)
2 CONT **7. Henry SCROPE (b. ABT 1471 - d. 6 Aug 1515)
2 CONT *'''Married 2: Gilbert TALBOT (High Sheriff) 20 Dec 1483, Whitechurch, Shropshire, England 
2 CONT *Children: 
2 CONT **8. Gilbert TALBOT (Sir)
2 CONT **9. Catherine TALBOT 
2 CONT **10. Jane TALBOT 
2 CONT **11. Humphrey TALBOT 
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/GREYSTOKE.htm#Elizabeth GREYSTOKE (B. Scrope of Masham)
2 CONT *_______________________________
2 CONT *'''Sir Gilbert Talbot of Grafton, KG (1452 – 16 August 1517 or 19 September 1518) was an English Tudor knight, a younger son of John Talbot, 2nd Earl of Shrewsbury and 2nd Earl of Waterford, and Elizabeth Butler.
2 CONT *He was a soldier, Knight of the Order of the Garter in 1495 and Lord Deputy of Calais in 1509, where he continued in a joint appointment with Richard Wingfield.[1]
2 CONT *Talbot supported Henry Tudor at Bosworth, where he commanded the right wing. He was given the Grafton estates in Worcestershire after Sir Humphrey Stafford was executed in 1486 for his part in the Stafford and Lovell Rebellion.[2
2 CONC ] Talbot was also given the honorary position of keeper of Feckenham Forest in 1492.[3]
2 CONT *'''He married firstly Elizabeth Greystoke, daughter of Ralph de Greystoke, 5th Baron Greystoke and 7th Baron Boteler of Wem, and had three children:
2 CONT ** Sir Humphrey Talbot, who died in the Holy Land
2 CONT ** Sir Gilbert Talbot of Grafton, Worcestershire (died 22 October 1542), married Anne Paston, daughter of Sir William Paston (died 1496) and Lady Anne Beaufort, daughter of Edmund Beaufort, 2nd Duke of Somerset and Eleanor Beaucha
2 CONC mp, and had three daughters:
2 CONT *** Elizabeth Talbot, who married Sir John Littelton, son of Sir William Littelton and his second wife, Mary Whittington, daughter of William Whittington, by whom he had seven sons and two daughters.[4]
2 CONT *** Margaret Talbot
2 CONT *** Mary Talbot
2 CONT **Eleanor Talbot, wife of Geoffrey Dudley, younger son of Edward Sutton, 2nd Baron Dudley and Cecily Willoughby, ancestors of the Dudleys of Russell's Hall
2 CONT *He married secondly Etheldreda, called Audrey, Cotton, daughter of William Landwade Cotton of Landwade, Cambridgeshire, and had one child:
2 CONT ** Sir John Talbot of Albrighton, Shropshire (1485 - 22 October 1542 or 10 September 1549), married firstly Margaret Troutbeck, daughter of Adam Troutbeck of Mobberley, Chester, and had three sons and five daughters; he married se
2 CONC condly Elizabeth Wrottesley (died 10 May 1558), daughter of Walter Wrottesley of Wrottesley Hall, Staffordshire (died 1563), and Elizabeth Harcourt and had four sons and four daughters: .... etc.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gilbert_Talbot_(soldier)
2 CONT *_________________________
2 CONT *TALBOT, Sir Gilbert (by 1479-1542), of Grafton, Worcs.
2 CONT *b. by 1479, 1st s. of '''Sir Gilbert Talbot of Grafton by Elizabeth, da. of Ralph, 5th Lord Greystoke, wid. of Thomas, 5th Lord Scrope of Masham'''. m. (1) by 1505, Anne, da. and coh. of William Paston of Norwich, Norf. and Londo
2 CONC n by Anne, da. of Edmund Beaufort, 1st Duke of Somerset, 3da.; (2) Elizabeth, da. of Sir John Hungerford of Down Ampney, Glos., wid. of Roger Winter (d.1534) of Huddington, Worcs.; 2s. 2da. illegit. Kntd. 14 Oct. 1513; suc. fa. 16
2 CONC  Aug. 1517.2
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1509-1558/member/talbot-sir-gilbert-1479-1542
2 CONT *__________________________
2 CONT *Llinks
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Talbot,_2nd_Earl_of_Shrewsbury
2 CONT
2 CONT *_______________________
