2 CONT *'''M, #107420, b. circa 1445, d. 12 August 1469
2 CONT *Last Edited=23 May 2004
2 CONT *'''     Sir John Woodville was born circa 1445.1 He was the son''' of Richard Wydevill, 1st Earl Rivers and Jacquetta de Luxembourg.2 '''He married Lady Katherine Neville''', daughter of Ralph de Neville, 1st Earl of Westmorland 
2 CONC and Lady Joan de Beaufort, '''circa 1465.3 He died on 12 August 1469 at Edgecote, England, beheaded after capture.
2 CONT *'''     He was also known as John Wydville. He fought in the Battle of Edgecote on 12 August 1469.
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct
2 CONC  or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 62. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 108. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Families.
