1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *''''''Margaret Wydville1,2,3,4
2 CONT *F, d. between 24 September 1485 and 4 August 1492
2 CONT *Father Sir Richard Widville, 1st Earl Rivers, Constable of England, Lord High Treasurer5,2,3,4 b. b 1408, d. 12 Aug 1469 
2 CONT *Mother Jaquetta (Jacqueline) of Luxembourg1,5,2,3 b. 1416 or 1417, d. 30 May 1472 
2 CONT *''''''     Margaret Wydville married Sir Thomas FitzAlan, 22nd (17th) Earl of Arundel, Chief Butler of England, Lt. of the Order of the Garter, Warden of the New Forest, Keeper of the Tower & Blockhouse of Portsmouth, Lord Maltra
2 CONC vers, son of Sir William FitzAlan, 21st (16th) Earl of Arundel, Chief Butler of England, Constable of Dover Castle and Joan Neville, in October 1464; Letter of 17 February 1466 stated they married shortly before that date; this ma
2 CONC rriage produced two sons (William and Edward) and two daughters (Joan and Margaret).6,5,2,3,4 Margaret Wydville died between 24 September 1485 and 4 August 1492; Buried at Arundel, Sussex.1,3
2 CONT *''''''Family Sir Thomas FitzAlan, 22nd (17th) Earl of Arundel, Chief Butler of England, Lt. of the Order of the Garter, Warden of the New Forest, Keeper of the Tower & Blockhouse of Portsmouth, Lord Maltravers b. 1450, d. 25 Oct 
2 CONC 1524 
2 CONT *Children 
2 CONT **◦Margaret FitzAlan7,3 d. a 1528
2 CONT **◦Joan FitzAlan+8,3,4 b. c 1470, d. 14 Nov 1508
2 CONT **◦Sir William FitzAlan, 23rd (18th) Earl of Arundel, Chief Butler of England, Lord Maltravers+1,3 b. c 1476, d. 23 Jan 1544
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. I, p. 250.
2 CONT *2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 783-784.
2 CONT *3.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 37.
2 CONT *4.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 170.
2 CONT *5.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 43.
2 CONT *6.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. I, p. 249-250.
2 CONT *7.[S11575] The Lineage and Ancestry of H.R.H. Prince Charles, Prince of Wales, by Gerald Paget, Vol. I, p. 25.
2 CONT *8.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 95.
