1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Elizabeth Somerset Brereton=
2 CONT ''Lady Elizabeth "De Breaufort" Somerset . Countess of Savage and Somerset. Baroness of Brereton and Savage'' - Full Title
2 CONT * BIRTH 1497
2 CONT * England DEATH 1545 (aged 47–48) England
2 CONT * BURIAL St. Michael's & All Angels Churchyard, Macclesfield, Cheshire East Unitary Authority, Cheshire, England
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID  148507762 photo added by Peter Cox
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1529 the widowed Elizabeth (by John Savage) married William Brereton of Malpas.  Elizabeth was a second cousin to Henry VIII and this union improved his status and his connections to the crown. As a result of this marriage, he 
2 CONC received 36 offices in Cheshire and North Wales. After his father's death, William received the office of chamberlain of Chester thanks to his ties with the king.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Sir Charles Henry Somerset 1460–1526
2 CONT Lady Elizabeth Herbert Somerset 1476–1507
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Sir John Savage 1493–1528
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings'''
2 CONT Henry Somerset 1495–1549
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT Mary Savage Hitchcock 1514–1570
2 CONT Sir John Savage 1524–1597
2 CONT Anne Savage Robinson unknown–1570
2 CONT
