1 NOTE {geni:about_me} latest news about Richard 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.nature.com/ncomms/2014/141202/ncomms6631/full/ncomms6631.html
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2014/dec/02/king-richard-iii-dna-cousins-queen-ancestry
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT A skeleton found beneath a Leicester car park has been confirmed as that of English king Richard III.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard III dig: DNA confirms bones are king's:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-england-leicestershire-21063882
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard III dig: University to release DNA results:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-england-leicestershire-21292381
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard III dig: 'Strong evidence' bones are lost king:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-england-leicestershire-19561018
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard III's scarred skeleton becomes a battlefield for academics: (contains an image showing his severe scoliosis 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.guardian.co.uk/uk/2013/feb/04/richard-third-skeleton-confirmed-leicester
2 CONT
2 CONT Remains of King Richard III: Analysis by Dr Steven Gunn, University of Oxford
2 CONT
2 CONT After the battle of Bosworth Henry VII didn't want anyone claiming that they were Richard III and had survived the battle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard's body was taken to Leicester, slung naked over the back of a horse, and publicly displayed so people could see he was dead.
2 CONT
2 CONT But there was the problem of how and where to bury him - what seems likely is that they wanted to avoid anything that would generate a posthumous cult.
2 CONT
2 CONT There was a tradition in medieval England that people who were political victims then became popular saints. They wouldn't have wanted to bury him in York, where he was very popular.
2 CONT
2 CONT Greyfriars was convenient and safe. Henry VII put steps in action for a tomb to be built, and the inscription was to be ambivalent, and in some ways rude about Richard III, talking about his nephews and indicating that he wasn't a
2 CONC  very good king. There is evidence that people talked about him being buried there.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT a short summary from Wikipedia:
