1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/SUTTON.htm#Margaret SUTTON (B. Powis)
2 CONT *''''''Margaret SUTTON (B. Grey of Powis)
2 CONT *''''''Born: 1485, Dudley, Worcester, England
2 CONT *''''''Died: 11 May 1525
2 CONT *Father: Edward SUTTON (2º B. Sutton of Dudley)
2 CONT *Mother: Cecily WILLOUGHBY (B. Sutton of Dudley)
2 CONT *''''''Married 1: John GREY (2° B. Grey of Powis) ABT 1501/5, Dudley, Worcester, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Edward GREY (3° B. Grey of Powis)
2 CONT **2. Antonhy GREY
2 CONT *''''''Married 2: Robert SUTTON (b. 1485 - d. AFT 1525) AFT 1504
2 CONT *_________________
2 CONT *''''''Plantagenet ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=p_yzpuWi4sgC&pg=PA279&lpg=PA279&dq=Robert+Sutton+1485&source=bl&ots=RQBQ9SV38b&sig=6SQWFH9DjxcKPXvz77knlK7D28A&hl=en&ei=nEB5TbGDKIL8rAHJ5JH_BQ&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=7&ved=0CDcQ6AEwB
2 CONC jgK#v=onepage&q=Robert%20Sutton%201485&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 279
2 CONT *15. EDWARD SUTTON (or DUDLEY), K.B., K.G., 2nd Lord Dudley, son and heir by his father's 1st marrieage, born about 1457-60 (aged 16 in 1486; aged 28 or 30 in 1487). He married CECILY WILLOUGHBY, daughter and co-heiress of William
2 CONC  Willoughby, Knt., of Boston, Lincolnshire (descendant of King Edward I), by Joan (descendant of King Edward III), daughter and co-heiress of Thomas Strangeways [ see ERESBY 12 for her ancestry]. They had Seven sons, John, Knt. [3
2 CONC rd Lord Dudley], Edward Thomas, Arthur (clerk), George, Geoffrey, and William, and eight daughters, ''''''Margaret (wife of John Grey, Lord Grey of Powis, and Robert Sutton),''''''  . . . . 
2 CONT *__________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Sutton was one of the seven daughters of Edward Sutton, 2nd baron Dudley (c.1457-January 31, 1531/2) and Cecily Willoughby (c.1463-August 1539). Her father, characterized as "unscrupulous" by T. B. Pugh in his essay "Henr
2 CONC y VII and the English Nobility" (in The Tudor Nobility, edited by G. W. Bernard), obtained the wardship and marriage of John Grey, baron Powis (1482/3-April 15, 1504) on November 29, 1494. Dudley married Powis to Margaret by 1502 
2 CONC and they had at least one child, Edward (1503-July 12, 1551), before his death. TudorPlace.com.ar gives them a second son, Anthony. Lord Dudley then obtained the wardship of young Edward and kept the profits for himself, failing e
2 CONC ven to pay Margaret the 1/3 dower share she was entitled to. In 1505, she married Robert Sutton of Burton by Lincoln and Washingborough, Lincolnshire (d. November 25, 1545). Online genealogies, give Robert an additional wife, Eliz
2 CONC abeth Boys, with varying life dates (one as late as 1583) and as many as eight children. Some say Margaret was his second wife and others his first. Eldest son Henry (1509-January 6, 1537/8) does appear to have been born to Margar
2 CONC et. Anne, John, Margaret, Robert, and Thomas may also be hers. Adding to the confusion is the will of Dame Margaret Sutton, vowess, of Burton by Lincoln, dated October 1, 1525. This Margaret (née Sheffield) was the widow of Hamon 
2 CONC Sutton and the mother of Robert Sutton, who is named as her executor. The will also mentions his oldest son Henry and my lady Powis (Margaret Sutton would have kept this title after her remarriage), to whom she leaves a standing m
2 CONC aser with a cover. Since Edward Grey did not marry until 1531, this could only be Margaret, which means she could not have died before May 11, 1525, as some accounts indicate. 
