2 CONT *'''Edmund Grey, 1st Earl of Kent1
2 CONT *'''M, #174791, b. 26 October 1416, d. 22 May 1490
2 CONT *Last Edited=1 May 2011
2 CONT *'''     Edmund Grey, 1st Earl of Kent was born on 26 October 1416.2 He was the son of Sir John Grey and Lady Constance de Holand.2 He married Lady Catherine Percy, daughter of Henry de Percy, 1st Earl of Northumberland and Lady E
2 CONC leanor de Neville, before January 1458/59.2 He died on 22 May 1490 at age 73.2
2 CONT *'''     He succeeded to the title of 4th Lord Grey, of Ruthin [E., 1325] on 20 September 1440.3 He was initially a Lancastrian in the War of the Roses.4 He fought in the Battle of Northampton on 10 July 1460, where he switched si
2 CONC des, thus probably being the chief cause of the Yorkist victory.4 He was created 1st Earl of Kent [England] on 30 May 1465.5
2 CONT *'''Children of Edmund Grey, 1st Earl of Kent and Lady Catherine Percy
2 CONT ** 1.Sir Anthony Grey6 d. bt 15 May 1480 - 27 Nov 1480
2 CONT ** 2.George Grey, 2nd Earl of Kent+7 d. 21 Dec 1503
2 CONT ** 3.Lady Anne Grey+1
2 CONT ** 4.Lady Elizabeth Grey+4
2 CONT ** 5.unknown son Grey4
2 CONT ** 6.unknown daughter Grey4
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume VI, page 181. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT * 2.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume VII, page 164.
2 CONT * 3.[S21] L. G. Pine, The New Extinct Peerage 1884-1971: Containing Extinct, Abeyant, Dormant and Suspended Peerages With Genealogies and Arms (London, U.K.: Heraldry Today, 1972), page 136. Hereinafter cited as The New Extinct Pe
2 CONC erage.
2 CONT * 4.[S37] BP2003 volume 2, page 1666. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT * 5.[S21] L. G. Pine, The New Extinct Peerage, page 137.
2 CONT * 6.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume VII, page 165.
2 CONT * 7.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume VI, page 160.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p17480.htm#i174791
2 CONT *____________________
2 CONT *'''Edmund GREY (1° E. Kent)
2 CONT *'''Born: 26 Oct 1416, Ruthin, Denbighshire, Wales
2 CONT *'''Acceded: 1465
2 CONT *'''Died: 22 May 1490, England
2 CONT *'''Notes: was summoned to Parliament from 3 Dec 1441 (20 Hen. V) to 28 Feb 1462/63 (2 Edw. IV). He survived his father and became his grandfather's heir. Cokayne, "Complete Peerage", 2° ed., vol. VII, pg. 160. Created E. Kent by 
2 CONC Edward IV, 30 May 1465 and confirmed in the dignity by Henry VII. L.G. Pine, "The New Extinct Peerage 1884-1971" (1973), Genealogical Publishing Co., Inc. Baltimore, pg. 137. Burke, "Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerag
2 CONC e Baronatage and Knightage", 97th ed:, (1826), pg.1154.
2 CONT *Father: John GREY (Sir Knight)
2 CONT *Mother: Constance HOLLAND
2 CONT *'''Married: Catherine PERCY (C. Kent) BEF Jan 1458/59
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Anthony GREY (4° B. Grey of Ruthin)
2 CONT **2. Elizabeth GREY
2 CONT **3. Anne GREY
2 CONT **4. George GREY (2° E. Kent)
2 CONT **5. John GREY
2 CONT **6. Edmund GREY (b. ABT 1457, Ruthin, Denbighshire, Wales)
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/GREY3.htm#Edmund GREY (1° E. Kent)
