3 TEXT In 1497, at the Battle of Blackheath, Hussey was knighted; "Knight of the Body", bodyguard to King Henry VII, followed by an appointment as "Master of Lyfield Forest", Rutland in 1505 and Comptroller of the Household in 1509. On 1
4 CONC 6 August 1513, at the battle of the Spurs, he was promoted to Knight banneret; 1493 appointed Sheriff of Lincolnshire; 5 February 1526, appointed a judge; Chief Butler of England; etc.
