1 NAME Agnes ‘Anne’ /Hussey/
2 GIVN Agnes ‘Anne’
2 SURN Hussey
2 _MARNM Browne
2 NICK Agnes
2 NICK Browne
2 NICK widow Ryther
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1528
2 ADDR
3 CITY Sleaford
3 CTRY England
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 1562
1 OCCU
1 TITL Lady
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Agnes-Saunders/6000000191717448865?through=6000000006927576350
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Agnes Hussey''', daughter of John Hussey and Anne Grey, was born about 1528, probably at Sleaford, Lincolnshire.  She was married about 1547 to Humphrey Browne, knight, son of Thomas Browne and Mary Charleton Browne of Langhous
2 CONC e, Essex, according to "Visitation of Kent."
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne or Agnes Hussey was a daughter of John Hussey (1464-1536)  and his second wife, Anne Grey.   John Hussey, [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chief_Butler_of_England chief butler of England], was implicated as complicit in the [ht
2 CONC tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pilgrimage_of_Grace Pilgrimage of Grace] uprising in 1536, found guilty of treason, and beheaded in Lincoln on 29 June 1537.  The charges may have been levied in part because of Hussey's Catholic sympat
2 CONC hies, and because Hussey and his wife, having served 'Princess' Mary, were partisans on her behalf. Anne Grey has married Sir John Hussey, Baron Sleaford, son of Sir William Hussey, Chief Justice of the King's Bench and Elizabeth 
2 CONC Berkeley, after 18 May 1509. She was the daughter of George Grey, 2nd Earl of Kent – by his second wife, Catherine Herbert. Lady Anne's paternal grandmother was Lady Katherine Percy, the great-great-granddaughter of King Edward II
2 CONC I of England, and  died between 1 March 1545 and 11 February 1546.  When Anne nee Grey Hussey, the second wife of John Hussey wrote her will in 1543, she refers to her two daughters & of the 4 younger daughters of John Hussey, “tw
2 CONC o are still living.”
2 CONT
2 CONT After his execution, Hussey's home in Sleaford, as well as his other estates were confiscated by the crown.  His children were restored to Parliament in 1563 during the reign of Queen Elizabeth, but Hussey's title was forfeited, a
2 CONC nd the estates were not returned.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne or Agnes married (secondly) to Sir Humphrey Browne, Justice of the Common Pleas, as his third wife of Sir Humphrey Browne. She and two of her brothers, Thomas and Gilbert, were named in his 1562 will.
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants of the anti-Church of England Lord Hussey, whose barony and estates were forfeited, were left in far less secure positions, both regarding their financial and social status; by 1633, the descendants of Lord Hussey's so
2 CONC n, Sir Giles Hussey, had left England to freely practice their [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nonconformist_(Protestantism) non-conformist] religion in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_England New England].
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Extracted from http://www.oxford-shakespeare.com/Probate/PROB_11-46-19.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT [Humphrey Browne] married thirdly, about 1547, Agnes Hussey (born c.1515), widow of Henry Ryther (1511 – 5 January 1544), esquire, of Harewood Castle, son of Sir Ralph Ryther (d. 2 April 1520) by his second wife, Maud Percy, the d
2 CONC aughter of Henry Percy, Earl of Northumberland. For the argument that Maud Percy was the daughter of Henry Percy (c.1449–1489), 4th Earl of Northumberland, by Maud Herbert, see:
2 CONT
2 CONT < [https://royaldescent.blogspot.ca/2010/02/ryther-1-who-was-maud-percy-dame-ryther.html “Who was Maud Percy?”] >
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT For the Ryther family, see Richardson, Douglas, Plantagenet Ancestry, 2nd ed., 2011, Vol. III, p. 111, and the pedigree of Ryther of Scarcroft, in Dugdale, William, The Visitation of the County of York, (London: Surtees Society, 1
2 CONC 859?), p. 235 at:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://books.google.ca/books?id=ykNjAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA235
2 CONT
2 CONT The testator’s third wife, Agnes Hussey, was one of the daughters of John Hussey (executed 29 June 1537), 1st Baron Hussey of Sleaford, by Anne Grey, the daughter of George Grey (d. 21 December 1503), 2nd Earl of Kent, and his sec
2 CONC ond wife, Katherine Herbert, third daughter of William Herbert (c.1423-1469), 1st Earl of Pembroke, by Anne Devereux, the daughter of Sir Walter Devereux (1411-1459). See the Hussey pedigree in Maddison, A.R., Lincolnshire Pedigre
2 CONC es (London: Harleian Society, 1908), pp. 526-30 at:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/lincolnshirepedi51madd#page/526/mode/2up
2 CONT
2 CONT There were no issue of Agnes Hussey’s first marriage to Henry Ryther, who made his first cousin, John Ryther, esquire, heir to certain of his properties. For the will, dated 23 January 1543 and proved 18 March 1544, of Henry Rythe
2 CONC r, in which he mentions his father, Ralph Ryther, his mother, Maud Percy, and his wife, Agnes Hussey, and bequeaths his lands to ‘John Ryther of London, squire, and cofferer to our Sovereign Lord Prince Edward’, see Testamenta Ebo
2 CONC racensia, Vol. VI, (London: Whittaker & Co., 1902), Surtees Society, Vol. CVI, pp. 170-1 at:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/visitationofyork00flow#page/366/mode/2up
2 CONT
2 CONT For the Ryther family, see also: 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~hwbradley/aqwg3252.htm#71027
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the will below, the testator had three daughters by his third wife, Agnes Hussey:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Mary Browne, who is said to have married Thomas Wilford of Hartridge, Kent.
2 CONT # Christian Browne, who married, as his second wife, Sir John Tufton (d. 2 April 1624),
2 CONT # Katherine Browne the younger (buried 20 February 1616 [=1617?]), … It appears that Katherine Browne’s husband was the grandson of the William Roper (1495x8-1578) who married Margaret More, i.e., William Roper (c.1557-1628), son 
2 CONC of Thomas Roper (buried 26 February 1597 [=1598?]), esquire,
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann HUSSEY [Parents] 1 was born about 1521 in . She married Humphrey BROWN KNIGHT about 1552.
2 CONT
2 CONT Other marriages:
2 CONT
2 CONT *         BERKELEY, John
2 CONT *         BROWN, Humphrey
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *       		F 	i 	Mary BROWN was born about 1553.
2 CONT *       		F 	ii 	Christian BROWNE was born about 1554.
2 CONT *       		F 	iii 	Catharine BROWN was born about 1557
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Lincolnshire, England on 1523 to John Hussey and Anne Grey. Ann married Humphrey Brown and had 3 children. Ann married John Berkeley. She passed away on 1557. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Comments 
2 CONT
2 CONT Date of death 4/12/1615 is a guess! Death field said only "12" while burial date said "4/28/1615", so I assume the next most credible date for which "12" could be a mistake, 1612, is too far away.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # Will of Sir William Hussey, PROB 11/10/592, proved 4 July 1496, National Archives 11 December 2013 < [http://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/SearchUI/Details?uri=D981409 link] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT ##http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/Bios/JohnHussey(1BSleaford).htm Hussey wrote his will 22 Oct 1535 in which he mentioned that he was "somewhat sick in body". In the will he requested "... to be buried in Sempringham church if I die 
2 CONC within seven miles of it...". He gave title to Brigeasterton manor and Rutland manor to his wife; his lands he left intail male to "... Sir William Huse, son and heir apparent; sons, Thomas, Gilbert, Sir Giles; brothers, Sir Willi
2 CONC am and Sir Robert Huse; daughters, Mary and Bridget Huse, each to have 500 marks; Executor, brother, Sir Robert Huse...".
