1 NOTE {geni:about_me} = Eleanor Poynings, Baroness Poynings=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Eleanor de Poynings,''' ''Baroness de Poynings'' was born circa 1422. She died circa 1484.  She gained the title of ''Baroness de Poynings'' by succeeding her paternal grandfather in 1446 as Baroness Poynings suo iure.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://www.luminarium.org/encyclopedia/henrypercy3.htm Biography]
2 CONT
2 CONT >By his wife Eleanor, who survived him, HENRY PERCY, third Earl of Northumberland, son of Henry, second earl, left a son Henry, afterwards fourth Earl of Northumberland, and three daughters: Eleanor, married Lord De la Warr; Marga
2 CONC ret, married Sir William Gascoigne of Gawthorp, Yorkshire; and Elizabeth, married Henry, lord Scrope of Bolton. He was, it is believed, buried in the church of St. Dionys at York, the church of the parish in which stood Percy's In
2 CONC n, the York town house of his family. In this church there was a painted window presenting several effigies of the Percys; it was taken down in 1590.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Family=
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:  daughter of  Sir Richard de Poynings and his second wife Eleanor de Arundel née Berkeley ([1422]-Feb 1484). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT # before 25 June 1435 to Henry Percy, 2nd Earl of Northumberland son of Henry de Percy, 1st Earl of Northumberland and Lady Eleanor de Neville.   From before 25 June 1435, her married name became Percy.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children of Eleanor de Poynings, Baroness de Poynings and Henry Percy, 2nd Earl of Northumberland=
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)'''Sir Henry Percy, 3rd Earl of Northumberland,'''+ b. c 1449, d. 28 Apr 1489.   He succeeded his father as Earl of Northumberland.  married  ([1476]) MATILDA Herbert
2 CONT * b)'''RALPH''' . Died young. [not noted in all sources]
2 CONT *c)  '''ELEANOR''' . married  Lord De la Warr [not noted in all sources]
2 CONT *d)   '''MARGARET''' .  married  WILLIAM Gascoigne, son of ---. 
2 CONT *e)   '''ELIZABETH''' (-after 20 May 1512, bur Wensley, Yorkshire).  m HENRY Le Scrope, son of JOHN Le Scrope Lord Scrope of Bolton & his first wife Joan FitzHugh ([1468]-1506, bur Wensley, Yorkshire).  He succeeded his father in 
2 CONC 1498 as Lord Scrope of Bolton. 
2 CONT * '''Lady Ann Percy''' (d. 5 Jul 1522), mar. (1) bef. 14 Oct 1460 Sir Thomas Hungerford, de jure 4th Baron Hungerford, (2) Sir Laurence Rainsford (d. 1490), and (3) Sir Hugh Vaughan, and had issue by her first husband.  [not noted
2 CONC  in all sources]
2 CONT
