1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Margaret Percy==
2 CONT '''The Lady Margaret Gascoigne (née Percy) (born c. 1447) was an English noblewoman''', the daughter of Henry Percy, 3rd Earl of Northumberland and Eleanor Poynings.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She married Sir William Gascoigne''', "the Younger", son of Sir William Gascoigne and wife. '''Their daughter''' Agnes (or Anne) Gascoigne married Sir Thomas Fairfax (died 1520–1521), who was an ancestor of Catherine, Duchess o
2 CONC f Cambridge.[1][2] '''Lady Margaret Percy was a descendant of Edward III.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She married Sir William Gascoigne V''' (c. 1450 – 1486),[4] son of Sir William Gascoigne IV (c. 1427 – c. 1463)[5] [great-grandson of Sir William Gascoigne I (c. 1350 – 1419), Chief Justice of England] and Joan Neville (c. 1436
2 CONC –1464) (great-granddaughter of Robert Ferrers, 5th Baron Boteler of Wem and Joan Beaufort). '''The couple had the following children''':[6][7]
2 CONT *Sir William Gascoigne VI: married firstly Alice Frognall and secondly Margaret Nevill (daughter of Richard Nevill, 2nd Baron Latimer of Snape). Had issue by both marriages. Second son by first marriage, Sir Henry Gascoigne, was a
2 CONC ncestor of the Wyvill Baronets (from the 3rd onwards).[8][9] Male line by primogeniture ended with his grandson William Gascoigne VIII, whose only daughter and heiress (other children died young) Margaret (1530–1592/93) married Si
2 CONC r Thomas Wentworth (1520–1586/87), High Sheriff of York (who thereby got possession of the Gascoigne family seat at Gawthorpe, York[10]), and became the paternal grandmother of Thomas Wentworth, 1st Earl of Strafford.[11]
2 CONT *Margaret or Margery (c. 1473 – 1515):[12] married Ralph Ogle, 3rd Baron Ogle, and had issue.[13]
2 CONT *Elizabeth (1470–1559):[14] married before April 1493 as his second wife Sir George Tailboys (c. 1467 – 1538), de jure 9th Baron Kyme and Sheriff of Lincolnshire, grandson of Sir William Tailboys, de jure 7th Baron Kyme. This coup
2 CONC le were ancestors of Mildred Warner[15] (paternal grandmother of George Washington, 1st president of the USA) and her sister Mary Warner[16] (ancestress of Elizabeth Bowes-Lyon, mother of Queen Elizabeth II of the United Kingdom) 
2 CONC (see here for descent chart).
2 CONT *Anne or Agnes (c. 1474 – 1504): married firstly Sir Thomas Fairfax (c. 1475 – 1520). She had twin sons: the elder, Nicholas, was ancestor of Diana, Princess of Wales and the younger, William, was an ancestor of Catherine, Duchess
2 CONC  of Cambridge (see here for descent chart). Married secondly Ralph Nevill, of Thornton Bridge.
2 CONT *Dorothy (c. 1475 – 1527):[17] married Sir Ninian Markenfield (died 1527).[18] Ancestors of William Howard Taft,[19] 27th president of the USA Sir Ninian's other wife was Eleanor Clifford, daughter of Henry Clifford, 10th Baron de
2 CONC  Clifford.[20] (Of interest: Sir Ninian's sister Anne was ancestress of George Gascoigne, poet, and Zachary Taylor,[21] 12th president of the USA)
2 CONT
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Percy _______________
2 CONT
2 CONT One merged profile listed birth date circa 1447. Another merged profile listed birth place as Northumberland, England. -SPF
2 CONT *__________________
2 CONT *'''Margaret Percy1,2
2 CONT *'''F, b. circa 1453
2 CONT *Father Sir Henry Percy, 6th Earl Northumberland, 6th Lord Percy2 b. 25 Jul 1421, d. 29 Mar 1461 
2 CONT *Mother Eleanor Poynings2 b. c 1422, d. 11 Feb 1484 
2 CONT *'''     Margaret Percy was born circa 1453 at of Warworth, Northumberland, England. She married Sir William Gascoigne, Justice of the Peace for the West Riding, Yorkshire''', son of Sir William Gascoigne and Jane Neville, '''befo
2 CONC re 1469; They had 6 sons''' (William, Henry, Thomas, Henry, John, & Thomas) '''and 7 daughters''' (Margaret, Eleanor, Maud, Joan, Elizabeth, Agnes/Anne, & Dorothy).2 '''Margaret Percy married Sir Ralph Ryther, Sheriff & Justice of
2 CONC  the Peace for Yorkshire''', son of Sir William Ryther and Eleanor FitzWilliam, '''after 12 March 1487; They had 1 son''' (Henry) '''and 1 daughter''' (Elizabeth).3
2 CONT *'''Family 1 Sir William Gascoigne, Justice of the Peace for the West Riding, Yorkshire b. c 1452, d. 12 Mar 1487 
2 CONT *Children 
