2 CONT *HENRY (25 Jul 1421-killed in battle Towton 29 Mar 1461, bur [York St Denis]).  A manuscript pedigree dated to [1500] names "Henry Earl of Northumberland" as son of "Eleanor Countess of Northumberland"[1012].  He succeeded his fat
2 CONC her as Earl of Northumberland.  m (25 Jun 1435 or before) ELEANOR de Poynings, daughter of Sir RICHARD de Poynings & his second wife Eleanor de Arundel née Berkeley ([1422]-Feb 1484).  A manuscript pedigree dated to [1500] names "
2 CONC dau and heir of the Lord Poynings" as wife of "Henry Earl of Northumberland"[1013].  She succeeded her paternal grandfather in 1446 as Baroness Poynings suo iure.  Henry & his wife had five children:  
2 CONT *'''d)         MARGARET .  m Sir WILLIAM Gascoigne . 
2 CONT *From: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm#HenryPercyNorthumberlanddied1455A _________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT A direct ancestor of George Washington, William, Duke of Cambridge and Catherine, Duchess of Cambridge A direct descendant of Edward III
2 CONT
2 CONT The Lady Margaret Gascoigne (née Percy) (born c. 1447) was an English noblewoman, the daughter of Henry Percy, 3rd Earl of Northumberland and Eleanor Poynings.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Sir William Gascoigne, "the Younger", son of Sir William Gascoigne and wife. Their daughter Agnes (or Anne) Gascoigne married Sir Thomas Fairfax (died 1520–1521).
2 CONT
2 CONT Family[edit] She married Sir William Gascoigne V (c. 1450 – 1486),[1] son of Sir William Gascoigne IV (c. 1427 – c. 1463[2], great-grandson of Sir William Gascoigne I, Chief Justice of England) and Joan Neville (c. 1436–1464, grea
2 CONC t-granddaughter of Robert Ferrers, 5th Baron Boteler of Wem and Joan Beaufort). The couple had the following children:[3][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Gascoigne VI: married firstly Alice Frognall and secondly Margaret Nevill (daughter of Richard Nevill, 2nd Baron Latimer of Snape). Had issue by both marriages. The second son by first marriage, Sir Henry Gascoigne, wa
2 CONC s an ancestor of the Wyvill Baronets (from the 3rd onwards).[5][6] His daughter Margaret married Sir Thomas Middleton, of Stockeld.[7] Male line by primogeniture ended with his grandson William Gascoigne VIII, whose only daughter 
2 CONC and heiress (other children died young) Margaret (1530–1592/93) who became the paternal grandmother of Thomas Wentworth, 1st Earl of Strafford.[8] Margaret or Margery (c. 1473 – 1515):[9] married Ralph Ogle, 3rd Baron Ogle, and ha
2 CONC d issue.[10] Elizabeth (1470–1559):[11] married before April 1493 as his second wife Sir George Tailboys (c. 1467 – 1538), de jure 9th Baron Kyme and Sheriff of Lincolnshire, grandson of Sir William Tailboys, de jure 7th Baron Kym
2 CONC e. Anne or Agnes (c. 1474 – 1504): married firstly Sir Thomas Fairfax (c. 1475 – 1520). She had twin sons: Nicholas and William. Married secondly Ralph Nevill, of Thornton Bridge. Dorothy (c. 1475 – 1527):[12] married Sir Ninian M
2 CONC arkenfield (died 1527).[13]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Percy
2 CONT
