2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p1119.htm#i11185
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Margaret Percy [1]
2 CONT *F, #11185, 
2 CONT *d. circa November 1540
2 CONT *Last Edited=4 Apr 2009
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.3%
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Margaret Percy was the daughter of Henry Algernon Percy, 4th Earl of Northumberland and Catherine Spencer.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Henry Clifford, 1st Earl of Cumberland, son of Henry Clifford, 10th Lord Clifford and Anne St. John, after 1515.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died circa November 1540.[1] She was buried on 25 November 1540.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Her married name became Clifford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lady Margaret Percy and Henry Clifford, 1st Earl of Cumberland
2 CONT *1. Lady Maud Clifford+[1]
2 CONT *2. Sir Ingelram Clifford [1]
2 CONT *3. Lady Elizabeth Clifford [1]
2 CONT *4. Lady Jane Clifford [1]
2 CONT *5. Lady Catherine Clifford+[2] b. 1513, d. 1598
2 CONT *6. Henry Clifford, 2nd Earl of Cumberland+ b. 1517, d. 2 Jan 1569/70
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1064. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *2. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume XI, page 548. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
