1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joan or Jane D'abridgecourt was one of 5 daughters of Sir John D'abridgecourt & his wife [name variously as Maud, Matilda or Margery!].
2 CONT
2 CONT When her father died in 1415, Joan was named in his will as the wife of Sir John Cokayne/Cockayne.Her husband was killed fighting in a campaign in France the same year.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan was still alive in 1439, when she was embroiled in a legal fight over her dower rights with her stepmother Isabel [nee Shirley] Cokayne [who confusingly, was the mother to yet another Sir John Cokayne, half brother of Joan's 
2 CONC deceased husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Jane Dabridgecourt1 
2 CONT *F, #326140
2 CONT *Last Edited=24 Dec 2008 
2 CONT *'''     Jane Dabridgecourt was the daughter of Sir John Dabridgecourt.2 She married Sir John Cokayne, son of Sir Edmund Cokayne and Elizabeth de Harthill.1 She died, without issue.1
2 CONT *'''      Her married name became Cokayne.
2 CONT *'''Children of Jane Dabridgecourt and Sir John Cokayne
2 CONT ** 1.John Cokayne+2 d. 1504
2 CONT ** 2.William Cokayne+2
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S37] Volume 1, page 988. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT * 2.[S37] See. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://thepeerage.com/p32614.htm#i326140
2 CONT *______________________
2 CONT *Sir John Dabridgecourt, Keeper of the Tower of London & Calais Castle1,2 
2 CONT *M, #58614
2 CONT *Father     Sir Nicholas III d' Auberchicourt, Seigneur d'Auberchicourt & Bugnicourt2 b. c 1325, d. bt 1375 - 1379 
2 CONT *     Sir John Dabridgecourt, Keeper of the Tower of London & Calais Castle married Margery de Grey, daughter of Sir Reginald de Grey, 4th Baron Grey and Maud Botetourt, before September 1378; They had 1 son (Robert) and 5 daughte
2 CONC rs (Joan, wife of Hugh Willoughby; '''Joan, wife of Sir John Cokayne'''; Marion; Agnes; & Philippe). He had 2 additional sons (illegitimate) (John; & William).1,2 Sir John Dabridgecourt, Keeper of the Tower of London & Calais Cast
2 CONC le left a will on 20 July 1415; Requesting burial at Elvaston, Derbyshire; or in Dale Abbey, Derbyshire.1,2 His estate was probated on 8 November 1415.1,2
2 CONT *Family      Margery de Grey b. c 1352, d. b 3 Nov 1405
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 721.
2 CONT * 2.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. IV, p. 215-216.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1951.htm#i58614
