2 CONT *__________
2 CONT *Ralph de Stafford, 2nd Baron Stafford, 1st Earl of Stafford, KG (24 September 1301 – 31 August 1372) was an English nobleman and notable soldier during the Hundred Years War against France.
2 CONT *Ralph was born on 24 September 1301, the son of Edmund de Stafford, 1st Baron Stafford and Margaret Bassett.[1] Having lost his father at the age of seven, Ralph grew up in the midlands with his mother's relatives, including her 
2 CONC second husband Thomas Pipe. He had his first experience of royal service, along with his brothers and stepfather, when he joined the retinue of Ralph, 2nd Lord Bassett.[2] ....
2 CONT *Around 1326, Stafford married his first wife, Katherine Hastang (also known as Katherine Hastings).[1][3] Katherine was the daughter of Sir John de Hastang, Knight, of Chebsey, Staffordshire.[4] Ralph and Katherine had two daught
2 CONC ers:
2 CONT **''' Margaret, married Sir John of Bramshall (or Wickham) de Stafford, Knight.
2 CONT ** Joan, married Sir Nicholas de Beke, Knight.
2 CONT *etc.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ralph_Stafford,_1st_Earl_of_Stafford
2 CONT *_______________
2 CONT *THIS MARGARET IS NOT MARRIED TO SIR JOHN STAFFORD
2 CONT *Lady Margaret de Stafford 
2 CONT *F, #2093, b. circa 1364, d. 9 June 1396
2 CONT *Last Edited=27 Jan 2013 
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.44% 
2 CONT *     Lady Margaret de Stafford was born circa 1364 at Brancepeth, County Durham, England.1 She was the daughter of Hugh de Stafford, 2nd Earl of Stafford and Philippa Beauchamp.2,3 She married Ralph de Neville, 1st Earl of Westmo
2 CONC rland, son of John de Neville, 3rd Lord Neville and Maud de Percy, circa 1382 at Stafford, Staffordshire, England.1 A contract for the marriage of Lady Margaret de Stafford and Ralph de Neville, 1st Earl of Westmorland was signed 
2 CONC before 1370.2 She died on 9 June 1396 at Raby Castle, Durham, County Durham, England.2,1 She was buried at Bracepeth, County Durham, England.3
2 CONT *     As a result of her marriage, Lady Margaret de Stafford was styled as Lady Neville on 17 October 1388.
2 CONT *Children of Lady Margaret de Stafford and Ralph de Neville, 1st Earl of Westmorland
