2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p668.htm#i20051 ___________________
2 CONT *'''William de Ros, 6th Lord de Ros of Helmsley1
2 CONT *'''M, #47282, b. circa 1369, d. 1 September 1414
2 CONT *Last Edited=19 Oct 2014
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.45%
2 CONT *'''     William de Ros, 6th Lord de Ros of Helmsley was born circa 1369'''.2 He was the son of Thomas de Ros, 4th Lord de Ros of Helmsley and Beatrice de Stafford.3 '''He and Margaret d'Arundel obtained a marriage license on 9 Oc
2 CONC tober 1394.2 He died on 1 September 1414.2
2 CONT *'''     He succeeded to the title of 6th Lord de Ros of Helmsley [E., 1299] on 6 August 1393.2 He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.).2 He held the office of Lord Treasurer from 1403 to 1404.2 He was invested as a Knight, O
2 CONC rder of the Garter (K.G.) in 1404.2
2 CONT *'''Children of William de Ros, 6th Lord de Ros of Helmsley and Margaret d'Arundel
2 CONT **Margaret de Ros+1 d. a Sep 1423
2 CONT **Elizabeth de Ros+4
2 CONT **William de Ros4
2 CONT **Sir Robert de Ros4
2 CONT **Sir Richard de Ros4
2 CONT **Alice de Ros4
2 CONT **Beatrice de Ros4
2 CONT **John de Ros, 7th Lord de Ros of Helmsley2 b. c 1397, d. 22 Mar 1420/21
2 CONT **Thomas de Ros, 8th Lord de Ros of Helmsley+5 b. 26 Sep 1406, d. 18 Sep 1430
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct
2 CONC  or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 341. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *[S37] BP2003 volume 1, page 1107. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT *[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume XI, page 102.
2 CONT *[S5792] Robin Dening, "re: Rochfort Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger LUNDY (101053), 2 January 2012. Hereinafter cited as "re: Rochfort Family."
2 CONT *[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume XI, page 104.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p4729.htm#i47282 _________________________
2 CONT *'''William De ROS (7º B. Ros of Hamlake)
2 CONT *'''Born: ABT 1369, Hamlake, Yorkshire, England
2 CONT *'''Died: 1 Sep 1414, Stoke Albany, Northamptonshire, England
2 CONT *'''Buried: Belvoir
2 CONT *'''Notes: Knight of the Garter. Lord Treasurer of England. Brother & Heir''' to John de Ros, '''aged 24 at his brother's death. Summoned to Parliament from 20 Nov 1394. According to Cockayne's "Complete Peerage", he was summoned 
2 CONC to parliament regularly 1394-1413. He served on the Privy Councils of both Richard II and Henry IV. He was in Calais in 1396 for the wedding of Richard II to Isabelle, the 8 year old daughter of King Charles VI of France. This mar
2 CONC riage was very unpopular with the English nobility and added to their discontent with the King's rule in general. In 1399, while Richard was on an expedition to Ireland, Henry Bolingbroke, the Duke of Lancaster (the future Henry I
2 CONC V), who had been banished by Richard, returned to England with an army to claim the throne for himself. William threw his support to Henry. He was present at the abdication of Richard and assented to his inprisonment (which led to
2 CONC  his death shortly thereafter). William was Treasurer of England in 1403 &1404; made a Knight of the Garter in 1404; was one of the auditors of he war accounts in 1406; and in 1413-14 was the King's chief commissioner for the shir
2 CONC es of Middlesex, Nottingham, and Derby in the matter of determining the facts relating to rebellions and treasons commited by the Lollards.
2 CONT *Father: Thomas De ROS (5º B. Ros of Hamlake)
2 CONT *Mother: Beatrice STAFFORD (C. Desmond)
2 CONT *'''Married: Margaret FITZALAN (B. Ros of Hamlake) 9 Oct 1394
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. John De ROS (8º B. Ros of Hamlake)
2 CONT **2. Margaret De ROS (B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT **3. Thomas De ROS (9º B. Ros of Hamlake)
2 CONT **4. Elizabeth De ROS (B. Morley)
2 CONT **5. Robert De ROS (Sir)
2 CONT **6. William De ROS (d. 1421, Beauge)
2 CONT **7. Beatrice De ROS (Nun)
2 CONT **8. Alice De ROS
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/ROS.htm#William De ROS (7º B. Ros of Hamlake) __________________
2 CONT *'''Sir William de Roos
2 CONT *'''Birth: 	1370
2 CONT *'''Death: 	Sep. 1, 1414  Belvoir, Leicestershire, England
2 CONT *'''Knight of Helmsley, Yorkshire, 6th Lord Helmsley. Privy Councillor, Lord Treasurer of England. 
2 CONT *'''Son and heir''' to Sir Thomas de Roos and Beatrice de Stafford. '''Grandson of''' Sir William de Roos and Margery Badlesmere, Sir Ralph de Stafford and Margaret de Audley. 
2 CONT *'''Husband of Margaret de Arundel''', daughter of Sir John de Arundel of Buckland and Eleanor Maultravers. '''They were married at Sterborough in Lingfield, Surrey by licence dated 09 Oct 1394 and had five sons and four daughters
2 CONC :
2 CONT ** Sir John de Roos, 7th Lord Helmsley
2 CONT ** Sir William de Roos
2 CONT ** Sir Thomas de Roos, 8th Lord Helmsley, married Eleanor de Beauchamp
2 CONT ** Sir Robert de Roos
2 CONT ** Sir Richard
2 CONT ** Alice
2 CONT ** Margaret, wife of James Audley
2 CONT ** Beatrice, a nun
2 CONT ** Elizabeth, wife of Lord Robert Morley
2 CONT *'''William was summoned to Parliament 1394 to 1413, attended the King Richard's wedding to Isabella, the daughter of Charles, the King of France, in Calais in 1396. He was present at the Tower of London in 1399 when King Richard 
2 CONC signed his abdication. 
2 CONT *'''Sir William died estate at Belvoir Castle, Leicestershire and was buried at Bevoir Priory.
2 CONT *Family links: 
2 CONT * Parents:
2 CONT *  Thomas de Ros (1337 - 1384)
2 CONT * Spouse:
2 CONT *'''  Margaret Arundel Roos (____ - 1438)*
2 CONT * Children:
2 CONT **  John de Roos (1396 - 1421)*
2 CONT * Siblings:
2 CONT *  Margaret de Ros Grey (____ - 1414)*
2 CONT *  John de Ros (____ - 1393)*
2 CONT *  William de Roos (1370 - 1414)
2 CONT *'''Burial:  Belvoir Priory, Bottesford, Melton Borough, Leicestershire, England
2 CONT *Find A Grave Memorial# 101361349
2 CONT *From: http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=roos&GSfn=william&GSbyrel=all&GSdyrel=all&GScntry=5&GSob=n&GRid=101361349&df=all& ________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT William De Ros Fifth Lord Ros [Parents] was born in 1368 in Belvoir, Leicester, England. He died on 1 Sep 1414 in Belvoir, England. He married Margaret Arundel. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Arundel was born in 1370 in Arundel, Sussex, England. She died on 3 Jul 1438 in England. She married William De Ros Fifth Lord Ros. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT    F i Margaret De Ros 
2 CONT
2 CONT    M ii Thomas De Ros Duke of Somerset 
2 CONT
2 CONT    M iii Robert De Ros 
2 CONT
2 CONT ________________________
