2 CONT *William de Ros, 6th Baron de Ros of Helmsley, KG (c.1370 – 1 September 1414) was Lord Treasurer of England.
2 CONT *He was a son of Thomas de Ros, 4th Baron de Ros and Beatrice Stafford, daughter of Ralph Stafford, 1st Earl of Stafford. He was also a younger brother of John de Ros, 5th Baron de Ros.
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *William de Ros married, by licence dated 9 October 1394, Margaret Fitzalan (d. 3 July 1438), the daughter of John FitzAlan, 1st Baron Arundel, by Eleanor Maltravers (c.1345 – 12 January 1405), younger daughter and coheir of Sir J
2 CONC ohn Maltravers (d. 22 January 1349) and his wife Gwenthlian, by whom he had five sons and four daughters:[2]
2 CONT **John de Ros, 7th Baron de Ros.
2 CONT **William de Ros.
2 CONT **Thomas de Ros, 8th Baron de Ros.
2 CONT **'''Sir Robert de Ros, who married Anne Halsham.
2 CONT **Sir Richard de Ros.
2 CONT **Alice de Ros.
2 CONT **Margaret De Ros, who married James Tuchet, 5th Baron Audley about 1415.
2 CONT **Beatrice de Ros (a nun).
2 CONT **Elizabeth de Ros, who married Robert de Morley, 6th Baron Morley.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_de_Ros,_6th_Baron_de_Ros _________________
2 CONT *Sir William de Roos
2 CONT *Birth: 	1370
2 CONT *Death: 	Sep. 1, 1414  Belvoir, Leicestershire, England
2 CONT *Knight of Helmsley, Yorkshire, 6th Lord Helmsley. Privy Councillor, Lord Treasurer of England. 
2 CONT *Son and heir to Sir Thomas de Roos and Beatrice de Stafford. Grandson of Sir William de Roos and Margery Badlesmere, Sir Ralph de Stafford and Margaret de Audley. 
2 CONT *Husband of Margaret de Arundel, daughter of Sir John de Arundel of Buckland and Eleanor Maultravers. They were married at Sterborough in Lingfield, Surrey by licence dated 09 Oct 1394 and had five sons and four daughters:
2 CONT ** Sir John de Roos, 7th Lord Helmsley
2 CONT ** Sir William de Roos
2 CONT ** Sir Thomas de Roos, 8th Lord Helmsley, married Eleanor de Beauchamp
2 CONT **''' Sir Robert de Roos
2 CONT ** Sir Richard
2 CONT ** Alice
2 CONT ** Margaret, wife of James Audley
2 CONT ** Beatrice, a nun
2 CONT ** Elizabeth, wife of Lord Robert Morley
2 CONT *William was summoned to Parliament 1394 to 1413, attended the King Richard's wedding to Isabella, the daughter of Charles, the King of France, in Calais in 1396. He was present at the Tower of London in 1399 when King Richard sig
2 CONC ned his abdication. 
2 CONT *Sir William died estate at Belvoir Castle, Leicestershire and was buried at Bevoir Priory.
