1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==John Ros, 7th Baron Ros==
2 CONT '''John Ros, 7th Baron Ros of Helmsley (c.1397 – 22 March 1421) was an English nobleman.'''
2 CONT '''He was the eldest son''' of William Ros, 6th Baron Ros, and Margaret Fitzalan (d. 3 July 1438), the daughter of John FitzAlan, 1st Baron Arundel, by Eleanor Maltravers (d. 3 July 1438), younger daughter and coheir of Sir John M
2 CONC altravers.[2]
2 CONT '''He served as a soldier of Henry V of England during the Hundred Years' War. Six years after the Battle of Agincourt, John participated in the Battle of Baugé. He was among the casualties along with his brother''' William Ros, T
2 CONC homas of Lancaster, Duke of Clarence, the governor of Normandy and others. '''He was buried at the Belvoir Priory.'''
2 CONT '''Marriage'''
2 CONT '''John de Ros married Margery le Despencer''', daughter and heiress of Philip le Despencer, 2nd Baron le Despencer, '''but had no issue by her. After his death, Margery married''' Roger Wentworth (d. 24 October 1452), esquire, yo
2 CONC unger son of John Wentworth of Elmsall, Yorkshire, by whom she had issue. She was fined £1000 for having contracted a dishonourable marriage far beneath her station.[3]
2 CONT Ancestry
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Ros,_7th_Baron_Ros
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________________
2 CONT ==Sir John de Roos==
2 CONT '''Birth	2 Aug 1396'''
2 CONT '''England'''
2 CONT '''Death	20 Mar 1421 (aged 24)'''
2 CONT '''France'''
2 CONT '''Burial	Belvoir Priory'''
2 CONT '''Bottesford, Melton Borough, Leicestershire, England'''
2 CONT Find a Grave Memorial ID: 109973539
2 CONT '''Knight, 7th Lord Roos of Helmsley, Captain of Chateau Gaillard, Captain of Mantes.'''
2 CONT Son and heir to Sir William Roos, Knight of Bath, 6th Lord Roos of Helmsley and Margaret de Arundel, daughter of Sir John Arundel, Lord Arundel.
2 CONT '''First husband of Margery le Despenser,''' daughter of Sir Philip Despenser and Elizabeth Tibetot. '''They were married by dispensation for consanguinity dated 13 Sept 1404 and had no children.'''
2 CONT '''Sir John was present at the Battle of Agincourt in 1415 and at the Siege of Rouen 1417 to 1419, after which was was granted the castle and lordship of Barcquesville. John also took part in the siege of Muelen in 1420.'''
2 CONT '''Sir John was slain at the Battle of Beauge in Anjou 22 March 1421, and buried in Belvoir Priory. His widow, Margery, would marry''' Roger Wentworth.
2 CONT '''John was buried originally in Belvoir Abbey and moved to St Mary's Church, Bottesford during the dissolution.'''
2 CONT '''The family surname is found both Ros and Roos.'''
2 CONT Family Members
2 CONT '''Parents'''
