2 CONT ==John de Ros, 7th Lord de Ros of Helmsley1 ==
2 CONT '''M, #368998, b. circa 1397, d. 22 March 1420/21'''
2 CONT Last Edited=6 Mar 2011
2 CONT Consanguinity Index=0.17%
2 CONT '''John de Ros, 7th Lord de Ros of Helmsley was born circa 1397.1 He was the son''' of William de Ros, 6th Lord de Ros of Helmsley and Margaret d'Arundel.1 '''He married Margaret Despenser,''' daughter of Philip le Despenser, 2nd 
2 CONC Lord Despenser and Elizabeth Tiptoft.1 '''He died on 22 March 1420/21, killed in action.'''1
2 CONT '''He succeeded as the 7th Lord de Ros of Helmsley [E., 1299] on 1 September 1414.1 He fought in the Battle of Agincourt in 1415.1 He fought in the Siege of Rouen between 1417 and 1419.1 He fought in the Sige of Melun in 1420.1 He
2 CONC  fought in the Battle of Beaugé on 22 March 1420/21.'''1
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT 1. [S37] BP2003 volume 1, page 1107. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT From: https://www.thepeerage.com/p36900.htm#i368998
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________________
2 CONT ==John De ROS (8º B. Ros of Hamlake)==
2 CONT '''Born: ABT 1403, Hamlake, Yorkshire, England'''
2 CONT '''Died: 1421'''
2 CONT '''Father''': William De ROS (7º B. Ros of Hamlake)
2 CONT '''Mother''': Margaret FITZALAN (B. Ros of Hamlake)
2 CONT '''Married: Margery (Margaret) DESPENCER (B. Ros of Hamlake) 5 Sep 1401'''
2 CONT From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/ROS.htm#John%20De%20ROS%20(8%C2%BA%20B.%20Ros%20of%20Hamlake)
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________________
2 CONT B.      LORDS ROS (of Helmsley)
2 CONT WILLIAM de Ros, son of ROBERT de Ros & his wife Isabel de Albini (-[12 May/16 Aug] 1316, bur Kirkham).  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Rievaulx Abbey names "Willielmum de Ros" as son of "Robertum de Roos" and his wife “I
2 CONC sabellam hæredem D’Albany”, adding that he was buried in Kirkham monastery[430].  A writ dated 4 Jun "13 Edw I", after the death of "Robert de Ros of Beuveyr alias Beuvayr", names "William his son aged 30 is his next heir"[431].  
2 CONC He was summoned to parliament in 1299, whereby he is held to have become Lord Ros of Helmsley. 
2 CONT m (before 1287) MATILDA de Vaux, daughter of JOHN de Vaux & [his wife Joan ---] ([1260/61]-[before 1316], bur Pentney Priory, Norfolk).  An undated manuscript names “Petronilla et Matilda” as the two daughters of John de Vaux, add
2 CONC ing that Matilda married “domino Willielmo de Ros et genuit Willelmum primogenitum suum...”[432].  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Rievaulx Abbey records that "Willielmum de Ros" married "Matildam de Vaus hæredem medietat
2 CONC is terrarium Johannis de Vaux"[433].  Inquisitions following a writ dated "15 Edw I" after the death of "John de Vallibus...on Thursday before the Exaltation of the Holy Cross 15 Edw I” name “Petronilla [...aged 28...[who married]
2 CONC  William de Nerford] and Maud [...aged 26...[who] married William de Ros] his daughters are his next heirs and of full age”[434]. 
2 CONT William & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT *1.         WILLIAM de Ros (-3 Feb 1343, bur Kirkham).  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Rievaulx Abbey names "Willielmum de Roos" as the son of "Willielmum de Ros" and his wife "Matildam de Vaus", adding that he was burie
2 CONC d in Kirkham monastery[435].  Lord Ros.  m as her first husband, MARGERY de Badlesmere, daughter of BARTHOLOMEW de Badlesmere Lord Badlesmere & his wife Margaret de Clare (-after 31 May 1356).  A manuscript narrating the foundatio
2 CONC n of Rievaulx Abbey records that "Willielmus de Roos" married "Margeriam de Badilsmere"[436].  She married secondly (royal licence 6 Mar 1351) Sir Thomas de Arundel.  She married thirdly as his third wife, Sir John Avenel.  The wi
2 CONC ll of "Elizabeth de Bohun Countess of Northampton", dated 31 May 1356, bequeathed property to “Humphrey my son...Elizabeth my daughter...my sister the Countess of Oxford...my sister Roos...Agnes Devereux, John Avenell, Richard Wal
2 CONC degrave”[437].  William & his wife had five children: **a)         WILLIAM de Ros (Frieston, Lincolnshire 19 May 1329-before 3 Dec 1352).  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Rievaulx Abbey names "Willielmum, Thomam, Margaret
2 CONC am et Matildam" as the children of "Willielmus de Roos" and his wife "Margeriam de Badilsmere", adding that William died childless "in terra sancta" and was buried there[438].  Lord Ros.  m (before 8 May 1341) as her first husband
2 CONC , MARGARET Neville, daughter of RALPH Neville Lord Neville of Raby & his wife Alice de Audley (-May 1372).  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Rievaulx Abbey records that "Willielmum", son of "Willielmus de Roos" and his wif
2 CONC e "Margeriam de Badilsmere", married "Margaretam filiam domini Radulphi de Nevill"[439].  She married secondly (royal licence 26 Feb 1358) as his first wife, Henry de Percy Lord Percy, who was created Earl of Northumberland. 
2 CONT **b)         THOMAS de Ros (Stoke Albany, Northamptonshire 13 Jan 1337-Uffington, Lincolnshire 8 Jun 1384).  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Rievaulx Abbey names "Willielmum, Thomam, Margaretam et Matildam" as the childre
2 CONC n of "Willielmus de Roos" and his wife "Margeriam de Badilsmere", adding that he died "apud Uffington versus terram sanctam" and was buried "in monasterio Ryevallis"[440].  Lord Ros.  m (royal licence 1 Jan 1359) as her second hus
2 CONC band, BEATRICE de Stafford, widow of MORICE FitzThomas Earl of Desmond, daughter of RALPH de Stafford Earl of Stafford & his wife Margaret de Audley of the Earls of Gloucester (-Apr 1415).  A manuscript narrating the foundation of
2 CONC  Rievaulx Abbey records that "Thomas", son of "Willielmus de Roos" and his wife "Margeriam de Badilsmere", married "Beatricem filiam Radulphi comitis Staffordiæ"[441].  She married thirdly (before 20 Aug 1385) Sir Richard de Burle
2 CONC y.  Thomas & his wife had children: 
2 CONT ***i)          JOHN de Ros ([1364/1368]-Paphos, Cyprus 6 Aug 1393, bur Rievaulx).  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Rievaulx Abbey names "Johannem, Willielmum, Thomam et Robertum, Elizabetham et Margaretam" as the children
2 CONC  of "Thomas de Roos" and his wife "Beatricem filiam Radulphi comitis Staffordiæ", adding that John died "sine hærede masculo apud Cypresse peregrinans versus terram sanctam" and was buried "apud Ryevallum"[442].  Lord Ros.  m (bef
2 CONC ore 22 Jun 1382) MARY de Percy, daughter of HENRY Lord Percy & his second wife Joan de Orreby (-York 25 Aug 1394).  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Rievaulx Abbey records that "Johannem", son of "Thomas de Roos" and his w
2 CONC ife "Beatricem filiam Radulphi comitis Staffordiæ", married "Mariam de Orebe --- comitis Northumbriæ"[443]. 
2 CONT ***ii)         WILLIAM de Ros ([1367/68]-Belvoir 1 Sep 1414).  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Rievaulx Abbey names "Johannem, Willielmum, Thomam et Robertum, Elizabetham et Margaretam" as the children of "Thomas de Roos"
2 CONC  and his wife "Beatricem filiam Radulphi comitis Staffordiæ", and that William died “apud Belverum 1 Sep 1414” where he was buried[444].  Lord Ros. 
2 CONT ***-        see below. 
2 CONT ***iii)        THOMAS de Ros .  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Rievaulx Abbey names "Johannem, Willielmum, Thomam et Robertum, Elizabetham et Margaretam" as the children of "Thomas de Roos" and his wife "Beatricem filiam
2 CONC  Radulphi comitis Staffordiæ"[445]. 
2 CONT ***iv)        ROBERT de Ros .  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Rievaulx Abbey names "Johannem, Willielmum, Thomam et Robertum, Elizabetham et Margaretam" as the children of "Thomas de Roos" and his wife "Beatricem filiam 
2 CONC Radulphi comitis Staffordiæ"[446]. 
2 CONT ***v)         ELIZABETH de Ros (-Mar 1424).  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Rievaulx Abbey names "Johannem, Willielmum, Thomam et Robertum, Elizabetham et Margaretam" as the children of "Thomas de Roos" and his wife "Bea
2 CONC tricem filiam Radulphi comitis Staffordiæ"[447].  m THOMAS de Clifford Lord Clifford, son of ROGER [V] de Clifford Lord Clifford & his wife Matilda de Beauchamp ([1362/63]-18 Aug 1391). 
2 CONT ***vi)        MARGARET de Ros .  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Rievaulx Abbey names "Johannem, Willielmum, Thomam et Robertum, Elizabetham et Margaretam" as the children of "Thomas de Roos" and his wife "Beatricem filia
2 CONC m Radulphi comitis Staffordiæ"[448]. 
2 CONT **c)         MARGARET de Ros .  ... etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT WILLIAM de Ros, son of THOMAS de Ros Lord Ros & his wife Beatrice de Stafford of the Earls of Stafford ([1367/68]-Belvoir 1 Sep 1414).  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Rievaulx Abbey names "Johannem, Willielmum, Thomam et
2 CONC  Robertum, Elizabetham et Margaretam" as the children of "Thomas de Roos" and his wife "Beatricem filiam Radulphi comitis Staffordiæ", and that William died “apud Belverum 1 Sep 1414” where he was buried[453].  Lord Ros. 
2 CONT m MARGARET d’Arundel, daughter of JOHN d’Arundel & his wife Eleanor Baroness Mautravers (-3 Jul 1438).  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Rievaulx Abbey records that “Willielmus de Roos” married “Margaretam filiam domini Jo
2 CONC hannis de Arundell”, '''by whom he was father of “Johannem''', Willielmum, Thomam, Robertum et Ricardum, Beatricem, Aliciam, Margaretam et Elizabetham”[454]. 
2 CONT William & his wife had children: 
2 CONT *1.         THOMAS de Ros (Belvoir 26 Sep 1406-France 18 Aug 1430).  Lord Ros.  m as her first husband, ELEANOR Beauchamp, daughter of RICHARD Beauchamp Earl of Warwick & his wife Elizabeth Berkeley (Wedgenock, Warwickshire 1407-B
2 CONC aynard’s Castle, London 6 Mar 1467).  She married secondly ([1431/35]) Edmund Beaufort Earl of Somerset, who was created  Duke of Somerset in 1448.  She married thirdly Walter Rokesley. 
2 CONT From: https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3P-S.htm#WilliamRosdied1414A
2 CONT
