2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_de_Ros,_9th_Baron_de_Ros
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas de Ros, 9th Baron de Ros of Helmsley (26 September 1406 – 18 August 1430) was an English nobleman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lineage
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the second son of William de Ros, 7th Baron de Ros and Margaret Fitzalan. His mother was a daughter of John FitzAlan, 2nd Baron Arundel and Elizabeth le Despenser.
2 CONT
2 CONT Inherited rank and privileges
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also a younger brother of John de Ros, 8th Baron de Ros.
2 CONT
2 CONT His older brother died childless in the Battle of Beaugé of 1421. Thomas inherited his rank and privileges. He followed the example of his brother in participating in the Hundred Years' War.
2 CONT
2 CONT Military service
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought in the Battle of Verneuil under the successful command of John, Duke of Bedford. He was honored for his efforts, knighted by Henry VI of England on 19 May 1426. Henry was nephew of the Duke.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas resumed service under the Duke in 1427. He was summoned to the Parliament of England in 1429.
2 CONT
2 CONT Drowned in the Seine
2 CONT
2 CONT He fell into the Seine during a minor skirmish and drowned in 1430.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and succession
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Lady Eleanor Beauchamp, daughter of Richard de Beauchamp, 13th Earl of Warwick and his first wife Elizabeth Berkeley. Eleanor was an older half-sister of Henry de Beauchamp, 1st Duke of Warwick and Anne Neville, 
2 CONC Countess of Warwick. They were parents of three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT  Thomas de Ros, 10th Baron de Ros (9 September 1427 – 17 May 1464).
2 CONT  Richard de Ros (8 March 1429 – after 1492).
2 CONT
2 CONT  Margaret de Ros (1432 – 10 December 1488). Married first William de Botreaux, 3rd Baron Botreaux(d.1462), secondly Thomas Burgh, 1st Baron Burgh of Gainsborough.
2 CONT
2 CONT His widow was remarried to Edmund Beaufort, 2nd Duke of Somerset.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestry
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_de_Ros,_9th_Baron_de_Ros#Ancestry
