2 DATE 23 SEP 1459
2 ADDR
3 CITY Blore Heath
3 CTRY England
1 OCCU Sir, Knight
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "1459. Sir Thomas de Dutton, with his brother John Dutton, and his eldest son Peter Dutton, killed at the battle of Blore heath, in Cheshire (Sunday, Sept. 23), during the Wars of the Roses."
2 CONT
2 CONT 14th Lord of Dutton
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.penrose.org/getperson.php?personID=I31315&tree=penrose
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Dutton
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT "Memorials of the Duttons of Dutton in Cheshire"
2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=OrsPAAAAMAAJ&pg=PR19&output=text
2 CONT
2 CONT Died at the battle of Blore Heath in Cheshire (September 23, 1459) during the Wars of the Roses along with his brother John and eldest son Peter.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas's father-in-law James Touchet, 5th Baron Audley, also died in the battle of Blore Heath.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Thomas Dutton (1 August 1421 – 23 September 1459) was a medieval English knight.
2 CONT
2 CONT His family owned an estate, Dutton Hall, that was originally located in Cheshire, England. It is now located in Sussex, the original building having been moved there in the 1930s. The building is now a private school, Stoke Brunsw
2 CONC ick, at Ashurst Wood, just south of East Grinstead.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Thomas Dutton married Anne Touchett, daughter of James Touchet, Lord Audley 5th Baron of Audley and Heliegh Castle. Sir Thomas Dutton and his father in law, Lord Audley died on 23 September 1459 at the Battle of Blore Heath, B
2 CONC lore Heath, England. Lord Audley was in command of approximately 10,000 troops defending the throne of King Henry VI.
2 CONT *<nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/TOUCHET.htm#Anne TOUCHET1
2 CONT *''''''Anne TOUCHET
2 CONT *Born: 1422, Heleigh, Staffordshire, England
2 CONT *Died: 1503
2 CONT *''''''Notes: Sir Thomas de Dutton with his brother John and eldest son Peter Dutton killed at the battle of Blore-Heath in Cheshire Sunday, 23 Sep 1459, during the War of the Roses. In 1527, at the death of Laurence Dutton of Dut
2 CONC ton without a male heir, Dutton property passed to Sir Piers Dutton of Hatton whose right contested by heirs-general of Sir Hugh Dutton. In 1534, Termination of the Dutton lawsuit by awary of Henry VIII (May 16) by which Sir Piers
2 CONC  Dutton of Hatton became owner of Dutton, confirmed by Act of Parliament in 1536.
2 CONT *Father: James TOUCHET (2º B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT *Mother: Margaret De ROS (B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT *''''''Married 1: Thomas DUTTON (Sir) (son of John Dutton and Margaret Savage)
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Peter DUTTON
2 CONT **2. Margaret DUTTON (m.1 Thomas Aston - m.2 Ralph Vernon)
2 CONT **3. Anne DUTTON (m. Thomas Molyneux)
2 CONT **4. Isabel DUTTON (m. Christopher Southworth)
2 CONT **5. Maud DUTTON (m. William Booth)
2 CONT **6. John DUTTON (b. ABT 1444 - d. ABT 1473) (m. Margaret Molyneux)
2 CONT **7. Eleanor DUTTON (m. Richard Cholmondeley, Esq.)
2 CONT **8. Elizabeth DUTTON (m. Ralph Bostock)
2 CONT **9. Alice DUTTON
2 CONT **10. Laurence DUTTON (b. ABT 1458 - d. AFT 1522)
2 CONT *Married 2: Hugh DONE
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **11. Elizabeth DONE (m. John Egerton)
2 CONT *__________________
2 CONT *http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p360.htm#i10814
2 CONT *''''''Sir Thomas Dutton1
2 CONT *''''''M, d. 23 September 1459
2 CONT *Father Sir John Dutton b. c 1403, d. 1445 
2 CONT *Mother Margaret Savage b. c 1403, d. a 1450 
2 CONT *''''''     Sir Thomas Dutton was born at of Dutton, Cheshire, England. He married Margaret Touchet, daughter of Sir James Touchet, 5th Lord Audley and Margaret Roos.2 Sir Thomas Dutton died on 23 September 1459 at Battle of Blore
2 CONC  Heath, Staffordshire, England.
2 CONT *''''''Family Margaret Touchet b. c 1424, d. 1503 
2 CONT *Children 
2 CONT *◦Elizabeth Dutton+ d. 5 Feb 1516
2 CONT *◦John Dutton d. 1473
2 CONT *◦Peter Dutton d. 23 Sep 1459
2 CONT *◦Eleanor Dutton+
2 CONT *◦Anne Dutton+ d. 22 Oct 1520
2 CONT *◦Margaret Dutton+
2 CONT *◦Isabel Dutton+ b. c 1443
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S2720] Unknown author, The History of the County Palatine and City of Chester, by George Ormerod, 1819, p. 480; Magna Charta Sureties, 1215, 4th Ed., by F. L. Weis, p. 109.
2 CONT *2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 722-723.
2 CONT *_______________
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sir Thomas Dutton (1 August 1421 â 23 September 1459) was a medieval English knight. His family owned an estate, Dutton Hall, that was originally located in Cheshire, England. It is now located in Sussex, the original building h
2 CONC aving been moved there in the 1930s. The building is now a private school, Stoke Brunswick, at Ashurst Wood, just south of East Grinstead. Sir Thomas Dutton married Anne Touchett, daughter of James Touchet, Lord Audley 5th Baron o
2 CONC f Audley and Heliegh Castle. Sir Thomas Dutton and his father in law, Lord Audley died on 23 September 1459 at the Battle of Blore Heath, Blore Heath, England. Lord Audley was in command of approximately 10,000 troops defending th
2 CONC e throne of King Henry VI.
