2 DATE 22 OCT 1520
2 ADDR
3 CITY Dutton
3 STAE England
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Isabel Dutton
2 CONT *'''F, #44450, b. circa 1443
2 CONT *Father      Sir Thomas Dutton d. 23 Sep 1459
2 CONT *Mother     Anne Touchet b. c 1424, d. 1503
2 CONT *'''     Isabel Dutton was born circa 1443. She married Sir Christopher Southworth, son of Richard Southworth, Esq. and Elizabeth Molyneux, on 11 July 1463.
2 CONT *'''Family      Sir Christopher Southworth b. c 1443, d. 12 Aug 1502
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Sir John Southworth, Lord Samlesbury, Sheriff of Lancashire+ b. bt 1474 - 1475, d. bt 1517 - 1519
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1479.htm#i44450 _________________
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Isabel Sutton
2 CONT *F, #322461
2 CONT *Last Edited=11 May 2012
2 CONT *'''     Isabel Sutton is the daughter of Sir Thomas Sutton and Anne Touchet. She married Sir Christopher Southworth.
2 CONT *'''      Her married name became Southworth.
2 CONT *'''Child of Isabel Sutton and Sir Christopher Southworth
2 CONT ** 1.Sir John Southworth+
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p32247.htm#i322461
2 CONT
2 CONT == Ancestry ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabelle (Dutton) de Southworth is a direct decendent and bloodline of the kings of England, Scotland, France, and Norse Kings from Denmark/Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabelle's identified family bloodline runs to the Plantagenet kings through her mother's line, starting with English King Edward III (her 3rd Great Grandfather), and traveling through the English manarchy to Kings Edward II (Plan
2 CONC tagenet) and Edward I (Plantagenet) "Longshanks" of England (reign 1272-1307ad) her 5th great grandfather. Through this bloodline, Isabelle is a direct decendent and blood line of the House of Mercia, House of Wessex, House of Nor
2 CONC mandy, and the House of Plantagenet (Angevin). (King Edward I of England; King Edward II; King Edward III; Edmund Plantagenet, KG, of Langley; 1st Duke of York; Constance Plantagenet; Duchess of Gloucester; Eleanor (de Holland) Tu
2 CONC chet, Baroness of Audley; Anne Margaret (Tuchet) Dutton; Isabelle (Dutton) de Southworth.
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT *Anne TOUCHET
2 CONT *Born: 1422, Heleigh, Staffordshire, England
2 CONT *Died: 1503
2 CONT *Notes: Sir Thomas de Dutton with his brother John and eldest son Peter Dutton killed at the battle of Blore-Heath in Cheshire Sunday, 23 Sep 1459, during the War of the Roses. In 1527, at the death of Laurence Dutton of Dutton wi
2 CONC thout a male heir, Dutton property passed to Sir Piers Dutton of Hatton whose right contested by heirs-general of Sir Hugh Dutton. In 1534, Termination of the Dutton lawsuit by awary of Henry VIII (May 16) by which Sir Piers Dutto
2 CONC n of Hatton became owner of Dutton, confirmed by Act of Parliament in 1536.
2 CONT *Father: James TOUCHET (2º B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT *Mother: Margaret De ROS (B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT *Married 1: Thomas DUTTON (Sir) (son of John Dutton and Margaret Savage)
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Peter DUTTON
2 CONT **2. Margaret DUTTON (m.1 Thomas Aston - m.2 Ralph Vernon)
2 CONT **3. Anne DUTTON (m. Thomas Molyneux)
2 CONT **'''4. Isabel DUTTON (m. Christopher Southworth)
2 CONT **5. Maud DUTTON (m. William Booth)
2 CONT **6. John DUTTON (b. ABT 1444 - d. ABT 1473) (m. Margaret Molyneux)
2 CONT **7. Eleanor DUTTON (m. Richard Cholmondeley, Esq.)
2 CONT **8. Elizabeth DUTTON (m. Ralph Bostock)
2 CONT **9. Alice DUTTON
2 CONT **10. Laurence DUTTON (b. ABT 1458 - d. AFT 1522)
2 CONT *Married 2: Hugh DONE
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **11. Elizabeth DONE (m. John Egerton)
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/TOUCHET.htm#Anne TOUCHET1
