1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Elizabeth Done1
2 CONT *F
2 CONT *Father Hugh Done 
2 CONT *Mother Margaret Touchet b. c 1424, d. 1503 
2 CONT *'''     Elizabeth Done was born at of Oulton, Cheshire, England. She married John Egerton, Esq., son of Philip Egerton, Esq. and Margery Mainwaring, circa 1480 at of Egerton, Cheshire, England.2
2 CONT *'''Family John Egerton, Esq. b. c 1463, d. 1483 
2 CONT *Children 
2 CONT **Philip Egerton, Esq.+ d. 1535
2 CONT **Susan Egerton2
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S11221] Unknown author, The History of the County Palatine and City of Chester, by George Ormerod, 1819, p. 350.
2 CONT *2.[S10297] Unknown author, History of the County Palatine and City of Chester, by George Omerod, 1819., p. 350.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1216.htm#i36523 _________________
2 CONT *'''Elizabeth Done1
2 CONT *F, #448736
2 CONT *Last Edited=21 Sep 2010
2 CONT *'''     Elizabeth Done is the daughter of Hugh Done and unknown daughter Tuchet.1 She married John Egerton, son of Philip Egerton and Margery Mainwaring.1
2 CONT *'''     Her married name became Egerton.1
2 CONT *'''Child of Elizabeth Done and John Egerton
2 CONT **1.Philip Egerton+1 d. 1534
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 1673. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p44874.htm#i448736 ___________________
2 CONT *Anne TOUCHET
2 CONT *Born: 1422, Heleigh, Staffordshire, England
2 CONT *Died: 1503
2 CONT *Notes: Sir Thomas de Dutton with his brother John and eldest son Peter Dutton killed at the battle of Blore-Heath in Cheshire Sunday, 23 Sep 1459, during the War of the Roses. In 1527, at the death of Laurence Dutton of Dutton wi
2 CONC thout a male heir, Dutton property passed to Sir Piers Dutton of Hatton whose right contested by heirs-general of Sir Hugh Dutton. In 1534, Termination of the Dutton lawsuit by awary of Henry VIII (May 16) by which Sir Piers Dutto
2 CONC n of Hatton became owner of Dutton, confirmed by Act of Parliament in 1536.
2 CONT *Father: James TOUCHET (2º B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT *Mother: Margaret De ROS (B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT *Married 1: Thomas DUTTON (Sir) (son of John Dutton and Margaret Savage)
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Peter DUTTON
2 CONT **2. Margaret DUTTON (m.1 Thomas Aston - m.2 Ralph Vernon)
2 CONT **3. Anne DUTTON (m. Thomas Molyneux)
2 CONT **4. Isabel DUTTON (m. Christopher Southworth)
2 CONT **5. Maud DUTTON (m. William Booth)
2 CONT **6. John DUTTON (b. ABT 1444 - d. ABT 1473) (m. Margaret Molyneux)
2 CONT **7. Eleanor DUTTON (m. Richard Cholmondeley, Esq.)
2 CONT **8. Elizabeth DUTTON (m. Ralph Bostock)
2 CONT **9. Alice DUTTON
2 CONT **10. Laurence DUTTON (b. ABT 1458 - d. AFT 1522)
2 CONT *Married 2: Hugh DONE
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **'''11. Elizabeth DONE (m. John Egerton)
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/TOUCHET.htm#Anne TOUCHET1 ___________
2 CONT *'''The history of the county palatine and city of Chester: .... Vol. II.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/historyofcountyp02orme
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyofcountyp02orme#page/350/mode/1up
2 CONT **EGERTON, OF EGERTON. Pg.350-351
2 CONT *PHILIP GOCH, second son of David de Malpas, surnamed Le Clerk, which David was lord of a moiety of the barony of Malpas. = CATHERINE, daughter of Jorveth, alias Yawrwrit de Hulton, of Hulton, in Lancashire. ; ch: David (m. Ceclil
2 CONC ia le Roter) de Malpas alias de Egerton, Hova de Hampton
2 CONT **HOVA DE HAMPTON, second son, father of David de Wigland. Had issue.
2 CONT **DAVID DE MALPAS, alias DE EGERTON, son and heir, by deed s. d. = CECILIA, daughter of Randle le Roter, lord of Thornton, by deed s. d. ; ch: Philip (m. Margaret de Wrenbury) de Egerton
2 CONT ***PHILIP DE EGERTON, son and heir, sheriff of Cheshire 23 and 24 Edw. I. = MARGARET, daughter of Richard de Wrenbury, by Catherine his wife, by deed s. d. ; ch: David (m. Isabella de Fulleshurst), Urian (m. Amelia de Caldecote), 
2 CONC Sir Brian (a knight of Rhodes), Richard, Philip, John, . . . . (wife of David de Malpas of Hampton) de Egerton
2 CONT ****URIAN DE EGERTON, 2d son, lord of Caldecote in right of his wife, ancestor of the Egertons of Betley, and also of those of Wrinehill, whose representative, Edw. Egerton, conveyed his estates to sir John Egerton, of Egerton, kn
2 CONC t. = AMELIA, dau. and heiress of David de Coldecote. ; ch: 
2 CONT ****DAVID DE EGERTON, eldest son and heir, sheriff of Cheshire 7 Edw. III. = ISABELLA, daughter of Richard de Fulleshurst, lord of Crewe. ; ch: Philip (m. Ellena de St. Pierre & Matilda . . . ), Urian (m. Amelia Warburton), David 
2 CONC (2d son), Margaret (unmarried 29 Edw. III.) de Egerton
2 CONT *****DAVID EGERTON, 2d son, living 29 Edw. III. o. s. p. ante 19 Ric. II.
2 CONT *****PHILIP DE EGERTON, son and heir, Inq. p.m. 36 Edw. III. = ELLENA, dau. of John de St. Pierre, marriage covenant dated 9 Edw. II. ; ch: David (m. Isabella Venables), Elllena (m. Sir William Brereton), Isabella (m. Robert de Bu
2 CONC lkeley & John Venables & Sir John Delves) de Egerton ; = MATILDA, dau. of . . . . , Edw. III.
2 CONT ******DAVID DE EGERTON, son and heir, married before 20 Edw. III. Isabella, dau. of sir Hugh Venables, of Kinderton, knight; o. s. p.
2 CONT ******ELLENA, sister, and finally sole heiress, wife of sir William Brereton, of Brereton, knt. claimed a moiety of a fourth of the barony of Malpas against John Sutton in 1368, and nother moiety of a fourth against sir Walter Cok
2 CONC esay, in 1379. = ; ch: Sir William Brereton
2 CONT ******ISABELLA, sister and coheiress, wife of Robert de Bulkeley; 2dly, of John Venables; and 2dly, of sir John Delves, knight; recovered a moiety of a fourth of the barony of Malpas from John de Brunham, trestee of the Cokesays, 
2 CONC in 1363; and another moiety of a fourth from John, son of sir John de Sutton, in 1368; o. s. p. 19 Ric. II.
2 CONT *****URIAN DE EGERTON, 3d son; living 29 Edw. III. died before 19 Ric. II. = AMELIA, daughter of John Warburton, esq. ; ch: Philip (m. Matilda de Malpas), John, David, Ellen de Egerton
2 CONT ******PHILIP DE EGERTON, son and heir, succeeded to a portion of the estates of Isabella Delves, 19 Ric. II. Inq. p.m. 24 Hen. VI. = MATILDA, dau. of David de Malpas, of Hampton and coheiress of her niece Ellen, wife of Urian de B
2 CONC rereton, marr. by dispensation, dated 1 Sept. 1403. ; ch: Sir John (m. Margaret Fitton), Jane (m. sir Richard Scarfe) Egerton
2 CONT *******JANE, wife of sir Richard Scarfe, alias Moore.
2 CONT *******Sir JOHN EGERTON of Egerton, knight, slain at the battle of Blore Heath. Inq. p.m. 38 Hen. VI. = MARGARET, dau. of sir John Fitton, knight. ; ch: Philip (m. Margery Mainwaring), William (of Hampton, 2d son), Ralph, Hugh, Pe
2 CONC ter Egerton
2 CONT ********PHILIP EGERTON, of Egerton, esq. son and heir. Inq. p.m. 13 Edw. IV. = MARGERY, daughter of William Mainwaring, of Ightfield, co. Salop. Inq. p.m. 1 Hen. VIII. ; ch: Anne, Catherine, Ellen, Elizabeth, William (m. Margaret 
2 CONC Egerton), '''John (m. Elizabeth Done)''', Sir Ralph (m. Margaret Basset) Egerton
2 CONT *********WILLIAM EGERTON, esq. eldest son and heir apparent, married Margaret daughter of sir Ralph Egerton, of Wrinehill, knt.; o.s.p. ante patrem.
2 CONT *********Sir RALPH EGERTON, of Ridley, in the co. of Chester, knight, by gift of King henry the Eighth, chief ranger of Delamere forest, and standard bearer of England. = MARGARET, dau. and heiress of Ralph Basset, of Blore. ; ch:
2 CONT *********'''JOHN EGERTON, of Egerton, esq.''' eldest son and heir by survivorship. Inq. p.m. 1 Ric. III. '''= ELIZABETH, daughter and heiress of Hugh Done, of Oulton (the third son of John Done, of Utkinton, esq.) and of his wife,
2 CONC  Anne, daughter of James Touchet lord Audley. ; ch:''' Philip (m. Joanna Smith, wid. of Richard Winnington), Susan (m. Randle Egerton) Egerton
2 CONT ********** .... etc. ________________________
2 CONT *'''Burke's genealogical and heraldic history of the peerage and baronetage, the privy  ... 
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=Pf8cAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA700#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.700
2 CONT **GREY-EGERTON.
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *   PHILIP EGERTON, of Egerton, who m. Margery, dau. of William Mainwaring, and dying 13 EDWARD IV., left two sons,
2 CONT **'''	1. JOHN, his successor.
2 CONT **	2. Ralph (Sir), whose son, Sir Ralph, left a natural son, THOMAS EGERTON, who becoming lord chancellor of England, was created Viscount Brackley, and from him descended the noble houses of BRIDGEWATER, EGERTON OF TATTON, &c.
2 CONT *Mr. Egerton was s. by his elder son,
2 CONT *'''   JOHN EGERTON, of Egerton, who m. Elizabeth''', dau. and heir of Hugh '''Done''', of Oulton, co. Chester, and granddau., maternally, of James Touchet, Lord Audley; and dying in the 1st year of RICHARD III., '''was s by his o
2 CONC nly son, 
2 CONT *   .... etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From Magna Brittanica: The county palatine of Chester.  By Daniel Lysons.  Page 380.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=_ysgAQAAMAAJ&lpg=PA380&ots=O4lwoh2PZA&dq=Done%20of%20Utkinton%2C%20Flaxtards%20and%20Duddon&pg=PA380#v=onepag
2 CONC e&q=Done%20of%20Utkinton,%20Flaxtards%20and%20Duddon&f=false GoogleBooks]
2 CONT
2 CONT >The Dones were of Utkinton, as early as the twelfth century; a younger son of Henry Done, who acquired the office of bow-bearer of the forest of Delamere, by marriage with the co-heiress of Kingsley, about the reign of King John,
2 CONC  or the beginning of that of Henry III. ", settled at Crowton, which branch became extinct in the male line in the year 1508; the heiress married Birkenhead. John Done of Utkinton, in or about the reign of Henry VI., had three son
2 CONC s; the second son settled at Flaxyards, the younger son at Oulton, the latter died without male issue in 1498, leaving an only daughter who brought Oulton in marriage to the Egertons ...
