1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Rogers (d 1450) was the first husband of Anne Echyngham.  Their son was Henry Rogers.
2 CONT * [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=120742075 Anne Echingham Touchet, Baroness Audley] Find A Grave Memorial# 120742075
2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bermondsey_Abbey Bermondsey Abbey] From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT * http://thepeerage.com/p4730.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Echingham was the daughter of Sir Thomas Echingham and Margaret Knyvett.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, firstly, John Rogers before August 1450.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, John Tuchet, 6th Lord Audley (of Heleigh), son of James Tuchet, 5th Lord Audley (of Heleigh) and Margaret de Ros, before 1456.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 7 March 1498.[1] She was buried at Bermondsey Abbey, Bermondsey, London, England.[1] Her will (dated 11 November 1497) was probated on 24 June 1498.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT From before 1455, her married name became Rogers.1 From before 1456, her married name became Tuchet.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Anne Echingham and John Tuchet, 6th Lord Audley (of Heleigh)
2 CONT *1.Sir James Tuchet, 7th Lord Audley (of Heleigh)+2 b. c 1463, d. 28 Jun 1497
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extin
2 CONC ct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 341. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume I, page 342.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/TOUCHET.htm#John TOUCHET (3° B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT
2 CONT John TOUCHET (3º B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT *Born: 1420, Heleigh, Staffordshire, England
2 CONT *Died: 26 Sep 1490, Heleigh, Staffordshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes: had livery of his lands in 1459-60, joined Edward IV, was summoned to parliament from 1461 to 1483, and was sworn of the privy council in 1471. He was employed in Britany in 1475, and was present at the coronation of Richar
2 CONC d III, who appointed him lord treasurer in 1484.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Father: James TOUCHET (2º B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT *Mother: Margaret De ROS (B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT *Married: Anne ECHINGHAM (B. Audley of Heleigh) (b. ABT 1420 - d. 7 May 1498) (dau. of Sir Thomas de Echyngham and Margaret Knyvett) (w. of Sir John Rogers) BEF 1456, Heleigh, Staffordshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT *1. Eleanor TOUCHET
2 CONT *2. Anne TOUCHET
2 CONT *3. Elizabeth TOUCHET
2 CONT *4. James TOUCHET (4º B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT *5. John TOUCHET
2 CONT *6. Thomas TOUCHET
