1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Known as Sir John Audley (Awdeley) of Swaffam Market in County Norfolk (Knight). Also known as John Audley, of Aldithley.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Sir John Awdley, lived at Swaffham in 1526, and had two wives; Elizabeth, his second wife, and Muriel, daughter of Sir Thomas Brewse of Wenham in Suffolk, by whom he had
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Richard Awdley of Swaffham, Esq. who married Catharine, daughter of Richard, younger son of the Lord Scroop of Bolton,...'' [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Manor of East-Hall in Great-Pagrave'''<br />
