1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/TOUCHET.htm#Anne TOUCHET2
2 CONT *''''''Anne TOUCHET
2 CONT *Born: ABT 1446
2 CONT *Father: James TOUCHET (2º B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT *Mother: Eleanor HOLLAND (B. Audley of Heleigh)
2 CONT *Married 1: Edward COBHAM
2 CONT *''''''Married 2: Richard De La BERE ABT 1462, Heleigh, Staffordshire, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Thomas De La BERE
2 CONT **2. Seneca De La BERE (b. ABT 1486 - d. 1526) (m. Elizabeth Baskerville)
2 CONT *_______________________
2 CONT *http://www.mayfamilyhistory.co.uk/abear/delabere/richard.html
2 CONT *''''''Sir Richard De La Bere
2 CONT *of Kinnersley Castle & Clehonger Manor
2 CONT *''''''Sir Richard, the son of Sir Kynard De la Bere of Kinnersley Castle and Joan De la Barré of Clehonger, was a very wealthy man. At his father’s death, he had inherited the estates of both his grandfathers and, splitting life 
2 CONC between the two manors, he lived the life of luxury. He became Sheriff of Herefordshire and his pre-eminence in the county can be easily judged by examining his fine brass in Hereford Cathedral. Here are displayed Richard, his fir
2 CONC st wife Anne daughter of John Tuchet, Lord Audley, his second wife Elizabeth daughter of William Mores (Sergeant to the Hall of Henry VII), one son and four daughters by Anne, and ten sons and six daughters by Elizabeth. He appare
2 CONC ntly took an interest in political affairs during the “Wars of the Roses”, though whether he took up arms is unclear. Sir Richard did have Beaufort/Lancastrian connections, but he appears to have been a Yorkist with personal conne
2 CONC ctions to Henry Stafford, Duke of Buckingham through the same source. Sir Richard’s brother-in-law, James, Lord Audley, was married to Margaret Dayrell, half-sister to Buckingham. Their mother was co-heiress of Edmund Beaufort, Du
2 CONC ke of Buckingham.   
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2919.htm#i87704
2 CONT *''''''Sir Richard Delabere1,2
2 CONT *''''''M, b. circa 1440, d. 15 July 1514
2 CONT *Father Sir Kynard Delabere1 b. c 1408, d. a 1435 
2 CONT *Mother Joan (Jane) Barre1 b. c 1412 
2 CONT *''''''     Sir Richard Delabere was born circa 1440 at of Kinnardesley, Herefordshire, England.1 He married Anne Touchet, daughter of Sir James Touchet, 5th Lord Audley and Eleanor de Holand, circa 1483.3,1,2 Sir Richard Delabere
2 CONC  died on 15 July 1514.1 He left a will on 5 August 1514; Will proved.1
2 CONT *''''''Family Anne Touchet b. c 1446 
2 CONT *Child 
2 CONT *◦Kynard Delabere4 b. c 1488
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S11588] Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 57.
2 CONT *2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 722-723.
2 CONT *3.[S11588] Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 112.
2 CONT *4.[S11588] Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 58.
2 CONT *_______________________
