2 CONT *''''''Plantagenet Ancestry: A Study In Colonial And Medieval Families, 2nd Edition ...  By Douglas Richardson
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=kjme027UeagC&printsec=frontcover&dq=Plantagenet+ancestry&hl=en&sa=X&ei=U8VLUYTME-boiALhroHwBw&ved=0CEcQ6AEwBA#v=onepage&q=puleston&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 265
2 CONT *12. ROBERT WHITNEY, Esq., of Whitney, Herefordshire, Sheriff of Herefordshire, 1474-5, son and heir. He married (1st) CONSTANCE AUDLEY (or TUCHET), daughter of James Tuchet (or Audley), Knt., 5th Lord Audley (descendant of King J
2 CONC ohn), by his 2nd wife, Eleanor, illegitimate daughter of Edmund Holand, K.G., 4th Earl of Kent [see TUCHET 12 for her ancestry]. They had two daughters, Joan and ''''''Eleanor (wife of Thomas Vaughan, Knt., of Bredwardine)''''''. 
2 CONC He married (2nd) ELIZABETH VAUGHAN, daughter of Thomas Vaughan, of Hergest, Herefordshire, by Ellen Gethin, daughter of Dafydd ap Cadwgan ap Phylip Dorddu. They had four sons, James, Esq., John, Hugh, and Robert, and three daughte
2 CONC rs, Eleanor (wife of John Puleston), Sibyl (wife of Roger ap Richard), and Elizabeth (wife of John Pye). He was attainted as a Yorkist by the Lancastrian Parliament in 1459. ROBERT WHITNEY, Esq., died shortly before 6 Oct. 1494. H
2 CONC is widow Elizabeth, was living 4 May 1525. ....
2 CONT *13. JOAN WHITNEY, daughter by her father's 1st marriage. She married ROGER VAUGHAN, Knt., of Porthaml (in Talgarth), Breconshhire, Wales, Steward and Receiver of the Lordship of Dinas, 1509, 2nd son of Robert Vaughan, Knt., of Tr
2 CONC etower, Breconshire, by his 1st wife Denise, daughter of Thomas ap Philip Vaughan of Tyle-Glas. They had four sons, Watkin, Esq., John, Harry, Esq., and Thomas, Esq., and four daughters, Elinor (wife of Thomas Gwyn, Hywel ap Gwily
2 CONC m, and William Dometh), Elizabeth, __ (wife of Jenkin ap Thomas), and Margaret (wife of John Parker). By a ....
2 CONT *Pg. 266 - NOT VIEWABLE
2 CONT *______________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Welsh Biography Online
2 CONT
2 CONT It is also said that John Vaughan, father of Sir Hugh Johneys, knight of the Sepulchre, 1441, was an illegitimate son of Walter Vaughan. Walter Vaughan's heir was ''''''Sir THOMAS VAUGHAN, who m. Eleanor , daughter of Robert Whitn
2 CONC ey''''''.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://wbo.llgc.org.uk/en/s-VAUG-BRO-1350.html
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *''''''Vaughan Family of Wales
2 CONT *http://archive.org/details/VaughanFamilyOfWales
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/VaughanFamilyOfWales/VaughanFamily#page/n3/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg. 6
2 CONT *Watkin Vaughan was killed by an arrow one source says at Hereford another at the battle of Mortimers Cross. He had married Elizabeth daughter of Sir Henry Wogan and had at least fifteen children. One of them William Vaughan Of Rh
2 CONC ydhelig the second son slew the earl of Warwick, the kingmaker, when the earl was trying to escape from the battle at Barnet in 1471. He was regarded as the supreme champion on the battle field after the death of his uncle Thomas 
2 CONC ap Roger of Hergest He was constable of Aberystwyth castle 
2 CONT *Another of Watkins sons, Lewis Vaughan was described as being of Llanbedr, Painscastle and Rhulen. 
2 CONT *From John Vaughan another of his sons were descended the Vaughans of Pont-faen 
2 CONT *Another John Vaughan, an illegitimate son of Watkin Vaughan was father of Sir Hugh Johneys knight of the Sepulchre 
2 CONT *Watkin Vaughan's heir was ''''''Sir Thomas Vaughan who married Eleanor daughter of Robert Whitney. 
2 CONT *His heir was Sir Richard Vaughan knighted at Tournai on the 14th October 1513, Sheriff of Herefordshire in 1530 and 1541 (therefore must have owned considerable property in that county at the time) and married Anne ....
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/VaughanFamilyOfWales/VaughanFamily#page/n4/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg. 5
2 CONT *daughter of John Butler and heiress of the Dunraven and Pen-bre estates. The main line of the family moved from Bredwardine to Dunraven  •__________________________
2 CONT *''''''(according to Plantagenent and the listing for her father Robert on Our Royal, Titled, Noble, and Commoner Ancestors & Cousins, this Eleanor was the dau. of Robert's first wife Constance, the dau. of Elsbeth Vaughan also na
2 CONC med Eleanor is the wife of John Puleston) 
2 CONT *''''''Eleanor Whitney1 
2 CONT *''''''F, #58576, b. circa 1454
2 CONT *Father       Sir Robert Whitney, Sheriff of Herefordshire b. c 1418, d. c 6 Oct 1494
2 CONT *Mother      Elsbeth Vaughan1 b. c 1428, d. a 4 May 1525
2 CONT *''''''     Eleanor Whitney was born circa 1454 at of Whitney, Herefordshire, England.1 She married Sir Thomas Vaughan, son of Watkin Vaughan and Ellen (Janet) Wogan, circa 1475.2
2 CONT *''''''Family       Sir Thomas Vaughan b. c 1439, d. a 1509
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11588] Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 145.
2 CONT * 2.[S11588] Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 117.
