1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Primary Sources
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000046556244882& Inquisitions Post Mortem] for Katherine Lutrell, Writ. 1 September 1435. <br>
2 CONT mention: John Strecche and Katherine then his wife, lately the wife of Hugh Lutrell, knight <br>
2 CONT Her IPMs give two different death dates, 31 July 1435 and 28 August 1435. James Lutrell was her kin and next heir, viz., son of John, son of Katherine, and was aged 9 years and more.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT He [http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1386-1421/member/stretch-sir-john-1341-90 STRETCH, Sir John (1341-90), of Pinhoe and Hempston Arundel (Little Hempston), Devon]'s only son, John, had predeceased him, leaving a w
2 CONC idow, Katherine, who by this time was married to Sir Hugh Luttrell*, and it was she who retained possession of the manors of Sampford Arundel and Woolston until her demise in 1435. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1386-1421/member/luttrell-sir-hugh-1364-1428 LUTTRELL, Sir Hugh (c.1364-1428), of Dunster, Som.] b.c.1364, yr. s. and event. h. of Sir Andrew Luttrell of Chilton, Devon by Elizabeth
2 CONC  (d. 7 Aug. 1395), da. of Hugh Courtenay, earl of Devon, and Margaret de Bohun, gdda. of Edw. I, wid. of Sir John de Vere. m. bef. 1384, Katherine (d. 28 Aug. 1435), da. of Sir John Beaumont† of Saunton and Sherwell, Devon, wid. o
2 CONC f John, s. of Sir John Stretch* of Wambrook, Som., 2s. 4da.1 Kntd. by 1390.
2 CONT
2 CONT .... The estate he had inherited after the deaths of his father and paternal grandmother in 1378 was small, though he had added to it his wife’s dower in the Stretch manors of Sampford Arundel, Somerset, and Woolston and Otterton,
2 CONC  Devon. ... Luttrell died on 24 Mar. 1428, apparently while on a visit to one of his daughters, a nun at Shaftesbury, Dorset. Spices worth 44s. were purchased at Shaftesbury, presumably to embalm his body, which was then carried t
2 CONC o Dunster. The cortege passed through Bridgwater, where the churchwardens spent 12d. on torches. A further sum of nearly £10 went to the provision of white and black cloth to make gowns and capes for 16 poor people who attended th
2 CONC e funeral. Luttrell’s obit was celebrated at Bruton, and a monument was erected to his memory in Dunster church. Thus died one of the most outstanding west country figures of www.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Katherine Beaumont Luttrell
2 CONT BIRTH	1354
2 CONT DEATH	28 Aug 1435 (aged 80–81)
2 CONT BURIAL	
2 CONT Priory Churchyard of St. George
2 CONT Dunster, West Somerset District, Somerset, England 
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID	101213206
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Sir John Beaumont (d. 12 Mar. 1379/80) of Saunton and Sherwell, Devonshire, by Joan Crawthorne (d. 20 Feb. 1429).
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members
2 CONT Spouse
2 CONT Hugh Luttrell
2 CONT 1364–1428
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT Robert Luttrell
2 CONT 1389–1437
2 CONT John Luttrell
2 CONT 1394–1430the period. His career had spanned three reigns, in all of which he was prominent in different spheres.20
