1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Primary Sources
2 CONT Nov. 21. 1407 Gloucester.	<br>
2 CONT To the treasurer and the barons of the exchequer. Order not to trouble '''Thomas Brugge, who has taken to wife Alice the second daughter and heir of Thomas Berkeley of Coberley''', nor suffer him to be troubled for his homage, rel
2 CONC easing any distress upon him made; as for a fine paid in the hanaper the king respited until a day now past the homage of Nicholas Mattesden, who took to wife Margaret one of the said daughters and heirs, and of Thomas Brugge for 
2 CONC the purparties of the said Margaret and Alice of their father's lands, due by reason of issue between them and their wives begotten, and commanded livery of those purparties to be given them; and now the king has taken the homage 
2 CONC of Thomas Brugge. By p.s. [5443.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: 'Close Rolls, Henry IV: November 1407', in Calendar of Close Rolls, Henry IV: Volume 3, 1405-1409, ed. A E Stamp (London, 1931), pp. 297-301. British History Online http://www.british-history.ac.uk/cal-close-rolls/hen4/vol
2 CONC 3/pp297-301 [accessed 3 February 2018].
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000075313254128& Inquisition Post Mortem] for Thomas Brugge, Writ 2 May 1408. He died on 7 April [1408]. Edmund his son and heir was aged 23 years and more. Mentions Alice his wife w
2 CONC ho survived him.
