2 CONT Sir Godfrey Foljambe BIRTH	1367 Derbyshire, England DEATH	9 Sep 1388 (aged 20–21) Bakewell, Derbyshire Dales District, Derbyshire, England BURIAL	 All Saints Churchyard Bakewell, Derbyshire Dales District, Derbyshire, England  MEM
2 CONC ORIAL ID	89801165
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Sir Godfrey Foljambe and Margaret de Villiers; grandson of Sir Godfrey Foljambe and Avena Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT By the autumn of 1382, as John Leeke and his father then obtained joint custody of the estates of the grandson and heir of the distinguished lawyer, Sir Godfrey Foljambe (d.1376), who was then about 15 years old. Sir Simon did not
2 CONC  live much longer; and it seems to have been on Sir John’s initiative that a marriage contract was arranged between his sister, Margaret Leeke, and the young Godfrey Foljambe. When the latter died suddenly, in 1388, leaving a baby
2 CONC  daughter, Sir John not only seized the welcome opportunity to resume his wardship of the Foljambe inheritance (for which he had been paying £30 p.a. to the Exchequer), but also purchased the marriage of his infant niece from the 
2 CONC Crown for 50 marks. This he sold in 1392 for double the price to his neighbour, Sir William Plumpton, who wanted a suitable bride for his son, Robert*. The widowed Margaret (Leeke) Foljambe, meanwhile, became the wife of Sir Thoma
2 CONC s Rempston I. Contributor: Deb Kunkle
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members Parents Godfrey Foljambe 1344–1376
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret De Villiers Foljambe 1349–1398
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse Margaret Leek Rempstone unknown–1454 (m. 1385)
2 CONT
2 CONT   Died: 1416 - Spofforth, Yorkshire, England
2 CONT
