1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=257111141-1-507253&action=showRecord MyHeritage Family Trees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]
2 CONC : ''Jun 17 2016, 16:19:37 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.aemyers.net/genealogy/d0040/g0000050.html
2 CONT
2 CONT His information is from Find A Grave memorial 143635363. Robert m. Jennet ca. 1542. He inherited the manors of Clint & Thorpe. In 2018 https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Beckwith-I-of-Clint-and-Thorpe offers different dates, etc. 
2 CONC Also see http://www.davinciknight.com/Genealogy_page5.html which states: "He left an only son Robert Beckwith of Clint and Thorp whose will was dated October 16th, 1536 and was proved March 24th 1537 - He married Lennet - and had 
2 CONC issue 1st Robert who died young 2nd Marmaduke Beckwith of Clint and Dacre who sold the manor of Clint - that had been in the family since 1226 and bought the manor of Feather - Stone and Aeton in Yorkshire. He married twice and by
2 CONC  his first wife Anne, daughter of Danly of Bramhope. County York he had ten children, his second wife was Ellen daughter of William Style of Haddochson, county York. His children were 1st Thomas, 2nd William, 3rd Roger, 4th Syman 
2 CONC of Pontefract (in England pronounced Pomfret) who was married at Featherstone in 1580 to Catherine Austurcke of Pontefract, 5th Jane married John Thorp 1635, 6th Alice married Robert Banister, 7th Graver married John Novield, 8th 
2 CONC Anne 9th Matthew, 10th Catherine. Of there children Thomas the eldest inherited Acton, and married Frances daughter and heiress of William Frost of Acton and had three sons, Thomas, William, and Marmaduke, baptised in 1573." Cf. "
2 CONC American Bigraphy . . . , Vol. 6," (New York: The American Historical Society, 1919). p. 83. 
