1 NAME Lawrence /Stoughton/
2 GIVN Lawrence
2 SURN Stoughton
2 _MARNM Stoughton
1 NAME Lawrence Stoughton, of Stoke
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1491
2 ADDR
3 CITY Stoughton
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE APR 1572
2 PLAC Stoughton, Surrey, England
2 ADDR
1 OCCU 5th Lord of Stoke Manor
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 26 January 1529 he renewed his father's lease of Stoke Manor for £5 6s. 8d. per year. He entered into this agreement with his mother and step-father, but three days later they released their right to him for £20 a year. In 1547 he
2 CONC  renewed the lease again, and on 10 June 1549 he purchased the advowson of Stoke parsonage from Henry Polsted, Esq. He made his will 10 May 1571 at Stoughton. It was proved 28 April 1572.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Martin Hollick, [http://mhollick.typepad.com/slovakyankee/2010/02/the-royal-line-of-rose-stoughton-otis-part-ii.html The Royal Line of Rose (Stoughton) Otis 1629-ca. 1677 of Dover, N.H. Part II], Feb. 6, 2010
