1 NOTE {geni:about_me} By his wife, Isabel Mede, Maurice Berkeley had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.  '''Thomas Berkeley''', ''de jure 5th Baron Berkeley'' (1472 - 22 January 1532), 2nd son, who was knighted on 9 September 1513 by Thomas Howard, Earl of Surrey at the Battle of Flodden. He married firstly in 1505 to Alienor Con
2 CONC stable (c. 1485 - d. 1540), widow of John Ingleby of Yorkshire and daughter of Marmaduke Constable by his wife Joyce Stafford. He married secondly to Cecily Arnold, a daughter and co-heiress to Sir .... Arnold of Gloucestershire, 
2 CONC and widow of Richard Rowdon, Sheriff of Gloucestershire.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Berkeley,_5th_Baron_Berkeley
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From thePeerage.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Berkeley, 5th Lord Berkeley was born in 1472 at Thornbury, Gloucestershire, England. He was the son of Sir Maurice Berkeley and Isabel Meade. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, firstly, Eleanor Constable, daughter of Sir Marmaduke Constable and Joyce Stafford, between 1504 and 1505. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, Cicely Arnold in 1526. He died on 22 January 1532/33 at Mangotsfield, Bristol, Gloucestershire, England.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was buried at St. Augustine's, Bristol, Gloucestershire, England. His will (dated 28 April 1532 to 11 January 1532/3) was probated on 6 June 1533.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Berkeley, 5th Lord Berkeley also went by the nick-name of Thomas 'the Sheep Master'. He was invested as a Knight on 9 September 1513 from the Earl of Surrey. He fought in the Battle of Flodden on 9 September 1513. He held t
2 CONC he office of Constable of Berkeley Castle on 15 May 1514. He held the office of Sheriff of Gloucestershire between November 1522 and November 1523. He succeeded to the title of 5th Lord Berkeley [E., 1421] on 12 September 1523, by
2 CONC  writ.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Thomas Berkeley, 5th Lord Berkeley
2 CONT
2 CONT #    Muriel Berkeley+
2 CONT #     Joan Berkeley+
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Thomas Berkeley, 5th Lord Berkeley and Eleanor Constable
2 CONT
2 CONT # Thomas Berkeley, 6th Lord Berkeley+ b. 1505, d. 19 Sep 1534 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
