2 CONT *''''''William Reade, Burgess of Cricklade1 
2 CONT *''''''M, #70134, b. circa 1486, d. 1557
2 CONT *Father      John (William) Reade b. c 1460
2 CONT *Mother      Margery Beauchamp b. c 1462
2 CONT *''''''     William Reade, Burgess of Cricklade was born circa 1486 at of Mitton, Bredon, Worcestershire, England.1 He married Catherine Rowdon, daughter of Richard Rowdon, Esq., Alderman of Gloucester, circa 1510. William Reade, 
2 CONC Burgess of Cricklade died in 1557.
2 CONT *''''''Family      Catherine Rowdon b. c 1488
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Elizabeth Ann Reade+ b. c 1520
2 CONT **Giles Reade, Esq., Sheriff of Gloucestershire & Worcestershire+2,1 b. c 1541, d. 1611
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S6] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry: 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 330.
2 CONT * 2.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 270.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2334.htm#i70134
2 CONT *___________________
2 CONT '''William Rede (c. 1500 – 3 November 1558) was the member of Parliament for Cricklade in the parliament of 1529 and for Gloucestershire in November 1554.'''[1]
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Rede_(died_1558)
2 CONT ________
2 CONT A Record of the Redes of Barton Court, Berks: With a Short Précis of Other .. By Compton Reade. Page 119.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=cqtCAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA119&ots=8GL0Haugum&dq=Catherine%20(Rowdon)%20Rede&pg=PA119#v=onepage&
2 CONC q&f=false GoogleBooks]
2 CONT William Reade of Bodington on the decease of Margery Beauchamp married Anna, sister of Sir Giles Bruges, and by her had (with daughters who married respectively-Cassye, Higford, and Vaughan), a son, '''William of The Wenyerde, Tew
2 CONC kesbury (will 1557), who, by Catherine, daughter of Richard Rowdon, had (with a daughter who = H. Chatterton, and another daughter who = (1) Silvester Danvers, (2) Sir Richard Berkeley), a son, the Worshipful Giles Reade of Mitton
2 CONC  (will 1611).'''
