2 CONT ↑ The son of Scotangle: Sir John Steward (d. 1447). By Michael Bennett. Journal of the Sydney Society for Scottish History. Vol. 15, May 2015, pp 17-47 see p 39 Sydney.
2 CONT ↑ Will of Nicholas Stward of Outwell, Cambridgeshire. 24 January 1499. PROB 11/11/545. The National Archives, Kew Discovery.
2 CONT ↑ STEWARD, Mark (1524-1604), of Heckfield, Hants; later of Stuntney, Cambs. The History of Parliament: the House of Commons 1558-1603, ed. P.W. Hasler, 1981
2 CONT John Morrill, ‘Cromwell, Oliver (1599–1658)’, Oxford Dictionary of National Biography, Oxford University Press, 2004; online edn, Sept 2015
2 CONT <http://minerdescent.com/2011/06/08/sir-henry-cromwell/ />
2 CONT Dickinson, Wharton. Record of the Lambert-Dickinson Family (Flushing, N.Y., 1901) Page 85
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edmund_Steward
