2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In [https://archive.org/details/visitationcambr00britgoog/page/n24/mode/2up?q=iunior The visitation of Cambridge made in 1575, page 10-11,] Simeon Steward, of Lakenheath and Stuntney is given a son John: "Johannes Steward of Morsh
2 CONC  in Norff. m .... d. & heire of ... Shouldham of Shouldham."
2 CONT
2 CONT These John Stewards are not the same. John Steward, of Marham son of Simeon, has his will dated February 1604: https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000213487663856
2 CONT
2 CONT This is well after the death date of John Stewart, of Pattishall (1577) https://www.freereg.org.uk/search_records/5818bdfce93790ec7592b550/...
2 CONT
2 CONT I suggest that the Pattishall Stewart family should be detached from the Lakenheath and Stuntney Stewards. John Stewart, of Pattishall parents are currently unknown, but they were not Simeon Steward, of Lakenheath and Stuntney and
2 CONC  Joanne Steward.
