2 CONT *''''''Sir Roger Vaughan1 
2 CONT *''''''M, #73934, b. circa 1436, d. before 25 September 1514
2 CONT *Father       Sir Roger Vaughan2 b. c 1404, d. 26 Jul 1469
2 CONT *Mother      Denise fil Thomas2
2 CONT *''''''     Sir Roger Vaughan was born circa 1436 at of Porthaml Talgarth, Breconshire, Wales. He married Jane Whitney, daughter of Sir Robert Whitney, Sheriff of Herefordshire and Constance Touchet, circa 1469; They had 4 sons (W
2 CONC atkin, Esq., John, Harry, Esq., & Thomas, Esq.) and 4 daughters (Elinor, wife of Thomas Gwyn, of Hywel ap Gwilym, & of William Dometh); Elizabeth; Margred, wife of John Parker; & a daughter married to Jenkin ap Thomas). By a mistr
2 CONC ess or mistresses he also had Thomas, Roger, & Robert.1,2 Sir Roger Vaughan died before 25 September 1514 at of Porthaml, Talgarth, Breconshire, Wales.3,2
2 CONT *''''''Family      Jane Whitney b. c 1450
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Elizabeth Vaughn+1,2,4 b. c 1485
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 709.
2 CONT * 2.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 190.
2 CONT * 3.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 105.
2 CONT * 4.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. IV, p. 185.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2460.htm#i73934
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT I have three sources that have Watkin Vaughan as the son of Roger Vaughan and Joan Whitney. The first is the National Library of Wales (Electronic Resouces/Welsh Biography Online) https://www.llyfrgell.cymru/index.php?id=6860. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They cover all branches of the Vaughan family. All of the Vaughan lines are discussed by place of residence. Watkin is found in the Vaughans of Porthaml section. This source does not even mention a marriage to Eleanor of Somerset.
2 CONT
2 CONT The second source is The Bingham Genealogy Project, 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.telusplanet.net/public/dkbing/genproj.htm 
2 CONT
2 CONT Douglas Bingham has an extensive list of resources that he used in his research. He has Roger Vaughan marrying Joan Whitney first, Watkin as their oldest child (consistent with the previous source) + 7 others. He has Roger marryin
2 CONC g Eleanor Somerset second, no children.
2 CONT
2 CONT The third source is a family history, "Kin of Mellcene Thurman Smith". I don't know the source of the info contained in this book. This author has Roger first married to Eleanor of Somerset, no children, and married second to Joan
2 CONC  Whitney with Watkin as their oldest child.
2 CONT
2 CONT (THIS THIRD SOURCE WOULD NOT BE CORRECT AS THE ROGER THAT MARRIED ELEANOR SOMERSET HAS A DIFFERENT DEATH DATE THEN ROGER THAT MARRIED JOAN WHITNEY)
2 CONT
2 CONT From Welsh Biography Online
2 CONT
2 CONT VAUGHAN family, of Porthaml , parish of Talgarth , Brecknock . This branch of the Vaughan family was founded by ROGER VAUGHAN, second son of Sir Roger Vaughan of Tretower. Roger Vaughan of Talgarth was granted the offices of stewa
2 CONC rd and receiver of the lordship of Dinas, 17 Jan. 1509, and was dead before 25 Sept. 1514, when those offices were granted to Sir Griffith ap Rice. His wife was Joan, daughter of Robert Whitney by Constance, daughter of James, lor
2 CONC d Audley. The Vaughans of Tregunter descended from his second son, Thomas Vaughan. The heir, WATKIN VAUGHAN, m. Joan, daughter of Ieuan Gwilym Vaughan of White Peyton. The family became prominent with his heir, WILLIAM VAUGHAN, wh
2 CONC o obtained a lease of the demesne lands of Dinas, 14 Feb. 1529.
2 CONT *____________________________
2 CONT *''''''Vaughan Family of Wales
2 CONT *http://archive.org/details/VaughanFamilyOfWales
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/VaughanFamilyOfWales/VaughanFamily#page/n23/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg. 24
2 CONT **VAUGHAN family, Of Porthaml, parish of Talgarth, Brecknock. X ref Tretower 
2 CONT *''''''   This branch of the Vaughan family was founded by Roger Vaughan, second son Of Sir Roger Vaughan of Tretower-see Vaughan family of Tretower. He was possibly the Roger Vaughan Of Tyle-glas who was pardoned on 9 July 1491, 
2 CONC and figures again in Henry VIII's pardon roll (1509) as Roger ap Roger of Tyle-glas, or Roger Vaughan Of Talgarth. He was granted the offces of steward and receiver of the lordship of Dinas, 17 Jan. 1509, and was dead before 25 Se
2 CONC pt. 1514, when those offices were granted to Sir Griffith ap Rice. His wife was Joan, daughter of Robert Whitney by Constance, daughter of James, lord Audley. The Vaughans of Tregunter descended from his second son, Thomas Vaughan
2 CONC . The heir, Watkin Vaughan married. Joan, daughter of leuan Gwilym Vaughan Of White Peyton.  ....
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/VaughanFamilyOfWales/VaughanFamily#page/n24/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg. 25
2 CONT *Sir Roger Vaughan third son of Roger Vaughan of Bredwardine-see Vaughan family of Bredwardine-by Gwladys, daughter of Dafydd Gam, was the first of the Vaughans to reside at Tretower. It is said that the residence  ....
2 CONT * ....  He was twice married. The first wife was Denise, daughter of Thomas ap Philip Vaughan of Talgarth, and she was the mother of the heir (Sir) Thomas Vaughan, ''''''Roger Vaughan-see Vaughan family of Porthaml''''''-and four 
2 CONC daughters who married into prominent families, the wives of Robert Raglan, Henry Donne,  Morgan Gamage, and Morgan ap Thomas ap GrufFudd ap Nicolas. His second wife was Margaret, lady Powis, daughter of James, lord Audley, by his 
2 CONC second wife, Eleanor, illegitimate daughter of Edmund, earl of Kent.  (Her first husband, Sir Richard Grey, lord Powis, d. 17 Dec. 1466. She was dead before 2 Feb. 1480/1.) She had one daughter by Sir Roger, the wife of Humphrey K
2 CONC ynaston. A large number of illegitimate children are ascribed to Sir Roger Vaughan. 
2 CONT *_________________________
