2 CONT *Sir Thomas Kitson (1485 – 11 September 1540) was a wealthy English merchant, Sheriff of London, and builder of Hengrave Hall in Suffolk.
2 CONT *Thomas Kitson was the son of Robert Kitson of Warton, Lancashire. His mother's name is unknown. His sister, Margaret .... etc.
2 CONT *Secondly, Thomas Kitson married Margaret Donnington (d. 12 January 1561), the only child and sole heiress of '''John Donnington (d.1544) of Stoke Newington, a member of the Worshipful Company of Salters,[6][7] by his wife Elizabe
2 CONC th Pye''', by whom he had a son born posthumously and four daughters:[2] .... etc.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Kitson
