2 CONT *''''''13. WILLIAM GRIFFITH, Knt., of Penrhyn, Caernarvonshire, Esqure of the Body to King Henry VIII, Chamberlain of North Wales, Deputy Justice of North Wales, son and Heir by his father's 1st marriage, born about 1480''''''. He
2 CONC  married (1st) Jane Stradling, daughter of Thomas Stradling, of St. Donat's, Glamogan, by Janet, daughter of Thomas Mathew, Esq. [see STRADLING 11 for her ancestry]. They had five sons, William, Edward, Esq., Rhys, Knt., John, and
2 CONC  Hugh, and eight daughters, Grace (wife of William Stanley, Knt.), Jane (wife of Thomas Mostyn), Elin/ Elinor (wife of Hugh Conway, Esq.), Catherine (wife of Richard Bulkeley, Knt.), Anne (wife of Hugh Lewis, Esq.), Elizabeth (wif
2 CONC e of John Philips, Esq.), Dorothy, and Margaret (wife successively of Peter Mytton, Thomas Griffith, and Hugh Thelwall). He served in the French campaign in 1513, being present at the Siege of Therouanne, the Battle of the Spurs, 
2 CONC and the Siege of Rournai. His wife Jane died before 1520. ''''''He married (2nd) by marriage settlement dated 2 Aug. 1522 JANE PULESTON, widow of Robert ap Maredudd, of Glynllifon, Caernarvonshire, and daughter of John Puleston, o
2 CONC f Hafoyd-y-Wern, Wrexham, and Bersham, Denbighshire, Constable of Caernarvon, Chamberlain of North Wales, by Eleanor, daughter of Robert Whitney, Esq., of Whitney, Herefordshire. They had three sons, William Esq., Rowland, and Geo
2 CONC rge [Archdeacon of Anglesey], and two daughters, Mary (wife of Randall Brereton, Knt., and Hugh Cholmondeley, Knt.) and Sibyl (or Isabel). SIR WILLIAM GRIFFITH died in 1531. ...
2 CONT *Child of William Griffith, Knt., by Jane Stradling:
2 CONT **	i. DOROTHY GRIFFITH [see next].
2 CONT *''''''Child of William Griffith, Knt., by Jane Puleston:
2 CONT **	i. SIBYL (or ISABEL) GRIFFITH, married OWEN AP HUGH AB OWEN, Esq. of Bodeon, Anglesey, Wales [see OWEN 14].
2 CONT *______________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Died after giving child birth. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT *'''2 Sir William Griffith II (d. 1531) of Penrhyn''' m, (1) Jane (W), d. of Thomas Stradling (d. 1480) of St. Donat's, co. Glamorgan (WG 1400-1500, VIII, 1268; Rice Merrick, Morganiae Archaiographia ed. B LI James (South Wales Re
2 CONC cord Society, vol. 1, 1983), p. 163) and '''(2) Jane (W), d. of John Puleston of Hafod-y-wern, Wrexham, and Bersham, co. Denbigh and widow of Robert ap Maredudd of Glynllifon, co. Caerns (WG 1400-1500, VIII, 1268; IX, 1454).
2 CONT *From: http://welshjournals.llgc.org.uk/browse/viewpage/llgc-id:1277425/llgc-id:1288291/llgc-id:1288328/getText
2 CONT *_______________
