2 CONT *Welsh Biograph Online
2 CONT *GLYN (also GLYNNE ) , family of Glynllifon , Caerns. Traditionally the family was derived from Cilmin Droed-ddu , who settled in the place after his flight from his native Cumbria in the 9th cent. , and historically from Tudur Go
2 CONC ch who for war services under Edward III obtained a grant of escheat lands in Nantlle . By his marriage with Morfudd , another descendant of Cilmin , he obtained Glynllifon , which became the chief seat of his descendants. HWLKIN 
2 CONC LLOYD , Tudur 's son, held the town of Caernarvon for the king under William de Tranmere in 1403 , and d. the following year. MEREDYDD LLOYD , his son, was bailiff of Uwch Gwyrfai in 1413-15 , and accompanied some forces sent to p
2 CONC rotect Guernsey in 1456 . The next heir, '''ROBERT  AP [d. c. 1509 ] was twice m., each wife being a member of English families who administered Gwynedd for the English kings'''. The first wife was Ellen Bulkeley of Beaumaris , an
2 CONC d by her Robert had six sons and four daughters. Two of these sons were prominent clerics in the early Tudor period— MORUS GLYN , LL.D. [d. 1525 ], was archdeacon of Merioneth , and WILLIAM GLYN , LL.D. [d. 1557 ], archdeacon of A
2 CONC nglesey . '''Robert ap Meredydd 's second wife was Jane Puleston of Caernarvon , and the issue of their marriage was known as''' WILLIAM GLYNNE the Sergeant [of Arms , temp . Hy. VIII], whose son WILLIAM GLYNNE [ fl. 1588 ] m. Low
2 CONC ry , the heiress of Lleuar , and founded the house of the Glynnes of Lleuar . Upon the death of Robert ap Meredydd his estates were divided between two of his sons: EDMUND LLOYD obtained Glynllifon , and RICHARD AP [d. 1539 ] got 
2 CONC Plas Newydd and Nantlle . Richard became the head of the family known as Glynns of Plas Newydd and Nantlle . Edmund Lloyd was sheriff of Caernarvonshire , but he d. during his year of office ( 1541 ). 
2 CONT *From: http://wbo.llgc.org.uk/en/s-GLYN-LLI-0850.html
2 CONT *_______________
2 CONT *i. Hwlkin Lloyd of Glynllifon
2 CONT *   m. Nest (dau of Cynwrig ap Meredydd ddu ap Goronwy, of Perthamel)
2 CONT **	a. Meredydd (a 1402)
2 CONT **	   m. Gwenhwyfer (dau of Llewelyn ap Edmund ap Gruffydd ap Ednyfed ap Gruffydd)
2 CONT ***'''		(1) Robert of Glynllifon (a 1440)
2 CONT ***		   m1. Elin Bulkeley (dau of William Bulkeley of Beaumaris)
2 CONT ****			(A) Edmund Llwyd of Glynliffon, Sherrif of Carnarvonshire (d 1540-1, 2nd son?)
2 CONT ****			   m. Annes (Agnes) (dau. of William ap Gruffydd ap Robin, of Cochwillan, relict of Foulk Salusbury of Llanrwst)
2 CONT ****			(B) Richard Glynne of Plas Newydd (d 24.03.1539, 4th son?)
2 CONT ****			   m. Catherine (d 1585, dau/heir of William ap Jenkin ap Iorwerth, of Ynysmaengwyn)
2 CONT ****			(C) Jonet Glyyne
2 CONT ****			   m1. Hugh Prees ap Evan, of Llanddyfnan
2 CONT ****			   m2. John ap Rhys, of Trefeilir
2 CONT ****			(D) Gaynor Glyyne
2 CONT ****			   m. Sir John Puleston (d 1551)
2 CONT ****			(E) Elin Glynne
2 CONT ****			   m1. Owen ap Meyrick, of Bodeon
2 CONT ****			   m2. Robert ap Meredydd, of Bronheulog
2 CONT ****			(F) Elizabeth Glyyne
2 CONT ****			   m1. Rhys ap Evan ap Hwlkin
2 CONT ****			   m2. Gruffydd ap William ap Madog Vychan, of Llwynduryn
2 CONT ****			(G)+ other issue - Morris (d 1525, Archdeacon of Merioneth, rector of Llaniestyn etc.), William (d 1557, archdeacon of Anglesey, rector of Clynnog etc.), John (dsp after 07.1534), Simon
2 CONT ***'''		   m2. Jane Puleston (dau. of John Puleston Hen, m2. Sir William Griffith of Penrhyn)
