2 CONT *Welsh Biograph Online
2 CONT *'''(3) A cadet branch of the Pulestons of Hafod-y-wern flourished at Caernarvon for part of the 16th cent. , its founder being the son''' by his first marriage (to Elin , daughter of Robert Whitney), of John Puleston (‘ Hen ’) , 
2 CONC '''Sir JOHN PULESTON (d. 1551 ), who was sheriff of Caernarvonshire , 1543-4 , Member of Parliament for Caernarvon , 1541-4 , and for Caernarvonshire , 1545-7 and 1547-51 , chamberlain of North Wales , 1547 , and constable of Caer
2 CONC narvon castle , 1523-51 . He m. (1) Gaynor , daughter of Robert ap Meredydd ap Hwlcyn Llwyd of Glynllifon , and (2) Sioned , daughter of Meredydd ap Ieuan ap Robert , of Cesail Gyfarch and Gwydir''' . From HUGH PULESTON , '''his s
2 CONC on by his second wife''', who m. Margaret , daughter and heiress of Hugh Lloyd , of Llwynycnotiau , near Wrexham , were descended the Pulestons of that place. There is evidence that the Rev. EDWARD PULESTON (d. 1621/2 ), second so
2 CONC n of this Hugh , who became rector of Burton Latimer, Northants , in 1592 , and ultimately inherited Llwynycnotiau from his childless elder brother, was a confidant of captain John Salisbury of Rûg (see Salusbury of Rûg ), one of 
2 CONC the principal conspirators in the Essex revolt of 1601 ; while his younger brother, RICHARD PULESTON , had served under the captain in Ireland . On the death, without issue, March 1677/8 , of Edward 's grandson, JOHN PULESTON , Ll
2 CONC wynycnotiau came into possession of his wife's brother, Simon Thelwall , of Plas-y-ward (see Thelwall of Plas-y-ward ), by virtue of a settlement made in 1672 . 
2 CONT *From: http://wbo.llgc.org.uk/en/s-PULE-EMR-1294.html
2 CONT *______________________
2 CONT *Robert Puleston (by 1526 - 15 August 1583), was a Welsh politician.
2 CONT *He was the eldest surviving son of '''Sir John Puleston of Caernarvon and Bersham, who was MP for Caernarvon and Caernarvonshire'''. He succeeded his father in 1551.
2 CONT *He was a Justice of the Peace for Denbighshire in 1555-61, Justice of the Peace of the Quorum from 1562 until his death, and appointed High Sheriff of Denbighshire for 1558-59 and 1569-70. He was also High Sheriff of Montgomerysh
2 CONC ire for 1571-72 and from 1573 to his death a J.P. for Caernarvonshire.
2 CONT *He was elected a Member (MP) of the Parliament of England for Caernarvon Boroughs in 1547 and for Denbighshire in March 1553 and 1571.
2 CONT *He married Ellen, the daughter of William Williams of Cochwillan, Caernarvonshire; they had 6 sons and 2 daughters.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Puleston_(MP)
2 CONT *______________________
