3 CONT This monument was discovered behind the tomb of Sir John Pakington when it was removed to its present position in the west of the chapel. the 3 carved shields, repainted in modern times are to (1) Pakington; (2) Pakington impaling
3 CONC  Dacres (the arms are wrongly painted); (3) Dacres.
3 CONT The brass inscription above it states that it was erected to Sir John Pakington who died in 1560. He was a judge, who received the grant of the Westwood property from Henry VIII, and married Anne daughter of Henry Dacres, alderman
3 CONC  of London
