1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anne has a very extensive will in her own right, which exhaustively details children, grandchildren, other relatives and relatives-to-be, etc. http://www.oxford-shakespeare.com/Probate/PROB_11-47_ff_73-5.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Sir John Pakington (c.1477 – 21 August 1551), was Chirographer of the Court of Common Pleas, a Member of Parliament for Gloucester, and Sheriff of Herefordshire and Worcestershire. In 1529 he received an extraordinary grant fr
2 CONC om Henry VIII permitting him to wear his hat in the King's presence.
2 CONT *Although the Pakington family is of great antiquity, being recorded at the time of the foundation of St Mary's Abbey, Kenilworth, in the reign of Henry I, according to Burke the 'founder of the fortunes of the house of Pakington'
2 CONC  was the lawyer Sir John Pakington in the reign of Henry VIII.[1]
2 CONT *Born about 1477,[2] he was the eldest son of John Pakington of Stanford-on-Teme, Worcestershire, and Elizabeth Washbourne, the daughter and heiress of Thomas Washbourne.[3][4][5] He had three brothers, Humphrey, Robert and August
2 CONC ine, and three sisters: Joyce married firstly a husband surnamed Blount, and secondly John Corbet of Leigh, Shropshire;[6] Eleanor married a husband surnamed Gravener, of Shropshire; and Margery married a husband surnamed Neve.[7]
2 CONT * Pakington began his legal career  ....
2 CONT * Pakington made his last will on 16 August 1551, and died five days later.[3] He was buried at Hampton Lovett in the chapel of St Anne in the parish church.[3][8] As he had no male issue, he was succeeded by Sir Thomas Pakington 
2 CONC (died 2 June 1571), the eldest son of his brother, Robert Pakington (died 1536).[3]
2 CONT *''' Pakington married, by 1530,[3] Anne (d. 22 August 1563),[16] the daughter of Henry Dacres of Mayfield, Staffordshire,[17] Alderman of London in 1526 and Sheriff in 1528,[18][19] a descendant of 'the ancient family of the Dacr
2 CONC es in Westmorland',[20] by his first wife, Elizabeth (d. 26 April 1530).[17] She had a brother''', Robert Dacres (d. 20 November 1543), Privy Councillor and Master of Requests to Henry VIII, who married Elizabeth Monoux (widow of 
2 CONC Sir Thomas Denny (d.1527), elder brother of Sir Anthony Denny, and daughter of Sir George Monoux (d.1544), Lord Mayor of London),[21][22] '''and two sisters''', Eleanor Dacres, who married George Rolle (d.1552); and Alice Dacres, 
2 CONC who married Robert Cheeseman (d. 24 July 1547).[23]
2 CONT *'''At the time of the marriage, Anne was the widow of Robert Fairthwaite (d.1521),[2] citizen and Merchant Taylor of London, by whom she had a daughter, Elizabeth Fairthwaite, who married Nicholas Tichborne of Roydon, Essex, as w
2 CONC ell as two sons, Martin Fairthwaite and Geoffrey Fairthwaite, who died without issue.[18]
2 CONT *'''By his wife Anne, Pakington is said to have had two daughters, Ursula (d.1558),[24] who married William Scudamore (d.1560),[24] by whom she was the mother of Sir John Scudamore (1542–1623),[24][25] and Bridget, who married Sir
2 CONC  John Littleton of Frankley, Worcestershire,[3] and after his death three other husbands.[8]
2 CONT *'''There is a memorial to Pakington's widow, Anne, in the church of St Botolph, Aldersgate which depicts Anne, a knight in armour, and a daughter. The inscription reads:
2 CONT **''' Here under this tombe lyeth ye bodye of Dame Anne Packington, Widdow, late wife Sr John Packington, Kt: late Chirographer in the court of ye comon Please wch. Dame Anne deceassed the 22nd. day of August in the yeare of our L
2 CONC ord God 1563.[16]
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Pakington_(died_1551) ___________________________
2 CONT *'''PAKINGTON, John (by 1488-1551), of Hampton Lovett, Worcs. and London.
2 CONT *b. by 1488, 1st s. of John Pakington by Elizabeth, da. of Thomas Washborne of Stanford-le-Teme, Worcs.; bro. of Robert. educ. I. Temple. '''m. by 1530, Anne, da. of Henry Dacres of London, wid. of Robert Fairethwatt of London, at
2 CONC  least 1s. d.v.p. 2da.''' Kntd. 23 Nov. 1546/9 Feb. 1547.3
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1509-1558/member/pakington-john-1488-1551 ___________________
