1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In the name of God Amen, I Sybill De la Bere of Tiberton in the Countie of Herefordshire widow being sick in body but whole in mind and of good and perfect memory ( for the which I give most hartie thanks unto my L
2 CONC ord God) do constitute and make this my last will and testament And hereby I doe dispose of all such goods... Item, I give and bequeath the sum of forty pounds which is due unto me by bond of Kinard De la bere John Broadshowe and 
2 CONC James Price unto Alice, Sibill and Elizabeth, daughters of the said Kinard, equally to be divided. And the payment thereof to be made unto them by this my executors within the space or at the end of 6 months next after the said Ki
2 CONC nard De la bere John Broadshowe or James Price aforesaid or either of them shall make payment thereof accordingly. Item I give and bequeath unto Cathe- rin and Blanche other daughters of the said Kinard De la bere the sum of nine 
2 CONC pounds equally to be devided between then within six monthes as aforesaid which is due unto me by a bill of debt of my sonne Kinard De la bere aforesaid. Item, I give unto my daughter Elizabeth Niccolls the sun of tewntie pounds. 
2 CONC Item, I give unto my daughter Maude Lawrence ten  both which sums of money are due unto me by a bonde obligation of Robert Smith gent as thereby appeareth. And my will is that the said some of 30 pounds shallbe paid as aforesaid I
2 CONC tem I give and bequeath unto my sonne Kinard De la bere all my household stuff of bedding brass and pewter and such implements of household whatsoever. Item allother my goods money plate jewells and whatsoever I give remayninge un
2 CONC bequeathed in this my last will and Testament I give and dispose unto my sonne William Dasey Esq whom I doe onlie nominate and appoint to be my sole and onlie Executor of this my last will and testament. And hereby I renounce and 
2 CONC revoke all other wills heretofore by me made, In witness wheeof I have  hereunto set my mark and subscribed my name, read and delivered in the presence of Kinard De la bere John Browne John Marten Elizabeth Nicholls, Sibill De la 
2 CONC bere marks.  Proved PCC London 1 Aug 1611 by William DANSEY the Exor
