1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Kyrle Baronetcy, of Much Marcle in the County of Hereford, was a title in the Baronetage of the United Kingdom. It was created on 12 May 1627 for John Kyrle, twice High Sheriff of Herefordshire. The second Baro
2 CONC net sat as Member of Parliament for Herefordshire. The title became extinct on his death in 1680.
2 CONT
2 CONT James Money, a descendant of the Kyrle Baronets, assumed the additional surname of Kyrle in 1809 and was created a baronet in 1838.
2 CONT
