1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *2B) ELEANOR CORNEWALL, born 1430/5, married 1st, Sir Hugh Mortimer, of Kyre Wyard and Martley, Worcestershire, and Tedstone Wafer, Herefordshire, heir of the Tedstone Wafer Mortimers. He was killed at Wakefield in
2 CONC  December 1460, and was buried in the Church of St. Peter, Martley. By him she had a son and a daughter. She married 2nd, Sir Richard Croft (d. 29 July 1509), of Croft Castle, Herefordshire, sheriff of Herefordshire 1471-72, 1477,
2 CONC  1486, MP Herefordshire 1477, and had three more sons and five more daughters. The Crofts had occupied Croft Castle since before the Conquest. Eleanor was the governess of Edward IV's sons at Ludlow Castle. She died 23 Dec. 1519, 
2 CONC at an advanced age, and was buried with her second husband in the chapel of Croft Castle (tomb now in St. Michael church, Croft). Issue: 
2 CONT **2B1) Sir JOHN MORTIMER, of Kyre Wyard, etc., born 1450/5, sheriff of Herefordshire 1477-8, 1481-2, steward of Abberley, Worcestershire during Warwick's minority 15 Aug. 1480, Squire of the Body 1481-5, knighted 1485, Knight of t
2 CONC he Body 1485-1504, sheriff of Worcestershire 1485-6, banneret at Stoke 16 June 1487, sheriff of Herefordshire 1493-4, 1501-2, MP Worcestershire 1495. He married, after 1485, Margaret Nevill (c.1466-31 Jan. 1528), third daughter an
2 CONC d co-heiress of John Nevill, Marquess of Montagu (d. 1471) by his wife Isabel Ingaldesthorpe. They had no issue, and Margaret went on to marry Charles Brandon, have it annulled the same year (1507), and then marry in 1522, one Rob
2 CONC ert Downes, in addition to having had an illegitimate daughter. Sir John Mortimer died without issue in October 1504 (writ of d.c.e. 1 Nov. 1504). 
2 CONT **2B2) ELIZABETH MORTIMER, LADY DE LA WARR, born 1455/60, married about 1480, Sir Thomas West, 8th Lord De La Warr (c.1457- 11 Oct. 1525), and died 29 June 1502, having had issue at least one son and four daughters. 
2 CONT **2B3) Sir EDWARD CROFT, of Croft Castle, born about 1465, sheriff of Herefordshire 1505, married Joyce Scull, said to be daughter of Sir Walter Scull, of Holt Castle, Worcestershire (d. about 1472; buried at Holt Castle church), 
2 CONC by his first wife Margaret Beauchamp of Holt (d. 1456; buried at Holt Castle church), but this seems unlikely due to chronology, and she was probably his daughter by his second wife Frances Mulle (d. 1483). Sir Edward died 23 Marc
2 CONC h 1541, having had four sons and seven daughters, and was ancestor of the Crofts of Croft Castle, descendants of whom still occupy the castle today. 
2 CONT **'''2B4) JOHN CROFT, of Holt, Worcestershire, born 1465/70, married Elizabeth Seymour''', daughter of John Seymour of Wolf Hall, Wiltshire (d. 1491), by his wife Elizabeth Darrell, '''and was ancestor of the Crofts of Holt. 
2 CONT **2B5) ROBERT CROFT, of Kyre Wyard, Worcestershire, married and had a sole daughter and heiress. 
2 CONT **2B6) ANN CROFT, married Sir Thomas Blount (1455- 4 June 1524), of Kinlet, Shropshire, and died 27 Sep. 1549, having had at least five sons and six daughters. 
2 CONT **2B7) ELIZABETH CROFT, married John Whittingham, of Pauntley, Gloucestershire. 
2 CONT **2B8) JOYCE CROFT, married Thomas Mill, of Avenbury, Herefordshire. 
2 CONT **2B9) JANE CROFT, married Sir Edward Darrell (1465/6- 9 Mar. 1530), of Littlecote, Witshire, and died by 1492, having had issue, two sons and two daughters. 
2 CONT **2B10) SYBIL CROFT, married Sir George Herbert (c.1463/5- died after 1504), of St Julians, Monmouthshire, third son of William Herbert, Earl of Pembroke. He was knighted in 1487 at the battle of Stoke. Dame Sybil had two sons and
2 CONC  one daughter. 
2 CONT *From: http://newsgroups.derkeiler.com/Archive/Soc/soc.genealogy.medieval/2005-08/msg00683.html ____________________
2 CONT *Sir Richard Croft, Sheriff of Herefordshire, Treasurer to Henry VII1,2,3
2 CONT *M, #77311, b. circa 1427, d. 29 July 1509
2 CONT *Father	William Croft3 b. c 1393, d. a 1433
2 CONT *Mother	Margaret Walwyn3 b. c 1395
2 CONT *     Sir Richard Croft, Sheriff of Herefordshire, Treasurer to Henry VII was born circa 1427 at of Croft Castle, Herefordshire, England.2,1,4 He married (Miss) Blount circa 1444.5 Sir Richard Croft, Sheriff of Herefordshire, Trea
2 CONC surer to Henry VII married Eleanor Cornwall, daughter of Sir Edmund Cornwall and Elizabeth Barre, between 1460 and 1465; They had 3 sons (Sir Edward; '''John'''; & Robert) & 5 daughters (Anne, wife of Sir Thomas Blount; Elizabeth,
2 CONC  wife of John Whittington, Esq; Joyce, wife of Thomas Mill, Esq; Jane (Alice), wife of Edward Darrell; & Sibyl, wife of Sir George Herbert). He also had an illegitimate son (Thomas).3 Sir Richard Croft, Sheriff of Herefordshire, T
2 CONC reasurer to Henry VII left a will on 11 July 1509.3 He died on 29 July 1509; Buried in the church of St. Michael, Croft Castle, Herefordshire.2,3 His estate was probated on 11 November 1509.3
2 CONT *Family 1     (Miss) Blount b. c 1428
2 CONT *Family 2     Eleanor Cornwall b. c 1435, d. 1520
2 CONT *Children	
2 CONT **Anne Croft+1 b. c 1463, d. 27 Sep 1549
2 CONT **Sibyl Croft5 b. c 1464
2 CONT **Sir Edward Croft, Sheriff of Herefordshire+6,3 b. c 1465, d. 23 Mar 1547
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S11571] A Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Commoners of Great Britain and Ireland, Vol. III, by John Burke, Esq., p. 199.
2 CONT *[S147] Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage, Baronetage, and Knightage, 1938 ed., by Sir Bernard Burke, p., 695.
