2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2573.htm#i77311 ________________
2 CONT *'''Elizabeth SEYMOUR
2 CONT *Born: ABT 1471, Wolfhall, Wiltshire, England
2 CONT *Father: John SEYMOUR
2 CONT *Mother: Elizabeth DARRELL
2 CONT *'''Married: John CROFT
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/SEYMOUR.htm#Elizabeth SEYMOUR3 ___________________
2 CONT *'''Annals of the Seymours : being a history of the Seymour family from early times to within a few years of the present     by St. Maur, H
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/annalsofseymours00stma
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/annalsofseymours00stma#page/16/mode/1up
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *   The elder brother, John Seymour of Wolfhall, was born in 1450. He was, therefore, barely 14 years of age 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/annalsofseymours00stma#page/17/mode/1up
2 CONT *when his father and grandfather died. He was twice married, first to Elizabeth, daughter of Sir George Darell, of Littlecote in Wilts, by Margaret, daughter of John, Lord Stourton ; secondly to a daughter of Robert Hardon, by who
2 CONC m he had one son, Roger, who in turn left four daughters, his coheirs. The death of John Seymour occurred in 1491.* By his first wife, Elizabeth, he left numerous issue : 
2 CONT **	Sir John Seymour, of whom we will speak next. 
2 CONT **	George Seymour, who was Sheriff of Wilts in 1499. 
2 CONT **	Robert Seymour. 
2 CONT **	Sir William Seymour, who was made a Knight of the Bath at the marriage of Arthur, Prince of Wales, November, 1501.† 
2 CONT **	Margaret Seymour, who married Sir William Wadham, knight. 
2 CONT **	Jane Seymour, who married Sir John Huddlestone, of Warleston, in Cumberland. 
2 CONT **'''	Elizabeth Seymour, who married John Crofts, Esq. 
2 CONT **	Catherine Seymour, who died unmarried. 
2 CONT *  .... etc ________________
2 CONT *John Seymour (c. 1450 - 26 October 1491) of Wulfhall, of Stalbridge, of Stinchcombe and of Huish, all in Wiltshire, was warden of Savernake Forest and a prominent member of the landed gentry in the counties of Wiltshire, Somerset
2 CONC  and Dorset. He was the grandfather of Queen Jane Seymour (c. 1508 – 1537), the third wife of King Henry VIII, and was thus great-grandfather of King Edward VI.
2 CONT *Seymour was the eldest of the three sons of John Seymour (c. 1425–1463), Knight of the Shire for Wiltshire and High Sheriff of Wiltshire, by his wife Elizabeth Coker (born circa 1436), daughter of Sir Robert Coker of Lydeard St L
2 CONC awrence, Somerset.
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *Seymour married twice:
2 CONT *Firstly he married Elizabeth Darrell (born c. 1451), daughter of Sir George Darrell (died c. 1474) of Littlecote, Wiltshire, by his wife Margaret Stourton (born c. 1433), a daughter of John Stourton, 1st Baron Stourton, and of Ma
2 CONC rgery or Marjory Wadham. By Elizabeth Darrell he had progeny four sons and four daughters:[2][3]
2 CONT **Sir John Seymour (1474–1536), knighted in 1497 after the Battle of Deptford Bridge, the father of Queen Jane Seymour (1508–1537).[3][4]
2 CONT **Sir George Seymour, Sheriff of Wiltshire in 1498[4]
2 CONT **Robert Seymour[3][4]
2 CONT **Sir William Seymour KB (born c. 1478, died c. 1503), married Margaret Byconnyll[3][4]
2 CONT **Margaret Seymour (born c. 1468), married (as his second wife) Sir Nicholas I Wadham (d.1542) of Merryfield in the parish of Ilton in Somerset and Edge in the parish of Branscombe, Devon, MP for Somerset in 1529, and Captain of t
2 CONC he Isle of Wight 1509-1520. She probably died at Carisbrooke Castle, her husband's seat as Captain of the Isle of Wight. Margaret Seymour's monument and tomb, dated circa 1520, survives in St Mary the Virgin Church, Carisbrooke,[5
2 CONC ] Isle of Wight, and is decorated with an effigy of herself and of six infirm persons, in memory of her having founded a hospital for the infirm. Her monument in Carisbrooke Church was described thus by Rogers (1888):[6] .... etc.
2 CONT **Jane Seymour (born c. 1469), married John Huddlestone of Cumberland[4]
2 CONT **'''Elizabeth Seymour (born c. 1471), married John Crofts, Esquire[3][4]
2 CONT **Catherine Seymour, who died unmarried.[3][4]
2 CONT *Seymour married secondly a daughter of Robert Hardon by whom he had one son:
2 CONT **Roger Seymour (born c. 1480, died before 1509), of Andover, Hampshire.[4]
2 CONT *From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Seymour_(died_1491) ________________________
2 CONT *Sir John Seymour, Hereditary Warden of Savernake Forest1,2,3
2 CONT *M, #22141, b. circa 1450, d. 26 October 1491
2 CONT *Father	John Seymour, Esq., Sheriff of Wiltshire, Burgess of Hindon4,5 b. c 1425, d. 29 Sep 1463
2 CONT *Mother	Elizabeth Coker4,5 b. c 1412, d. 19 Apr 1472
2 CONT *     Sir John Seymour, Hereditary Warden of Savernake Forest was born circa 1450 at of Wolfhall in Savernake, Stapleford, Stitchcombe, & Huish, Wiltshire, England; Age 14 in 1464, 26 in 1476, & 34 in 1485.2,3 He married Elizabeth
2 CONC  Darrell, daughter of Sir George Darrell, Sheriff of Wiltshire, Somersetshire, & Dorsetshire and Margaret Stourton, circa 1472; They had 4 sons (Sir John; Sir George; Sir Robert; & Sir William) & 4 daughters (Margaret, wife of Sir
2 CONC  William Wadham; Jane, wife of Sir John Huddleston; '''Elizabeth, wife of John Crofts, Esq'''; & Katherine).2,3 Sir John Seymour, Hereditary Warden of Savernake Forest died on 26 October 1491 at of West Bower in Bridgwater, Moorla
2 CONC nd in North Petherton, & Cokers in Wembdon, Somersetshire, England.2,3
2 CONT *Family    Elizabeth Darrell b. c 1454, d. c 1479
2 CONT *Children	
2 CONT **Sir John Seymour, Sheriff of Wiltshire, Constable of Bristol Castle+2,6,3 b. 1476, d. 21 Dec 1536
2 CONT **Joan Seymour7,8 b. c 1477
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S6795] Unknown author, Pedigrees of Some of the Emperor Charlemagne's Descendants, Vol. I, p. 223; Wallop Family, p. 702.
2 CONT *[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 109-110.
2 CONT *[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. IV, p. 615.
2 CONT *[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 109.
2 CONT *[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. IV, p. 614.
2 CONT *[S6] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry: 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 82.
