2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT '''Sir James Croft'''
2 CONT BIRTH 1518
2 CONT DEATH 4 Sep 1590 (aged 71–72)
2 CONT BURIAL Westminster Abbey, Westminster, City of Westminster, Greater London, England
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID 127175401 by julia&keld
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir James Croft was the son of Richard Croft and Catherine Herbert. He married, firstly, Alice Warncombe, daughter of Richard Warncombe. He married, secondly, Catherine Blount, daughter of Edward Blount. He died on 4 September 159
2 CONC 0.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir James Croft was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.).1 He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Herefordshire. He was invested as a Knight in 1547. He held the office of Governor of Haddington in 1549. He held th
2 CONC e office of Lord Depute of Ireland in 1551. He held the office of Deputy Constable of the Tower in 1552. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 21 February 1554 he was convicted of high treason and committed to the Tower. On 18 January 1555 he escaped with being bound to good bearing and fined £500. He held the office of a Lord of the Marches in 1557. He held the offic
2 CONC e of Governor of Berwick in 1560. He held the office of Comptroller of the Household. In 1586 he was one of the Privy Counsellors appointed to try Mary, Queen of Scots. He was Commissioner of the Treaty of Bourbourg in 1588. He li
2 CONC ved at Croft Castle, Herefordshire, England. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Richard Croft unknown–1562
2 CONT Katherine Herbert Croft
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Alice Warnecombe Croft unknown–1573
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT Herbert Croft 1571–1622
2 CONT
