1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir John Goddard married Elizabeth Fettiplace, daughter of John Fettiplace and Dorothea Danvers. Sir John Goddard was born circa 1518 at of Standen Hussey, Wiltshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT * Elizabeth Fettiplace b. 1524, d. 23 Oct 1584 Child	
2 CONT * Edward Goddard+ d. 1610
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p730.htm#i21942 —
2 CONT
2 CONT John Goddard was the son of John Goddard and Elizabeth Berenger Goddard.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Fettiplace circa 1543.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1567 having left a will naming his (second) wife Alice and children Anthony, Thomas, William, Edmund, Ann, and Vincent.
2 CONT
2 CONT "John Goddard, of Standon Hussey, Wilts, esq. Will dated July 12, 1567. [31 Steward.] To be buried in Hungerford Church. My sons Anthony, Thomas & William. My daughter Ann. My son Vincent. My wife Alice. My son Edmonde. My son in 
2 CONC law John Croke. My manor of Clyffe Pyppard. My brother Edmund Hungerford. My cousin John Tutt."[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Goddard-446 —-
