1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas Shirley pre-deceased his parents, having married Margaret, daughter of John Wroth, of Durance, in the parish of Enfield, co. Middlesex, esq. had issue Joyce, his only surviving daughter and heir, who married
2 CONC , first, Richard Abington, of Brockhampton, in the county of Hereford, esq. and, secondly, Thomas Blount, of Sodington, in Worcestershire, esq. progenitor of the ancient family of that name still settled there. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Jocosa 'Joyce' Shirley, daughter of Thomas Shirley and Margaret Wrothe. was born circa 1501 at Staunton Harold, Leicestershire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married first to Richard Abington, Esq., son of Richard Abington and Eleanor Hanley, circa 1520.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jocosa Shirley married second to Thomas Blount, Esq., son of Peter Blount and Anne Cornwall, after 1563 at of Staunton Harold, Leicestershire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 1
2 CONT Richard Abington, Esq. b. c 1502 
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT #     Eleanor Abington b. c 1521  (wife of Thomas Baskerville, Knt., and John Gage). 
2 CONT # Mary
2 CONT # Jane (wife of Edward Stanford, Gent., and Oliver Briggs)
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 2
2 CONT Thomas Blount, Esq. b. c 1520, d. 1564
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT # Peter Blount
2 CONT #Sir George Blount2 b, d. 20 Jan 1610 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes: From < [https://www.shirleyassociation.com/NewShirleySite/NonMembers/England/Lineages/Herfordshire_HughShirley_Stockton.html shirleyassociation.com] >
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 3(i). '''Joyce Shirley''' ''daughter and heiress.'' She married (1st) Richard Abington (or Habington), Esq., of Brockhampton, co. Hereford, son and heir of Richard Abington, of Brockhampton, co. Hereford, by Eleanor, daughter of J
2 CONC ohn Hanley. They had three daughters, Mary, Jane (wife of Edward Stanford, Gent., and Oliver Briggs), and Eleanor (wife of Thomas Baskerville, Knt., and John Gage). His widow, Joyce, married (2nd) (as his 2nd wife) Thomas Blount, 
2 CONC Esq., of Sodington, co. Worcester. They had two sons, George, Knt., and Peter. His wife, Joyce, was living in 1551–3. Thomas Blount, Esq., died testate (P.C.C., 20 Chayre) 10 Dec. 1562, and was buried at Mamble, co. Worcester.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
