1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =='''John Talbot, 10th Earl of Shrewsbury==
2 CONT '''John Talbot, 10th Earl of Shrewsbury, 10th Earl of Waterford (1601 - 8 February 1654) was an English nobleman.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was the only child and son of''' John Talbot of Longford, Newport, Shropshire (died London, 1607 or c. 1607), and wife Eleanor Baskerville, daughter of Sir Thomas Baskerville of Wolvershill, Herefordshire, and of Brinsop, He
2 CONC refordshire, and grandson of Sir John Talbot of Grafton and Catherine or Katharine Petre.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He remained in his family's Roman Catholic faith and took part on the side of King Charles I in the English Civil War. He was First Commissioner of Advice for the counties of Worcestershire, Shropshire and Staffordshire in 1644
2 CONC /45, and he served on the Royalist garrison at Worcester when it surrendered to Parliament in July 1646. In 1647 his estates were sequestered and compounded by Parliament on grounds of his being a "Papist and delinquent" (i.e. Cat
2 CONC holic and royalist).[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In September 1651 he accompanied Charles II when he fled after defeat at the battle of Worcester, escorting him to Whiteladies in Shropshire, where the king was hidden for a time.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He married Mary Fortescue, by whom he had five children:
2 CONT * Lady Frances Talbot (d. 17 July 1641), married George Winter, 1st Baronet (1622 - 1658) and had issue Thomas Winter
2 CONT * George Talbot, Baron Talbot (circa 1620 - 7 March 1644[1]), married Mary, daughter of Percy Herbert, 2nd Baron Powis. He had issue one daughter, Mary, living 1649 but died young and unmarried.[1]
2 CONT * Francis Talbot, 11th Earl of Shrewsbury (1623 - 1667)
2 CONT * Hon. Gilbert Talbot (bef. 1654 - 1711), married Jane Flatsburg and had issue, including Gilbert Talbot, 13th Earl of Shrewsbury
2 CONT * Lady Mary Talbot (bef. 1654 - c. March 1711), married first Charles Arundell and had issue, married second Mervyn Tuchet, 4th Earl of Castlehaven and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He later married Hon. Frances Arundell, daughter of Thomas Arundell, 1st Baron Arundell of Wardour and had three sons by her:
2 CONT * Hon. John Talbot
2 CONT * Hon. Bruno Talbot
2 CONT * Hon. Thomas Talbot
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Earl died in 1653/54 at Tasmore, Oxfordshire,[1] and was succeeded by his second son.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Talbot,_10th_Earl_of_Shrewsbury
2 CONT
2 CONT ____________________________
2 CONT ==John Talbot, 10th Earl of Shrewsbury1==
2 CONT '''M, #12344, b. circa 1601, d. 8 February 1653/54'''
2 CONT Last Edited=16 Jun 2017
2 CONT '''John Talbot, 10th Earl of Shrewsbury was born circa 1601.1 He was the son of''' John Talbot and Eleanor Baskerville.1 '''He married, firstly, Mary Fortescue''', daughter of Sir Francis Fortescue, '''before 1619.2,1 He married, 
2 CONC secondly, Hon. Frances Arundell''', daughter of Thomas Arundell, 1st Baron Arundell of Wardour and Anne Philipson, '''before 15 February 1647/48.3,1 He died on 8 February 1653/54.'''1
2 CONT '''He succeeded as the 10th Earl of Shrewsbury [E., 1442] on 2 April 1630.1 He succeeded as the 10th Earl of Waterford [I., 1446] on 2 April 1630.1 A Royalist during the Civil War.1 In 1647 he had his estates sequestered by the Co
2 CONC mmittee for Compunding.'''1
2 CONT '''Children of John Talbot, 10th Earl of Shrewsbury and Mary Fortescue'''
2 CONT 1. Lady Mary Talbot+2 d. c Mar 1710/11
2 CONT 2. George Talbot, Lord Talbot1 b. c 1620, d. 7 Mar 1642
2 CONT 3. Francis Talbot, 11th Earl of Shrewsbury+1 b. c 1623, d. 16 Mar 1667
2 CONT 4. Hon. Gilbert Talbot+1 b. c 1631, d. c 8 Apr 1702
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT 1. [S37] BP2003 volume 3, page 3604. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT 2. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extin
2 CONC ct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume III, page 88. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT 3. [S21] L. G. Pine, The New Extinct Peerage 1884-1971: Containing Extinct, Abeyant, Dormant and Suspended Peerages With Genealogies and Arms (London, U.K.: Heraldry Today, 1972), page 10. Hereinafter cited as The New Extinct Peer
