2 CONT ==John Talbot of Grafton==
2 CONT Sir John Talbot of Grafton, Worcestershire (1545 – 28 January 1611[1]) was a prominent recusant English Catholic layman of the reigns of Elizabeth I of England and James I of England. He was connected by marriage to one of the Gun
2 CONC powder Plot conspirators, and by acquaintance or family ties to other important Catholic figures. He fell often under suspicion from the English government.
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT He was the only son and heir of Sir John Talbot, of Grafton Manor, Worcestershire, and of Albrighton, Shropshire (died 6 June 1555), and wife Frances Giffard, daughter of Sir John Giffard, and grandson of Sir John Talbot of Albrig
2 CONC hton (died 10 September 1549) by his second wife Margaret Troutbeck.[5]
2 CONT He was the father, by Katherine Petre, daughter of Sir William Petre and his second wife, Anne Browne, daughter of Sir William Browne, Lord Mayor of London, of three sons and three daughters,[1] who included:
2 CONT *Anne Talbot, married 18 November 1585 Thomas Hanmer (died 18 April 1619), and had issue, including Sir John Hanmer, 1st Baronet
2 CONT *George Talbot, 9th Earl of Shrewsbury, a Catholic priest
2 CONT *Gertrude Talbot, married Robert Wintour of Huddington, Worcestershire (executed 30 January 1606)
2 CONT *John Talbot of Longford, Market Drayton, Shropshire (died London, in or around 1607), married Eleanor Baskerville, daughter of Sir Thomas Baskerville of Wolvershill, Herefordshire, and of Brinsop, Herefordshire, and had '''one so
2 CONC n, John Talbot, 10th Earl of Shrewsbury'''
2 CONT References
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Talbot_of_Grafton
2 CONT
2 CONT ____________________________
2 CONT ==The peerage of England; containing a genealogical and historical account of all the peers of England, ... By Arthur Collins, ...  1741: Vol 2==
2 CONT by Collins, Arthur
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/bim_eighteenth-century_the-peerage-of-england-_collins-arthur_1741_2/mode/1up
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/bim_eighteenth-century_the-peerage-of-england-_collins-arthur_1741_2/page/63/mode/1up
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT Which Sir John Talbot, in his laft Teftament, writes himfelf of Grafton, and died in 4 E. VI. as fhould feem by the Probate thereof, which bears date 11 Oct. 1549. And by Margaret his firft Wife, Daughter and Heir of Adam Troutbec
2 CONC k, of the County Palatine of Chefter, Efq; left Iffue, befides other Children, John Talbot of Grafton. And by his fecond Wife, Elizabeth, Daughter of ___ Wrotefley of Wrotefley, in Com' Staff. Efq; left Iffue John Talbot of Salwar
2 CONC p, in Com' Wigorn. Efq; from whom defcended a numerous Pofterity, as the Talbots of Salwarp, the Talbots of Badgworth, in Com' Glouc. and Okely, in Com' Wigorn, and the Talbots of Worril, Com' Salop, Sherington Talbot of Salwarp, 
2 CONC The eldeft Son, was Grandfather to William Talbot, late Lord Bifhop of Durham, who was Grandfather to the prefent Lord Talbot. But I return to John Talbot of Grafton, who died Anno 2 & 3 Phil. and Mary, and by Frances, his Wife, D
2 CONC aughter of Sir John Giffard of Chillington, in Com' Staff. Knt. had Iffue John Talbot of Grafton, and a Daughter, Joan, married to Sir John Bowes.
2 CONT Which John Talbot of Grafton, Efq; married Catherine, Daughter to Sir William Petre, Knt. Principal Secretary of State to Queen Mary, and left Iffue two Sons, George, who became Earl of Shrewbury, and John Talbot of Longford, in C
2 CONC om' Salop, Efq;
2 CONT Which George, in the 15th Year of King James I. fucceeded Edwared, Earl of Shrewbury, before-mention's, but died unmarried the 2d of April 1630, and was buried in the Church of Albrighton, in Com' Salop. '''To whom fucceeded John 
2 CONC his Nephew, viz. Son to John his brother, by Eleanor his Wife, Daughter and Coheir of Sir Thomas Baskerville, of Wolverfhil,
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/bim_eighteenth-century_the-peerage-of-england-_collins-arthur_1741_2/page/64/mode/1up
2 CONT in Com' Wigorn, Knt.''' who had Iffue by him likewife a Daughter, Catharine, Wife of James Pool of Pool, in Com' Cefter. Efq;
2 CONT '''Which John, Earl of Shrewsbury, firft married Mary the Daughter''' of Sir Francis Fortfcue, of Salden-Hall, in Com' Buck. Knight of the Bath, '''by whom he had Iffue''' George Lord Talbot, who married Mary, Daughter of Piercy L
2 CONC ord Powis, but died Childlefs, in the '''Life-time of his Father''', and was buried by his Uncle at Albrighton. Francis, Earl of Shrewbury, '''fecond Son'''. Edward, '''third Son''', kill'd at the Battle of Marfton-moor on the Kin
2 CONC g's fide, 1 July 1644. Walter Talbort of Cookfey, in Com' Wigorn. Efq; '''fourth Son. Alfo three Daughters''', Lady Mary, married to Mervin Touchet, Earl of Caftlehaven; Lady Catherine, to Thomas Whetenall, of Eaft-Peckham in Kent
2 CONC , Efq; Lady Frances, to Sir George Wintour of Huddington, in Com' Wigorn, Knt. '''And afterwards taking to his fecond Wife, Frances, Daughter''' to Thomas Lord Arundel of Wardour, '''had Iffue three Sons''', Thomas Talbot of Longf
2 CONC ord Efq; John, who died young; Bruno; and Anne, '''a Daughter''', veil'd a Nun in France.
2 CONT '''This John, Earl of Shrewsbury, died on the 8th of Feb. 1653, to whom fucceeded in his Honours''', Francis '''his Son and Heir'''.
2 CONT Which Francis, Earl of Shrewsbury, firft married Anne Daughter and Heir to Sir John Coniers of Sockburne, in the county Palatine of Durham, Knt. by Elizabeth his Wife, Daughter to Sir George Simeon, of Brightwell, in Com' Oxon. Kn
2 CONC t. by Mary His Wife, Sifter to Edward Lord Vaux, of Harwedon, by whom he has Iffue Conyers, who died young, and Mary, married to ___ Stoner, of Watlington-Partk, in Com' Oxon. Efq; to his fecond Wife, he wedded Anna-Maria, Daughte
2 CONC r to Robert, Earl of Cardigan, by whom he had Iffue Charles late Duke of Shrewbury, and John kill'd in a Duel by Henry Duke of Grafton, on the 2d of February 1685.6, being within five or fix Days of the Age of 21 Years, when it wa
2 CONC s commonly reported, that he had been foretold by an Aftrologer, that he would be kill'd by a tall black Man, before he was 21 Years of Age; but his high Spirit would not permit him to refrain the Duel.
2 CONT The faid Earl Francis, his Father, died 15 Martii, Anno 1667, of a Wound received in a Duel with George Duke of Buckingham; his Lady furviving, who died on the 20th of April 1702.
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________________
2 CONT ==Shrewsbury, Earl of (E, 1442)==
2 CONT *5. Sir Gilbert Talbot KG, of Grafton, co. Worcester, fought on the Lancastrian side at the Battle of Bosworth 1485, Commander at the Battle of Stoke 1487, Deputy Captain of Calais (d. 19 Sep 1518), mar. (1) after 1475 Elizabeth l
2 CONC e Scrope (widow of Thomas [le Scrope], 5th Baron Scrope of Masham), 5th dau. by his first wife of Ralph [de Greystock], 5th Baron Greystock, and had issue:
2 CONT **1a. Sir Gilbert Talbot, of Grafton, co. Worcester, Sheriff of Worcestershire c. 1540 (dspms. 22 Oct 1542), mar. (1) Anne Paston, dau. and cohrss. of Sir William Paston, by his wife Lady Anne Beaufort, sister and cohrss. of Henry
2 CONC  [Beaufort], 2nd Duke of Somerset, and 5th dau. of Edmund [Beaufort], 1st Duke of Somerset, and (2) Elizabeth Wynter, and had issue by his first wife:
2 CONT ***1b. Humphrey Talbot  (dsp.)
2 CONT ***2b. Walter Talbot (dsp.)
2 CONT ***1b. Margaret Talbot, mar. Sir Robert Newport
2 CONT ***2b. Elizabeth Talbot, mar. Sir John Lyttelton, of Frankley in the County of Worcester (d. 17 May 1532), and had issue
2 CONT ***3b. Mary Talbot, mar. Sir Thomas Astley, of Patshull, co. Stafford, and had issue
2 CONT **2a. Sir Humphrey Talbot (dsp. in the Holy Land)
2 CONT *Sir Gilbert Talbot KG mar. (2) Etheldreda Gardiner (widow of (1) Thomas Barton and (2) Richard Gardiner, Lord Mayor of London), dau. of William Landwade, of Landwade, co. Cambridge, and had further issue:
2 CONT **3a. Sir John Talbot, of Albrighton, co. Shropshire, and later of Grafton, co. Worcester, High Sheriff of Shropshire 1528, 1538 and 1542 (d. 10 Sep 1549), mar. (1) Margaret Troutbeck, dau. and hrss. of Adam Troutbeck, of Mobberle
2 CONC y, co. Cheshire, and had issue:
2 CONT ***1b. Sir John Talbot, of Grafton and Albrighton (d. 6 Jun 1555), mar. Frances Giffard, dau. of Sir John Giffard, and had issue:
2 CONT ****1c. Sir John Talbot, of Grafton, mar. (1) Catherine Petre, 1st dau. of Sir William Petre, Secretary of State 1543-66, by his second wife Anne Tyrell, widow of Thomas Tyrell and dau. of Sir William Browne, Lord Mayor of London 
2 CONC 1514, and (2) Hon Margaret Windsor, dau. of Henry [Windsor], 5th Baron Windsor, and had issue by his first wife:
2 CONT *****1d. George Talbot, later 9th Earl of Shrewsbury
2 CONT *****2d. John Talbot, of Longford, co. Shropshire (d. 1607), mar. Eleanor Baskerville, dau. and cohrss. of Sir Thomas Baskerville, of Brinsop, co. Hereford, and had issue:
2 CONT ******'''1e. John Talbot, later 10th Earl of Shrewsbury
2 CONT *
2 CONT *'''John [Talbot], 10th Earl of Shrewsbury
2 CONT *'''1st son and heir of''' John Talbot, of Longford, co. Shropshire (by his wife Eleanor Baskerville, dau. and cohrss. of Sir Thomas Baskerville, of Brinsop, co. Hereford),''' yr. bro. of''' George [Talbot], 9th Earl of Shrewsbury
2 CONT *'''born	bef. 1601
2 CONT *'''mar. (1)	bef. 1619 Mary Fortescue''' (bur. 6 Jan 1635/6; bur. at Albrighton, co. Shropshire), dau. of Sir Francis Fortescue, of Salden Hill, co. Buckingham, by his wife Grace Manners, dau. of Hon Sir John Manners, of Haddon Ha
2 CONC ll, co. Derby (by his wife Dorothy Vernon, dau. and cohrss. of Sir George Vernon, of Nether Haddon, co. Derby), 2nd son by his second wife of Thomas [Manners], 1st Earl of Rutland
2 CONT *'''children by first wife
2 CONT **1. Hon George Talbot, styled Lord Talbot (b. c. 1620; dvp. and spm. May 1644; bur. at Albrighton, co. Shropshire), mar. Jan 1639 Hon Mary Herbert (bapt. 10 Oct 1623; d. aft. 16 Jan 1662/3), only dau. of Percy [Herbert], 2nd Baro
2 CONC n Powis, by his wife Elizabeth Craven, sister and in her issue cohrss. of William [Craven], 1st Earl of Craven, and 1st surv. dau. of Sir William Craven, Lord Mayor of London 1610-11, and had issue:
2 CONT ***1a. .... etc.
2 CONT **2. Hon Francis Talbot, later 11th Earl of Shrewsbury
2 CONT **3. Hon Gilbert Talbot (b. c. 1631; bur. 11 Apr 1702), mar. Jane Flatsbury, dau. of William Flatsbury, and had issue:
2 CONT ***1a. .... etc.
2 CONT **1. Lady Mary Talbot (bur. 15 Mar 1710/1), mar. (1) Charles Arundell, 2nd but 1st surv. son and heir of Hon William Arundell, of Horningsham, co. Wiltshire (by his wife and second cousin Hon Mary Paulet, widow of Lord William Pau
2 CONC let, styled Earl of Wiltshire, 1st son and heir of William [Paulet], 4th Marquess of Winchester, and 1st dau. of Anthony Maria [Browne], 2nd Viscount Montagu), 2nd son by his first wife of Thomas [Arundell], 1st Baron Arundell of 
2 CONC Wardour, and (2) Mervyn [Tuchet], 4th Earl of Castlehaven, and had issue by both husbands
2 CONT *'''mar. (2)	bef. 15 Feb 1647/8 Hon Frances Arundell''' (dsp. 2 May 1652), 4th dau. of Thomas [Arundell], 1st Baron Arundell of Wardour, by his second wife Anne Philipson, dau. of Miles Philipson, of Crook, co. Westmorland
2 CONT *'''died	8 Feb 1653/4
2 CONT *'''suc. by	son by first wife
2 CONT *
2 CONT *Francis [Talbot], 11th Earl of Shrewsbury
2 CONT *born	c.1623
2 CONT *mar. (1)	Anne Conyers, dau. and hrss. of Sir John Conyers, of Sockburn, co Durham, by his wife Elizabeth Simeon, dau. of Sir George Simeon, of Baldwin Brightwell, co. Oxford
2 CONT *only child by first wife
2 CONT **	1. Lady Mary Talbot, mar. John Stonor, of Watlington Park, co. Oxford
2 CONT *mar. (2)	10 Jan 1658/9 Lady Anna Maria Brudenell (mar. (2) bef. 24 Jun 1677 George Rodney Bridges, of Keynsham, co. Somerset;  d. 20 Apr 1702; bur. in St Giles's-in-the-Fields Church, co. Middlesex), dau. of Robert [Brudenell], 2
2 CONC nd Earl of Cardigan, by his second wife Lady Anne Savage, 4th dau. of Thomas [Savage], 1st Viscount Savage, by his wife Lady Elizabeth D'Arcy, suo jure Countess Rivers for life, 1st dau. and cohrss. of Thomas [Darcy], 1st Earl Riv
2 CONC ers
2 CONT *only child by second wife
2 CONT **1. Hon Charles Talbot, later 12th Earl of Shrewsbury later 1st Duke of Shrewsbury
2 CONT *died	10 Mar 1667/8 (bur. at Albrighton, co. Shropshire)
2 CONT *suc. by	son by second wife
2 CONT *note	fought at the Battle of Worcester 1651; Lord Housekeeper of Hampton Court 1661; Treasurer and Receiver General of Ireland 1661; died from wounds following a duel at Barn Elms with George [Villiers], 2nd Duke of Buckingham, h
2 CONC is wife's lover
2 CONT *From: http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/shrewsbury1442.htm?zoom_highlight=talbot ____________________________
2 CONT =='Talbot02'==
2 CONT *Sir John Talbot, 1st Earl of Shrewbury (b 1390, d Chastillon 20.07.1453)
2 CONT *  m1. (12.03.1406) Maud Nevill, Baroness Furnivall (b c1391, d before 1433, dau of Thomas Nevill, Lord Furnival)
2 CONT **	1. John Talbot, 2nd Earl of Shrewsbury, Lord Chancellor of Ireland (b 1413, d Northampton 10.07.1460, 2nd son)
2 CONT **	  m1. (before 08.06.1421, sp) Catherine Burnel (dau of Sir Edward Burnel) this marriage may not have taken place
2 CONT **	  m2. Elizabeth Butler (d 08.09.1473, dau of James Butler, 4th Earl of Ormonde, Lord Lieutenant of Ireland)
2 CONT ***		A. John Talbot, 3rd Earl of Shrewsbury (b 12.12.1448, d 28.06.1473)
2 CONT ***		  m. (1467) Catherine Stafford (d 26.12.1476, dau of Humphrey de Stafford, 1st Duke of Buckingham)
2 CONT ****			i. .... etc.
2 CONT ***		B. Sir Gilbert Talbot of Grafton, Sheriff of Shropshire (d 19.09.1518, 5th son)
2 CONT ***		Brydges identifies Sir Gilber's 1st wife as Elizabeth, widow of Thomas, Lord Scrope of Masham, dau of Henry, Lord Scrope of Bolton by Alice Scrope. BP1934 identifies her as ...
2 CONT ***		  m1. Elizabeth Greystock (dau of Ralph Greystock, 7th Lord of Greystoke, widow of Thomas, Lord Scrope)
2 CONT ****			i. .... etc.
2 CONT ***		  m2. Etheldreda/Audrey Cotton (dau of William (not John) Cotton of Landwade)
2 CONT ****			iii. Sir John Talbot of Albrighton & Grafton, Sheriff of Shropshire (d 10.09.1549)
2 CONT ****			  m1. Margaret Troutbeck (dau of Adam Troutbeck of Mobberley)
2 CONT *****				a. Sir John Talbot of Grafton & Albrighton (d 06.06.1555)
2 CONT *****				  m. Frances Giffard (dau of Sir John Giffard of Chillington)
2 CONT ******					(1) Sir John Talbot of Grafton
2 CONT ******					  m1. Catherine Petre (dau of Sir William Petre, Secretary of State)
2 CONT *******						(A) George Talbot, 9th Earl of Shrewsbury (d unm 02.04.1630)
2 CONT *******						(B) John Talbot of Longford (d 1607)
2 CONT *******						  m. Elizabeth Baskerville (dau of Sir Thomas Baskerville of Wolvershill)
2 CONT ********'''							(i) John Talbot, 10th Earl of Shrewsbury (d 08.02.1653-4)'''
2 CONT ********'''							  m1. Mary Fortescue''' (dau of Sir Francis Fortescue of Salden Hill)
2 CONT ********'''							  m2. Frances''' (dau of Thomas, 1st Lord Arundel of Wardour)
2 CONT ********							(ii)+ other issue (d unm)
2 CONT *******						(C) .... etc.
