2 CONT Excerpt:
2 CONT
2 CONT Adderley, Ralph (1784-1851) of Coton Hall and Barlaston Hall. Second son of Ralph Adderley of Coton Hall (1744-1819) and his wife Dorothy, daughter and heir of Thomas Kynnersley of Loxley Park (Worcs), born 15 June 1781. He marrie
2 CONC d, 4 July 1816, Rosamond (d. 1856), daughter and heir of William Mills of Barlaston Hall and had issue:
2 CONT (1) Sophia Catherine Adderley (1817-35), baptised 5 May 1818;
2 CONT (2) Mary Elizabeth Adderley (1818?-1903?); died unmarried;
2 CONT (3) Ralph Thomas Adderley (1826-68) (q.v.);
2 CONT (4) Anne Selina Adderley (1829-1911) (q.v.);
2 CONT (5) Randolph Ralph Adderley (1832-55), born 15 February 1832; served in 79th Regiment (Lt., 1854) and 60th Regiment (1st Lieutenant, 1854); died at King William's Town, Cape of Good Hope, 29 April 1855;
2 CONT (6) Myles Bagnall Bowyer Adderley (b.1835), born 6 June 1835; educated at Harrow and Trinity College, Cambridge (admitted 1853); served at Lieutenant, Royal Horse Guards (retired, 1857); m. 1872 Rosina Hannah Jacobs; living in Blo
2 CONC omsbury, London in 1881.
2 CONT He inherited the Coton Hall estate from his father in 1819 and Barlaston Hall in right of his wife in 1822.
2 CONT He died 31 January 1851.
