2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=flugar15136&id=I09840
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Knight of St. Donat's , died 1535; married Elizabeth, daughter of Sir Thomas Arundel and Catherine Dinham of Tremoderet in Dulve, Davon, and Lanhere, Cornwall.She died 1513 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From thePeerage.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT      Sir Edward Stradling was born in 1474 at St. Donats, Glamorgan, Wales. He was the son of Thomas Stradling and Janet Matthew. He married Elizabeth Arundell, daughter of Thomas Arundell and Catherine Dynham. He died on 8 May 15
2 CONC 35.2
2 CONT
2 CONT      He was the ancestor of the Stradlings, Baronets of St. Donats.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Sir Edward Stradling and Elizabeth Arundell
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Jane Stradling+ b. 20 Feb 1504/5, d. 1555
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Added by Lady Aimee Mack
2 CONT Source: The History of the Stradlings of St Donats Together with that of the Parish, Manor and Castle. by T.C.Evans -
2 CONT
2 CONT Cardiff central Library Manuscript No. 3.166 Transcribed from the original by Dr Hugh Stradling, 1996
2 CONT
2 CONT ***********************
2 CONT
2 CONT "Thomas  Stradling Esq the son, enjoyed the possession  of  St Donats  but  for  few years for he died at the castle  on  the  8th September  1480  when in his 26th year.    He left three  children, Edward,  Harry  and Jane.   Edw
2 CONC ard succeeded his father.    Harry's son  eventually came into the estates and Jane married Sir  William Griffiths of Caernarfonshire and took with her as waiting woman one Agnes,  wife of David Rhys who went as gardener.   The so
2 CONC n of  this pair  after  a somewhat adventurous childhood and youth became  the learned   Dr  John  Dafydd  Rhys,  who   must  presently   have   a biographical chapter to himself.    Thomas Stradling's widow became the  wife  of  
2 CONC Sir  Rhys ab Thomas and is buried  with  her  second husband at Caermathen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Edward Stradling  who succeeded to the estates when quite an  infant, was knighted in Tourney Church under the royal  banners of King Henry VIII on December 25th - 5th Henry VIII.    He married Elizabeth  Arundel of Llanhydroc
2 CONC k, Cornwall and had four  sons  and two  daughters of this marriage, besides nine or more  illegitimate children.     Of  the  four sons by  his wife,  Robert  the  second married the daughter of Watkin Lougher of Fythegstone;  Ed
2 CONC ward  the third  son  married the daughter and heiress of  Robert  Raglan  of Llantwit  Major;  and John his fourth became a  priest.     Of  the daughters, Jane married Alexander Popham of Somersetshire and  from them descended s
2 CONC everal respectable families;  and Catherine married Sir William Palmer of  Sussex and had issue."
2 CONT
2 CONT *********************** Added by Lady Aimee Mack Stradling Memorial at The Church of St Donats
2 CONT
2 CONT     "Here  lyeth Edward Stradlinge knight, the 4th of  that  name,
2 CONT      sone  to  Thomas  Stradlinge Esq.  and  Janet  his  wife,  the
2 CONT      daughter  of   Thomas Matthews of Radyr,  in  the  countie  of
2 CONT      Glamorgan, Esq;  who died in the castle of St Donats  the  8th
2 CONT      daie of Maie, in the year of our Lord 1535, and was  buried in
2 CONT      the  chancel of the church there, whose bones were  afterwards
2 CONT      translated by his nephew, Edward Stradling knight, the 5th  of
2 CONT      that name into the chapel there, in the year of our Lord 1573.
2 CONT      Also here lyeth Elizabeth his wyfe, daughter of Thomas Arundel
2 CONT      of  Lanheydrock in the county of Cornwall, knight, who died in
2 CONT      child-bed  at   Merthyr Mawr the 20th day of February  in  the
2 CONT      year  of  our  Lord 1513. and was buried there, - whose  bones
2 CONT      Thomas  Stradling knight her sonne, caused to be taken up  and
2 CONT      carried  to St Donats and buried in the chancel of the  church
2 CONT      there with her husband, the 8th day of May in the year of  our
2 CONT      Lord  1536 and afterwards by Edward Stradlinge translated into
2 CONT      the chapel there in the year of our Lord 1573."
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Added by Lady Aimee Mack Source: http://www.naturalgeographicmagazine.com/q/Stradling_Baronets
2 CONT
2 CONT The Stradling Baronetcy, of St Donat's in the County of Glamorgan, was a title in the Baronetage of England. It was created on 22 May 1611 for John Stradling, later Member of Parliament for St Germans and Old Sarum and Glamorgan. 
2 CONC The second Baronet also represented Glamorgan in Parliament. The fifth Baronet was member of Parliament for Cardiff. The title became extinct on the death of the sixth Baronet in 1738.[1] George Stradling, younger son of the first
2 CONC  Baronet, was Dean of Chichester Cathedral in 1672. Edward Stradling, eldest son of the fifth Baronet, was Member of Parliament for Cardiff in 1722 but died during his father's lifetime. His younger brother Thomas succeeded in the
2 CONC  baronetcy. The Stradlings were a family seated at St Donat's Castle, Glamorgan, Wales, from the early mediaeval period. The family thus played an important role in Glamorgan's history. Sir Edward Stradling, knight (died 1453) mar
2 CONC ried Jane the bastard da. of Cardinal Beaufort. A later Sir Edward Stradling, knight(d.1609), collected a famous library at St. Donat's and from old papers he had collected wrote one of the first histories of Glamorgan, The Winnin
2 CONC g of the Lordship of Glamorgan out of Welshmens' Hands, thereby creating the legend of the Twelve Knights of Glamorgan, followers of Robert FitzHamon, Norman conqueror of Glamorgan. He placed a Stradling knight 12th in his list, y
2 CONC et recent scholarship has found the Stradling family to have come to Britain after the Norman Conquest, invalidating the inclusion of the now but legendary Stradling knight. The Stradlings are a branch of the noble family of Strät
2 CONC tligen. Their castle, now ruined, is located near Thun in Switzerland. Johannes and his son Peter came to Wales in the late thirteenth century, following Otto de Grandson. Stradling baronets, of St Donats (1611)[edit]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Stradling, 1st Baronet (1563–1637) Sir Edward Stradling, 2nd Baronet (1601–1644) Sir Edward Stradling, 3rd Baronet (c. 1624–c. 1660) Sir Edward Stradling, 4th Baronet (c. 1643–1685) Sir Edward Stradling, 5th Baronet (1672
2 CONC –1735) Sir Thomas Stradling, 6th Baronet (1710–1738) External links[edit]
