1 NOTE {geni:about_me} St Donat's Castle (Welsh: Castell Sain Dunwyd), St Donats, Wales,is a medieval castle in the Vale of Glamorgan, about 16 miles (26 km) to the west of Cardiff, and about 1 ⁄2 miles (2.4 km) to the west of Llantwit M
2 CONC ajor.  Positioned on cliffs overlooking the Bristol Channel , the site has been occupied since the Iron Age,and was by tradition the home of the Celtic chieftain Caradog.
2 CONT
2 CONT See Peter Bartrum, https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173426987955 Stradling 2 (May 5, 2024; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
