1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Roger Mervyn of St. Stephen's Parish, Ipswich, in the County of Suffolk was born certainly as early as 1430, since he left a son who was old enough to be his executor when he died in 1475.  His wife was Matilda____
2 CONC ________.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Mervyn, son of Roger, was apparently living in Ipswich when his father died.  As he as made executor of his father's will in 1475, we place his birth about 1453.  The date of his death is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Mervyn-24
2 CONT
2 CONT Will
2 CONT In Dei Nomine, Amen. I, Roger Mervyn, of Ipswich, on Sunday next after the Feast of the Nativity of the Blessed Virgin Mary, 1475, do make my Will as follows : -- To be buried in the Parish Church of St. Stephen's, Ipswich. To the
2 CONC  high altar of the said Church, for my tithes forgotten, iijs, iiijd.; for the repairs of the said Church, xxs.
2 CONT
2 CONT To Matilda, my wife, and John, my son, all my lands and tenements, and all my goods and chattels, movable and immovable, and all debts due me on condition that they pay all my debts. And I require all my feoffees who are enfeoffed
2 CONC  in all the said lands and tenements to deliver to the said Matilda and John, and their heirs, full seisin of the aforesaid lands and tenements. To fulfill this my present Will I make the said Matilda and John executors. In witnes
2 CONC s whereof, etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT Proved in the borough of Ipswich, [Suffolk,] 10 September, 1475, and administration of all the goods of the said deceased Roger was granted to the executors within written.
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT He is a possible brother to Robert Mervyn (b.c.1432), of Ipswich.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT ↑ Marvin, William T.R> The English Ancestry of Reinold and Matthew Marvin of Hartford, Ct., 1638: Their Homes and Parish Churches (Boston, 1900) p. 21.
