2 CONT *'''Walter Hungerford, 1st Baron Hungerford KG (1378–1449) was an English knight, landowner, from 1400 to 1414 Member of the House of Commons, of which he became Speaker, then was an Admiral and peer.
2 CONT *He won renown in .... etc.
2 CONT *Son and heir of Sir Thomas Hungerford, by his second wife, Joan, was strongly attached to the Lancastrian cause at the close of Richard II's reign, his father having been steward in John of Gaunt's household. On Henry IV's access
2 CONC ion he was granted an annuity of £40 out of the lands of Margaret, duchess of Norfolk, and was knighted.[1]
2 CONT *In October 1400 he was returned to parliament ....etc.
2 CONT *'''Hungerford married firstly Catherine (daughter of Sir Thomas Peverell of Parke and Hamatethy, Cornwall,[3] and Margaret Courtenay (1355–1422[citation needed]) daughter of Sir Thomas Courtenay (died 1356[citation needed]) of Wo
2 CONC odhuish, Devon[3]) with whom he had three sons and at least one daughter:
2 CONT ** Walter, who was made a prisoner of war in France in 1425, was ransomed by his father for three thousand marks, was in the retinue of the Duke of Bedford in France in 1435, and died without issue.[15]
2 CONT ** Robert, by whom he was succeeded.
2 CONT ** Edmund, who was knighted by Henry VI after the Battle of Verneuil on Whit-Sunday 1426,[16] and married Margaret, daughter and coheiress of Edward Burnell, by whom had two sons:
2 CONT *** Thomas, ancestor of the Hungerfords of Down Ampney, Gloucestershire, of the Hungerfords of Windrush, Oxfordshire, and the Hungerfords of Black Bourton, Oxfordshire.
2 CONT *** Edward, ancestor of the Hungerfords of Cadenham, Wiltshire.[17]
2 CONT **Elizabeth, who married Sir Philip Courtenay (1404–1463) of Powderham, grandson of Sir Philip Courtenay (1340–1406) of Powderham.[citation needed]
2 CONT *He married secondly Eleanor (died 1 August 1455), daughter of Sir John Berkeley of Beverstone and his second wife, Elizabeth Betteshorne,(and widow successively of John FitzAlan, 13th Earl of Arundel (died 21 April 1421), and Sir
2 CONC  Richard Poynings (died 10 June 1429)), with whom he had no children.[18][19] .... etc.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Hungerford,_1st_Baron_Hungerford ___________________
2 CONT *'''HUNGERFORD, Sir Walter (1378-1449), of Farleigh Hungerford, Som. and Heytesbury, Wilts.
2 CONT *b. 22 June 1378, o. surv. s. of Sir Thomas Hungerford* by his 2nd w. '''m. (1) between Oct. 1396 and May 1399, Katherine, yr. da. and coh. of Thomas Peverell† of Parke and Hamatethy, Cornw. by Margaret, da. and coh. of Sir Thomas
2 CONC  of Courtenay† Woodhuish, Devon, 4s. inc. Sir Edmund†, 2da'''; (2) by May 1439, Eleanor (d. 1 Aug. 1455), da. of Sir John Berkeley I* of Beverstone, Glos. by his 2nd w., wid. of John Arundel, Lord Mautravers (de jure earl of Arund
2 CONC el), and of Sir Richard Poynings. Kntd. 11 Oct. 1399; KG 3 May 1421; cr. Baron Hungerford Jan. 1426.
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1386-1421/member/hungerford-sir-walter-1378-1449 ________________________
2 CONT *[http://search.ancestry.com/search/DB.aspx?dbid=49030 Ancestral Roots of Certain American Colonists Who Came to America Before 1700]
