2 CONT ==Family notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife lived until 7 February 1478, surviving all her descendants, excepting a great-granddaughter, Mary Hastings, 4th Baroness Hungerford. Her long and interesting will, dated 8 August 1476, is printed in Nicolas's "Testamenta 
2 CONC Vetusta", pp. 310 sq., and in Hoare's "Modern Wiltshire, Hundred of Heytesbury". A list of the heavy expenses she incurred in ransoming her son Robert appears in Dugdale's 'Baronage,' ii. 204 sq.[2]
2 CONT
