1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Margaret Hungerford
2 CONT *'''F, b. circa 1412
2 CONT *Father Sir Walter Hungerford, 1st Baron Hungerford, Sheriff of Somersetshire & Dorsetshire, Speaker of the House of Commons, Lord High Treasurer b. c 22 Jun 1378, d. 9 Aug 1449 
2 CONT *Mother Katherine Peverell b. c 1394, d. a 12 Nov 1432 
2 CONT *'''     Margaret Hungerford was born circa 1412 at of Farleigh Hungerford, Somersetshire, England. She married Walter Rodney, son of Sir John Rodney, Sheriff of Somerset & Dorset and Alice, circa 1447.
2 CONT *'''Family Walter Rodney b. c 1399 
2 CONT *Child 
2 CONT **Thomas Rodney+1 b. c 1448, d. 1471
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S61] Unknown author, Family Group Sheets, SLC Archives.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1582.htm#i47568 ______________________
2 CONT *'''Margaret Hungerford1
2 CONT *F, #568504
2 CONT *Last Edited=13 Dec 2012
2 CONT *'''     Margaret Hungerford is the daughter of Sir Walter Hungerford, 1st Lord Hungerford and Katherine Peverell.2 She married Sir Walter Rodney.1
2 CONT *'''      Her married name became Rodney.
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S37] Volume 3, page 3476. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT * 2.[S37] See. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p56851.htm#i568504 ________________
2 CONT *'''Plantagenet ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=p_yzpuWi4sgC&pg=PA407&lpg=PA407&dq=Walter+Rodney+1400&source=bl&ots=RRsL5O03f7&sig=mkJm4UpDYdLs-ZlU_MBS50xpmzI&hl=en&ei=tvC-TcelAZG-sAODl4y_BQ&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=10&ved=0CEUQ6AEw
2 CONC CQ#v=onepage&q=Rodney&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 407
2 CONT *9. KATHERINE PEVERELL, younger daughter and co-heiress, born about 1394 (aged 28 in 1422). She married as his (1st wife) before Sept. 1400 WALTER HUNGERFORD, K.B., K.G., king's knight, Knight of the Shire for Wiltshire and for So
2 CONC merset, Speaker of the House of Commons, Sheriff of Somerset and Dorset, Steward of the Household to Kings Henry V and Henry VI, Constable of Windsor Castle, Lord High Treasurer of England, 4th but 1st surviving son and heir of Th
2 CONC omas Hungerford, Knt., of Farleigh and Wellow, Somerset, and Heytesbury, Wilts, Speaker of the House of Commons, Chief Stewart to John of Gaunt, Duke of Lancaster, by his 2nd wife, Joan, daughter and co-heiress of Edmund Hussey, K
2 CONC nt. He was born about 22 Jun 1378. They had four sons, Walter, Robert, Knt. [2nd Lord Hungerford], Edmund, Knt., and Thomas, and two daughters, '''Margaret (wife of Walter Rodney, Knt.)''' and Elizabeth. He was pre-eminently disti
2 CONC nguished in the French wars, for which he was granted the lordship of Hommet d'Arthenay in Normandy. He was one of the executors of King Henry V and served on the Council of Regency in 1422. He was summoned to Parliament from 7 Ja
2 CONC n. 1425/6 to 2 Jan. 1448/9, by writs directed Waltero Hungerford Chivaler, whereby he is held to have become Lord Hungerford. His wife, Katherine, was living 12 Nov. 1432. He married (2nd) before 8 May 1439 ELEANOR BERKELEY, widow
2 CONC  of John Arundel, K.B., Lord Arundel and Mautravers [see ARUNDEL 12], and Richard Poynings, Knt., of Poynings, Sussex [see POYNINGS 12], and daughter of John Berkeley, Knt., of Beverstone, Gloucestershire, by his 2nd wife, Elizabe
2 CONC th, daughter and heiress of John de Betteshorne, Knt., of Betteshorne (in Sopley), Wilts [see FISHER 9]. They had no issue. SIR WALTER HUNGERFORD, 1st Lord Hungerford, died testate 9 August 1449, and was buried with his 1st wife i
2 CONC n Salisbury Cathedral. His widow Eleanor, died testate 1 August 1455.  _____________________
2 CONT *'''Magna Carta ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=wHZcIRMhSEMC&pg=PA442&lpg=PA442&dq=Walter+Rodney+1400&source=bl&ots=2EwaxtZB5J&sig=erORFMUYHOiVYpKY7rsXWlT1d88&hl=en&ei=O_W-TdO6H4i8sAPel5zEBQ&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=3&ved=0CCIQ6AEwA
2 CONC jgK#v=onepage&q=rodney&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 442
2 CONT *8. KATHERINE PEVERELL, younger daughter and co-heiress, born about 1394 (aged 28 in 1422). She married as his (1st wife) before Sept. 1400 WALTER HUNGERFORD, K.B., K.G., of Farleigh Hungerford, Somerset, and Heytesbury, Wiltshire
2 CONC , and, in right of his wife, of South Cadbury, Somerset, king's knight, Knight of the Shire for Wiltshire and for Somerset, Speaker of the House of Commons, Sheriff of Somerset and Dorset, Steward of the Household to Kings Henry V
2 CONC  and Henry VI, Constable of Windsor Castle, Lord High Treasurer of England, 4th but 1st surviving son and heir of Thomas Hungerford, Knt., of Farleigh and Wellow, Somerset, and Heytesbury, Wilts, Speaker of the House of Commons, C
2 CONC hief Stewart to John of Gaunt, Duke of Lancaster, by his 2nd wife, Joan, daughter and co-heiress of Edmund Hussey, Knt. He was born about 22 Jun 1378. They had four sons, Walter, Robert, Knt. [2nd Lord Hungerford], Edmund, Knt., a
2 CONC nd Thomas, and two daughters, '''Margaret (wife of Walter Rodney, Knt.)''' and Elizabeth. He was pre-eminently distinguished in the French wars, for which he was granted the lordship of Hommet d'Arthenay in Normandy. He was one of
2 CONC  the executors of King Henry V and served on the Council of Regency in 1422. He was summoned to Parliament from 7 Jan. 1425/6 to 2 Jan. 1448/9, by writs directed Waltero Hungerford Chivaler, whereby he is held to have become Lord 
2 CONC Hungerford. His wife, Katherine, was living 12 Nov. 1432. He married (2nd) before 8 May 1439 ELEANOR BERKELEY, widow of John Arundel, K.B., Lord Arundel and Mautravers [see ARUNDEL 10], and Richard Poynings, Knt., of Poynings, Sus
2 CONC sex [see POYNINGS 9], and daughter of John Berkeley, Knt., of Beverstone, Gloucestershire, by his 2nd wife, Elizabeth, daughter and heiress of John de Betteshorne, Knt., of Betteshorne (in Sopley), Wilts [see FISHER 7]. They had n
2 CONC o issue. SIR WALTER HUNGERFORD, 1st Lord Hungerford, died testate 9 August 1449, and was buried with his 1st wife in Salisbury Cathedral. His widow Eleanor, died testate 1 August 1455.  _____________________
2 CONT *'''Margaret HUNGERFORD
2 CONT *'''Born: ABT 1413
2 CONT *Father: Walter HUNGERFORD (1º B. Hungerford of Farleigh)
2 CONT *Mother: Catherine PEVERELL
2 CONT *'''Married: Walter RODNEY (Sir)
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/HUNGERFORD.htm#Margaret HUNGERFORD1 ____________________
2 CONT *'''[Publications] - Somerset Record Society
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/details/somersetpub16someuoft
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/somersetpub16someuoft#page/186/mode/1up
2 CONT **	1459. ROBERT HUNGERFORD, KNT. 
2 CONT **	[17 STOKTON. FO. 133.] 
2 CONT *   22nd April, A.D. 1459. I, Robert Hungerford, knight, lord of Hungerford, of Heytesbury and of Hamelethe, make my will in this manner : --
2 CONT *   I bequeath my body to ecclesiastical burial before the altar of St. Osmund the Bishop and Confessor in the cathedral church of Salisbury. 
2 CONT *'''   Item, I bequeath to the Lady Margaret Rodney, my sister, one image of St. Mary of silver gilt, with my arms under (sub) the feet thereof. 
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/somersetpub16someuoft#page/193/mode/1up
2 CONT *   Proved 7th July, 1459, and administration committed to Dame Margaret, relict of the deceased, and to John Merevyn, esquire, executors named, with power reserved for committing administration, &c.  _____________________________
2 CONC _
