2 CONT *George Manners, 11th Baron de Ros of Helmsley (c. 1470 – 27 October 1513) was an English peer. .... etc.
2 CONT *George Manners and Anne St. Leger had five sons and six daughters:[10]
2 CONT **Thomas Manners, 1st Earl of Rutland, who married Eleanor Paston, credited with saying to Anne of Cleves, 'Madam there must be more to it than that, or it will be long before we have a Duke of York which all this realm much desir
2 CONC eth'.[citation needed] Their son, Henry Manners, 2nd Earl of Rutland, married Margaret Neville, daughter of Ralph Neville, 4th Earl of Westmorland by Katherine Stafford.
2 CONT **Oliver Manners.
2 CONT **Anthony Manners.
2 CONT **Sir Richard Manners.
2 CONT **John Manners.
2 CONT **Anne Manners, who married Sir Henry Capell.
2 CONT **Eleanor Manners, who married John Bourchier, 2nd Earl of Bath.
2 CONT **Elizabeth Manners, who married Thomas Sandys, 2nd Baron Sandys.
2 CONT **Katherine Manners, who married Sir Robert Constable.
2 CONT **Cecily Manners.
2 CONT **'''Margaret Manners, who married firstly, Sir Henry Strangeways''', and secondly, Robert Heneage.
2 CONT *His monument, consisting of a grand chest tomb with sculpted effigies of himself and his wife, .... etc.
