1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Reverend '''Zechariah Symmes''', son of William Symmes (1570-1627)  & Mary Ingleram (1577-1599), was born on 5 Apr 1599 in Canterbury, Kent, England; died on 4 Feb 1671 in Charlestown, Suffolk, Massachusetts.  Immigrant from Dunst
2 CONC able, Bedford to Boston, MA 1634 on the ''Griffin''.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The Reverend Zechariah Symmes was one of the most important clergymen in the early Massachusetts Bay Colony, his virtues and those of his wife being lengthily extolled by Cotton Mather in his Magnalia. Symmes was educated at Emman
2 CONC uel College, Cambridge--that hotbed of Puritanism--and graduated in 1620. He was a lecturer at St. Anthony's in London, but he moved to Dunstable in Bedfordshire to escape persecution. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He arrived in Boston on Sep 18, 1634, on board the Griffin, with two hundred other passengers including William and Anne Hutchinson, at whose trial he would testify, and the Reverend John Lothrop.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 
2 CONT # Sarah Baker on 13 Aug 1622 in Southwark, Surrey, England. She was born 1604 in Canterbury, Kent, England; died on 10 Jun 1673 in Charlestown, Suffolk, Massachusetts. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Known children are:   
2 CONT # John Symmes 
2 CONT # Rebecca Symmes 1622 – 
2 CONT # Son Symmes 1623 –  TWIN 
2 CONT # Zechariah Symmes 1623 –  TWIN 
2 CONT # Sarah Symmes 1625 – 1681 
