1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hodges-32
2 CONT
2 CONT William Hodges aka Hedges
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1624 in Kent, England [uncertain]
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of William Hodges and Alice (Symes) Hodges
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Mary (Andrews) Pitts — married 1648 in Taunton, Bristol, Massachusetts Bay, British Colonial America
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of John Hodges and Henry Hodges
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 2 Apr 1654 in Taunton, Bristol, Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 1 Feb 2020 | Created 30 Aug 2010
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT William Hodges was born around 1624. He was born in Kent, England[1]He was baptized on 21 Mar 1624 at East Greenwich, Kent, England
2 CONT
2 CONT He may have been the "William Hedges" appointed on the jury at the Court held in Salem on March 27, 1638, although this may have been William Hedge of Lynn.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT William went to Taunton shortly after it was purchased by the first proprietors. He was in the second list of early settlers compiled by the town clerk, John Wilbore. He was in the list of males in Taunton able to bear arms in 164
2 CONC 3.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT On March 24, 1644, the town voted "that sufficient carte-way be made from the houses into the woods behind the ground of William Hodges, William Evans and Aaron Knapp, where it is most convenient."[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT William married Mary Andrews around 1648/1649 in Taunton.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT William was one of the original stockholders of the first Taunton Iron Works, subscribing £20 for a whole share.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT William Hodges died April 2, 1654, in Taunton, Plymouth Colony. He seems to have held considerable property and probably was comparatively young when he died.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 1.3 1.4 1.5 Hodges Page 71. ↑ Date based on birth date of first child.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hodges: Hodges, Almon D., Jr. Genealogical Record of the Hodges Family of New England, Third Edition, Frank H. Hodges, Boston, 1896 On Archive.org Abridgement of the Genealogical Record of The Hodges Family of New England, ending 
2 CONC December 21, 1954, Compiled by George F Hodges and other members of the Family, page 17. Appears without publishing information, printed sometime after 20 Jan 1956, the last date in the book. (T. H. Bredehoft, private library coll
2 CONC ection) No. 43 of 200 printed. https://archive.org/details/genealogicalreco00hodg/page/70
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~dearbornboutwell/fam7456.html New England Marriages Prior to 1700, by Clarence Almon Torrey (Boston, Massachusetts: New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2011) Vol. II, p. 770. HODGES/
2 CONC HEDGES, William (-1654 & Mary ANDREWS, m/2 Peter PITTS 1654?; ca 1648; Taunton (Pope's Pioneers has Hedges) {Taunton 1:30, 89; Reg. 5:259 has Hedges, 261, 4145, 51:455, 52:16; Hodges 11+; Babbitt 30; Fulton Anc. 248; Kendall Anc. 
2 CONC (ms) 20; Gardner (1915) 15; Shurtleff 145; Williams (#16) 98, 132; Bowen 179; Munsey-Hopkins 179; Sv. 1:53; Bassett-Preston 7; Pope's Pioneers; MD 11:152, 12:243; McCormick-Hamilton 469} Kent, England, Tyler Index to Parish Regist
2 CONC ers, 1538-1874 [S00132] Find-A-Grave. "William Hodges Birth: 1589, Kent, England; Death: Apr. 2, 1654,Taunton, Bristol County, Massachusetts William Hodges went from Salem to Taunton, soon after the latter town was purchased and i
2 CONC s on the second list of early settlers of Taunton. Spouse: Mary Andrews Pitts (1593 - ____)* Children: Joan Hodges Kent (1615 - 1699)* Burial: Unknown Created by: Robert DeVowe, Record added: Mar 10, 2014, Find A Grave Memorial# 1
2 CONC 26170395"
2 CONT
2 CONT "Mary Andrews Pitts Birth: 1593; Kent, England; Death: unknown 1654/55 March 15, On the same date when her mother's will was proved in Plymouth Colony, (Bristol Co was not organized until 1685), Mary (Andrews) Hedges came into cou
2 CONC rt to testify as to the correctness of the Inventory made 15 May 1654 of the Estate of her husband William Hedges of Taunton, dec'd on 2 Apr 1653/4. Mary Hodges' appearance was occasioned by her intended remarriage to Peter Pitts.
2 CONC  Spouse: William Hodges (1589 - 1654) Children: Joan Hodges Kent (1615 - 1699)* Burial: Unknown Created by: Robert DeVowe, Record added: Mar 10, 2014, Find A Grave Memorial# 126170456"
2 CONT
2 CONT [S00165] New England Marriages Prior to 1700. "Hodges/Hedges, William (-1654) & Mary Andrews, m/2 Peter Pitts 1654?; ca 1648; Tauton" [If web 1648, then not Joanna's mother as she was born 1621.]
2 CONT
