1 NAME Joan /Hadley/
2 GIVN Joan
2 SURN Hadley
2 _MARNM Hill
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1538
2 ADDR
3 CITY Woverly
3 STAE Worcestershire
3 CTRY England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1610
2 PLAC St Bridge
2 ADDR
3 ADR1 Fleet Street
3 CITY London
3 STAE England
3 CTRY UK
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Joane-Corke/6000000186924096835
2 CONT
2 CONT Not the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Hadley/6000000007535838797?through=6000000001986178053
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hill met and, in January 1558, married "Lady" Joane Hadley who was from the manor at Wolverley, a village in Worcestershire, over 100 miles northeast of Somerset. She must have inherited the property for John moved to Wolverl
2 CONC ey, the only of his immediate family to leave Somerset.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born of a Somerset (SW England) family, Edward Hill's father, John (Johan) Hill, married Joane Hadley of Wolverley, Worcestershire; they lived in the Midlands (Wolverley, Worcestershire), where the English Industrial Revolution be
2 CONC gan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward married "Elizabeth [Last-name Unknown]," a local girl, in 1579 and their daughter, Judith / Eydeth was born in December 1583 in Wolverley, Worcestershire. She married Justinian (John) Snow. Some say she died in England; oth
2 CONC ers say she emigrated to Maryland, following her son and daughter and died there in 1649.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
