2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT "The questionable supplementary content included in the 1872 publication of the 1620 Devon Visitation.  Margaret and probably also Jane being additional daughters, I suspect, of Thomas Cole and his wife Joane Hill.  Not daughters 
2 CONC of Thomasine, which this suggests.  I believe the connecting lines have been misdrawn and it is a simple transcription error".
2 CONT
2 CONT Supporting this statement above: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. See Fursland extract which says Margaret Cole wife of John Fursland is the daughter of Thomas Cole of Slade.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Devon, a son and heir, Thomas, who married, first, Joan, daughter of William Stourton, esq., and having no issue by her he married, secondly, Joane, daughter and heiress to John Hill of Buckland Touzsaints, in the county of Dev
2 CONC on, esq., and died 31 January 1541 (32 Henry VIII.) leaving three daughters, and three sons. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Margaret = Thomas Southcote, of Southcote and = John Fursland of Bickington 2. Joane = Hugh Hill of Heath, = Eobert Dowrish of Heath -  Barton  3. Thomasine = Sir Eoger Grenville, Esq  4. William= Elizabeth Champernon of Mowbur
2 CONC y 5. Richard = Alice Greenfield alias Grenville of Exeter 6. Robert = John  Evelyn of Kingston Upon Thames 7. Jane? = 
2 CONT
2 CONT I believe Jane is questionable in the Cole family tree she could be Joane. The supplement is not signed by the head of the family.
2 CONT
