2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/Bios/RichardGrenville.htm _______________
2 CONT *Sir Richard Grenville (15 June 1542 – 10 September 1591) (alias Greynvile, Greeneville, Greenfield etc.) lord of the manors of Stowe, Kilkhampton in Cornwall and of Bideford in Devon, was an English sailor who as captain of the R
2 CONC evenge, died at the Battle of Flores (1591), fighting heroically against overwhelming odds, and refusing to surrender his ship to the far more numerous Spanish. .... etc.
2 CONT *Richard Grenville was the '''eldest son and heir of Sir Roger Grenville''' (d.1545), who was captain of the Mary Rose when it sank in Portsmouth Harbour in 1545, '''by his wife Thomasine Cole''', daughter of Thomas Cole of Slade.
2 CONC [1] '''Thomasine survived her husband and remarried to Thomas Arundell.'''[1] The ancient Grenville family were lords of the manors of Bideford in Devon and of Stowe, Kilkhampton in Cornwall. He was a cousin of Sir Walter Raleigh 
2 CONC and the privateer and explorer Humphrey Gilbert.
2 CONT *Grenville's birthplace is believed to have been at Bideford. His father (who had pre-deceased his own father Sir Richard Grenville (c.1495-1550), MP for Cornwall in 1529[2]) died when he was an infant, aged 3, and '''his mother r
2 CONC emarried to Thomas Arundell of Clifton Arundell House''', where Grenville spent much of his childhood. At age 17 Grenville began law studies at the Inner Temple.
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *In 1565 Grenville married Mary St Leger (c.1543-1623), daughter of Sir John St Ledger of Annery, Monkleigh, near Bideford, and heir to her brother. She outlived her husband and died aged about 80 on 9 November 1623 and was buried
2 CONC  at St Mary's Church, Bideford. The family initially lived at Buckland Abbey before moving to a newly built house at Bideford. They had 4 sons, including Bernard Grenville.[4]
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Grenville ________________________________________
2 CONT *GRENVILLE, Richard II (c.1542-91), of Stowe in Kilkhampton, Cornw. and Buckland Abbey, Devon.
2 CONT *b. c.1542, '''1st s. of Roger Grenville by Thomasine, da.''' of Thomas Cole of Slade. educ. M. Temple 1559. m. c.1565, Mary, da. of Sir John St. Leger of Annery, Devon, 4s. inc. Bernard 3da. suc. fa. 1545. Kntd. 1577.
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/grenville-richard-ii-1542-91 _______________
