1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''The Visitations of the County of Devon: Comprising ..., Volume 1, Pages 1-452      edited by John Lambrick Vivian
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=GmqlIibS95IC&pg=PA721&lpg=PA721&dq=John+Affeton+1467&source=bl&ots=whHzN1T59P&sig=JK0PGjYO2QMFN8xcLw9t13hbOcM&hl=en&ei=b2rwTY2cBJGisQPhg_ShDg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=3&ved=0CCIQ6AEwA
2 CONC jhG#v=onepage&q=COLE&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.213
2 CONT **	COLE OF SLADE.
2 CONT *William Cole of Hittislegh, co. Devon, living 1243. = ; ch: Roger Cole
2 CONT **Roger Cole of Coleton, 25 Edw. I. ; ch: Roger, William (2 son.) Cole
2 CONT ***Roger Cole, son and heir. = ; ch: John Cole of Tamer
2 CONT ****John Cole of Tamer, son and heir, a Man at Arms. = ; ch: Sir John (m. Anne Bodrugan) Cole
2 CONT *****Sir John Cole, Kt., of Mythway in the parish of Brixham, knighted in France 25 July 1380 by the Lord Deputy. = Anne, da. and h. of Sir Nicholas Bodrugan, Kt. ; ch: William (m. Margaret Beaupell) Cole
2 CONT ******William Cole of Tamer, son and heir. = Margaret, da. of Sir Henry Beaupell, Kt. ; ch: Sir John (m. Agnes Fitzwarine) Cole
2 CONT *******Sir John Cole, Kt., present at the battle of Agincourt, 1514. = Agnes, da. of Sir ... Fitzwarine, Kt. ; ch: Adam (m. Elizabeth Weston), John (m. Jane Meriet), William (3 son.), Robert (4 son.) Cole
2 CONT ********Sir Adam Cole, son and heir. = Elizabeth, da. of Sir Richard Weston, Kt.
2 CONT ********John Cole of Slade, 2 son. = Jane, da. of Robert Meriet of Devon. ; ch: Symon (m. Alice Lure) Cole
2 CONT ********* Symon Cole of Slade in Devon, d. 1497. = Alice da. & coh. of ... Lure in Devon, Gent. ; ch: John (m. Thomasine Walcott), Joane (m. William Hele) Cole
2 CONT **********Joane, wife of 2 William Hele of Devon.
2 CONT **********John Cole of Slade, eldest son, d. 21 Nov. 1543, and named as deceased in the Inq. taken on the death of his grandson William. = Thomasine da. & h. of 1 Thomas Walcott of Devon, named in the Inq. taken on the death of he
2 CONC r grandson William, living at Buckish 1547. ; ch: Thomas (m. Joan Stourton & Joane Hill) Cole
2 CONT ***********Thomas Cole of Slade, d. 31 Jan. 1541, and named as deceased in the Inq. taken on the death of his son William. = Joan, da. of William Stourton, 1 wife, d. s.p. ; = Joane da. & h. of John Hill of Buckland, Co. Devon, 2 
2 CONC wife, named in the Inq. taken on the death of her son William, living 1547, remar. William Burgoyne, heir to her mother, aged 50 years and over 2 Edw. VI. ; ch: Joane (m. Hugh Hill & Robert Dowish), Margaret (m. Thomas Southcott &
2 CONC  John Fursland Cole, A (Pg.214 '''Robert Cole (3 sonne B Vide page 215)''', Richard (m. Alice Greenevile), Thomasine (m. Roger Greeneville & Thomas Arundell), William (m. Elizabeth Champernown) Cole)
2 CONT *Pg.214
2 CONT *A
2 CONT *Thomasine. = Roger Greeneville of Stowe in Corn. ; ch: Sir Richard Grenvile of Stowe ; = Thomas Arundell of Clifton in Corn. ; ch: Jane, Margaret Arundelll
2 CONT *Richard Cole of Buckland, 2 son, d. at Buckland Toutsaints 5 Feb 1573, Inq. p.m. 20 Eliz., pt. 1, No. 29. = Alice, da. of John Greenevile of Exeter, Esq. ; ch: John (m. Katherine Hele) Cole
2 CONT **     .... etc.
2 CONT *William Cole of Slade in Devon, eldest sonne, d. 23 Ap. 1547. Inq. p.m. W. & L., 1 Edw. VI, vol. iii, p 75. = Elizabeth, eldest da. of Sir Philip Champernown of Modbury, Kt., mar. at Modbury, named in the Inq. taken on her husban
2 CONC d's death, remar.  .... Pollard. Will 26 July 1567, pro. 13 May 1574, P.C.C. (Martyn 22). ; ch: Philip (m. Jane Williams) Cole.
2 CONT ** .... etc.
2 CONT *Pg.215
2 CONT *B
2 CONT *'''Robert Cole of Heston, co. Middlesex, 3 sonne of Thomas Cole of Slade. = ... da. of John Evelyn of Kingston on Thames, co. Surrey. ;''' ch: George (m. Frances Preston) Cole.
2 CONT ** .... etc. ____________________
2 CONT *'''The visitation of the county of Devon in the year 1620 Volume 6.      by Colby, Frederic Thomas
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/visitationofcoun06colbrich
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/visitationofcoun06colbrich#page/339/mode/1up
2 CONT **	COLE.—(Supp.)
2 CONT *Symon Cole of Slade in Devon = Alice d. & coh. of Lure of Devon gent. ; ch: John (m. Thomazine Mattcott), Joane (m. W. Hele of Devon) Cole.
2 CONT **John Cole of slade, 1 s. = Thomazine d. & h. of Mattcott of Devon ; ch: Thomas (m. Joane Hill) Cole
2 CONT ***Thomas Cole of Slade = Joane d. & h. of John Hill of Buckland co. Devon ; ch: '''Robert (, 3)''' Will. (of Slade, 1 s.), Thomazine (m. Roger Grenvile & Thomas Arundell), Richard (m. Alice Greenvile) Cole
2 CONT ****Thomazine = Roger Grenvile of Stowe Cornw., 1 husb. ; ch: ? ; = Thomas Arundell of Clifton in Cornw. ; ch: Jane, Margaret Arundell
2 CONT ****Richard Cole of Buckland = Alice d. of John Greenvile of Exeter Esq. ; ch: John Cole ____________________
2 CONT *'''The Genealogy of the Family of Cole, of the County of Devon: Of the County of Devon, and of ...     by JAMES. EDWIN-COLE
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/genealogyfamily00edwigoog
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/genealogyfamily00edwigoog#page/n15/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.2
2 CONT *1 WILLIAM COLE, of Hutenesleigh (now called Hittisleigh) in the county of Devon, living in the year 1243, whose son and heir 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/genealogyfamily00edwigoog#page/n16/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.3
2 CONT *2 ROGER COLE,* had "his dwelling at Coleton," in Chumleigh, and also held, in 27 Henry III., Hantesford, in that parish.† In 25th of Edward I. he was "returned from the county of Cornwall as holding lands or rents to the amount o
2 CONC f £20 yearly value and upwards, either in Capite or otherwise, and as such summoned under the general writ to muster at London, on Sunday next after the Octaves of St. John the Baptist (7 July, 1297), to perform Military Service i
2 CONC n person with horses and arms, &c., in parts beyond the Seas ;" ‡ and also again summoned with his son William§ to muster at Berwick-on-Tweed, on the nativity of St. John the Baptist, to perform service against the Scots in 1301. 
2 CONC He was father of 
2 CONT *3 ROGER (of whom immediately), and of the above-named William, who probably perished in this expedition, as there is no further trace of him ; and perhaps his early death may account for the omission of his name in the family ped
2 CONC igree drawn up, in July 1630, by Sir William Segar, Garter, King-at-Arms. 
2 CONT *3 ROGER was heir to his father Roger, and lived in the reign of Edward II. ; his son and heir was 
2 CONT *4 JOHN COLE, of the counties of Devon and Cornwall, who, in 1324, was described as "John Cole de Tamer, Man-at-Arms, || and 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/genealogyfamily00edwigoog#page/n17/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.4
2 CONT *returned by the Sheriff of the county of Devon, pursuant to Writ tested at Westminster, 9 May, as summoned by proclamation to attend the Great Council at Westminster, on Wednesday after Ascension Day, 30 May, 17 Edward II." In th
2 CONC e 9th of Edward III (1335) he had free warren in Tamer, Lydeston, Hokesbere, and Hutenesleigh in the county of Devon, and in Rispernatt ;* and it appears by a Fine of 15 Edward III. (1341) that he was possessed of the manors of Re
