1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Dates showing as same as https://www.geni.com/people/Dionise-Brandbridge/6000000209661208844 (1497-1560). Removed. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bowerman-676
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Dionis was the daughter of John Bowerman and Johanna Kirkham. She passed away after 1570 when she is named (as "my sister Dionise Bond, widow) in the Will of her brother, William Bowerman, subdean of Wells. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT >"At West Buckland, Somerset, not far from Hache Beauchamp, was seated in the reign of Henry VIII., a William Bond, who, according to the old pedigree above mentioned, represented a younger branch of the Bonds of Hache Beauchamp, 
2 CONC and was nearly allied to those of Dorsetshire. He is described in a MS. pedigree in the College of Arms, as "ex vetustissima Bondurum stirpe in provincia Cornubiae oriundus." <BR>
2 CONT
2 CONT > He d. in 1549, leaving by Dionese his wife, dau. of John Bourman, of Hemyoke, Devon, son of Nicholas Bourman, by Elizabeth, sister of John Russell, 1st Earl of Bedford,  [''her father’s parents are disputed''] 
2 CONT *1. William Bond, of Crosby Place London, Alderman and Sheriff of that city, d. 1576, and to whom and his son, Martin Bond there are interesting monuments in the church of Great St. Helen's Bishopsgate Street." [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Named in the Will of her brother William Bowerman, 1570.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT William Bond of Buckland, Somerset (d 1549)
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation (London, 1664, Bond) identifies William's wife as _ Hill but BLG1886 (Bond of Creech Grange), in a note, identifies her as ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Dionese Bourman (dau of John Bourman of Hemyoke, [son of Nicholas by Elizabeth, sister of John Russell, 1st Earl of Bedford)] ''[parentage of John Bourman is unknown, not Nicholas & Elizabeth]
2 CONT ''
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From ''A Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Extinct and Dormant Baronetcies'' ... By John Burke, Bernard Burke, (1841) p. 70 < [https://books.google.ca/books?id=zs2YIGYcFYMC&newbks=0&lpg=PA70&dq=%22william%20bond%22%20AND%20
2 CONC buckland&pg=PA70#v=onepage&q=%22william%20bond%22%20AND%20buckland&f=false GoogleBooks] > (names wife as __ Hill)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 sons, 4 daughters
2 CONT
2 CONT Sons:
2 CONT # William, of Crosby Palace, a merchant adventurer.  Married Margaret Aldy.  4 sons, 1 daughter.
2 CONT # Edward, m. and  had issue.
2 CONT # George (Sir), married Winifred Leigh
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughters;
2 CONT #Katherine, m. Palmer, of Trull
2 CONT # Avis, m. Otte Wescombe
2 CONT # Ann, m. to William Gifford 
2 CONT # Agnes, m. to __ Cade.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000221252503843&size=large}}
