2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bond-521
2 CONT
2 CONT “At West Buckland, Somerset, not far from Hache Beauchamp, was seated in the reign of Henry VIII., a William Bond, who, according to the old pedigree above mentioned, represented a younger branch of the Bonds of Hace Beauchamp, an
2 CONC d was nearly allied to those of Dorsetshire. He is described in a MS. pedigree in the College of Arms, as “ex vetustissima Bondorum stirpe in provincia Cornubiae oriundus.” 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Bond_(mayor) Wikipedia - George Bond (mayor)]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir George Bond''' (died 1592) was 
2 CONT * a 16th-century English politician who served as Lord Mayor of London in 1587/8.[1] 
2 CONT * A native of Somerset, 
2 CONT * he was the younger son of William Bond of Buckland and younger brother of William Bond, alderman and Sheriff of London.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From < [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/bb4fz/bond01.php Stirnet: Bond01] >
2 CONT
2 CONT Commoners reports that, said to have descended from "a Norman, who came in at the Conquest, and married the daughter and heiress of Bond, of Penryn, in Cornwall" (## see here ##), which Bond (or Bondi) was perhaps the one who "app
2 CONC ears to have been a Saxon", was ancestor of ...
2 CONT *Robert Bond of Earth, St. Stephens
2 CONT **1.	Thomas Bond (dspm)
2 CONT **2.	Robert Bond of Beauchamp's Hache, Somerset (a 1431)	Commoners reports that Robert obtained Lutton (Isle of Purbeck, Dorset) through his marriage with its heiress. However, BLG1952, which starts with this Robert, suggests that
2 CONC  Lutton came into this family when his grandson William purchased that estate in 1510. [disputed as son of Robert] 
2 CONT ***	A.	Robert Bond of Beauchamp's Hache 	m. (1453) Mary Hody (dau of Sir John Hody of Pillesdon, Lord Chief Justice)
2 CONT ***B.	William Bond of Buckland, Somerset (d 1549) This connection is given in Commoners but BLG1952 does not mention William at all whilst BEB1841 (Bond of Peckham) merely reports that William was "descended of a younger house of 
2 CONC Bond, of Cornwall." 	m. _ Hill or Dionese Bourman
2 CONT
2 CONT From < [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/bb4fz/bond03.php Stirnet: Bond03] >
2 CONT
2 CONT *William Bond of Buckland, Somerset (d 1549) Visitation (London, 1664, Bond) identifies William's wife as _ Hill but BLG1886 (Bond of Creech Grange), in a note, identifies her as ... m. Dionese Bourman (dau of John Bourman of Hemy
2 CONC oke, son of Nicholas by Elizabeth, sister of John Russell, 1st Earl of Bedford)
2 CONT ** 1.	William Bond of Crosby Palace (London), Sheriff of London (d 30.05.1576)	m. Margaret Aldy (bur 23.05.1588, dau of William Aldy of Guildford)
2 CONT ***  	A.	Sir Daniel Bond of Crosby Palace (bur 06.03.1586-7) m. (02.03.1579-80) Jane Walker
2 CONT *** B.	William Bond of London (bur 10.02.1608-9, haberdasher)	m. (13.04.1580) Margaret Gore (dau of Thomas Gore of London)
2 CONT ****	i.	Ann Bond (bpt 03.07.1588, a 1608) 	m. John Mannying of London (a 1608)
2 CONT ****  	ii.	Elizabeth Bond (bpt 23.11.1589, d 24.11.1619)	m. (22.06.1609) Henry Andowes (d 1638, Alderman of London)
2 CONT ****  	iii.+	other issue - Gore (bur 02.01.1623-4), William (b c1603, bur 21.09.1671), Mary (a 1608)
2 CONT *** C.	Anne Bond (d 09.10.1615) m1. Robert King m2. William Whitmore of Hackney (d 08.08.1593)
2 CONT ***  	D.+	other issue - Martin (b c1559, bur 11.05.1643/5), Nicholas (bur 03.02.1590/1)
2 CONT **2.	Edward Bond had issue
2 CONT ** 3.	Sir George Bond, Lord Mayor of London (d 03/4.1592)  	m. Winifred Leigh (d 1621, dau of Sir Thomas Leigh, Lord Mayor of London)
2 CONT *** A.	Sir William Bond of Highgate (bpt 29.06.1567, d 1617, alderman of London)	m. Catherine Povey (bur 21.11.1613, dau of John Povey of Barnard's Inn, Holborn)
2 CONT ***	B.	George Bond of Bridgewater	m. Gertrude Saunders (dau of William Saunders)
2 CONT ****  	i.	Mary Bond	m. Richard Musgrave of Nettlecomb
2 CONT ***  	C.	Sir Thomas Bond of Ogborn St. George	m. Frances Bale (dau of Edmund Bale of Soddington)
