2 CONT *ROGER LEIGH, of Wellington, in Shropshire and Rushall, in the county of Stafford. This gentleman had issue, . . . . 
2 CONT *And a younger son,
2 CONT **  THOMAS LEIGH, who was brought up under Sir Rowland Hill, a rich merchant of London, and Lord Mayor of that city; by whom, for his knowledge and industry, he was made his factor beyond sea; and in that trust deporting himself w
2 CONC ith the highest integrity, Sir Rowland bestowed upon him the hand of his favourite niece, Alice, daughter of John Barker, alias Coverall, of Wolverton, in the county of Salop, by Elizabeth, his wife, daughter of Thomas Hill, and u
2 CONC pon the issue of the marriage he entailed the greater part of his estate. Thomas Leigh subsequently served the office of Sheriff of London, and was Lord Mayor at the death of Queen Mary. He was knighted during his mayoralty, and d
2 CONC ying in 1571, was buried in Mercer's Chapel, London, with this epitaph upon is tomb:	. . . . 
2 CONT **   His widow lived at Stoneleigh to a very advanced age, having seen her chiildren's children to the fourth generation. She died in 1603, and was buried at Stoneleigh, where she had founded an hospital for five poor men, and fiv
2 CONC e poor women, all of them to be unmarried persons, and nominated after her decease by Sir Thomas Leigh, her son, and his heirs for ever. Sir Thomas Leigh had issue by this lady,
2 CONT ***	ROWLAND, who was largely provided for at Longborough, in Gloucestershire, by Sir Rowland Hill, his godfather. He m. first Margery, daughter of Thomas Lawe, of London, vintner, and secondly, __, daughter of Sir Richard Berkeley
2 CONC , Knt., of Stoke-Gifford, in Gloucestershire.
2 CONT ***	Richard, died s. p.
2 CONT ***	THOMAS, of whom presently.
2 CONT ***	William (Sir), of Newnham-Regis, in Warwickshire, who m. Frances, dauther of Sir James Harrington, of Exton, in Rutlandshire, and left a son, . . . . 
2 CONT ***	Mary, m. first, to Robert Andrews, of London and secondly, to __ Cobb.
2 CONT ***'''	Alice, m. to Thomas Connye, of Lincolnshire.
2 CONT ***	Katherine, m. Edward Barber, of Somersetshire, Serjeant at Law.
2 CONT ***	Winifred, m. Sir George Bond, Lord Mayor of London.
2 CONT **The second surviving son,
2 CONT ***  THOMAS LEIGH, was knighted by Queen Elizabeth, and created a baronet, upon the institution of that order, 29th June, 1611. Sir Thomas m. Catherine, fourth daughter of Sir John Spencer, Knt., of Wormleighton, in the county of 
2 CONC Warwick, and had issue,
2 CONT *_________________
2 CONT *'''Alice Leigh1
2 CONT *'''F, b. circa 1537, d. before 1621
2 CONT *Father Thomas Leigh1 b. c 1515, d. 17 Nov 1572 
2 CONT *Mother Alice Barker1 b. c 1518, d. 1600 
2 CONT *'''     Alice Leigh was born circa 1537 at of Stoneleigh, Warwickshire, England.1 She married Thomas Cony, son of Richard Coney and Jane Ellis, on 6 November 1554 at St. Olave, Old Jewry, London, Middlesex, England.1 Alice Leigh 
2 CONC died before 1621 at Bassingthorpe, Lincolnshire, England.1
2 CONT *'''Family Thomas Cony b. c 1529, d. 15 Oct 1611 
2 CONT *Child 
2 CONT **Susan Cony+1 b. 1 May 1568
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S61] Unknown author, Family Group Sheets, SLC Archives.
