1 NAME George /Hale/
2 GIVN George
2 SURN Hale
2 _MARNM Hale
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 13 JUL 1601
2 ADDR
3 STAE England
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.familysearch.org/tree/pedigree/landscape/K2J5-7RR
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Evidence needed to support the claim he is the same as https://www.geni.com/people/George-Hale-of-Northumberland-County/6000000003051227815
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William Hale and wife Rose Bond:
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.  George Hale, c. 13 Jul 1601, Herefordshire,England
2 CONT
2 CONT George was an indentured servant. He married a young woman of English blood in 1626
2 CONT
2 CONT George Hale, son of William Hale, Esq., of King's Walden, and wife Rose Bond, was born July 13, 1601 in Hertfordshire, England. Many believe that he was the original Hale or Hale emigrant to Virginia. This is not well proven, but 
2 CONC more information is below. Those who do not believe that this is the emigrant point out that this George was the son of a well-to-do landowner from Hertfordshire and the emigrant was an indentured servant. Also, George the emigran
2 CONC t is believed to be from Kent, not from Hertfordshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT See also: The New England Historical and Genealogical Register, Volume 35 (available as Google e-book)
2 CONT ==========
2 CONT George Hale (or Haile) left Bristol, England on the ship "Supply" and arrived in "James Cittie" (Jamestown), Virginia in 1620. George was an indentured servant. He married a young woman of English blood in 1626 and had a son, Nich
2 CONC olas, in 1628. Grandson Nicholas went to Baltimore with his sister Mary (Heale) King after Nicholas' death in 1671.
2 CONT <http://www.geocities.com/awoodlief/hale.html>
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas was born in 1628 near Elizabeth City VA. His father was George Hale who sailed from Bristol Eng. in 1620 on the Supply and is listed as "George Hale, a drummer, age 18 years." He landed at Elizabeth City in the fall and l
2 CONC ived with Sir Wyatt Governor of the colony. George was born in 1601 at Kings Walden, Hertfordshire,England at the Hale Manor House (which they owned 1575-1898).
2 CONT
2 CONT His father was William, son of Richard (1536-1620), whose father was Thomas of Codicote , whose father was Edward Hales, whose father was Gilbert Hales, whose father was Henry Hales , whose father was Thomas Hales , whose father w
2 CONC as Nicholas Hales, whose father was Nicholas Hales of Hales Place Halden in the County of Kent, England. [hmmm--there had to be some mothers in there too!]
2 CONT
2 CONT George Haile's wife was named Elizabeth. They had three sons; Francis, Nicholas and Thomas. Francis was the father of Capt. Richard Haile of his majesty's Dragoons and his wife was named Jane; Richard m. Mary, fathered John Haiale
2 CONC  of South Farnham Parrish in Essex County. The children of John Haile and Mary Fullerton are john, Francis (--d. Bedford, 1780, m. Adara Meador), Thomas, Benjamin, Mary, and Susanna. [buffalojwh@aol.com <mailto:buffalojwh@aol.com>
2 CONC ].
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestors beyond this individual may not be accurate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Updated from WikiTree Genealogy <http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Haile-25> via wife Mary Elizabeth Haile <http://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000003051212185> by SmartCopy <http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783>: Jul 24 2015
2 CONC , 17:54:16 UTC [1] added 18 May 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Re: George Haile (Hall, Hale, Heale) d. aft. 6/22/1652 Posted by: Jared Hale <EDGAR9779@GMAIL.COM>(ID *****9651) Date: January 22, 2011 at 21:41:58 In Reply to: George Haile (Hall, Hale, Heale) d. aft. 6/22/1652 by William Culverh
2 CONC ouse of 623
2 CONT
2 CONT The only information I have is:
2 CONT
2 CONT George Haile Born about 1602 in Bristol, England. He was a passenger on the Ship "Supply" that landed in Virginia in 1620. His occupation was a Drummer or Salesman. He married around 1626, wife unknown. His known children were Joh
2 CONC n, Thomas and Nicholas Haile Senior. He died about 1662 in Lancaster County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Other people on ancestry.com say his father was Nicholas Haile, but I have no clue if that is right or not.
2 CONT
2 CONT DISCLAIMER:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ed Haile <EHAILE@MSN.COM> Date: January 01, 2001 at 17:18:55 In Reply to: Re: George Haile(Hale) 1602(Eng)-ca1650(VA) by Linda Lawhon of 623
2 CONT
2 CONT I am a seventh generation decendant of the first Nicholas Haile of Virginia. I was personally acquainted with Maude Crowe. She did us all a great disservice with her sloppy research and by making a completely unwarranted connectio
2 CONC n with the drummer boy on the Supply. There is no documentation to support this. I have never seen any reliable link beyond the first Nicholas going back to England. Unfortunately the internet spreads a lot of misleading informati
2 CONC on. [8] Hale name meaning
2 CONT
2 CONT English (also well established in South Wales): topographic name for someone who lived in a nook or hollow, from Old English and Middle English hale, dative of h(e)alh ‘nook’, ‘hollow’. In northern England the word often has a spe
2 CONC cialized meaning, denoting a piece of flat alluvial land by the side of a river, typically one deposited in a bend. In southeastern England it often referred to a patch of dry land in a fen. In some cases the surname may be a habi
2 CONC tational name from any of the several places in England named with this fossilized inflected form, which would originally have been preceded by a preposition, e.g. in the hale or at the hale. Sources 	 [S7977] "George Haile (1601-
2 CONC 1671)" biography, last updated July 24, 2015, http://www.geni.com/people/George-Haile/60000000030512.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S5769] http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Haile-25.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S44730] http://www.geni.com/people/Nicholas-Haile-I-immigrant/6000000003051227826?through=6000000000804875595.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S52202] http://www.yatesandmore.com/Hale/d7329.htm#P7328.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S3893] http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=60975267.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S7982] "William Hale, Esq., Sheriff of Hertfordshire (~1568-1621)" biography, http://www.geni.com/people/William-Hale-Esq-Sheri.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S7992] "Hale of King's Walden" a Hale registry, , abstracted, September 28, 2015, by David A. Hennessee, http://www.hale-geneal.
2 CONT
