1 NOTE {geni:about_me} On behalf of his stepson Jerome Hawley had petitioned parliament because of the complexity of the line of inheritance down the family, with provision for the widows, if necessary, at each stage. Judith Hawkins Stur
2 CONC e and Jerome2 Hawley had three children of their own. One was a son, Robert, who died young. The second child, Susannah, was born at New Brentford and founded a Canoness Regular of the Holy Sepulchre to do with St James the Apostl
2 CONC e and St Helena at Liege. From 1652 to 1697 she was the elected Abbess and died in 1706. The order returned to England in 1794 and established at New Hall, Chelmsford in Essex. The Abbess was probably the last link that the Hawley
2 CONC  family had with a Prioress, a tradition that had lasted for centuries in places such as Buckland Abbey and Sutton-le Hone in Dartford. Judith was another daughter of Jerome Hawley. She married William de Bricq of Nuremburg, Middl
2 CONC e Franconia in Bavaria, in southern Germany. The Bricq family may have been involved in the East India Company as the Bix family. In time it appears that  Judith Hawkins Sture  died, perhaps in childbirth and Jerome Hawley married
2 CONC  again sometime before his departure to Maryland in 1633. Written by Darryll Clarke Teal
