1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''John FitzJohn1
2 CONT *'''M, #52357, b. circa 1570
2 CONT *'''     John FitzJohn was born circa 1570 at of Whitchurch, Devonshire, England.1 He married Bridget Courtenay, daughter of Sir William Courtenay, 22nd Earl of Devon and Elizabeth Manners, circa 1595.1
2 CONT *'''Family      Bridget Courtenay b. c 1574
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Mary FitzJohn1 b. 1 Aug 1596
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S61] Unknown author, Family Group Sheets, Family History Archives, SLC.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1742.htm#i52357
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *'''Bridget COURTENAY 
2 CONT *Born: ABT 1572
2 CONT *Father: William COURTENAY of Powderham (Sir Knight)
2 CONT *Mother: Elizabeth MANNERS
2 CONT *'''Married: John FITZ of Fitz Ford (Sir)
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Mary FITZ (chr. 1 Aug 1596 - d. 1671) (m.1 Sir Alan Percy - m.2 Sir Charles Howard - m.3 Thomas Darcy - m.4 Richard Grenville)
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/COURTENAY2.htm#Bridget COURTENAY1
2 CONT *____________________________
2 CONT *'''The Tendring Hundred in the olden time: a series of sketches .. (1877)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/cu31924028033078
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/cu31924028033078#page/n240/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.221
2 CONT *Thomas, the third Lord Darcy, married, in 1583, Mary, daughter and co-heiress of Sir Thomas Kitson, of Hengrave Hall, Suffolk. Among the household accounts on this occasion we find, among others — ....
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/cu31924028033078#page/n241/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.222
2 CONT *This marriage turned out a most unhappy one : what Sir Harbottle Grimston called "peevish jealousies" on the part of her husband, and haughty pride of the wife, led to differences, which ended in a separation in 1594, and they bo
2 CONC th lived for more than forty years afterwards.
2 CONT *Thomas, the only son of this Lord and Lady Darcy, married the daughter of '''Sir John Fitze, of Tavistock''', and widow of Sir Alde'r Percy, but had no issue by her. He died in 1613, and was buried at Hengrave, where, upon a monu
2 CONC ment to his memory, the following is a part of the inscription : —
2 CONT **Memoria sacrum
2 CONT **Of Thomas Darcy, here the body ly,
2 CONT **Only heire maile of Chiches Barony,
2 CONT *** * * * * *
2 CONT **With D'enshire Fitz's heire he wedded was,
2 CONT **But she from earth him issueless let pass.
2 CONT *** * * * * *
2 CONT *Lord Darcy's two brothers having previously died without issue, the death of his son kept him without male heirs, and as at his death it was supposed the estates would again revert to the Crown, once more the old game, as played 
2 CONC by Audley and Cromwell, begins again with other actors on the scene, facilitated, too, by the fact that Lord Darcy had openly professed the Roman Catholic religion. .....
2 CONT *_____________________________
