1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Theophilus Hastings, 7th Earl of Huntingdon PC (10 December 1650 – 30 May 1701) was an English politician. He was the son of Ferdinando Hastings, 6th Earl of Huntingdon, born in the 27th year of his parents' marria
2 CONC ge, and became Earl of Huntingdon on 13 February 1656 on his father's death. He married, firstly, Elizabeth Lewis, daughter of Sir John Lewis, 1st Baronet, on 19 February 1671/2. She died in 1680. He married, secondly, Mary France
2 CONC s Fowler, daughter of Francis Leveson Fowler, on 8 May 1690.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Theophilus Hastings, 7th Earl of Huntingdon and Elizabeth Lewis
