1 OCCU Countess of Huntingdon, Co-heir. 3rd & yst dau.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  Lady Elizabeth Stanley was born on 6 January 1588. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of '''Ferdinando Stanley, 5th Earl of Derby''' and '''Alice Spencer'''.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married '''Henry Hastings, 5th Earl of Huntingdon''', son of Francis Hastings, Lord Hastings and Sarah Harington, on 15 January 1601.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 20 January 1633 at age 45.1
2 CONT
2 CONT      Her married name became Hastings. As a result of her marriage, Lady Elizabeth Stanley was styled as Countess of Huntingdon on 31 December 1604.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children of Lady Elizabeth Stanley and Henry Hastings, 5th Earl of Huntingdon===
2 CONT Elizabeth Stanley was the youngest daughter of Ferdinando Stanley, 5th earl of Derby (1559-April 16, 1594) and Alice Spencer (May 4, 1559-January 16, 1637). She married Henry Hastings (1586-1643), later earl of Huntingdon, on Janu
2 CONC ary 15, 1601. They had five children: Ferdinando (January 18, 1608-1655), Alice (d.1667), Elizabeth, Henry (1610-1666), and Mary (1612-1660). A patron of the arts, she was also a writer herself. A series of devotions she wrote is 
2 CONC still extant. Biography: Oxford DNB entry under “Hastings [née Stanley], Elizabeth.” Portraits: miniature by Nicholas Hilliard c. 1601-10; portrait by Paul Van Somer, c. 1614.
2 CONT
2 CONT #  Lady Alice Hastings3
2 CONT #  Lady Elizabeth Hastings3
2 CONT #  Ferdinando Hastings, 6th Earl of Huntingdon+3 b. 18 Jan 1608/9, d. 13 Feb 1655/56
2 CONT #  Henry Hastings, 1st and last Baron Loughborough of Loughborough3 b. 28 Sep 1610, d. 10 Jan 1666/67
2 CONT
