1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Pilkington knights fought for Richard III at Bosworth field.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1485 after Bosworth field Sir Thomas Pilkington of Pilkington lost his estates by Royal Attainer to the Stanley's in 1489, who received the title 'Earl of Derby'. Sir Thomas Pilkington was granted Royal pardon in 1508.
2 CONT
2 CONT It should be noted that the Stanley's,  Earls of Derby and Pilkington's fought on the same side many times. The Pilkington Knights fought for Richard III in 1485 and the Stanley's opposed Richard III and fought for Henry VII. Howe
2 CONC ver the Stanley's later joined with the Pilkington's in 1487 to depose Henry VII in favour of the House of York. 
