2 CONT Jane m. (by indenture dated 1 Aug. 1490) John Kingsmill, son of Richard Kingsmill, of Basingstoke
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of William Gifford died 1548, who mentions his nephew Kingsmill in his will.
2 CONT
2 CONT In The Genealogist, v. 1 no. 1 (1980), Gary Boyd Roberts reviewed the Gifford/Kingsmill connection as part of his review of Paget's "Ancestry of Prince Charles", which does NOT incorporate the generations in question in this linea
2 CONC ge. He cites sources (see note 8 on p. 252) indicating that Joan Gifford Kingsmill was the sister, not the granddaughter, of the Sir William Gifford who m. Eleanor Paulet.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1490: Settlement in prospect of a marriage between John Kyngesmyll, son and heir of Richard Kyngesmyll of Basingstoke, gentleman, and Joan daughter of John Gyffard of Ichyll co. Hants[1] 11 Dec 1501: Licence from Richard, bishop o
2 CONC f Winchester, to John Kyngesmyll and Joan his wife, of Frefolk, to have mass and other divine offices celebrated in a suitable place in their house or elsewhere in the diocese. [2] Named as Jane in husband John Kingsmill's Will da
2 CONC ted on 14 Mar 1508/09 and proved on 20 May 1509.
