3 TEXT John attended Winchester College from 1470 to 1474 and went on to New College, Oxford, in the latter year. He was a full fellow of New College from 1476 to 1479. Between 1487 and 1489 he provided legal counsel to Magdalen College,
4 CONC  Oxford. The Middle Temple admitted him in 1489. From 1492 to 1504 he served as steward of Winchester College. Returned to parliament for Heytesbury, Wiltshire, in 1491, he became a JP for Hampshire in 1493, a position he retained
4 CONC  until his death, and in the same year began to try cases in the court of requests. Also lists his wife and children
