2 DATE 12 AUG 1607
2 ADDR
3 CITY Sydmonton
3 STAE England
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The widow of FitzGerald married George Raleigh as his second wife and had one daughter: Bridget.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestor  of Queen Elizabeth ll and of Elizabeth The Queen Mother  (Elizabeth Bowles  Lyon)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bridget Raleigh, daughter of George Raleigh and his second wife, married Sir William Kingsmill, son of Sir John Kingsmill and Constance Goring.
2 CONT
2 CONT William and his wife Bridget had 14 children. Their marriage would have been in 1553 or 1554, based on a 1553 reference[3] for the Conveyance of the Hampshire and Berkshire lands of John Kyngismyll to his son William, of Sydmonton
2 CONC , Hants., who was shortly to be married to Bryget, sister of Simon Raleygh of Farnborough, Warwickshire. His short, one page will (held by Hampshire Archives[20]) is dated 30 Jan 1586 and was proved in 1596. It names just his wife
2 CONC  and his heir/son and executor William.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Bridget Raleigh and Sir William Kingsmill, born at Hampshire, England,  include: 
2 CONT # William Kingsmill,  b. c 1555, d. 1600.  First son.  Married 1) Jane St. Leger 2) Anne Wilkes.
2 CONT # Constance Kingsmill, b. abt 1556.  First daughter. Married  Richard Fiennes, Lord Say 
2 CONT # Thomas Kingsmill, b. abt 1555.  Second son.  Married Dadeth Valeda.. 
2 CONT # Frances Kingsmill, b. abt 1563, d. 1 Jan 1627. Married John Croker. 
2 CONT # Francis Kingsmill+1 b. 1569, d. 1620. Sixth son.   Married Dorothy Hunt. 
2 CONT # Eleanor Kingsmill, b. bef 12 Jun 1571.  Married Henry Goring. 
2 CONT # Bridget Kingsmill, b. abt 1573, d. abt 1606.  Married Thomas Norris. 
2 CONT # Catherine Kingsmill, b.c. 1574.  Married Anthony Palmer of London
2 CONT # Richard Kingsmill. Third son.  Father of Frances Kingsmill.
2 CONT # Robert Kingsmill.  Fourth son.  s.p.
2 CONT # Ferdinando Kingsmill.  Fifth son.
2 CONT # George Kingsmill.  Seventh son.
2 CONT # John Kingsmill.  Eighth son.
2 CONT # John Kingsmill.  s.p.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT Brigitte and William are lying in the church of St. Mary's at Kingsclere a town near Sydmonton. The two marble figures lying on the top of the tomb. Sir William and Lady Brigitte
2 CONT
2 CONT Level Item FindingNo 19M61/1542 Title Acquittance: all goods, chattels and household stuff received by (i) following an agreement with William Kingsmill Date 7 Mar 1593 Description i) Dame Bridget Kingsmill, relict of Sir William 
2 CONC Kingsmill
2 CONT
2 CONT ii) William Kingsmill, her son and executor of the will of Sir William Kingsmill
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed: Bryghett Kyngismyll
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnesses: Henrie Goringe; Thomas Millman
2 CONT
2 CONT Endorsed: 'My mothers acquitans'
2 CONT
2 CONT Paper, folded short. PhysicalDescription Damaged. Seal of (i).
2 CONT
2 CONT 91 of 584
2 CONT
2 CONT Collection Kingsmill of Sydmonton
2 CONT
2 CONT "Letters and Papers, Foreign and Domestic, Henry VIII, vo. 10, p. 122, which contains a letter (dated 19 Feb. 1535/6) from George RALEGH to Thomas CROMWELL, regarding some income from lands he had in Ireland through this 2nd wife 
2 CONC whom he describes as lately dead, naming her first husband as Sir Thomas FITZGARETHE, viz.: "19 Feb. R. O.323. 323. George Ralegh to Cromwell.
2 CONT
2 CONT I have lately lost my wife, by whom I had 60l. land in cos. Warw. and Glouc., besides 40l. yearly, payable to her out of Ireland of the gift of her first husband, Sir Thos. Fitzgarethe. These have now descended to Sir Jas. Fitzgar
2 CONC ethe, brother and heir to Sir Thos. Geffrey. Please write to Sir Jas. that I may have the farm, during his life and mine, of these his lands in Gloucester and Warwick, of the yearly value of 60l. 4s. 3ï¿½d.
2 CONT
2 CONT Farnborough, 19 Feb. Signed.
2 CONT
2 CONT P. 1. Add.: Secretary. Endd."
2 CONT
2 CONT Note this appears to indicate that daughter Bridget may not be the daughter of Jane Connesby?
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Kingsmill, MS Harl 1544, fo. 5 - 7,''' click [https://www.wikitree.com/photo.php/a/a8/Kingsmill-10.jpg '''here'''] to see full sized original.
2 CONT
