2 CONT * “Correct mother of Bridget RALEGH or RALEIGH, wife of Sir William KINGSMILL (also GODDARD, and ERNLE or ERNELEY)” < [https://soc.genealogy.medieval.narkive.com/YNJZEAuJ/correct-mother-of-bridget-ralegh-or-raleigh-wife-of-sir-wil
2 CONC liam-kingsmill-also-goddard-and-ernle-or-#post1 link] > 
2 CONT ** Leo van de Pas's excellent website includes Bridget RALEGH wife of Sir William KINGSMILL, of Sidmanton, Hants., as one of the lines of the Prince of Wales's ancestry, quoting The Lineage and Ancestry of H.R.H. Sendrince Charles
2 CONC , Prince of Wales, Edinburgh, 1977, Paget, Gerald, Reference: M 7098, as the source. Her parents are given as George RALEGH (will dated 2 Apr. 1546), of Thornburgh, Warws., and his wife Jane CONINGSBY.
2 CONT ** In the Visitation of Warwickshire (1619), however, pp. 76-77 (pedigree of RALEIGH), George RALEIGH is said to have married three times. http://www.archive.org/stream/visitationcount01britgoog His first wife was Jane daughter of
2 CONC  William CONNYSBY, of Aldenha' Kt, by whom he had numerous progeny, but not BRIDGET. It was by his second wife who is described as "widow of Fitz Gerrard", by whom he had issue, one child, "Bridget ux. William KINGMILL." Finally, 
2 CONC George RALEIGH's third wife was Anne, daughter of ...ERNELEY. (this is where my interest first arose because I am tracing all references to ERNELEY or ERNLE and vars.)
2 CONT ** In an article for which I have only seen quoted material on the NEHGS website: "RALEGH of Farnborough: vol. 145, 1991, pp. 3-21, by Danny D. Smith, George RALEGH's 2nd wife is described as the widow of Sir Thomas FITZGARETHE. h
2 CONC ttp://www.newenglandancestors.org/research/services/articles_fiennes_collection1.asp
2 CONT ** This led me to the Letters and Papers, Foreign and Domestic, Henry VIII, vo. 10, p. 122, which contains a letter (dated 19 Feb. 1535/6) from George RALEGH to Thomas CROMWELL, regarding some income from lands he had in Ireland t
2 CONC hrough this 2nd wife whom he describes as lately dead, naming her first husband as Sir Thomas FITZGARETHE, viz.: … http://www.british-history.ac.uk/report.aspx?compid=75416 The index to this work (available via British History Onl
2 CONC ine) includes FITZGARETHE and FEISGERROT under the heading FITZGERALD, from which I take it that Sir Thomas FITZGARETHE would be known under the form, Sir Thomas FITZGERALD. http://www.british-history.ac.uk/report.aspx?compid=7544
2 CONC 7
2 CONT * "A Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Landed Gentry of Great Britain & Ireland" Vol. 2, B. Burke, 1898, page 235. 
2 CONT * http://powys.org/pl_tree/ps40/ps40_112.html Only child by her father’s second wife.
2 CONT ** [56, Hants of 1530 on, pub Harleian 1912, Kingsmill p. 3], [60, Saye and Sele article, Vol XI, p. 485]
2 CONT * http://www.thepeerage.com/p42441.htm#i424410
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Kingsmill-16
2 CONT * "Kingsmill, MS Harl 1544, fo. 5 - 7," in Vis. of Hants., 1530, 1575 & 1634, p. 2 - 3. Harleian Society. < [https://archive.org/details/PedigreesFromTheVisitationOfHampshireMadeByThomasBenolt/page/n13/mode/2up Archive.Org] >
