1 NOTE {geni:about_me} COOPER, John (1552-1610), of Pawlett, Som. b. 24 Sept. 1552, s. of '''John Cooper of Winscombe''' by Jane, da. of Sir John Kingsmill of Sydmonton, Hants. m. Martha, da. of Anthony Skutt of Stanton Drew, 1s. 4da. su
2 CONC c. fa. 1566. Kntd. by 1603.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/cooper-john-1552-1610
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sir_John_Cooper,_1st_Baronet
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Cooper, 1st Baronet (died 23 March 1630), was an English landowner and politician who sat in the House of Commons from 1628 to 1629. He was father of Anthony Ashley Cooper, 1st Earl of Shaftesbury.
2 CONT Life.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Cooper was the only son of another Sir John Cooper (1552–1610), who in 1586 served as a member of parliament for Whitchurch in Hampshire, by his marriage to Margaret (or Martha), a daughter of Anthony Skutt, of Stanton Drew in Som
2 CONC erset. He had four sisters, Bridget, Margaret, Martha and Jane.[1] On his father's death in 1610, Cooper inherited the manor of Pawlett in Somerset.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Apparently misidentified in Burke’s as RICHARD
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.thepeerage.com/p69446.htm#i694454
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Cooper married June Kingsmill, daughter of John Kingsmill.1 He died on 8 May 1566.1
2 CONT
2 CONT He purchased Manor of Paulett circa 1532 from Sir Amyas Paulet.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Richard Cooper and June Kingsmill
2 CONT * Sir John Cooper+1 d. 1610.  Married Martha Skutt
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Citations
2 CONT * [S37] BP2003 volume 3, page 3575. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter
