1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Family and Education==
2 CONT b. c.1530, 1st s of John Norton† of East Tisted by Anne, da. of Sir George Puttenham of Sherfield. m. (1) by 1564, Elizabeth, da. and h. of William Wayte of Wymering, Hants, 2s. inc. Richard Norton II; (2) Catherine, da. of Sir Jo
2 CONC hn Kingsmill of Sydmonton, 2s. 1da. suc. fa. 1561. Kntd. by 1577.  He died 11 Mar. 1592, and was succeeded by his eldest son, Richard.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT [http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/norton-richard-i-1530-92 History of Parliament Online]
2 CONT
2 CONT Will dated 3 Aug 1586, proved 20 March 1592.
2 CONT In his will, made 3 Aug. 1586, he asked to be buried at East Tisted without any pomp. To three sons [William Norton, Richard (commonly called Charles Norton) & Daniel Norton] he left amounts of money, dividing between them the man
2 CONC ors of Overton and Old Alresford, granted to him by the Queen after they had been devised to her by the bishop of Winchester. Another son, Henry, received £100, but no land. To his daughter Constance he bequeathed 1,000 marks as w
2 CONC ell as the manor of Rotherfield, which she was to enjoy until her elder half-brother, Richard Norton, agreed to pay her a further £500 on her marriage or at the age of twenty one. Brother Kingsmill. His wife Katherine was the sole
2 CONC  executrix. He died a year later, 11 Mar. 1592, and was succeeded by his eldest son, Richard.
