1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From [https://books.google.com/books?id=1SApAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA21&ots=tKPQJ8cFnj&dq=John%20Thornborough%20of%20Shoddesden&pg=PA21#v=onepage&q&f=false page 21] of A Perfect Booke: Of All the Landes as Well Arable as Pas
2 CONC ture, Meadowes ... edited by Walter Money
2 CONT
2 CONT >J John Thornborough, Esq., of the family of this name of Thornburgh, co. York. He was one of the commissioners for musters and for disarming recusants, high-sheriff of Hants, 1578, and is described as of "Shetesden," or as otherw
2 CONC ise entered "Spaddesden," co. Hants. Probably Shoddesden, in the parish of Kimpton, near Andover. By Margaret, daughter of Sir John Kingsmill, of Sydmonton, he was father of many children, amongst them Sir John, Edward, Henry, Fra
2 CONC nces, and Katharine, (who died in 1650), wife to Alexander Dyer. [SIC: sister Katherine, not daughter]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=nCYVAAAAQAAJ&lpg=PA548&ots=wJSPCI6WNz&dq=sir%20anthony%20windsor%20anne%20thornborough&pg=PA108#v=onepage&q&f=false page 108] The History of the Part of West Somerset Comprising the Parishes
2 CONC  ..., Volume 1 By Sir Charles Edward Heley Chadwyck-Healey
2 CONT
2 CONT >This last share no doubt came through Lady Gorges. William Thornborough, son and heir of Robert Thornborough, refers in his will * to the hereditaments in Hampshire, Wiltshire, Devon, and Somerset, descended by the death of Lady 
2 CONC Gorges. This property he left to his wife Frances for her life and after her death " to the use of such right heirs as stand now inheritable thereunto." Other lands descended from his father were to be held upon like uses after th
2 CONC e death of his M mother in law Dame Anne Wyndsor." John Thornborough was son and heir of this William who died on the 3rd December 1535, as we learn from a survey of his estates.5 From the same record we find that " Dame Anne Wynd
2 CONC sor " was the wife of Sir Anthony Wyndsor and "grandmother in lawe" to John Thornborough. The survey merely refers to the Somerset property, " Certen landes and tenementes in Weste Luckham," as " descended" and as being worth by t
2 CONC he year, with other property in Devon, 6oj. John Thornborough was aged one year and a half in June, 1536.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=M0cJAAAAIAAJ&lpg=PA154&ots=bNH_lOB9in&dq=maurice%20rodney%201588%20johan%20dyer&pg=PA154#v=onepage&q=maurice%20rodney%201588%20johan%20dyer&f=false page 154] of Notes & Queries for Somerset 
2 CONC and Dorset, Volume 10
2 CONT
2 CONT >Sir Thomas Dyer, Kt., of Weston, Somerset, eldest son of Alexander Dyer, married, first, '''Frances Darcy''', widow of William Thornborough, whose marriage licence (Faculty Office) is dated 7 February, 1532-3. [https://books.goog
2 CONC le.com/books?id=gvwUAAAAQAAJ&lpg=PA8&ots=2a_NuhKfRl&dq=william%20thornborough%20frances%20darcy&pg=PA8#v=onepage&q=william%20thornborough%20frances%20darcy&f=false link] William and Frances Thornborough left issue Catherine Thornb
2 CONC orough, who was married to Alexander Dyer [and also a son, John Thornborough, mentioned in Thomas Dyer's will]
2 CONT
