1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From Pedigrees from the Visitation of Hampshire Page 195: Pitt [https://archive.org/details/pedigreesfromvis64beno/page/195 Archive.Org]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Pitt (son of William Pitt & daughter de Haviland) married Joane, daughter of John Swayne of Blandford
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue 
2 CONT *1.  William m Edith Cadbury
2 CONT *2. John “hath issue in Ireland”
2 CONT *3.  Thomas 
2 CONT *1.  Agnes m Anthony Dannett
2 CONT *2.  Elizabeth m Jonohab Sherley
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Pitt-81
2 CONT
2 CONT Death and Burial
2 CONT
2 CONT John Pitt died 1596 in Blandford, Dorsetshire, England. He wrote his Will on 28 Sep 1599 (41 Eliz). Probate was granted to his wife Johane on 13th February, 1601/2 but may have been delayed since there were no witnesses to his wil
2 CONC l. 
2 CONT
2 CONT As well as sums of money and goods, he made bequests to his sons of leases on land in Preston and in Charlton, Dorset and also of houses and shops in Blandford and Poole. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His Will, named his heir as William, followed in age by John and Thomas; daughters Eleanor Pitt and Susan received bequests as did his other unnamed grandchildren. 
2 CONT
2 CONT At the time of the Will, his son John was married to an Alice, his son Thomas was unmarried. His son William was married but the name of his wife was not mentioned, he had a son Edward. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *  John Burke A General and heraldic dictionary of the peerage and baronetage of ..., Volume 2 Page 353.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=seAKAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA353&lpg=PA353&dq=%22William+Pitt%22+%22Comptroller%22&source=bl&ots=osj
2 CONC IjIctXW&sig=WB8_M9vjUn-tsh2H-T7B0AMxcEc&hl=en&ei=mmXiTrTzO8jP8gPm4-CIBA&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22William%20Pitt%22%20%22Comptroller%22&f=false GoogleBooks]
