2 CONT Will of Rebecah IZARD dated 20 Oct. 1675 "being sick in body." "After daughter Rebeccah BAGNALL's estate be taken out of the whole estate of mine and daughter Martha IZARD & the debts paid then the estate to be equally divided bet
2 CONC wixt me & my aforesd Daughter Martha IZARD then out of my proportion I give as followeth: To Rebeccah BAGNALL & Mary BENNETT & Martha IZARD & James BAGNALL the sonne of James BAGNALL, Nehemiah HUNT, the sonne of Godfrey HUNT & Eli
2 CONC zabeth REEVES, the daughter of Henry REEVES all my proportion of estate before expressed to be equally divided betwixt them and my will is that my sonne James BAGNALL, Henry REEVES, & Ambrose ? be my overseers to see this my will 
2 CONC performed. Wit. John BURWELL, Wm. WESTAN. Proved 20 Oct. 1675. Bk. 2, p.135
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Henry REEVES Sr (1630 to April 6, 1687) was born in Warwick Parish, Middlesex, England.  He married Elizabeth Bagnall (1640 to February 1711)  daughter of Roger Bagnall and Rebecca.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died before 6 Apr 1687 in Old Rappahannock, Virginia. First of this Ryves line to come to America. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Henry Reeves was dated 9 January 1686
2 CONT
2 CONT "I give & bequeath unto my eight Children Henry, Joseph, James, Elizabeth, Rebecca, Martha, Mary, & Ann, all the remaining part of my personal Estate that is not here above given away to be Equally Devided between all Shear & Shea
2 CONC r alike It ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
