3 STAE England
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 OCCU
1 TITL Maj.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Berkeley-1006
2 CONT
2 CONT Maurice Berkeley was the younger son of Edward Berkeley of Pylle Somersetshire and his wife Philippa, daughter of George Speke of Whitelackington. He was named in the 1669 Will of his father [1] dated 4 December 1669 and proved 21
2 CONC  February 1669/70.
2 CONT
2 CONT He wrote his own Will on 22 February 1667/8, [2] in which he named his two sisters, Elizabeth Baily and Phillipp sic Berkeley, and his brother Edward, as residuary legatee and executor. Also named but not identified - William Cowa
2 CONC rd of Wells. He apparently died without wife or children.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was buried at Pylle on 15 March 1677/8, as "Major Maurice Berkeley". [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT ↑ Will of Edward Berkeley of Pill, Somerset PROB 1/332/306
2 CONT ↑ Will of Maurice Berkeley of Pill, Somerset, proved 21 November 1678 PROB 11/358/319
2 CONT ↑ Parish Register Pylle 1591-1759 Img 23/27 Ancestry UK
