1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT === Biography: Walter Coplestone (– d. c. 1490)
2 CONT Walter Coplestone was a 15th-century English gentleman and the progenitor of the Coplestone branch situated at Bowden, in the parish of Yealmpton, South Devon. As the third son of one of the county’s most powerful administrative f
2 CONC amilies, Walter established a significant junior line that maintained influence in the South Hams for several generations.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lineage and Estate
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter was the son of John Coplestone II (d. 1458) and Elizabeth Hawley (d. 1457).[^1] While his father resided in the Hawley mansion in Dartmouth and his eldest brother, Philip, inherited the primary seat at Colebrooke, Walter wa
2 CONC s settled on the manor of Bowden. This estate became the seat of his descendants, distinct from the primary "Great Coplestone" line.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter married Elizabeth Stone, the daughter and heiress of Thomas Stone of Bowden.[^2] Through this marriage, Walter secured the Bowden estate, which had been in the Stone family for generations.
2 CONT
2 CONT The union produced the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Thomas Coplestone: Of Bowden, the son and heir who continued the line and married Catherine, daughter of the Exeter historian John Vowell alias Hooker.[^3]
2 CONT *Margaret Coplestone: Who married into the regional gentry.[^4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Historical Context
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter’s marriage followed the established pattern of the Coplestone family: marrying heiress-progenitors to consolidate land and regional authority. By acquiring Bowden through Elizabeth Stone, Walter ensured that his branch of t
2 CONC he family held a stable, independent landed base, allowing them to serve as local magistrates and landowners in their own right throughout the Tudor period.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===NGS Style Register Report
2 CONT
2 CONT First Generation
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter Coplestone was born in Devon, England, the son of John Coplestone and Elizabeth Hawley. He died circa 1490. He married Elizabeth Stone, daughter and heiress of Thomas Stone, circa 1450.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Walter and Elizabeth (Stone) Coplestone:
2 CONT
2 CONT # i. Thomas Coplestone, of Bowden. He married Catherine Vowell, daughter of John Vowell alias Hooker of Exeter.
2 CONT #ii. Margaret Coplestone.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
