2 TITL Richard Skydmore (1580 - 1606) - Find A Grave Memorial
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-2782
1 NOTE [Master.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT [Master.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT The branch of the family that Thomas Skidmore comes from is the one known as the Scudamores of holme Lacy Herefordshire.
2 CONT Holme Lacy is one of the "stately homes of England" it is located on the crest of the knoll in the Valley of the River Arye,
2 CONT Herefordshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The name Skidmore is derived from the Norman-French "Escu d' amour", the shield of love.
2 CONT
2 CONT MOTTO: Scuto Amoris Divini
2 CONT TRANSLATION: "Defended by the shield of Divine love"
2 CONT
2 CONT ARMS: Gules, three stirrups, leather and buckles or
2 CONT CREST: A unicorn's head erased sable Platie
2 CONT OR
2 CONT ARMS: Gules, three stirrups, leathered and buckled or
2 CONT CREST: Out of ducal cornet or a lions gamb sable armed gules.
2 CONT
2 CONT The early family was noted for excellent horsemanship and the superior breed of horses they possessed. The Scudamore family
2 CONT came into England from Northern France. The Scudamore family is distinguished in early history as being one of the most eminent
2 CONT families in West England. They were strong Royalist. They resided mostly in Herefordshire, and Herefordshire County on the Wales
2 CONT border. The Scudamores were people of greath wealth and influence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Seyut Scudamore
2 CONT The Ancestor of the Skidmore family arrived in England from Northern France, with William the Conqueror (William I) in 1066
2 CONT when he assumed the throne of England. His name was inscribed on the Roll of Battle Abbey as "Seyut Scudamore" (Saint).
1 SOUR
