1 NOTE Ancestral File Number:<AFN> 3926-4F
2 CONT !ORDINANCE: Ancestral File, Lake Stevens Family History Center, WA, Mar 1994.
2 CONT
2 CONT !NOTE: The Ancestral File gives the Birth date as 'In the spring of 1605' and the Birth place as 'Mayshill In Westerleigh, Gloucestershire, England' and the Burial place as 'Burial Hill South Side of Conc St, Fairfield,CT'.
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-2782
1 NOTE Thomas was a blacksmith 
2 CONT Other Wives:
2 CONT Sarah Treadwell (3rd wife)-see below
2 CONT
2 CONT (2nd Wife)Joanna Baldwin brn about 1610 (Joanna was the widow of Nathaniel Baldwin, previously widow of Richard Wescott. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (3rd wife) Sarah Keeler, brn about 1605 married after 1672, died Dec 8, 1684 (same as Sarah Treadwell - Sara was the widow first of Edward Treadwell, second of Henry Whelpley and third of Ralph Keeler - she died late in 1684)
2 CONT
2 CONT This information comes from the book: History and Genealogy of The Families of Old Fairfield, Vol I, compiled by Donald Lines Jacobus, published by the Genealogical Publishing Co. in 1976
2 CONT
2 CONT Evans genealogy web page has the death date as: abt 31 Oct 1684
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas was a blacksmith
2 CONT
2 CONT Joanna brought 7 children to the relationship from previous marriages. There are a number of documents in Fairfield settling the estates of these stepchildren as they become of age.
2 CONT
2 CONT Friend to Governer Winthrop and his son
2 CONT
2 CONT Which daughter or step daughter married William Reed ( step sister to Daniel Westcott)?
