2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Skidmore [Parents] 1, 2, 3 was born in 1605 in Mayshill, Westerleigh, Gloustershire, England. He died on 31 Oct 1684 in Fairfield, Connecticut. He was buried in Burial Hill, Fairfield, Connecticut. He was sealed to his pare
2 CONC nts on 26 Jul 1990 in the Salt Lake temple. He was baptized on 20 Jul 1990 in the Salt Lake temple. He was endowed on 25 Jul 1990 in the Salt Lake temple. He married Ellen Whitehead about 1626 in Westerleigh, Gloucester, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Other marriages: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Howes, Sarah 
2 CONT , Joanna 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [Notes] 
2 CONT Ellen Whitehead was born in 1605 in Wyne Valley, Herford, England. She died 1646 - 1702 in Cambridge, Massachusettes. She married Thomas Skidmore about 1626 in Westerleigh, Gloucester, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [Notes] 
2 CONT They had the following children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT    M i Thomas Skidmore 
2 CONT    F ii Dorothy Skidmore 
2 CONT    F iii Jedidah Skidmore 
2 CONT    M iv John Skidmore 
2 CONT    M v Richard Skidmore 1 was christened on 11 Mar 1637/1638 in Church of St. James the Great, Westerleigh, Gloucestershire. He died after 15 Oct 1661 in Norwalk, Fairfield, Connecticut. He was sealed to his parents on 2 Mar 2005 
2 CONC in the Redlands California temple. He was baptized on 19 Jun 2003 in the Los Angeles California temple. He was endowed on 15 Dec 2004 in the Redlands California temple. [Notes]  
1 NOTE [Master.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT [Master.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Skidmore, Esq.
2 CONT Thomas Skidmore, Esq., son of Richard & Agnes (Lawrence) Skidmore, b. abt 1600, Westerly County, England; d. 1684, Fairfield,
2 CONT Connecticut (will dated 20 Apr 1684); m.1st- 1635, England to Ellen Whitehead,; m.2nd- Joanna Stanford (Westcott)(Baldwin), she
2 CONT had been twice widowed, b. 1612; d. will 1667; m.3rd 1672 to Sarah Treadwell, widow of Edward Treadwell, Henry Whelpley, and
2 CONT Ralph Keeler.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the age of 35 Thomas Skidmore was married and living in Westerlleigh, Gloucester County, England. In 1635, he was an Agent
2 CONT of Governor Winthrop in planning Saybrook. In Apr 1635 he sent cattle over for Governor John Winthrop. In 1639, he set sail for
2 CONT New England, aboard the same ship as Governor Winthrop, Jr. They arrived at what is now known as Cambridge, Massachusetts.
2 CONT From 1636 until 1639, he assisted Governor Winthrop in the settlement of Saybrook, Connecticut. He assisted in the preparing a
2 CONT plantation at Saybrook, Connecticut for Governor Winthrop, Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Skidmore's homestead in Cambridge, Massachusetts was located on the westerly side of Brighton Street, North of Mount
2 CONT Auburn. This location is now Harvard Square, Cambridge, Massachusetts and a post office stands on a portion of his lands. He was
2 CONT living in Boston, Massachusetts in 1639. In the spring of 1640, he sent back to England for his wife and family to join him. At the
2 CONT time he sent for his family, he also gave power of attorney to Henry Hazzard of Bristol England to sell his property at Westerly,
2 CONT county of Gloucester, England. On 1 Jan 1646, Thomas Skidmore sold his property in Cambridge and moved with his wife and six
2 CONT (6) children to Connecticut Colony, New York.
2 CONT In 1647-48, Thomas Skidmore owned a home lot and ear marks for cattle in New London (at that time known as Pequot Harbor),
2 CONT Connecticut. In 1649, he received a large land grant in Fairfield, Connecticut. He was instrumental in founding the settlement of
2 CONT Huntington, Long Island. Thomas Skidmore was a Smithy (blacksmith) by trade. He located his shop on land near the Harbor - it
2 CONT appears that he had a great affection for the water. In 1663 he is shown as a smithy of Huntington Harbor, Long Island. In 1673: He
2 CONT was one of the Patentees of Huntington.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also in 1673, Thomas Skidmore became the town Clerk in Huntington and a representative to the General Assembly. On 4 Mar
2 CONT 1669, he appears as the first attorney for Suffolk County. In 1676, he served in King Philip's War. He is listed in 1693 as One of
2 CONT Associates of Lancaster, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas & Ellen (Whitehead) Skidmore had (5) five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Thomas, b. England.
2 CONT 2. Dorothy, b. ca. 1631, England; m. 20 Jul 1652, Stafford to Hugh Griffen
2 CONT 3. Jedidah (female), b. England; m. Edward Highby
2 CONT 4. John, b. 11 Apr 1643; m. Susannah Davis.
2 CONT 5. Grace m. John Goulding of Huntington.
