1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *''''''The peerage of England: containing a genealogical and historical account of ... By Arthur Collins
2 CONT *[http://books.google.com/books?id=IkhAAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA191&lpg=PA191&dq=Bartholomew+Cherchile&source=bl&ots=ul23pCmAxi&sig=OgcAKenWWq3dAnifwRGowAUEQdc&hl=en&ei=68DrTYOME-rjiALP_IjhCA&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0CC8Q6
2 CONC AEwBA#v=onepage&q=Bartholomew%20Cherchile&f=false/ The peerage of England: containing a genealogical and historical account of ... By Arthur Collins]
2 CONT *Pg. 191
2 CONT *   This Roger, by his Wife Gertrude, Daughter to Sir Guy de Torbay, had John, His Son and Heir, whofe Wife was Joan de Kilrington, by whom he had Sir Bartholomew de Cherchile, who held the Caftle of Briftol for King Stephen. He m
2 CONC arried Agnes, Daughter to Ralph Fitz-Ralph, Lord of Tiverton, and by her had Pagan de Cherchile, whofe swon Roger Had Free-Warren in his Lands in Cherchile, in the Reign of Edward I.
2 CONT *   To this Roger fucceeded Elias de Churchelle, whofe Wife was Dorothy, a Daughter of the ancient Family of Columbiers, and by her had three Sons, John, who married Joan, Daughter and Co-heir to Roger Dawney of Norton, and left o
2 CONC nly two Daughters his Co-heirs, Margaret, the Wife of Andrew Hilberfdon of the County of Devon, and Agnes, married to Thomas Gifford, of Theuborough in Cornwall, whereby the Lordfhip of Churchill and other Lands devolved on them.
2 CONT *   Giles, fecond Son, had the Lordfhip of Yampton and Lineham, n Devonfhire; which Eftates, by a Female Heir, defcended to the Family of Croker of the fame County; fo that William the third Son of Elias, was the chief Heir Male.
2 CONT *   This William was feated at Rockbear in the County of Devon, and left Iffue Giles Churchill, Efq; Father of ''''''Charles Churchill, Efq; who for his firm Adherence to the Houfe of York, was in great Favour with King Edward IV.
2 CONC  who advanced him to the Marrieage of Margaret, only Daughter of Sir William Widvile, by whom he had'''''' Thomas Churchill, Efq; whofe Wife was Grace,
2 CONT *Pg. 192
2 CONT *Daughter and Co-heir to Thomas Tylle, of Tylle-Houfe in the County of Cornwall, and by her he had William Churchill, his Heir and Succeffor, who married Mary, eldeft Daughter to Richard Creufe of Wicroft-Caftle in the County of D
2 CONC evon, Efq; and by her he had three Sons, Roger of Catherfton, William of Corton, and John who was feated at Mufton, all in the County of Dorfet.
2 CONT *______________________________
2 CONT *''''''The Churchill family in America (1904)
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/details/churchillfamilyi01chur
2 CONT * http://www.archive.org/stream/churchillfamilyi01chur#page/n21/mode/1up
2 CONT *   4. JOHN DE COURCIL, eldest son of Roger, married JOAN DE KILRINGTON, by whom he had a son, 
2 CONT **   5. BARTHOLOMEW, who was knighted under King Stephen [1135-1154] as SIR BARTHOLOMEW DE CHERCHILE, and who was made Master of the Castle at Bristol, holding it for the king. He married AGNES, daughter of Ralph Fitz Ralph of Tiv
2 CONC erton, and had son, 
2 CONT ***   6. PAGAN DE CHERCHILE, who married (___) and had a son, 
2 CONT ****   7. ROGER DE CHERCHILE, who married (___) and had a son, 
2 CONT *****   8. ELIAS DE CHIRCHIL, who married the daughter of the ancient house of Columbers, and by her had three sons, John and Giles, neither of whom left male issue, and 
2 CONT ******http://www.archive.org/stream/churchillfamilyi01chur#page/n22/mode/1up
2 CONT *******   9. WILLIAM CHURCHILL, the third son, who assumed that form of the name, resided at Rockbear in Devonshire, married (___) and had a son, 
2 CONT ********   10. GILES CHURCHILL, who married (___) and had a son, 
2 CONT *********''''''   11. CHARLES CHURCHILL, who married MARGARET, only daughter and heiress of Sir William Widville, who brought him considerable estate. They had a son, 
2 CONT **********   12. THOMAS CHURCHILL, who married GRACE, daughter of Thomas Tylle, of Tylle House in Cornwall, and by her had a son, 
2 CONT *___________________________
2 CONT *5-Bartholomew,who was Knighted under King Stephen(1135-1154) as Sir Bartholomew de Cherchile,was Master of the Castle at Bristol, holding it for the King. He married Agnes, dau. of Ralph Fritz (or son of)Ralph of Tiverton. 
2 CONT **6-Pagan de Cherchile 
2 CONT ***7-Roger de Cherchile. 
2 CONT ****8-Elias de Chirchil m. dau. of ancient house of Columbers 
2 CONT *****9-William Churchill, who assumed that form of the name, resided at Rockbear in Devonshire. 
2 CONT ******10-Giles Churchill. 
2 CONT *******''''''11- Charles Churchill married Margaret, only daughter and heiress of Sir William Widville, who brought him considerable estate. 
2 CONT ********12-Thomas Churchill married Grace daughter of Thomas Tylle of Tylle House in Cornwall. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.multiwords.de/genealogy/churchill1.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://www.ebooksread.com/authors-eng/charles-a-atwood/the-ancestry-of-one-atwood-family-owt/page-6-the-ancestry-of-one-atwood-family-owt.shtml
2 CONT *_________________________
2 CONT *''''''The life of John, Duke of Marlborough : Prince of the Roman empire (1743)
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/details/lifeofjohndukeof01lediiala
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/lifeofjohndukeof01lediiala#page/4/mode/1up
2 CONT *   With this Roger, the Son of Pagan, lived cotemporary, Richard de Cherchile, who Ann. 14. Edw. I. was Witnefs to the Agreement made between the Brethren of the Hofpital of St. John Baptift, in Bath, and Thomas de Hereford, one 
2 CONC of the Burgeffes of Briftol, about a Houfe in Reedclive, in the Suburbs of Briftol, of the Fee of Berkley. 
2 CONT *   Who was the Wife of Roger, I likewife, do not find ; But his Succeffor was Elias de Cherchile. I find mention made of one Otho de Churchill, as a Defcendant of Sir Bartholomew de Cherchile, who was the Founder of a fpreading F
2 CONC amily in Devonfhire, Sommerfetfhire and Wiltfhire ; But by him muft probably be meant this Elias, or elfe one of the nine Sons of John Churchill, the Son of William Churchill of Mufton, Efq ; of whom, I fhall make farther Mention 
2 CONC below. Of this Elias, we find, that Ann. 8. Edw. II. he granted to John Bampfield, his Meadow call'd Pleynfold, in Clifton. He married Dorothy, a Daughter of the ancient Family of the Columbers, by whom he had Iffue three Sons, (1
2 CONC .) John Churchille, of Litlar, of whom we find, that he was Witnefs to a Charter of Thomas Bampfield, Ann. 5. Richardi II. and who is likewife mentioned in another Charter, Ann. II. Henry IV. He married Jane (or, as fome Authors f
2 CONC ay, Joan) Daughter and Coheirefs of Roger Dawny, of Norton, by Juliana his Wife, the Daughter and Coheirefs of William de Widdebere. He had Iffue only two Daughters, his Coheireffes ; Margaret, the youngeft, was Wife of Andrew Hil
2 CONC lerfdon, of Devonfhire, and Agnes, the eldeft, Wife of Thomas Gifford, of Therwborough, in Cornwal, who by that Marriage, became poffefs'd of the Lordfhip of Churchill, and other Lands. (2.) Giles Churchill, who had the Lordfhips 
2 CONC of Yampton and Lineham , in Devonfhire, which Eftates defcended, by a Daughter and Heirefs, to the Family of the Crokers, of Devonfhire, Lords of Lineham. Thefe two elder Brothers dying thus without Male-Heirs, (3.) William, the t
2 CONC hird, and youngeft Son of Elias, was the chief Male-Heir, who propagated the Family. 
2 CONT *  This William Churchill had his Seat at Rockbear, in Devonfhire.  Who his Wife was, I do not find ; But he left Iffue Giles
2 CONT * http://www.archive.org/stream/lifeofjohndukeof01lediiala#page/5/mode/1up
2 CONT *Churchill, Efq; who was Father of ''''''Charles Churchill, Efq;  This Charles Churchill was engaged by ____ Courtney, Earl of Devonfhire, in the Caufe of King Edward IV. And, when Thomas Courtney, Earl of Devonfhire, forfook the 
2 CONC Interefts his Father had efpoufed, continuing faithful, that Prince took him into his Favour, and advanced his Fortune, by procuring him, in Marriage, Margaret, only Daughter and Heirefs of Sir William Widville, who brought him a 
2 CONC confiderable Eftate.'''''' 
2 CONT *''''''   By this Margaret, Charles Churchill had Iffue'''''', Thomas Churchill, Efq; who married Grace, Daughter and Coheirefs of Thomas Tylle, of Tylle-Houfe, in Cornwal. He was fucceeded by William, his Son and Heir, who marrie
2 CONC d Mary, the eldeft Daughter of Richard Cruefe, of Wicroft-Caftle, in Devonfhire, Efq; 
2 CONT *_____________________
