2 NOTE
3 CONT English: Remnants of chest-tomb of Sir Robert Poyntz (d.1520) lord of the manor of Iron Acton in Gloucestershire, in the Gaunt's Chapel, Bristol, in which he had built the Poyntz Chapel. He married Margaret Woodville, the illegiti
3 CONC mate daughter and only child of Anthony Woodville, 2nd Earl Rivers (c. 1440-1483), Knight of the Garter (brother of Queen Elizabeth Woodville who married King Edward IV), by his mistress Gwenlina Stradling, a daughter of William S
3 CONC tradling of St Donat's Castle in Glamorgan, Wales. The shields display left: the arms of Poyntz of 4 quarters: 1:Poyntz; 2:de Acton; 3:Clanvowe; 4:FitzNichol ([[John MacLean (historian) |Maclean, Sir John]] & Heane, W.C., (Eds.), 
3 CONC The Visitation of the County of Gloucester Taken in the Year 1623 by Henry Chitty and John Phillipot as Deputies to William Camden Clarenceux King of Arms, etc, London, 1885, p.130); right: Poyntz with 4 quarters as left, quarteri
3 CONC ng in addition Woodville and that family's own quarterings. 5th quarter is Woodville with baton sinister for bastardy; 6:Scales: Gules, six escallops or (Burkes General Armory, 1884[1]), an heiress of Woodville.
3 CONT Date	Shield painted c.1520, restored; photo c.2014
