1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===John Gould===
2 CONT * Birth:	Circa 1476 - Of, Staverton, Devonshire, England
2 CONT * Death:	After 1524
2 CONT * Parents:	Thomas Gould, Elinor Staverton
2 CONT * Married: Katherine Preston
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT * Thomas (m. Joan Ball), 
2 CONT * Robert (m. Elizabeth Petre)
2 CONT *  James (d. bef. 1558)
2 CONT *  Richard (m. Margaret Petre)
2 CONT * John (d.1562)
2 CONT *  Agnes (m. John Bagwell)
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://archive.org/stream/notesqueriesfor00unkngoog#page/n112/mode/2up 58. "Golde-Strechleigh of Seaborough. Somerset, And Ermington, South Devon"]   Notes and Queries for Somerset and Dorset ..., Volumes 7-8.  J. C. Sawtel
2 CONC l, 1901 - Somerset (England).  Page 91:
2 CONT
2 CONT >The history of the Golde family of Seaborough, from their first settlement there in the thirteenth century, down to their extinction in the main descent at the conclusion of the sixteenth, and their immediate descendants, contain
2 CONC s much of an interesting nature .... The grandson of this last John Golde, Thomas Golde, of Seaborough, who died 5 May, 1502,— he married Eleanor—who was living in 1522-4. They had three sons, Thomas, the heir, of whom presently,—
2 CONC John and James.
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''John Golde or Gould''', second son, was of Staverton in South Devon, having married Katherine, the daughter of Richard Preston, of that place, and from them proceeded the Dorsetshire and Exeter, &c, descents. They appear to ha
2 CONC ve used different arms from those belonging to the main line at Seaborough, which were, Or, on a chevron between three roses gules, as many bunches of grapes, or rose leaves of the first,—and gave, Per saliire azure and or, a lion
2 CONC  rampant counterchanged.
2 CONT
2 CONT _________________
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=NuBBAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA62&lpg=PA62&dq=thomas+Gould+1511&source=bl&ots=swMw_J-ZQG&sig=SvxHodp4VoLSQFMDXHMPa4RHJ6Q&hl=en&sa=X&ei=UixyVarKNsmiNuSUgNAH&ved=0CCcQ6AEwAw#v=onepage&q&f=true "Pedigree of Go
2 CONC uld"] Visitation of England and Wales, Volume 5  edited by Joseph Jackson Howard, Frederick Arthur Crisp.  Page 62.  '''John Gould of Staverton, co. Devon''' (eldest son of Thomas Gould of Seaborough, co. Somerset, who died 5 May 
2 CONC 1502) ; '''living 1522-24; died before 1526. = Katherine Preston, dau. of Richard Preston of Staverton. Will dated 21 February 1529 (Peculiar of Bishop of Exeter). ; ch: '''Thomas (m. Joan Ball), Robert (m. Elizabeth Petre) Gould,
2 CONC  (Pg.63 James (d. bef. 1558), Richard (m. Margaret Petre), John (d.1562), Agnes (m. John Bagwell) Gould)
2 CONT
2 CONT __________________________
2 CONT *'''John Gould1
2 CONT *'''M, #105129, b. circa 1476, d. before 1526
2 CONT *Father      Thomas Gould1 b. c 1437, d. 5 May 1502
2 CONT *Mother     Eleanor1 b. c 1449
2 CONT *'''     John Gould was born circa 1476 at of Staverton, Devonshire, England.1 He married Katherine Preston''', daughter of Richard Preston, '''circa 1510.1 John Gould died before 1526.1
2 CONT *'''Family      Katherine Preston''' b. c 1485, d. a 21 Feb 1529
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **James Gould+1 b. c 1517, d. b 13 Aug 1558
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S61] Unknown author, Family Group Sheets, Family History Archives, SLC.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p3500.htm#i105129 _______________
2 CONT *'''Notes & Queries for Somerset and Dorset (1901) Vol. VII.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/notesqueriesfor00unkngoog
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/notesqueriesfor00unkngoog#page/n113/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.91
2 CONT *   Ralph de Vallibus had one daughter and heiress, Grecia, who married Eudo de Rochford, and they settled the manor, &c, on their son John, who in the year 1320, disposed of it to John Golde, a presumed descendant of the Crusader
2 CONC , and at the time possessor of property there ; he presented to the rectory in 1341, and his grandson John Golde, gave a piece of land for the building of a new church at Seaborough, 3 Henry V, 1414-15. The edifice was considerabl
2 CONC y added to, and partially rebuilt in 1728. 
2 CONT *   The grandson of this last John Golde, Thomas Golde, of Seaborough, who died 5 May, 1502,— he married Eleanor — who was living in 1522-4. They had three sons, Thomas, the heir, of whom presently, — '''John''' and James. 
2 CONT *'''   John Golde or Gould, second son, was of Staverton in South Devon, having married Katherine, the daughter of Richard Preston, of that place, and from them proceeded the Dorsetshire and Exeter, &c, descents. They appear to ha
2 CONC ve used different arms from those belonging to the main line at Seaborough, which were. Or. on a chevon between three roses gules, as many bunches of grapes, or rose leaves of the first, — and gave, Per saltire azure and or, a lio
2 CONC n rampant counterchanged. 
2 CONT *   James Gould, third son, — he married Margaret daughter and coheir of Roger Appleton, and apparently sister to Edith, the wife of his brother Thomas. He died March 1529-30; and is described aa being of Henley in Crewkerne, the 
2 CONC estate on which his nephew John Gould, was murdered in 1555 : the owner and occupier at the date of that event being John Weeks, or Wyke, From them descended the families of Gould of Wilts, and London. 
2 CONT *   Thomas Golde, or Gould, eldest son and heir, aged thirty at his father's death. He married Edith, daughter and coheir of Roger Appleton. By her he had one son and heir John, and four daughters, Margaret, Katherine, Alice, and 
2 CONC Anne. He died 13 Sep. 1525, and was buried in Crewkerne Church, where, on the south wall of the chancel is a brass to his memory.  .... etc. ____________________________________
