1 TITL Dr.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert Old was the son of John Old and the husband of Dorothy Granger. He served in King Philip's War and participated in Turner's Falls Fight under Capt. William Turner. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=40372471
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Old (or Ould) married Susannah and had by her 9 children, one of whom, Mindwell, was the first thite child born in Suffield.  Susannah died 1/6/1688, and he married Dorothy Granger.  He died Jan. 16, 1728 and a small slab i
2 CONC n the old burying-ground marks his grave.  His ancestry is unkown.  He was never a freeman.  He practiced medicine and was called doctor, though probably not strictly deserving the title.  His last residence was at the corner of t
2 CONC he High Street and the road now leading to the railway station.  Some of his sons removed to W. Springfield  and Westfield, Mass., and were the ancestors of the Old's, or Olds as the names were later spelled, of those towns.  Besi
2 CONC des atttending to the suffereing, "Dr." Old sometimes occupied his time in making and laying brick.  The town records say:   At a legall meeting of the Inhabitants of Suffield January ye 27 1695-96:  it was agreed and voted, to em
2 CONC ploy Goodman Old in building the chimneys for the minister's house, and accordingly said Old did then promose and convenant to and with the towne to build a stock of chimneys in said house, with five tunnels; and to carry it up fr
2 CONC om the bottome of the celler; which chimneys he, the said Old, doth engage to build according to his best art and skill, and in all respects substantial, compleatm, and workmanlike, and to finishe the same by the middle of May nex
2 CONC t ensueing the date hereof," etc. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=mOgK8dM9qqUC&lpg=PA316&ots=ZhDpbdLMKe&dq=joanna%20adams%201634%20granger&pg=PA543#v=onepage&q=Old&f=false New England Marriages Prior to 1700] By Clarence Almon Torrey.  Page 543.  1/wife Susan
2 CONC  [Hanford] 31 Dec 1669
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=mOgK8dM9qqUC&lpg=PA316&ots=ZhDpbdLMKe&dq=joanna%20adams%201634%20granger&pg=PA316#v=onepage&q=Granger%20olds&f=false New England Marriages Prior to 1700] By Clarence Almon Torrey.  Page 316.  2
2 CONC /wife Dorothy Granger
2 CONT --------------------
