2 CONT Wikisource DNB: [http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Wenlock,_John_(DNB00)   WENLOCK, JOHN, Lord Wenlock] (d. 1471), was the son of William Wynell de Wenlock    probably married his second wife, Agnes, daughter of Sir John Danvers of Co
2 CONC thorpe in Oxfordshire, about 1467. He was her third husband, and after his death she married Sir John Say [q. v.], speaker of the House of Commons.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===================
2 CONT
2 CONT Little is known of Sir John’s early life. He married Elizabeth, daughter and heir of Laurence Cheyne of Fen Ditton in Cambridgeshire and settled at Broxbourne... .Say was knighted in 1464 and following his first wife’s death in 14
2 CONC 73 married Agnes, daughter of Sir John Danvers of Cothorpe, Oxfordshire. Sir John died on 12th April 1478, the year after his marriage. '''His second wife died within a few months and was buried with her first husband, Sir John Fr
2 CONC ay, at St Bartholomew-the-Great, London.'''http://www.mbs-brasses.co.uk/page111.html
2 CONT
2 CONT =======================
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John SAY 1449-1462, 1466-71 1477-8 Married for his first wife Elizabeth (widow of Frederick Tilney) daughter and heir of Laurence Cheynes of Fen Ditton, and lived at Broxbourne Herts... He married again in 1478 to Agnes daught
2 CONC er of Sir John Davers of Cothorpe, Oxfordshire (widow of Sir John Fray) died on 12th April 1478 the same year.' http://heraldry.9f.com/chanc.html
2 CONT
2 CONT =========
