1 NOTE {geni:about_me} When Sir William Tracy was born in 1501 in Toddington, Gloucestershire, England, his father, Willem, was 36 and his mother, Margaret, was 31. He married Lady Agnes Digby in 1519 in Coleshill, Warwickshire, England.
2 CONC  They had five children during their marriage. He died in September 1557 in Coleshill, Warwickshire, England, at the age of 56.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Tracy_(JP)
2 CONT
2 CONT William Tracy (died 1530) was an English justice of the peace and prominent early Lutheran convert. After his death both his will and his remains became caught up in the struggle around the Protestant Reformation in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT By his wife Margaret, daughter of Sir Thomas Throckmorton, William Tracy had issue two sons, William and Richard. William, the elder, inherited the Toddington estates, and was great-grandfather of Sir John Tracy, in 1642–43 create
2 CONC d Baron and Viscount Tracy of Rathcoole in the peerage of Ireland. Robert Tracy, the judge, was younger son of the second viscount.[2] The peerage became extinct on the death of Henry Leigh Tracy, 8th Viscount Tracy on 29 April 17
2 CONC 97.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/205218202/william-tracy
