2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT <strong>PYE, Robert (c.1586-1662), of St. Stephen's Court, Westminster and Richmond, Surr.; later of Faringdon, Berks.</strong>
2 CONT
2 CONT === Family and Education ===
2 CONT b. c.1586, 5th but 2nd surv. s. of Roger Pye (d.1591) of the Mynde, Much Dewchurch, Herefs. and Bridget (d.1624), da. of Thomas Kyrle of Walford, Herefs.; bro. of Walter I*. educ. M. Temple 1607. m. by 1620, Mary (bur. 5 Jan. 1654
2 CONC ), da. of John Croker of Batsford, Glos., 3s. 2da. kntd. 13 July 1621. d. May 1662. sig. Robert Pye.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Offices Held ===
2 CONT Servant, household of William Spencer, 2nd Lord Compton by 1614-16, George Villiers, earl (later 1st duke) of Buckingham by 1617, recvr. by 1620-at least 1624, commr. of finances by 1623-at least 1627, solicitor until ?1626.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clerk of the patents, Chancery, 1618-25 (jt.); auditor of the receipt and writer of tallies, Exchequer 1620-?54, 1660-2; commr. revenue 1620, 1626; collector, Palatine benevolence 1622, Privy Seal loans, merchant strangers 1625-6;
2 CONC  commr. navy 1625-8, prizes 1625, 1627 (French), sale of Crown lands 1626-at least 1627, St. Paul’s Cathedral repair 1631, treaty payments to Scots 1641.
2 CONT
2 CONT J.p. Westminster 1620-at least 1640, Mdx. 1625-at least 1642, Surr. 1625-42; commr. subsidy, Westminster 1621, 1624, 1625, 1628-9, 1641-2, Forced Loan 1627, charitable uses, Surr. 1630, Mdx. 1633-4, Berks. 1634, sewers, Berks. and
2 CONC  Oxon. 1634, view Blackwall docks, Kent 1635, maltsters, Surr. 1636; vestryman, St. Margaret’s Westminster 1642-at least 1659; sequestrator delinquents, Westminster 1643; commr. assessment, Westminster 1643, Berks., Herefs., Mdx.,
2 CONC  Oxon., Westminster 1647-8, volunteers, Mdx. 1643, assessment [I], Mdx. and Berks. 1643-4, execution of ordinances 1644, New Model ordinance, Mdx. and Westminster 1645, excise 1645, collegiate church of St. Peter, Westminster 1645
