2 CONT >The MD Bulldog mentions that Walter Pye, late of the West Indies, was Edward’s son. Since Edward’s children were all minors at the time of his death, this would not be possible. This same Walter died in 1699 and lists Edward’s ch
2 CONC ildren as nieces and nephews, showing that Walter was an uncle to the children and not a brother. Also, it was discovered that the term “late of” doesn’t indicate death, but instead shows the person is no longer in that place and 
2 CONC has moved on to another area.
