1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Price_(judge)#:~:text=He%20was%20appointed%20a%20judge,a%20Baron%20of%20the%20Exchequer. Wiki]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1em>On 23 September 1679 [Robert] Price married Lucy, eldest daughter and coheiress of Robert Rodd of Foxley in Yazor, Herefordshire, by Ann Sophia, only child of Thomas Neale of Warneford, Hampshire. Robert Rodd died two years la
2 CONC ter and Price inherited the Foxley estate. With her he had two sons and a daughter but in 1690, after her adultery with a cousin of hers (whom she bore a child), the couple separated without divorce, Price providing for her and th
2 CONC eir children throughout his life and in his will.
