0 @N6000000001877506092@ NOTE 1st Earl of Pembroke 8.9.1468 The first Welshman to become an earl (Welsh by language and by birth)
1 CONT summoned to Edward iv's first parliament as Sir William Herbert
1 CONT In high favour wth Edward iv who ordered him to trace his pedigree. A Norman ancestory was tacked on to his g g grandfather, tracing him back to Herbert, Chamberlain to Henry i. It was unfashionable to be Welsh
1 CONT To the Welsh he was known as Gwillim ddu
1 CONT Chepstow Castle was granted to him
1 CONT known as Black Will
1 CONT 1440 Seneschal of Uske and Carleon
1 CONT fought in Normandy with Matthew Gough
1 CONT 1449 KCB at Formiguy
1 CONT 1450 Gough and Herbert held Bayeux
1 CONT 1450 taken prisoner by the French at Battle of Formigny, the French victory ended English rule. Gough escaped but was killed a few months later by Jack Cade on London Bridge
1 CONT 14.10.1452 general pardon for Sir William Herbert of Raglan
1 CONT march 1456 helped to seize Hereford and forced Hereford JP to judicial murder of 6 townsmen for alledged killing his kinsman Walter Vaughan
1 CONT april 1456 with others he assaulted and robbed a servant of the Earl of Wiltshire
1 CONT aug 1456 with 2000 men took Carmarthen Castle and Edmund Tudor, and attacked Aberystwyth.
1 CONT apr 1457 Ordered to appear before king
1 CONT june 1457 was pardoned
1 CONT 22.5.1457 grant to Sir William of Gascon wine forfeit by him to the king in Bristol by reason of a treason adjudged against him in Hereford
1 CONT 7.6.1457 general pardon for Sir William
1 CONT 1459 Steward of Uske
1 CONT Feb 1459/60 offices of Sheriff of Glamorgan, Steward of Burgavenny & Lacey & Ewyas, Constable of Usk Castle
1 CONT 5.3.1459/60 Lordships of Usk & Caerleon
1 CONT june 1460 general pardon for treason
1 CONT 2.2.1461At battle of Mortimer's Cross
1 CONT 8.5.1461 Chief Justice & chamberlain of S Wales, Steward & Chief Forester of Carmarthenshire and Cardiganshire
1 CONT 1461 Steward of Brechnock Castle
1 CONT may 1461 grant of town, castle and lordship of Newport
1 CONT Aug 1461 Patent Rolls, commission to take County of Pembroke including Dunster Castle from Jasper Tudor, Earl of Pembroke, a rebel
1 CONT 12.8.1461 commission to enquire into treasons in S Wales
1 CONT sept 1461 commission to take lands during minority of son and heir of Duke of Buckingham; ordered to take all of Earl of Stafford's lands in S Wales into the King's hands, 3 days after Earl of Warwick was given this command - Will
1 CONC iam was made steward and in effect ruled until 1469
1 CONT 7.9.1461 grant during minority to include Steward of castle and lordship of Brecon
1 CONT 1462 KG
1 CONT 3.2.1461/62 grant for good service against the king's enemies many properties including Magor, Redwick, Caldicot and Pembroke
1 CONT march 1461/62 commission to take ships within port of Bristol
1 CONT grant of Lordship of Llanstephan
1 CONT grant of castles Lordships of Crickhowell & Tretower
1 CONT 1462/63 Baron Herbert of Gower together with the town and castle of Cilgerian for services against Henry vi and the rebels
1 CONT 1463 Chief Justice of N Wales
1 CONT 12.6.1463 the king releases all claim to Crickhowell and Tretower, now held in chief, previously from the king
1 CONT 16.6.1463 grant of lands Devon, Somerset and Suffolk, forfeit by Sir James Luttrell
1 CONT 17.6 1463 Chief justice of Merioneth and Constable of Harlech and Merioneth
1 CONT oct 1464 commission re Hardelach (Harlech?) and county Merioneth
1 CONT 26.9.1466 grant of towns, lordships and manors of Herefordshire, Gloucestershire and S Wales
1 CONT aug 1468 took Harlech Castle together with Jasper Tudor and Henry Tudor (later to be Henry vii). Henry was held prisoner and Wiliam planned to marry Hery to his daughter Maud, but this failed
1 CONT 12.9.1468 grant of castle, manor and lordship of Chepstow and lands of Tudenham
1 CONT feb 1468/69 trustee of Sudeley castle
1 CONT John Donne to be keeper of castle and lordship during William H's minority
1 CONT Yorkist
1 CONT 1468 relieved Harlech
1 CONT At battle of Mortimer's Cross
1 CONT 26.7.1469 Taken at Battle of Edgcot
1 CONT 28.7.1469 beheaded at Northampton
1 CONT buried Prior Church Abergavenny or at Tintern
1 CONT monument in Llantilio Gosseney church
1 CONT will executor Dame Anne
1 CONT Source GWH 1
