0 @N6000000001877506127@ NOTE Sir
1 CONT of Troy
1 CONT May 1486 Rent (?) from Uske from many incl Sir Walter H & Wm H of Troy
1 CONT 1490 Sir Walter (1B) released his rights to the lands of his uncle Thos to Wm H of Troy his brother
1 CONT 1492 Steward of Ebboth
1 CONT 1493-1500 Wm of Troy Exchange of lands
1 CONT 1499 leased Grossmont demesne & was Receiver there
1 CONT Oct 1501 Commission to many incl Wm H of Troy & Sh of Herefords re riots & trespass at Wylton Castle, Herefords
1 CONT 1504 Release of Chepstow etc, ex E of Huntingdon, by Wm H of Troy to Sir Walter H
1 CONT 1504 Recog by Sir Walter H (1B), Wm H of Troy, & Henry Mile of Newport, 500 marks. Walter to keep the peace for himself.
1 CONT June 1504 Commission (de Wallis et fossatis) issued to Sir Walter H Kt, Sir Geo H Kt, William H esq & others (GWH suggests brothers ie Caldicot, St Julians & Troy)
1 CONT 1507 / 08 Release of manors, Chepstow etc, ex Wm E of Huntingdon by Wm H of Troy & Blanche his wife
1 CONT July 1508 Commission to many incl Wm H Esq as Justices in Eyre, Lps of Usk Trelleck & Caerlleon - to meet at Usk
1 CONT 13.4.1510 - king's payments included to Wm H of Troy
1 CONT June 1510 Pardons granted to ... Wm H of Troy (16th May)
1 CONT 1514 Abbot of Tintern granted Stewardship of abbey lands to Sir Wm & Chas
1 CONT Aug 1515 - Commission of Peace - Usk, Caerlion & Trillick in Wm H of Troy
1 CONT Sep 1515 - Commission re fishery at Caerlion - Sir Wm H of Troy, Walter H (1c1) & 7 others receivers of Lordships of Uske & Caerleon
1 CONT 1516 (after Easter) Knighted William H of Troy Sheriff of Herefordshire
1 CONT 1517 / 18 Prioress of Usk granted Stewardship of priory lands to Sir Wm of Troy & his sons Chas & Thos for their lives
1 CONT 1517 / 18 Pior of Monmouth granted Stewardship of his lands Monmouth & 3 castles to Sir Wm
1 CONT 1518 refers to grant of stewardship of lands ex dissolved priory of Usk to Sir William H Knt & to Charles H his son. The case was by Thos of Worceser asking for it
1 CONT Nov 1519 - lease of site of Troy Magna, late of E of March, for 21 years to Sir Wm H of Troy
1 CONT 1520 E of Worcs Receivers A/Cs. Receiver of Lps of Chepstow, Tidenham, Caldicot & Wyesham was Sir Wm H of Troy
1 CONT 1523 Wonaston Manor belonged to Sir Wm H. He left it in his will to his wife Blanche.
1 CONT 16.4.1524 Sir Chas Somerset attained of office of Master Sgt of Lps of Monmouth, Grossmont, Whitecastle & Skenrith now in the king's hands through the death of Sir Wm H
1 CONT Their son Sir Charles directed in his will (1557) that the estate should be sold. Probably bought by his brother Sir Thomas
1 CONT will dated 15.3.1523 / 24 refers to w. Margery, present w. Blanche, eldest son Charles, younger son Thomas, base son Richard
1 CONT proved 15.4.1524
1 CONT Source GWH 1 / 1G
