1 CONT 2 undated cases re pasture at Usk, parish of Llangevewe. In one he is of Chepstow and the other of Wallston, co. Glos. Woolaston and Tidenham are neighbouring villages between the Wye and Severn and next to Chepstow
1 CONT 25.1.1537/38 Sir Rice Mansell to Cromwell re letter from E of Worcs who said that Walter H and Watkin H had taken a ship to Chepstow on his orders so Sir R.M. could take no further action. ( Must be Walter of St Julians, 1st cousi
1 CONC n of Watkin)
1 CONT 3.5.1538 Letter - E of Worcs to Cromwell. Defense of Watkin H
1 CONT Nov 1555 Pardon to Walter H late of Tyddenham, Glos, gent, for debt £40 - outlawed for non appearance, surrendered to Fleet Prison - pardoned.
1 CONT Officers of E of Worcs 1526 - 49 Watkin H Steward of Chepstow & Tidenham
