0 @N6000000001877504920@ NOTE Sir  kt
1 CONT of St Julians
1 CONT 1549 Knighted
1 CONT Lease to inhabitants of Llantilio Perthday of the chapel etc, witnesses incl Walter H Knt "Steward of our court of Abergavenny" - possibly 1516
1 CONT 1534 / 35 - letter re council of Marches - saying that there were living unpunished many thieves and murderers under the protection of Sir Walter H, Lordship of Magor. One of the murderers is Thomas H the elder, outlawed, proclaim
1 CONC ed a rebellion and fined £100
1 CONT Went with H viii to siege of Boulogne
1 CONT 1509 - 47 History of the Star Chamber -
1 CONT Compl. Jane Carne (for Roger C ) Def. Walter H et al Murder of compl's husband at Sully
1 CONT Compl. Rich. Hore Def. Walter H et al False imprisonment, and seizure of ship and cargo at Cardiff
1 CONT Def. Walter H customs officer Seizure of 7 tuns of wine
1 CONT Compl Walter H Def Sir Wm Morgan Abetting felonies
1 CONT Compl Geo ap Morgan Def Walter & Wm H (poss his son) Riots and assaults
1 CONT Compl Walter & Wm H Def Geo ap Morgan Breach of the peace
1 CONT Def Walter H Subornation of perjury
1 CONT Compl Walter H Def Wm Morgan Jones Taking of escheats and felons goods, Lordship of Newport
1 CONT Compl Henry Morgan, priest Def Walter H Seizure of corn at Rectory St. Bride Wentlooge and assaults and damage church of Mynnydd Islwyn
1 CONT Compl Sir Wm Morgan Def Walter H Murders, riots and rape
1 CONT 1516 Royal Household including Gentleman Usher
1 CONT 1530 granted surveyorship of E of Worcs lands ex Tintern Abbey
1 CONT mid 1530s appears to have acted as "chef juge" (presumably Dep Sheriff) of Glam under E of Worcs
1 CONT 28.2.1533 The Abbot of Llantarnam persuaded Sir Wm H to withdraw from Newport to prevent armed conflict between the Hs of St Julians and the Morgans of Pencoed
1 CONT The reference is to Llantarnam Abbey by a sister of the order of St Joseph)
1 CONT Sir Wm presumably Sir Walter
1 CONT Sir Wm Morgan of Pencoed conducted IPM 1567 on his kinsman Wm H of St J's, Sir Walter's son - Feud presumably healed
1 CONT 10.4.1535 - letter to Cromwell from Cardiff Castle - Refutes the charge that he took grain (and ship) intended for troops in Ireland. Ship taken (by 40 commons incl some of his servants) and brought before him as "the king's deput
1 CONC y in the lordship"
1 CONT 25.1.1537 / 38 Sir Rice Mansell to Cromwell re letter of E of Worcs saying that Walter H and Watkin H had taken ship to Chepstow "on his command", therefore he, Sir RM, could take no further action
1 CONT Letter re Walter & Wm H from Sir Wm Morgan (Commissioner of the Marches & Chief Officer of the District) to Cromwell in support of the case in Star Chamber (see above) re running battle between Wa H & Wm H and George ap Morgan. Jo
1 CONC hn Sisillt, Walter H's servant, murdered Roger David Tewe in Newport - Geo ap Morg, as one of officers of Wenlocke and Newport, seized murderers good - Walter H gathered a number of men - breach of the peace prevented by Sir Wm Mo
1 CONC rg - on 23rd Feb last Wm H struch Geo ap Morg - on 27th Feb with an inordinate company assaulted Geo ap Morg and an honest man John Thomas was murdered.
1 CONT from 1535 steward of lordship of Caldicot & receiver
1 CONT Oct 1536 Sale of Llandough by E of Worcs to Sir Ed Carne
1 CONT 1537 A note Cts of Marches ordered Walter to send them "a strong thief" in his custody, a nephew of Ed Lewis. Walter repied they should ask E of Worcs. Council reprimanded them both. Walter then sent him, with a letter from Worcs 
1 CONC taking responsibility
1 CONT Oct 1537 Letter shows Walter as Deputy Steward to E of Worcs
1 CONT 3.5.1538 further to the above Walter sore sick so E of Worcs sent "bearer" as rep
1 CONT Cardiff Records - Rich Hore (Master of ship Valentine) charged Eof Worcs and his agent Walter H of Chepstow. Walter had seized a ship and cargo in Cogan Pill - "Portugees" escaped, one died - Here arrested for causing the death
1 CONT 7.1.1540 Armed retainers murder a Carne ( 2years after the attack on Roger Carne - see court cases above). It was clear that W instigated - they flee to Cardiff and on to Newport Castle
1 CONT Jan 1539 / 40 Letter Lee to Cromwell - a deposition taken Feb 1539 / 40 re death of John Carne on wed after epiphany, killed by servants of Walter H for ploughing the land of Parissheley for which Herbert had refused to pay him re
1 CONC nt
1 CONT 1539 - 40 Officers of E of Worcs - Walter H of St Julians - Receiver of his lands in Glam
1 CONT 1541 / 42 Sheriff of Mars (?)
1 CONT 1542 Sheriff of Monmouths
1 CONT 1543 JP
1 CONT Bishop Lee in his 1st yr of presidency of Wales to Cromwell - Malefactors protected by Walter H in the Lordship of Magor, Steward under E of Worcs - Murderers & others now servants of Sir Walter - 43 in all incl 5 Herberts
1 CONT 1544 - army against France - Monmouth's muster book incl Walter H
1 CONT 1545 MP
1 CONT 1549 Kntd
1 CONT 1550 Sheriff - but died before completion
1 CONT will dated Sept 1550 - To Dame Sycill Monyngton my wife .... unless she be vexatious. Mentions son William, daughter Joan, 2 other daughters, son George, son Harry, overseers to the will Sir William H kt & nephew Matthew H esq (of
1 CONC  Coldbrook)
1 CONT Will left mansion house at Dunraven to his wife
1 CONT buried Woollos Church, Newport
1 CONT Proved Feb 1550 / 51
1 CONT Source GWH 1C / 1C1
