0 @N6000000003275850154@ NOTE [Lurene Family File 7 Copy #2.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT Timothy Rives is mentioned by Hutchins as a Gent. of the Paris h of St. Mary Magdalene in Oxford City and as a Steward of the U niversity of Oxford.
1 CONT He was apparently an orphan and an only child.
1 CONT Timothy's death and burial are mentioned in Wood's "Survey of th e Antiquities of Oxford". This indicates that he was a man of pr ominence.
1 CONT It seems likely that young Timothy may have owed his prefermen t at Oxford to two of his Kinsmen: Dr. George Ryves (Chancello r of Oxford in 1601 and Warden of New College in 1599), and Si r William Ryves (Chancellor at Law in 161
1 CONC 5 and J.P. of the Paris h of St. Mary Magdalene in 1618).
