0 @N6000000001877493584@ NOTE of Troy Parva
1 CONT Steward of Duchy of Lancaster & receiver
1 CONT 1526 - 49 Officers of E of Worcs - Chas H of Troy Steward of Monmouth & Wyesham
1 CONT 1533 Officers at coronation of Ann Boleyn "Kts & Gents to be servitors" incl Chas H of Troy
1 CONT 1533 - 35 Defendant Charles H Knt land parish of Monmouth
1 CONT Jan 1534 / 35 List of 21 prominent people re tithes Diocese of Llandaff incl Chas, Walter, George, Rich
1 CONT Feb 1538 / 39 Commission to defend coast of S Wales incl Chas H
1 CONT Undated but presumed to be 1539 "The New Bodyguard" "the names of the Spears numbered 1-50" incl Chas H
1 CONT 1540 There used to be a window in Wonaston church raised by Sir Chas of Troy and his wife Elizabeth
1 CONT Nov 1540 Sheriffs Roll Monmouths Chas H - selected
1 CONT Sheriff 1541 & 1549 Monmouths
1 CONT June 1542 JP Monmouth - also shown on list of 1547 & 1555 but not in 1558 / 89
1 CONT 1543 / 44 Commission of Peace Monmouths incl Chas H
1 CONT 1544 Muster Book for army against France. Monmouths incl Chas H
1 CONT Also Persons to go in person into France incl "Pensioners ... Chas H, 7 horsemen & 4 archers"
1 CONT Also "Chas H who hath the charge of bearing the king's standard ... for so long as the king is the field"
1 CONT 1545 King's household
1 CONT Knighted between 1545 & 1549
1 CONT 1547 - 51 Defendant was servant to Charles H esq Sheriff of Monmouthshire
1 CONT Dec 1548 Nominated for Sheriff of Mons - pricked
1 CONT 1551 Comm to collect tax Mons incl Sir Chas H
1 CONT Nov 1551 Nominated for Sheriff of Herfords - Sir Chas H pricked
1 CONT March 1552 JP Radnor
1 CONT May 1553 Comm re possessions of Chapels etc Mons incl Sir Chas H
1 CONT MP 1553 & Jan 1545
1 CONT 1553 reference to Sir Chas H as steward of the manor of Uske
1 CONT 1575 Riots & forcible entry to lands late seized of Sir Chas H Knt & Thos H esq (1G3) at Llanthomas
1 CONT Will dated 1552 mentions dau Joan, base son Watkin, brother Thomas, wife Cecil. mother Dame Blanche. Exors wife Cecil, Edward of Montgomery & William of Coldbrook
1 CONT Proved 1557
1 CONT Source GWH 1G / 1G1
0 @N6000000001877504840@ NOTE Sir
1 CONT of Wonastowe
1 CONT
1 CONT Source GWH 1F4A1 & 1G3Sir  Knt
1 CONT of Wonastow
1 CONT Sir Thos probably bought Wonastow from his brother Chas. Thos lived there and passed it to his son Henry
1 CONT Sept 1529 Pardon for the murder of Wm Vaughan of Bristol, to Wm H of Cardiff (either Wm E of Pembroke 1F1 or Wm of Cardiff 1F2B), Thos jun of Moorgrange (3D), Thos of Troy (presum this one) & John H of Bristol (who may be this one
1 CONC 's brother)
1 CONT Norton in Skenfrith granted at the Dissolution to Sir Thos of W. It was the residence of Watkin (base son of Sir Chas of Troy) & his descendants
1 CONT JP Monmouths prob 1542 - 84 (not on list 1591)
1 CONT Feb 1543 Commiss of Peace Monmouths incl Thos H
1 CONT 1545 / 46 Obtained Parc Grace Dieu probably incl 2 farms called the Hendre in Llangattock
1 CONT lease dated July 1545 to Thos H of Winoscoe & Wm Brereton £517-8-4 site of Grace Dieu & lands at Llangattock, Trehurgan, Skenfrith, Monmouth, Llantillis & Llanvihangell (also Hunts, Notts, Beds, London, Cambridge, Norfolk & Salop 
1 CONC (Culmington)
1 CONT 1551 Comm to collect tax incl Thos H
1 CONT May 1553 Comm to collect possessions of chapels etc Mons incl Thos H
1 CONT MP Monmouths 1554 - 55 & 1559 - 62
1 CONT Dec 1555 Grant to Thos H esq, for £296 land Skenfrith, Whitecastell & Penfhos all formerly Priory of Grace Dieu to holf for 1/4 of knts fee as of the Manor of Estgrenewicke in fee soccage
1 CONT c 1557 mentioned in will of brother Sir Chas of Troy
1 CONT 1571 / 72 Def Thos H of Mynystowe (Monmouth) Sheriff. Attempting to secure election of his son as MP (Henry?)
1 CONT Nov 1574 Appointment of commission to enquire re Tanners, County of Monmouth Sir Thos H, Town of Monmouth, the Mayor and Sir Thos H
1 CONT 1575 Riots & forcible entry to lands late seized of Sir Chas H Knt (1G1) & Thos H esq at Llanthomas
1 CONT Undated - Def Sir Thos H Knt & Wm Mason. Outcome of an affray at Monmouth between Wm Vaughan & Def. Compl is the widow of a servant of Thos H who was killed. This is an appeal against the corrupt way. Def negotiated on the widow's
1 CONC  behalf.
1 CONT Lease to Lewis H of Chepstow (3A2A) incl refs to land of Thos H of Wonastow in Chepstow.
1 CONT 1576 Site of Abbey of Grace Dieu granted to Thos H & Wm Bretton (see 1545/46)
1 CONT 1582 Gt & Lt Beaulieu held on lease by Anne (of Hadnock 3A1A) from Sir THos of Wonastow
1 CONT Will dated 30.10.1588 Refers to sons Edmund, Harrie, William, Edward, to daughters of my son Harry, Elinor, Christian, Elizabeth, Joan & to William his son (under 21), to Charles the son of my Charles to maintain him at school
1 CONT Proved 26.11.1588
1 CONT Source GWH 1G / 1G3
