0 @N6000000001877506065@ NOTE 1st Earl of Pembroke cr. oct 1551
1 CONT Lord Herbert of Cardiff
1 CONT A cutting suggests that he could neither read nor write. Described as a bonny red haired Welshman with sharp eyes and a stern look, also grasping, scheming and ambitious, with great influence at court
1 CONT Introduced to court by Earl of Worcester
1 CONT Had large estates in England and Wales.
1 CONT Amongst those appointed to receive Anne of Cleves
1 CONT 1527 fled to France after 2 days of affrays - young hooligans from Wales
1 CONT Returned to England
1 CONT married Anne Parr circa 1534
1 CONT 1539 Annuity £11/13/4
1 CONT 1540 Queen's household, Anne of Cleves - Gentlewoman of the Privy Chamber, Mistress Herbert
1 CONT july 1540 chief steward of lands of Wilton Monastery
1 CONT 1541 jewels given by king to Queen Catherine Howard handed to Anne Parr for safekeeping
1 CONT 1542 or 1544 Following the Dissolution of the Monasteries bought Wilton and the lordships of Monmouthshire
1 CONT july 1543 Hviii married Katherine Parr, sister of Anne, both William and Anne at the small wedding - henceforth favours showered upon him
1 CONT 1543 Knight Bachelor
1 CONT 1544 Captain of town and castle of Aberystwyth and Carmarthen
1 CONT 1546 gent of privy chamber
1 CONT received Baynards Castle, Cardiff Castle and estates, and the manor of Hendon
1 CONT 1547 helped to surpress Western Rising
1 CONT Executor of Hviii
1 CONT PC to Evi
1 CONT 1548 KG
1 CONT 1548-52 Master of the Horse
1 CONT 1549 led the forces to put down Wyatt's rebellion
1 CONT 1549 KG
1 CONT 1550-53 & 1555-58 President of the Council of Wales
1 CONT 6.7.1553 Evi died. William involved in making Lady Jane Grey Queen but withdrew just in time
1 CONT William married his son to her sister as part of the plot
1 CONT 1554 Governor of Calais
1 CONT 1557 Captain General  of  the English army in France
1 CONT 1562 in highest favour with Ei
1 CONT 1566 out of favour - pleaded to Ei fot Duke of Norfolk who was only offering advice on marriage
1 CONT 1567 Lord High Steward of the Household
1 CONT sept 1569 appeared to be implicated in plot to marry Duke of Norfolk to Mary Queen of Scots - put under house arrest
1 CONT nov 1569 JP for Devon, Lord Lt for Somerset and Wiltshire, and in command of 15000 men
1 CONT On his death he was mourned by the Welsh whose leader he was and whose language he spoke
1 CONT He took pride in his Welsh descent and his command of the language
1 CONT died in office at Court
1 CONT buried St Paul's Cathedral
1 CONT Source  Herbert and Clive family tree - National Trust
1 CONT GWH 1F / 1F1
1 CONT www.thepeerage.com
1 CONT www.stirnet.com
1 CONT rootsweb turner-thomas
