0 @N6000000008630690783@ NOTE I031378 Name: George Hastings 1 2 Sex: M Birth: ABT 1488 Death: 24 MAR 1543/44 Burial: Stoke Poges, BKM, ENG Note:
1 CONT BARONY OF HUNGERFORDV. 5.BARONY OF HASTINGS OF HASTINGSIII. 3. EARLDOM OF HUNTINGDONXVIII. 1. GEORGE (HASTINGS) (of Hastings), LORD HASTINGS (of Hastings) [1461], and LORD HASTINGS (of Hungerford) [1482], son and heir of Edward, L
1 CONC ORD HASTINGS (of Hastings) and LORD HASTINGS (of Hungerford), by Mary, suo jure BARONESS BOTRFAUX [1368], BARONESS HUNGERFORD [1426], and BARONESS MOLEYNS [14451, was born 1488; K.B. 17 November 1501; succeeded to his father's pee
1 CONC rage between 4 and 15 November 1506, and was summoned to Parliament, by writs directed Georgio Hastynges de Hastynges, from 17 October 1509 to 3 November 1529; was at the taking of Thérouenne and Tournay in 1513; P.C. to Henry VII
1 CONC I, by whorn he was created, 8 December 1529, EARL OF HUNTINGDON, with an annuity of £20. He succeeded on his mother's death, 10 July 1533, as LORD BOTREAUX, LORD HUNGERFORD, and LORD MOLEYNS. In 1536 he was in command against the 
1 CONC rebels in the rising called "the Pilgrimage of Grace." He married, about December 1509, Anne, widow of Sir Walter HERBERT, [who died 16 September 1507), and daughter of Henry (STAFFORD), 2nd DUKEof BUCKINGHAM, by Catherine (sister
1 CONC  of Elizabeth, the Queen Consort), daughter of Richard (WYDVILLE), EARL RIVERS. He died 24 March 1543/4, and was buried at Stoke Pogis, Bucks. Will, in which he directs his burial to be at Ashby-de-la-Zouch, co. Leicester, where h
1 CONC e had lived, dated 13 June 1534. Admonishment 5 February 1560/1. His wife survived him, holding in dower Stoke Pogis, where she was buried. [CP 6:654-5, 14:395]
1 CONT
