0 @N6000000008630690747@ NOTE : Francis Hastings , Sir 1 2 Sex: M Birth: ABT 1514 Death: 23 JUN 1560 in Ashby-de-la-Zouch, LEI, ENG Burial: Ashby-de-la-Zouch, LEI, ENG Note:
1 CONT BARONY OF HASTINGS OF HASTINGSIV. 4. EARLDOM OF HUNTINGDONXIX. 2. FRANCIS (HASTINGS), EARL OF HUNTINGDON, &c., son and heir, born about 1514; styled LORD HASTINGS 1529-44; K.B. 29 May 1533; carried Saint Edward's staff at the Coro
1 CONC nation of Edward VI, 20 February 1546/7; KG. 24 April 1549. Lord Lieutenant of Rutland 1550-59, of co. Leicester 1551-60, of co. Derby 1552-60, and of co. Warwick 1551-59. P.C. 4 September 1550. Though at first concerned in opposi
1 CONC ng the accession of Queen Mary, he came over to her side and took the Duke of Suffolk prisoner. He was in 1558 Captain of the Vanguard forces to the Queen. In 1559 Ile was Master of the Harthounds. He married (indenture 20, for ma
1 CONC rriage before St. James the Apostle, 25 June 1531) Catherine, eldest daughter and coheir of Henry (POLE), LORD MONTAGUE, by Jane, daughter of George (NEVILL), LORD ABERGAVENNY. He died 23 June 1560, aged about 47, and was buried a
1 CONC t Ashby-de-la-Zouch; M.I. His widow, whose claim dejure hereditario to the Crown was by many considered good, died 23 September 1576, and was buried with him. [CP 6:655-6]
1 CONT Father: George Hastings </cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=utzing&id=I031378> b: ABT 1488 Mother: Anne Stafford </cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=utzing&id=I028527> b: ABT 1493Marriage 1 Catherine Pole </cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=utzing&id=I03
