0 @N6000000001877504097@ NOTE of Crindan
1 CONT Brother William's will 1567 - tenement in Llantarnam
1 CONT Brother George of Newport - Bark "The Stephen", £100 and all my salt
1 CONT Sir Wm of St Julians will dated 1587 left immense properties to his daughter Mary provided that she married a Herbert. If not, the estate would pass to Miles' sons William, William, Thomas, Edward
1 CONT His fathers will does not mention Miles
1 CONT 1580 Defs Sir Wm H kt, sheriff (1C1A1), Miles H & Rees H (not identified) et al. Misuse of powers & cruel assault on compl and his servants
1 CONT 1583 Compl Andrew Morgan gent of Newport. Defs Sir Wm H kt (St Julians), Wm Williams, Miles H JP et al Dispute re bridge at Newport, over Usk (wooden 15 arches) - collapsed - JPs to rebuild - Miles H appointed so as to enlist aid 
1 CONC of Herberts. He converted gifts unto himself. With the aid of Sir Wm H kt constable of castle of Newport induced corrupt election.
1 CONT Source GWH 1C1 / 1C1D
0 @N6000000001877495558@ NOTE of Newport
1 CONT Fathers will 1550 left lands at Tintern and my shipp The James
1 CONT Defs George H & others accused of smuggling on the coast of Glam & Monmouths to value of 2000 marks
1 CONT Customs duties circumvented by gentry who liked wines. Geo H owned a bark "The Green Dragon" which transgressed the regulations each time it left port - its cargo usually wheat carried down the Severn in barges from Gos & Hereford
1 CONC s.
1 CONT MP Monmouths 1562 - 72
1 CONT Brother William's will dated 1566 - lands in Glam & leases Anglesey & Carnarvon
1 CONT Nov 1575 grant to Geo H, exor of Wm Morgan dec'd, of wardship & marriage of Wm H (1c1a1) s & h/o Wm H & Jane his wife with annuity of 40s from 22nd July 2-3 Ph & M when Jane died (Wm (1c1a)'s will "to my bro Geo the lease of my so
1 CONC n Wm's lands...from Ct of Wards...in Anglesea & Carnarvon")
1 CONT will dated 26.9.1580 - left most of his possessions to Sir Wm of St Julians incl lands Monmouthshire, gold chain of £200, ship called The Green Dragon, 1000 marks. To my brother Myles my bark called The Stephen, £100 and all my sa
1 CONC lt. Mentions sister Cecill Matthews, Walter H s/o Alice Jaynes, my sister Barbara who was also exor. Also Jane d/o Bessie Williams (a child ? his)
1 CONT proved 21.10.1580
1 CONT Source GWH 1C1 / 1C1B
0 @N6000000001877506024@ NOTE of St Julians
1 CONT Sheriff of Monmouth 1553
1 CONT see his father's notes re Star Chamber records
1 CONT MP Monmouth 1553 - 58
1 CONT 1559 Queen Elizabeth - General pardon incl Wm H late of St Julian's esq, alias of Westminster, alias s & h/o Walter H knt, alias Mayster Wm H
1 CONT A number of documents re inheritance of the daughters of Ed Griffiths of Penrhyn Anglesey incl a suit in chancery between Wm H & Jane (St Julians) Wm H & Kathryn (Swansea) and Sir Nick Bagnell & Helen. Also IPM 1544 on Ed Griffith
1 CONC  and award 1542 following his death. Also bond 1559 / 60 following suit in chancery incl Sir Nick B, Wm (Swansea) & John H of Byldwas (Welshpool)
1 CONT fathers will
1 CONT will of William Morgan of Tredegar - refers to William & to Miles his bro
1 CONT 1567 IPM conducted by Sir Wm Morgan of Pencoed - his kinsman
1 CONT Source GWH 1C1 / 1C1A
