1 CONT Elizabeth Wydevill was the daughter of Sir Richard Wydevill, 1st Earl Rivers <p10292.htm> and Jacquetta de Luxembourg <p10197.htm>. She was born circa 1437 at Grafton Regis, Northamptonshire, England.2 She married, firstly, Sir Jo
1 CONC hn Grey, 7th Lord Ferrers of Groby <p10166.htm> circa 1452.2 She married, secondly, Edward IV Plantagenet, King of England <p10164.htm>, son of Richard Plantagenet, 3rd Duke of York <p10164.htm> and Lady Cecily Neville <p10164.htm
1 CONC >, on 1 May 1464 at Grafton Regis, Northamptonshire.2 She died on 8 June 1492 at St. Saviour's Abbey, Bermondsey, London, England.2 She was buried at St. George's Chapel, Windsor Castle, Windsor, Berkshire, England.2  She was also
1 CONC  known as Elizabeth Woodville. Through her marriage, Elizabeth Wydevill gained the title of Queen Consort Elizabeth of England on 26 May 1465.2 Her marriage to Edward IV Plantagenet, King of England was annulled on 25 June 1483 by
1 CONC  an Act of Parliament, known as the 'Titulus Regius', because of King Edward's alleged precontract to Eleanor Butler. The marriage was ultimately recognised as valid in October 1485 by the first Act of Parliament of King Henry VII
1 CONC .2
1 CONT Children of Elizabeth Wydevill and Sir John Grey, 7th Lord Ferrers of Groby <p10166.htm>:
1 CONT Thomas Grey, 1st Marquess of Dorset <p10757.htm>+ b. 1451, d. 10 Apr 1501 Sir Richard Grey <p10166.htm> b. c 1456, d. 26 Jun 1483
