1 CONT [edit] Bibliography
1 CONT
1 CONT Source material on all aspects of Richard's reign is neatly and impartially brought together by Keith Dockray in Richard III: A Reader in History (Sutton, 1988).
1 CONT
1 CONT     * The Trial of Richard III by Richard Drewett & Mark Redhead (Sutton, 1984) (ISBN 0-86299-198-6)
1 CONT     * Royal Blood: Richard III and the mystery of the princes by Bertram Fields (HarperCollins, ©1998) (ISBN 0-06-039269-X)
1 CONT     * Richard III: The Road to Bosworth Field by Peter W. Hammond & Anne Sutton ( Constable, 1985) (ISBN 0-09-466160-X)
1 CONT     * Richard the Third by Michael Hicks (Tempus, 2001) (ISBN 0-7524-2302-9)
1 CONT     * Richard III: A Study in Service by Rosemary Horrox (Cambridge University Press, 1991) (ISBN 0-521-40726-5)
1 CONT     * Richard III and the North edited by Rosemary Horrox (University of Hull, 1986) (ISBN 0-85958-066-0)
1 CONT     * Bosworth 1485 by Michael K. Jones (Tempus Publishing, 2002) (ISBN 0-7524-2334-7) [2]
1 CONT     * Richard III: The Great Debate edited by Paul Murray Kendall (W.W. Norton, 1992) (ISBN 0-393-00310-8)
1 CONT     * Richard the Third by Paul Murray Kendall (W.W. Norton, 1956) (ISBN 0-393-00785-5)
1 CONT     * The Betrayal of Richard III by V.B. Lamb (A. Sutton, 1991) (ISBN 0-86299-778-X)
1 CONT     * Richard III and the Princes in the Tower by A.J. Pollard (St Martin's Press, 1991) (ISBN 0-312-06715-1)
1 CONT     * Good King Richard? by Jeremy Potter (Constable, 1983) (ISBN 0-09-464630-9)
1 CONT     * Richard III by Charles Ross (Methuen, 1981) (ISBN 0-413-29530-3)
1 CONT     * Richard III: England's Black Legend by Desmond Seward (Penguin Books, 1997) (ISBN 0-14-026634-8)
1 CONT     * The Coronation of Richard III: The Extant Documents by Anne Sutton & Peter W. Hammond (St Martin's Press, 1984) (ISBN 0312169795)
1 CONT     * Richard III's Books by Anne Sutton & Livia Visser-Fuchs (Sutton Pub, 1997) (ISBN 0-7509-1406-8)
1 CONT     * The Princes in the Tower by Alison Weir (Ballantine, 1995) (ISBN 0-345-39178-0)
1 CONT     * Joan of Arc and Richard III: sex, saints, and government in the Middle Ages by Charles Wood (Oxford University Press) (ISBN 0-19-506951-X)
1 CONT     * History of the English Speaking Peoples by Winston Churchill, Vol. 1, The Birth of Britain
