0 @N6000000003658765836@ NOTE THOMAS BERKELEY, Knt., of Thornbury, Gloucestershire, and Hovingham, Yorkshire, Constable and Porter of Berkeley Castle, younger son, born in 1472.  He married (1st) in 1504/5 ELEANOR CONSTABLE, widow of John Ingleby, of Ripley, Y
1 CONC orkshire, and daughter of Marmaduke Constable, Knt., of Flamborough, Yorkshire, by his 2nd wife, Joyce, daughter of Humphrey Stafford, Knt. ... They had two sons ... and two daughters. ... He was knighted by the Earl of Surrey 9 S
1 CONC ept. 1513 on the field at the Battle of Flodden.  He was heir in 1523 to his older brother, Maurice Berkeley, K.B.  He was summoned to Parliament from 9 August 1529 by writ directed Thome Berkley de Berkley, and, though not in pos
1 CONC session of the Berkeley estates, was ranked in the precedency of his ancestors as third Baron on the roll.  His wife, Eleanor, died in 1525, and was buried at St. Augustine's, Bristol.  He married (2nd) in 1526 CECILY ARNOLD, wido
1 CONC w of Richard Rowdon, Esq., of Gloucester, Gloucestershire, Rowdon, Herefordshire, and London, Alderman of Gloucester, Sheriff of Gloucester, and daughter and co-heiress of _____ Arnold, of Gloucestershire.  SIR THOMAS BERKELEY, st
1 CONC yled Lord Berkeley, Mowbray, and Segrave, died testate at Mangotsfield, Bristol 22 Jan. 1532/3, and was buried with his 1st wife.  His widow, Cecily, died testate between July and Nov. 1558, and was buried at St. Augustine's, Bris
1 CONC tol.
