0 @N6000000003177806873@ NOTE Illegitimate daughter of Henry Beaufort and Alice FitzAlan
0 @N6000000000640046604@ NOTE Sir Edward fought at Agincourt in 1415 in the retinue of Duke Humphrey of Gloucester, a brother to Henry V. 
1 CONT     He married Jane Beaufort. Jane was the natural daughter of Henry, Cardinal Beaufort and Alice Fitz Alan, the daughter of Richard Fitz Alan, Earl of Arundel. 
1 CONT     Henry Beaufort was the natural son of John Plantagenet, a. k. a. John of Gaunt, Duke of Lancaster, by Katherine Swynford, whom he later married.  Katherine was the widow of Sir Hugh Swynford and the daughter of Sir Payne Rouet
1 CONC , a knight of Hainault.  After John's marriage to Katherine, their children, surnamed Beaufort, were legitimized by Act of Parliament. 
1 CONT     Because of this alliance with the house of Lancaster, the Stradling family's fortune and status were at their peaks during his lifetime. 
1 CONT     Inspired by the actions of his father, he made a pilgrimage to Jerusalem at the age of sixty-three.   He was also made a Knight of the Holy Sepulchre, and died shortly thereafter.
0 @N6000000002116211588@ NOTE Most of the references describe Edward Stradling father of Katherine as "of Gloucestershire".  There is also one which identifies him as Sir Edward Stradling of St. Donat's in Glamorgan, who m. Jane Beaufort.  The pedigrees that I
1 CONC  have seen for the Stradlings of St. Donats do not show a daughter Katherine, but in the absence of any contrary information, the St. Donat's Stradlings are shown as the ancestors.  
